    ('05', '01', '0000000361', '025',
     'Community Paramedic', 'Paramedics are Emergency Medical Service Providers who administer advanced prehospital medical treatment to sick or injured persons enhancing the role of EMS as a partner in public health and community healthcare delivery. Community paramedics may perform health screenings, home inspections, and other services while in the field or in a client''s home. They address access to primary care and reduce the usage of emergency care resources.  Requirements: 1) Must be at least 18 years of age. 2) Must be a licensed Paramedic. 3) Must complete an approved Community Paramedic course with training consisting of a minimum of 210 clinical hours and required number of patient contacts. 
