    ('06', '01', '1004', '184',
     'Clinical Chemist License', 'This license permits you to direct a laboratory certified under CLIA for performing high complexity testing in all areas of the specialty of chemistry.
Fees: Fees are subject to change with each fiscal year. Refer to the LFS General Fee Information Page  for a full list of fees associated with licensing. 
Exams: Applicants must refer to the LFS Website for the list of approved certifying organization examinations for each license category.
Academic, Training, and Experience Requirements: Master of Science or doctoral degree in chemistry with specific course requirements plus one year of post-graduate training in clinical chemistry and three years of applicable work experience in a clinical laboratory certified under Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA), two years of which shall have been at a supervisory level.
Renewal Period: Every two years.
Refer to the LFS Website for more complete information.
Comments: Clinical laboratory director as defined by law in clinical laboratories.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Division 2, Chapter 3, Section 1200-1327. California Code of Regulations, Title 17, Section 1030, 1030.5, 1030.6, 1030.7, 1030.8, and 1031.4.',
