    ('06', '01', '150', '131',
     'Real Estate Broker License', 'Real estate agency activities for compensation.
Fees: Examination: $95; License: $300; Fingerprint processing: $49; Renewal $300
Examination Frequency:  Weekly.
Exam Locations: Sacramento, Fresno, Oakland, San Diego, and Los Angeles.
Experience Requirement: Two years full-time licensed salesperson experience within last 5 years or college graduate with a degree that includes a major or minor in real estate and 8 specified college level courses in real estate.
Average Time to Process Application: Approximately 4 weeks.
Renewal Period: 4 years.
Special License Requirements: Fingerprints and proof of legal presence.
Comments: Corporations are licensed through a person qualified as a real estate broker. Brokers have a continuing education requirement of 45 clock hours of specified courses that must be taken before renewal. Real Estate Brokers may conduct Mineral, Oil, and Gas activity by virtue of the broker license.
Real estate brokers who conduct residential mortgage loan activities are required to obtain an Mortgage Loan Originator license endorsement to their real estate license.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Section 10130 through 10171.6; Section 10200 through 10226.',
     '1', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '151', '131',
     'Real Estate Salesperson', 'Real estate agency activities for compensation.
Fees: Examination: $60; License: $245 with evidence of completion of three college level courses in specified areas; Fingerprint processing: $49; Renewal $245
Examination Frequency:  Daily.
Exam Locations: Sacramento, Fresno, Oakland, Los Angeles, San Diego.
Experience Requirement: Three semester units (college level) in real estate principles, real estate practice, and one additional specified real estate course prior to taking the examination.
Average Time to Process Application: 4 weeks.
Renewal Period: 4 years.
Special License Requirements: Fingerprints and proof of legal presence.
Comments: Licensee must meet continuing education requirement of 45 clock hours of specified courses prior to renewal of license.
Real estate salespersons who perform residential mortgage loan origination activities are required to obtain an Mortgage Loan Originator license endorsement to their real estate license.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Section 10130 through 10171.6; 10200 through 10226.',
