    ('06', '01', '312', '135',
     'Chiropractor', 'Doctor of chiropractic.

Fees: Initial Licensing: $137; License application $345; License certification / Out of state license verification $83; License renewal fee $336
Examination Frequency:  California Law and Professional Practice Exam (CLPPE) is given on a continual basis.
Exam Locations: CLPPE offered in United States, Puerto Rico, and Guam.
Experience Requirement: High school diploma or equivalent; 60 pre-chiropractic college credits; graduation from a board-approved chiropractic college; passage of National Board parts I, II, III, IV, and Physiotherapy.
Average Time to Process Application: Approximately five months.
Renewal Period: Annually. (Continuing education is required for renewal.)
Special License Requirements: Chiropractors intending to take or supervise x-rays must obtain an X-ray Supervisor and Operator Certificate, from the Department of Health Services, Radiologic Health Branch.
Comments: Licentiates of other states may qualify for reciprocal licensure. 
Authority: Chiropractic Initiative Act; Business and Professions Code, Section 1000 et seq. California Code of Regulations, Title 16, Chapter 4.',
