    ('06', '01', '5801', '123',
     'Safety Representative Certification', 'It is the policy of the Division that every tunnel project and underground mine shall have a certified safety representative who directs the required safety program and corrects unsafe conditions.  Examination and certification of safety representatives by the Mining and Tunneling Unit promotes the safe operation of underground mines and tunnels and ensures that safety representatives possess adequate knowledge and competence in underground work safety and health.

Fees: Application: None; Examination: $15; License: None.
Examination Frequency:  As needed.
Exam Locations: Contact Division of Occupational Safety and Health, Mining and Tunneling Unit.
Experience Requirement: At least two years of underground safety experience. Knowledge of blasting methods, safety orders, and hazardous concentrations of gas. 
Average Time to Process Application: Varies.
Renewal Period: 5 years.
Special License Requirements: Proof of legal alienage.
Comments: N/A
Authority: California Labor Code, Sections 6710, 6711 and 7990-8002.',
     '1', '1', '0', '0', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '5802', '123',
     'Blasters License', 'It is the policy of the Division of Occupational Safety and Health to require that a person be licensed as a blaster at operations where explosives are used, as defined in Labor Code Sections 6710(b) and 6711. The licensed blaster shall supervise and visually direct the operation.  The examination and licensing ensures that blasters possess an adequate level of knowledge about blasting safety, to restrict the use of explosives by blasters to those categories about which they have knowledge and experience, and to establish and maintain a list of licensed blasters.

Fees: Application: None; Examination: $15; License: None.
Examination Frequency:  As needed.
Exam Locations: Contact Division of Occupational Safety and Health, Mining and Tunneling Unit.
Experience Requirement: At least three years of blasting experience. Knowledge of blasting methods, safety orders, and hazardous concentrations of gas.
Average Time to Process Application: Varies.
Renewal Period: 5 years.
Authority: California Labor Code, Sections 6710, 6711 and 799.',
     '1', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '5803', '123',
     'Gas Tester Certification', 'It is the policy of the Division that any person who performs the required gas testing in tunnels or underground mines, during the course of employment, shall obtain certification from the Division.  Examination and certification of gas testers by the Mining and Tunneling Unit promotes the safe operation of underground mines and tunnels and ensures that gas testers possess adequate knowledge and competence in underground gas testing.

Fees: Application: None; Examination: $15; License: None.
Examination Frequency:  As needed.
Exam Locations: Contact Division of Occupational Safety and Health, Mining and Tunneling Unit.
Experience Requirement: At least 1 year of underground experience. Must have experience in gassy situations if applying for gassy certification. Bring your testing instrument and unexpired calibration gases. 
Average Time to Process Application: Varies.
Renewal Period: 5 years.
Special License Requirements: Proof of legal alienage.
Comments: N/A
Authority: California Labor Code, Sections 6710, 6711 and 7990-8002.',
