    ('06', '01', '631', '109',
     'Public Display Fireworks', 'Persons firing dangerous fireworks for public displays, special effects fireworks in motion pictures, stage productions and television.

The original and annual renewal fees shall be as follows:
Fingerprints (DOJ charge) - $37
Basic commercial - $125
Restricted commercial - $50
Rockets - $50
Special Effects (1st Class) - $500
Special Effects (2nd Class) - $400
Special Effects (3rd Class) - $200
Theatrical - $400
Theatrical Trainee - $200
Performer - $250
Duplicate License- $25
Examination Frequency:  One time.
Exam Locations: Varies.
Experience Requirement: Proven knowledge of installation and firing of dangerous fireworks.
Average Time to Process Application: 4 - 6 weeks.
Renewal Period: Annually (Fiscal Year).
Special License Requirements: References (in writing) from at least 5 licensed pyrotechnic operators.
Comments: License may be denied if convicted of a felony involving explosives or dangerous fireworks or convicted as a principal or accessory in a crime against property involving arson or other fire related offense.
Authority: Health and Safety Code, Sections 12570-12578; California Code of Regulations, Sections 981-981.9, Title 19.',
