     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '673', '118',
     'Manufactured Home, Mobilehome, and Commercial Modular Salesperson License', 'Required for all salespersons selling manufactured homes, mobilehomes, or commercial modular structures. 

Fees: NOTE: Fees subject to change, Original Application: $219 for each applicant (two-year increments), plus a $25 fee for the Manufactured Home Recovery Fund (MHRF) for Manufactured Home applicants—this fee does not apply to Commercial Modular applicants; Renewal of License: $150.
Verification of the applicant’s U.S. citizenship or alien status has a one-time fee of $13 for each applicant (Not applicable to businesses owned under partnerships or corporations).
Examination Frequency:  Salespersons for manufactured homes, mobilehomes or commercial modulars must pass an examination. The examination may be repeated as often as needed to pass; however, the $86 fee applies to each examination taken. A Study Guide is available at a cost of $29 at HCD''s HQ office.  The Study Guide is also available as a free download.
Exam Locations: Riverside, Sacramento, El Cajon, and San Luis Obispo 
Experience Requirement: Completion of six (6) hours preliminary education before examination and continuing education after licensure for manufactured home/multifamily manufactured home/mobilehome applicants.
Average Time to Process Application: Within one week of submittal of a complete application, a temporary permit may be issued allowing operation up to 120 days while the department investigates and processes the license.
Renewal Period: Licenses will be issued for a two-year period expiring on the last day of the month in which the temporary permit or license was issued. Applications to renew licenses must be delivered to the department before the date of license expiration, or if mailed, must bear a postmark date on or before the expiration date.
Authority: Health and Safety Code (HSC), Division 13, Part 2 and California Code of Regulations, Title 25, Chapter 4.  Reference HSC section 18045.',
     '1', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '674', '118',
     'Manufactured Home, Mobilehome 90 Day Salesperson Certificate', 'This certificate allows the applicant to work as a limited salesperson for 90 days under limited authority and closer supervision, for the purpose of allowing applicants to see if this career choice is for them.
Fees: NOTE: Fees subject to change, Application: $134.  Note:  To continue as a fully licensed salesperson, the 90-day certificate holder must complete any remaining salesperson’s prerequisites within the 90-day certificate period.  After the expiration date, holders can submit their expired certificates, with all other salesperson requirements, within three (3) months of the certificate''s expiration date. 
Verification of the applicant’s U.S. citizenship or alien status has a one-time fee of $13 for each applicant (not applicable to businesses owned under partnerships, limited liability companies, or corporations).
Examination Frequency:  N/A
Exam Locations: N/A
Experience Requirement: N/A
Average Time to Process Application: Within one week of submittal of a complete application a 90-Day certificate may be issued.  Exception: If the application contains criminal history or incorrect information.
Renewal Period: The Department may, on a one-time-only basis, issue a 90-day Certificate to an applicant for an original salesperson license. A certificate holder shall be employed for not more than 90 days from the date of issuance by a licensed dealer and may, under direct supervision, induce others to buy or sell a manufactured home, mobilehome or commercial modular except as noted in the comments section.
Special License Requirements: Visit HCD website.
Authority: Health and Safety Code (HSC), Division 13, Part 2 and California Code of Regulations, Title 25, Chapter 4.  Reference HSC section 18052.6.',
     '1', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '680', '142',
     'Acupuncture License', 'Persons (excluding physicians, surgeons, podiatrists, and dentists) who perform acupuncture in connection with their practices.
Fees: 
Initial Exam Application: $250- $350
Fingerprint processing: $49 if using hard cards- livescan is paid directly to site
Approved for Examination: $800 exam fee
Approved for Re-examination: $800 exam fee
Initial Licensure: $500, including 1 Initial Wall licnese as part of the Initial License fee
Wall License: $50.00 for each place of practice address
Renewal: $500
Delinquency Fee: $150
Examination Frequency: daily
Exam Locations: Multiple locations (at PSI Testing centers as of 10/2018) 
Experience Requirement: Completion of (1) an education and training program approved by the Board; or (2) a tutorial program in the practice of an acupuncturist which is approved by the Board; or (3) documented educational training and clinical experience outside the U.S. which meets the standards pursuant to Sections 4939 and 4941 of the Business and Professions Code.
Average Time to Process Application: 45 days.
Renewal Period for both AC and Wall License: Biennially (every second year) prorated for the initial license period to allow for birthday month renewal.
Special License Requirements: N/A
Comments: N/A
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Chapter 12, Sections 4925-4979.
California Code of Regulations, Title 16, Chapter 13.7.',
