    ('06', '01', '708', '149',
     'Dental License', 'California dentists.
Fees: Application: $400-$800 (This does not include initial licensing fee, which will be assessed upon approval of application.)
Fingerprint processing: $49
Renewal: $650
Experience Requirement:: Must have graduated from a Board-approved or CODA accredited Dental School, completed a CODA approved advanced residency program in addition to having graduated from a Board-approved or CODA accredited school, or satisfy clinical experience requirements and holding a current active license in another state or US territory.
Average Time to Process Application: 4-6 weeks.
Online Update of license status: 48 hours and Arrival of pocket license: 2-3 weeks . 
Mail Update of license status: 6-8 weeks and Arrival of pocket license: 6-8 additional weeks.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year).
Comments:California offers five pathways to licensure as a dentist each with different requirements.  Completion of the ADEX and WREB clinical examinations, completion of a General Practice Residency or Advanced Education in General Dentistry and completion of clinical practice hours in another state or US territory.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Sections 1628-1628.5, 1632, 1634.1 & 1635.5.
