    ('06', '01', '726', '153',
     'Hearing Aid Dispenser License', 'Individuals who fit and sell hearing aids must obtain a hearing aid dispenser license from the Hearing Aid Dispensers Bureau in order to practice in California.
Fees: Application: $75
Permanent License/Renewal: $280
Written exam: $225
Practical exam: $500
Branch office license: $25
Temporary license: $175
Trainee license: $175
Examination Frequency:  The written exam is offered electronically on a continuous basis. 
Exam Locations: Written exams are administered in approximately 20 locations throughout California and several other states.
The practical exam is administered 2-4 times a year. Practical exams are administered in Sacramento. Note: Written exam must be passed before taking the practical exam.
Experience Requirement: Must be at least 18 years of age and possess a high school diploma or equivalent.
Average Time to Process Application: 189 days after completion of the application (per California Code of Regulations, Section 1399.113).
Renewal Period: Annually.
Special License Requirements: Fingerprints are required of all applicants.
Comments: N/A
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Chapter 7.5, Section 2530 et seq.',
     '1', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '727', '154',
     'Landscape Architect, Licensed', 'Landscape architects and any person who uses the title or does the work of a landscape architect as defined in Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 3.5.
Fees: 
National Examination (Landscape Architects Registration Examination) - administered by The Council of Landscape Architectural Registration Boards (CLARB):
Inventory, Analysis, and Project Management       $ 525.00
Planning and Design       $ 525.00
Construction Documentation and Administration       $ 525.00	
Grading, Drainage, and Stormwater Management       $ 525.00
*Final fees established as part of the annual CLARB budget process. Fees are subject to change. 
Eligibility Application Evaluation Fee: $100.00
Local Examination (California Supplemental Examination): $350.00
CSE Application Evaluation Fee: $100.00
Initial License: $700.00
Renewal: $700.00

Examination Frequency:  National Examination - three (3) times a year, Local Examination - continuous
Examination Locations: Multiple
Experience Requirement: Must be at least 18 years of age or have graduated from high school in order to receive training/experience credit; have six years of qualifying education and/or work experience. Multiple years of credit are granted for a masters/bachelors degree, or approved extension certificate in landscape architecture OR an architecture degree from a NAAB-accredited program; two-year degree in landscape architecture accepted for one year; any four-year degree accepted for one year. Work experience may be done under a licensed landscape architect, architect/registered civil engineer, or licensed landscape contractor and may be combined with education or used to satisfy all six years (credit limits vary by profession).

Average Time to Process Application: Target application processing time is 30 days.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year).
Special License Requirements: N/A
Comments: The Board of Landscape Architects was sunsetted effective July 1,1997, after which the Technical Committee was established under the purview of the California Architects Board.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Section 5615 et seq.; California Code of Regulations, Title 16, Division 26.',
     '1', '3', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '728', '157',
     'Contact Lens Dispenser', 'Contact Lens Dispensers are individuals who fit and adjust prescription or cosmetic contact lenses.

Fees: 
Application processing: $200
Initial Registration Fee: $300
Fingerprint processing: $49
Registration renewal: $300
Examination Frequency:  Four times per year (February, May, August and November)
Exam Locations: Contact the American Board of Opticianry (ABO) / National Contact Lens Examiners (NCLE) at (703) 719-5800 or (800) 296-1379.
Experience Requirement: Applicants must pass the Contact Lens Registry Examination (CLRE) administered by the National Contact Lens Examiners (NCLE).
Average Time to Process Application: 4-6 weeks.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year).
Special License Requirements: N/A
Comments: The practice of contact lens dispensing is the fitting and adjusting of prescription and cosmetic contact lenses from a registered dispensing optician firm.  Prescriptions are written by optometrists or ophthalmologists (M.D.).  Registration is not required for individuals under the direct supervision of an ophthalmologist or optometrist or working under the direct supervision of a registered contact lens dispenser.  The examination is given by the NCLE.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Section 2560.',
     '1', '2', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '730', '157',
     'Spectacle Lens Dispenser', 'Spectacle Lens Dispensers are individuals who fit and adjust eyeglass lenses with prescription.

Fees: 
Application processing: $200
Initial Registration Fee: $300
Fingerprint processing: $49
Registration renewal: $300
Examination Frequency:  Four times per year (February, May, August and November)
Exam Locations: Contact the American Board of Optometry (ABO) / National Contact Lens Examiners (NCLE) at (703) 719-5800 or (800) 296-1379.
Experience Requirement: Applicants must pass the National Opticianry Competency Examination (NOCE) administered by the American Board of Opticianry.
Average Time to Process Application: 6-8 weeks.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year).
Special License Requirements:  N/A
Comments: The practice of spectacle lens dispensing is the fitting and adjusting of prescription spectacle lenses from a registered dispensing optician firm.  Prescriptions are written by optometrists or ophthalmologists (M.D.).  Registration is not required for individuals under the direct supervision of an ophthalmologist or optometrist or working under the direct supervision of a registered spectacle lens dispenser.  The American Board of Opticianry gives the examination.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Section 2559.1.',
     '1', '2', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '731', '155',
     'Physician and Surgeon', 'Doctor of Medicine.
Fees: Application and fingerprint: $674.00
Initial license: $888, reduces to $456.50 to those enrolled in postgraduate training at time of licensure.  Biennial: $888.
Examination Frequency:  Ongoing national exam administered by Federation of State Medical Boards.  See their website at www.fsmb.org and the United States Medical Licensing Examination website at www.usmle.org.
Exam Locations: Computerized sites, see above for notation.
Experience Requirement: Two years pre-professional education, a minimum of four-academic years medical education from a medical school recognized by the Medical Board of California with diploma and one or two-year Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education or Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada approved/slotted post-graduate training.
Average Time to Process Application: 80 days for initial review.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year).
Special License Requirements: N/A
Comments: Please visit www.mbc.ca.gov for additional information.
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Sections 2080-2099,2100-2115,2135,2135.5,2141,2143,2151,2170,2184.',
