    ('06', '01', '76932', '182',
     'Proprietary Private Security Officer', 'A proprietary private security officer is defined generally as an unarmed individual, (1) who is employed exclusively by a single employer, (2) whose primary duty is to provide security services for that employer, (3) whose services are not contracted to any other entity or person, and (4) who meets both of the following criteria:

A)	He or she is required to wear a distinctive uniform clearly identifying the individual as a security officer, and
B)	He or she is likely to interact with the public while performing his or her duties.

Requirements:
o	Be 18 or older.
o	Undergo a criminal history background check through the DOJ and the FBI.

Application Fee - $55
CA Department of Justice (DOJ) Fingerprint Processing Fee - $32
Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) Fingerprint Processing Fee - $17
Renewal Fee - $40
Delinquent Renewal ($40 renewal fee + $25 delinquency fee) - $65

The initial license is valid for 2 years.  Each renewal cycle extends the registration for an additional 2 years.

The annual continuing education requirement in Section 7574.18 of the Code shall be two hours.

Average time to process an application is 60 days.

Authority: Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 11.4',
     '1', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '76933', '182',
     'Private Patrol Operator', 'A Private Patrol Operator is a person/company who agrees to furnish, or furnishes, a watchman, guard, patrolperson, or other person to protect persons or property or to prevent the theft, unlawful taking, loss, embezzlement, misappropriate, or concealment of any goods, wares, merchandise, money, bonds, stocks, notes, documents, papers, or property of any kind.
Requirements:
o	Be 18 or older.
o	Undergo a criminal history background check through the DOJ and the FBI.
o	Possess a minimum of 6,000 hours of compensated experience in security work (equates to 3 year of full-time employment).
o	Pass a multiple-choice examination covering the Private Security Services Act. 
o	Have committed no offense or violation of the Private Security Services Act that would be grounds for license suspension or revocation.
Exams are given by a State contracted company known as PSI. If the individual meets the minimum requirements for admittance to the examination after the application has been reviewed and approved, he/she will receive a letter to contact PSI for scheduling. 

Application and Exam Fee - $550
Initial License Fee - $770
DOJ Fingerprint Processing Fee - $32
FBI Fingerprint Processing Fee - $17
Renewal Fee - $900
Delinquent Renewal ($900 renewal fee + $450 delinquency fee) - $1,350

The initial license is valid for 2 years.  Each renewal cycle extends the registration for an additional 2 years.

A registrant shall annually complete 8 hours of specifically dedicated review or practice of security officer skills prescribed in this section, Section 7583.7, or by the bureau by regulation.

Average time to process an application is 60-125 days.

Authority: Business and Professions Code, Chapter 11.5',
