    ('06', '01', '795', '171',
     'Dental Hygienist, Registered', 'Fees: Application Fee:   $100
 DHCC no longer administers a clinical examination and relies on 3rd party regional examinations administered by the Western Regional Examination Board (WREB) and the Central Regional Dental Testing Services (CRDTS) for clinical examination results to apply toward licensure.
Examination Frequency:  Computer-based examinations on California Dental Law and Ethics specific to RDHs; eligibility is given after application requirements are met.

License Issuance Fee: $100.00
License Renewal: $300
Delinquent Renewal Fee: $150
Experience Requirement: Graduation from an accredited (CODA) and DHBC approved dental hygiene program.
Average Time to Process Application:   30 business days.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every two years).
Special License Requirements: N/A
Comments: N/A
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Sections 1900-1966.6.
California Code of Regulations, Title 1, Chapter 3, Article 3, Sections 1072, 1076. 1079, Article 4, Sections 1082-1082.1.',
     '1', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '796', '171',
     'Registered Dental Hygienists in Alternative Practice (RDHAP)', 'Fees: Application:   $100
License Issuance Fee: $150
Examination Frequency:  Computer-based examinations on California Dental Law and Ethics specific to RDHAPs; eligibility is given after application requirements are met.
Exam Locations: In test centers throughout the State of California.
Experience Requirement: Must be licensed dental hygienist with a minimum of 2,000 hours during the immediately preceding 36 months. Must have completed prescribed classes either through an approved RDHAP Program or through the Health Manpower Pilot Project (HMPP) and have established an independent practice under the HMPP by June 1, 1997.
Average Time to Process Application:   30 business days.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every two years).
Renewal Fee: $160.00
Delinquent Renewal Fee: ½ of current License Renewal Fee (currently $80)
Special License Requirements: N/A
Comments: N/A
Authority: Business and Professions Code, Sections 1922-1931.Note: The Dental Hygiene Committee (DHCC) was changed to a Board in 2018 and are now known as the Dental Hygiene Board of California (DHBC) and is the only state government agency in the United States that’s mandated to oversee its dental hygiene licensees and dental hygiene educational programs.',
     '1', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '80008', '130',
     'Pest Control Dealer Designated Agent', 'Any person who is responsible for supervising the operations of a licensed pest control dealer. Each licensed pest control dealer must maintain a designated agent at the principal office and an agent at each branch location.  
Exemptions: Individuals who have a DPR-issued Agricultural Pest Control Adviser License, Qualified Applicator License, or Journeyman Pest Control Aircraft Pilot Certificate may operate as a Dealer Designated Agent.
Fees: Initial application: $25; Renewal: $25 each year
Examination Fee: $50
Examination Information: DPR’s Licensing and Certification Program offers computer-based exams at testing centers state-wide for all individual licenses and certificates. Applications for all exams must be mailed to DPR''s Licensing and Certification Program. You can find more examination information on DPR''s website. 
Requirements: N/A
Examination Requirements: An applicant for a Dealer Designated Agent License must pass an examination that cover laws, regulations, and basic principles of a licensed pest control dealer, including the supervision and operation of dealer locations.
Average Time to Process Application: 30 days.
Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year). Continuing education is not required for the renewal of this license. 
Authority: Food and Agricultural Code, Section 11901, 11903, 11905, 11906, 11907 and 11910; Code of Regulations, Section 6000.2, 6511-6514, and 6540.',
