    ('06', '01', '80009', '124',
     'Limited Lines Automobile Insurance Agent', 'A limited lines automobile insurance agent is a person authorized to transact automobile insurance, as defined in California Insurance Code section 660.  

Qualifications 
• Minimum Age: 18 years
• Residency: California residency is not required
• Prelicensing Experience/Education: A minimum of 20 hours of approved prelicensing study and 12 hours of approved prelicensing study on ethics and the California Insurance Code
• Entity: Individual and Business Entity
Fees: 
• Filing Fee: $188 
• Examination fee: $55
• Renewal: $188 each two-year term –Late-Renewal fee: $282
• Fingerprint processing: The fee at the California Department of Insurance (CDI) test centers is $59. The fee at PSI test centers is $68.95.  
Other license information and requirements:
• Examination required: Yes
• Examination information: PSI Services, LLC, schedules the examinations for CDI''s limited lines automobile insurance agent applicants. For scheduling examinations use PSI''s Examination Scheduling Service at PSI Online - One stop Solution for Test Takers (psiexams.com).  Individuals may schedule their examinations with PSI either online or by telephone.
• Fingerprint impressions: Fingerprint impressions are required for all unlicensed resident and most non-resident applicants
• Average Time to Process Application: two to three weeks
• Renewal Period: Renewal Period: Two-year license
• Continuing Education: 20 hours of continuing education which includes three hours of ethics each two-year license period
Authority: California Insurance Code section 1625.55.',
