    ('06', '01', '80010', '124',
     'Accident and Health Agent or Sickness', 'The Accident and Health or Sickness license authorizes an individual to transact insurance products providing coverage for sickness, bodily injury, or accidental death and may include benefits for disability income. The licensee may also transact 24-hour care coverage and long-term care. The following list are samples of some of the insurance products that can be transacted with this license: health insurance, disability insurance, and credit disability insurance. 

Qualifications
• Minimum Age: 18 years
• Residency: California residency is not required
 • Prelicensing Experience/Education: Complete prelicensing requirements consisting of 20 hours of approved accident and health or sickness prelicensing study and 12 hours of approved prelicensing study on Ethics and the California Insurance Code
• Entity Type: Individual and Business Entity

Fees: 
• Application: $188
• Examination $55
• Renewal: $188 each two-year license term
• Fingerprint processing: The fingerprint fee at the California Department of Insurance (CDI) test centers is $59.  At PSI test centers, the fingerprint fee is $68.95.  

Other license information and requirements:
• Examination required: Yes
• Examination information: PSI Services, LLC, schedules the examinations for CDI''s  Accident and  Health or Sickness license applicants. To schedule examinations review PSI''s Examination Scheduling Service at PSI Online - One stop Solution for Test Takers (psiexams.com).  Individuals may schedule their examinations with PSI either online or by telephone.
• Fingerprint impressions: Fingerprint impressions are required for all unlicensed resident and most non-resident applicants.
• Average Time to Process Application: two to three weeks
• Renewal Period: Two-Year license term
For more information, review the following link: http://www.insurance.ca.gov/0200-industry/0050-renew-license/0200-requirements/accident-health/index.cfm 
