    ('06', '01', '80024', '108',
     'Certified Rangeland Manager (CRM)', 'The Certified Rangeland Manager (CRM) license is a "certified specialty" of forestry created by the Board under the authority of the Professional Foresters Law.

A Certified Rangeland Manager applies scientific principles to the art and science of managing rangelands.  Rangelands are lands supporting grass, shrub, and savanna vegetation types. 
Minimum requirements for licensure include an undergraduate or higher degree in range science or a related discipline, five years of professional work experience in range management, and successful completion of a comprehensive written examination. 
Fees: $200.00 for members of the California-Pacific Section, $300.00 for non-members. Application fee for change of status from Associate Rangeland Manager to CRM: $100.00 for Section member, $200.00 for non-member. A renewal fee is also required every two years.
Examination Frequency: October and, with adequate number of applicants, April of each year.
Exam Location: Sacramento
Renewal Period: Biannually. Licenses expire on July 1 of each alternating year.
Authority: Professional Foresters Law, Public Resources Code Sections 762 and 772.
More information may be found at the California-Pacific Section of the Society for Range Management website:  www.rangelands.org/casrm.
Alternate titles a CRM might use:
- Consulting range managers and scientists. 
- University of California Cooperative Extension Range and Livestock Advisors.
- University instructors in range science.',
     '1', '1', '2', '9', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '80028', '124',
     'Special Lines'' Surplus Line Broker', 'A Special Lines'' Surplus Line Broker is a person who places the following types of insurance with non-admitted insurers:  A)Insurance against perils of navigation, transit or transportation upon hulls, freights or disbursements, or other ship owner interests; upon goods, wares, merchandise and all other personal property and interests therein, in course of exportation from or importation into any country or transportation coastwise, including transportation by land or water from point or origin to final destination and including war risks; and marine builder''s risks, dry docks and marine railways, including insurance of ship repairer''s liability, and protection and indemnity insurance, but excluding insurance covering bridges or tunnels; B) Aircraft insurance; and C) Insurance on property or operations of railroads engaged in interstate commerce.

Qualifications:
• Minimum Age: 18 years 
• Residency: California residency is not required 
• Experience: Must hold a Property Broker-Agent and Casualty Broker-Agent license in resident state 
• Entity Types: Individual and Business Entity

Fees: Individual Application: $646 for Surplus line brokers who are only transacting on behalf of a licensed surplus line broker business entity; $1,296 for brokers who do not only transact on behalf of a special lines'' surplus line broker business entity.
Organization application: $1,296 (two year term)
Renewal: $646 or $1,296 as noted above for two-year term
Fingerprint processing fee: None  

Bond Information: Special lines'' Surplus Line brokers who are only transacting on behalf of a licensed surplus line broker business entity are not required to file a bond. All other Special lines'' Surplus Line Brokers must comply with the $10,000 bond requirement.
For more information: http://www.insurance.ca.gov/0200-industry/0050-renew-license/0200-requirements/special-lines-surplus.cfm#act.

Section 1760.5 of the California Insurance Code.',
