    ('06', '01', '80046', '155',
     'Registered Polysomnographic Technologist', 'Registered Polysomnographic Technologist: The registration is required for individuals who are responsible for the treatment, management, diagnostic testing, control, education, and care of patients with sleep and wake disorders in California.
Fees: Application: $120.00
Fingerprint: $49.00 plus any rolling fees (varies depending on location)
Initial license: $120.
Biennial Renewal: $220.00 Currently, Polysomnographic Trainees, Technicians, or Technologists are unable to renew their license online. Polysomnographic registrants must renew by mail.
Examination Information: Board of Registered Polysomnographic Technologist: www.brpt.org
Examination:  Registered Polysomnographic Technologist Examination for Polysomnographic Technologists (RPSGT). 
Minimum Requirements: 
1) You must have valid, current credentials as a Polysomnographic Technologist issued by the Board of Registered Polysomnographic Technologists (BRPT). The certificate is issued by BRPT once you have taken and passed the Registered Polysomnographic Technologist Exam (RPSGT); and 
2) You must have graduated from a polysomnographic educational program approved by the Board. You must submit a copy of your transcript and certificate of completion. 
3) You must possess at the time of application a current certificate in Basic Life Support issued by the American Heart Association or the American Safety and Health Institute.
Average Time to Process Application: 30 days
Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year).
Special License Requirements: N/A
Comments: Please visit www.mbc.ca.gov for additional information.
