    ('06', '01', '80054', '112',
     'Wastewater Treatment Plant Operator', 'Persons operating wastewater treatment facilities must be certified.
Wastewater treatment operators employed at municipalities or privately-owned wastewater treatment facilities.

Fees: The fee varies with the level of certification.
Grade; Exam; Certification; Renewal
Grade I: $120; $125; $150
Grade II: $155; $170; $150
Grade III: $295; $225; $150
Grade IV: $365; $255; $150
Grade V: $365; $255; $150
Examination Frequency:  Wastewater Operator Certification examinations are Computer Based and are available year-round. 

For additional information on Operator Certification, visit the links below:
https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/water_issues/programs/operator_certification/docs/cbt_faqs.pdf
https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/water_issues/programs/operator_certification/docs/cbt_process_overview.pdf

Exam Locations: Wastewater Operator Certification Computer Based Tests are available at more than 30 sites throughout California.  

