     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '925', '124',
     'Fire and Casualty Broker-Agent', 'A fire and casualty licensee is a person authorized to act as an insurance agent, broker, or solicitor, and a fire and casualty broker-agent license is a license so to act.



Qualifications

• Minimum Age: 18 years;

• Residency: California residency is not required;

• Prelicensing Experience/Education: Complete prelicensing requirements

  consisting of 40 hours of approved fire and casualty prelicensing study and

  12 hours of approved prelicensing study on ethics and the California

  Insurance Code;

• Entity: Individual and Business Entity


Fees: 

• Application: $128 for two-year term; 

• Re-examination: $37;

• Renewal: 128, two-year term;

• Fingerprint processing: $60.95 


Other license information and requirements:
• Exam required: Yes;

• Examination Frequency and Locations: Monday through Friday in San

• Francisco, San Diego, Sacramento, and Los Angeles;

• Fingerprint impressions: Fingerprint impressions are required for all

  unlicensed resident and most non-resident applicants.

• Average Time to Process Application: 1 to 2 weeks;

• Renewal Period: Renewal Period: Biennially (every second year)



Special License Requirements: 

Continuing Education: During each of the first four 12-month periods following issue of license, complete 25 hours of continuing education, thereafter, complete 24 hours of continuing education during each two-year license term. 

For more information on this license type use this URL http://www.insurance.ca.gov/0200-industry/0050-renew-license/0200-requirements/fire-casualty/auth-act.cfm

