     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '927', '124',
     'Life and Disability Insurance Analyst', 'A Life and Disability Insurance Analyst is a person who, for a fee or compensation of any kind, paid by or derived from any person or source other than an insurer, advises, purports to advise, or offers to advise any person insured under, named as beneficiary of, or having any interest in, a life or disability insurance contract, in any manner concerning that contract or his or her rights in respect thereto.

Qualifications:
• Minimum Age: 23 years
• Residency: California residency is required 
• Pre-licensing Experience/Education: Section 1849 of the California Insurance Code (CIC) was amended to clarify the eligibility requirements to qualify for the life and disability insurance analyst license. Specifically, to qualify to apply for this license, individuals must be licensed as both a life-only (LO) and accident and health (AH) licensee for five years prior to taking the qualifying examination. 

Fees: License Filing: $622
Fingerprints: The fee at the California Department of Insurance (CDI) test centers is $59.  At PSI test centers, the fingerprint fee is $68.95. 
Renewal: $622 each two-year license term.

Exam required: Yes
Exam Fee: $155
•Examination information: PSI Services, LLC, schedules the examinations for CDI''s life and disability insurance analyst applicants. For scheduling examinations use PSI''s Examination Scheduling Service at http://media.psiexams.com/LC/apps/Attention.htm. Individuals may schedule their examinations with PSI either online or by telephone. 

• Fingerprint impressions: Fingerprint impressions are required for unlicensed applicants.
• Average Time to Process Application: two to three weeks
• Renewal Period: Two-year license term

For more information on this license use http://www.insurance.ca.gov/0200-industry/0050-renew-license/0200-requirements/life-disability.cfm.

