Authority: Sections 11100-11107 of the California Insurance Code.',
     '1', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20240522'),
    ('06', '01', '93', '132',
     'Yacht and Ship Broker''s License', 'Yacht (a yacht refers to a vessel over 16 feet in length and under 300 gross tons) and ship brokerages.
Fees: Application: None; Examination: $25; License: $200; Fingerprint fees are paid to a Live-Scan Facility.
Examination Frequency:  Once a month at each examination location.
Examination Locations: Lake Perris, Sacramento, and San Diego.
Experience Requirement: One (1) year as a licensed yacht salesman, as shown on the Department''s records, has owned and operated a marine business selling new and used yachts for a minimum of three continuous years preceding application for a broker’s license in California, or has been licensed as a yacht broker or yacht salesperson in another state for a minimum of three continuous years preceding application for a broker’s license in California.
Average Time to Process Application: 1 month.
Renewal Period: Annually.
Special License Requirements: None; however, they need compliance with a local license and U.S. and State tax requirements.
Comments: A $15,000 surety bond or cash deposit is required when applying for a yacht broker''s license. Bond is not required for a Salesperson; they are covered under the sponsoring licensed California broker. 
Authority: Harbors and Navigation Code, Chapter 5, Article 2, Sections 700-740; California Code of Regulations, Title 14, Sections 7601-7623.',
