     'Tattoo Technician', 'Licensing Requirements

Each person seeking licensure must document to the Department''s satisfaction that the applicant:
Is eighteen years of age or older;
Has successfully completed, within the three years prior to submitting an application, a course on prevention of disease transmission and blood-borne pathogens that complies with the standards adopted by the federal Occupational Safety and Health Administration, as described in 29 CFR 1910. 1030 et seq., as amended from time to time, and that requires the successful completion of a proficiency examination as part of such course;
Holds current certification by the American Red Cross or the American Heart Association in basic first aid; and
Form verifying completion of two thousand (2,000) hours of practical training and experience under the personal supervision and instruction of a tattoo technician; OR

Form verifying five years of continuous practice of tattooing in this state prior to January 1, 2015.

Please be advised that training hours completed after January 1, 2015 will only be credited if the supervisor was licensed during the period of training.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://portal.ct.gov/DPH/Practitioner-Licensing--Investigations/Tattoo/Tattoo-Technician', '20240320'),
    ('09', '01', '189', '001',
     'Tattoo Technician - Training Permit', 'A student tattoo technician may practice tattooing under the personal supervision of a tattoo technician for a period not to exceed two years.
 
A student tattoo technician shall register with the department for purposes of completing the practical training and experience required to obtain a license. 
 
In order to qualify for registration, an applicant must submit the following:
 
Verification of completion of a course on prevention of disease transmission and blood-borne pathogens that complies with the standards adopted by the federal Occupational Safety and Health Administration, as described in 29 CFR 1910. 1030 et seq. , as amended from time to time, and that requires the successful completion of a proficiency examination as part of such course;
 
Verification of current certification by the American Red Cross or the American Heart Association in basic first aid; and
 
A notarized statement signed by a licensed tattoo technician acknowledging responsibility for personally supervising the applicant''s practical training and experience in tattooing.',
