     'https://portal.ct.gov/DEEP/Municipal-Wastewater/Wastewater-Treatment-Plant-Operator-Certification-Fact-Sheet', '20240320'),
    ('09', '01', '208', '013',
     'Water Treatment Plant Operator - Class IV', 'Class IV Operator – An applicant for Class IV Operator certification shall (A) submit satisfactory evidence of (i) at least four years of experience in the operation of a Class III or IV wastewater treatment facility, of which experience at least two years are direct responsible charge experience as a chief operator at a Class III wastewater treatment facility or shift or process control operator at a Class IV wastewater treatment facility; (ii) a high school diploma or G.E.D.; and (iii) successful completion of higher education equivalent to at least 135 CEUs in a field determined by the commissioner to be related to the operation of a wastewater treatment facility; of which at least 27 CEUs are directly related to the operation of a wastewater treatment facility; and (B) pass the Class IV examination.',
