     'http://www.myfloridalicense.com/DBPR/boxing-commission/#1511278704691-c8ecc918-5cec', '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '158', 'BP1',
     'Veterinarians', 'Florida Statute 474. A “veterinarian” means a person who is licensed to engage in the following activities: diagnosing of medical conditions of animals; prescribing, dispensing, or administering drugs, medicine, appliances, applications, or treatment of whatever nature for the prevention, cure, or relief of a wound, fracture, bodily injury, or disease thereof; performing any manual procedure for the diagnosis of or treatment for pregnancy or fertility or infertility of animals; or determining the health, fitness, or soundness of an animal; and surgery, acupuncture, obstetrics, dentistry, physical therapy, radiology, theriogenology, and other branches or specialties of animal medicine.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.myfloridalicense.com/DBPR/veterinary-medicine/', '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '159', 'BP1',
     'Yacht & Ship Salesperson or Broker', 'Florida statute 326. (1) “Broker” means a person who, for or in expectation of compensation: sells, offers, or negotiates to sell; buys, offers, or negotiates to buy; solicits or obtains listings of; or negotiates the purchase, sale, or exchange of, yachts for other persons. (3) “Salesperson” means a person who, for or in expectation of compensation, is employed by a broker to perform any acts of a broker.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.myfloridalicense.com/DBPR/yacht-and-ships/', '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '16', 'ACS',
     'Security Officer Instructor', NULL,
     '0', '0', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '160', 'DEP',
     'Drinking Water Treatment Plant Operator', 'The Drinking Water Treatment Plant Operator contains four classes of licensure. Treatment plant classes are A, B, C and D with class A being the highest. Licensure in Florida is a linear process in that an operator must obtain a lower level license prior to becoming eligible to receive a higher level license. For each level of licensure each applicant must also demonstrate the applicable number of years of experience. Licenses are issued for a two-year period with an expiration date of April 30 of every odd numbered year. In order for individuals to renew their license they must complete a specified amount of continuing education (CEU). Without the appropriate CEUs, the license will not be renewed.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://floridadep.gov/water/certification-restoration/content/water-and-domestic-wastewater-operator-certification-program', '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '161', 'DEP',
     'Waste Water Treatment Plant Operator', 'The Waste Water Treatment Plant Operator contains four classes of licensure. Treatment plant classes are A, B, C and D with class A being the highest. Licensure in Florida is a linear process in that an operator must obtain a lower level license prior to becoming eligible to receive a higher level license. For each level of licensure each applicant must also demonstrate the applicable number of years of experience. Licenses are issued for a two-year period with an expiration date of April 30 of every odd numbered year. In order for individuals to renew their license they must complete a specified amount of continuing education (CEU). Without the appropriate CEUs, the license will not be renewed.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://floridadep.gov/water/certification-restoration/content/water-and-domestic-wastewater-operator-certification-program', '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '162', 'DEP',
     'Water Distribution System Operator', 'The Water Distribution System Officer contains four classes of licensure. Distribution levels are 1, 2, 3, & 4 with level 1 being the highest. Licensure in Florida is a linear process in that an operator must obtain a lower level license prior to becoming eligible to receive a higher level license. For each level of licensure each applicant must also demonstrate the applicable number of years of experience. Licenses are issued for a two-year period with an expiration date of April 30 of every odd numbered year. In order for individuals to renew their license they must complete a specified amount of continuing education (CEU). Without the appropriate CEUs, the license will not be renewed.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://floridadep.gov/water/certification-restoration/content/water-distribution-system-operator-licensing', '20200225'),
