    ('12', '01', '17', 'BAR',
     'Lawyer (Attorney)', 'Articl V, Section 15 of Florida Constitution and Rule Regulating the Florida Bar: An individual who represents clients in court, before quasi-judicial officials, or before administrative agencies of the government.  Attorneys may also act as trustees, guardians, or executors; may specialize in a particular phase or type of law (i.e., corporate law, real estate law, criminal law, etc.); and may also teach college courses in the law.<br><br><b>Articl V, Section 15 of Florida Constitution and Rule Regulating the Florida Bar  <br><br>Educational Requirements:</b><br>Doctorate of Jurisprudence and passage of the Florida bar exam',
