    ('12', '01', '306', 'BPE',
     'Professional Engineer', 'Florida Statute 471; Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 61G15. The Principles and Practice of Engineering (PE) exam tests for a minimum level of competency in a particular engineering discipline. It is designed for engineers who have gained a minimum of four years’ post-college work experience in their chosen engineering discipline.',
