     'Bail Bond (Professional Bail Bond)', 'Florida Statutes 648.25: defines a “Professional Bail Bond Agent” as any person who pledges United States currency, United States postal money orders or cashier’s check as security for a bail bond in connection with a judicial proceeding and receives or is promised therefore money or things of value.',
