     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://myfloridacfo.com/division/agents/Licensure/General/default.htm', '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '266', 'DOI',
     'Property and Casualty (Personal Lines Non-Resident)', '626.015 & 626.732: A "PERSONAL LINES AGENT" is defined as a general lines agent who is limited to transacting business related to property and casualty insurance sold to individuals and families for noncommercial purposes.',
     '4', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://myfloridacfo.com/division/agents/Licensure/General/default.htm', '20200225'),
    ('12', '01', '267', 'DOI',
     'Property and Casualty (Personal Lines Resident (Temporary))', '626.175: A “TEMPORARY PERSONAL LINES AGENT” may be issued to an individual who is executor or administrator of the estate of a deceased individual licensed and appointed as a personal lines agent at the time of death; or to a surviving next of kin of the deceased individual, if no administrator or executor has been appointed and qualified.

OR

To an individual appointed to represent an insurer of the industrial or ordinary-combination class solely for collecting premiums and servicing in-force policies. Such licensee may not directly or indirectly solicit, negotiate, or effect contracts of insurance.  Individuals applying for this reason MUST complete the 60 hour Personal Lines Pre-Licensing Course.',
