    ('12', '01', '319', 'DLE',
     'Law Enforment', 'Florida Statutes; Rule 11A-B, Florida Administrative Code: A law enforcement officer is any person who is elected, appointed, or employed full-time by any municipality, the state, or any political subdivision thereof.  This individual is vested with authority to bear arms and make arrests, and primary responsible for maintaining civic order.<br><br><b>Chapter 943, Florida Statutes; Rule 11A-B, Florida Administrative Code.  <br><br>Educational Requirements:</b><br>Graduation from high school or the equivalent degree and successful completion of a basic recruit training course.  At least 40 hours continuing education are required every 4 years.  Licensee must complete eight hours of human diversity training.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
