    ('13', '01', '144', '018',
     'General Contractor Individual', 'Applicant requirements:
General Contractor:
- Is at least 21 years of age

- Is of a good character and is otherwise qualified as to competency, ability, and
integrity; 

-  Has received a baccalaureate degree from an accredited four-year college and has at least one year of proven experience working as or in the employment of a general contractoror other proven experience deemed substantially similar by the division; 

Residential contractor:
- Is at least 21 years of age

- Is of a good character and is otherwise qualified as to competency, ability, and
integrity; 

- Has at least two years of proven experience working as or in the employment
of a residential contractor, predominantly in the residential-basic category, or other
proven experience deemed substantially similar by the division; and has had significant responsibility for the successful performance and completion of at least two projects falling within the residential-basic category in the two years immediately preceding application

Fees:
Application:	$200.00
Testing/Renewals: $106.00 for General Contractors
		  $72 for Residential Contractors

Examination:
Type:	Computer-based
When:	Annually
Where:	Check with PSI licensure (http://www.psiexams.com)
Repeats:	2',
