    ('15', '01', '0000000003', '012',
     'Architect', 'DESCRIPTION OF OCCUPATION:
	An Architect plans and designs private residences, buildings and other structures to meet their client''s functional, economic, and aesthetic requirements.

REQUIREMENTS FOR LICENSING:
	Professional requirements:  Certify to reading, understanding, and agreeing to comply with the laws and rules that the board determines are required for licensure.

	Education and Experience requirements:  Have one of the following:  (1) Bachelor''s, master''s, or higher degree in architecture from an approved institution, and completion of the Intern Development Program (IDP); OR  (2) Graduate of a 4-year architectural, pre-architectural or arts and science curriculum from an approved school or college, completion of IDP, and 2 years of additional lawful experience, OR  (3) Graduate of a 2-year architectural technology curriculum from an approved community college or technical training school, completion of IDP, and 5 years of additional lawful experience; OR  (4) Completion of IDP and 8 years of additional lawful experience.

EXAMINATIONS:
A.R.E., a computer-based exam.
	
FEES:
Application fee of $150 for endorsement or $100 for exam, $128 for 2-year license, and $100 for biennial compliance resolution fund. License renewal every 2 years is $104.

OTHER:
There were 1,045 licenses currently active as of February 24, 2022.

~ revised 12/16',
