     'Massage Therapist', 'DESCRIPTION OF OCCUPATION:
	A Massage Therapist massages customers using a variety of techniques such as kneading, rubbing, or pressing motions of the hands, elbows, or fingers to stimulate blood circulation, relieve muscle tension, or treat other conditions.
	
REQUIREMENTS FOR LICENSING:
	Personal requirements:  Be beyond 18 years of age. Be a U.S. citizen, U.S. national, or alien authorized to work in the U.S.

	Professional requirements:  Have a current cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) certificate for both infant and adult issued by the American Red Cross or American Heart Assn.

	Education requirements:  1) Complete 50 hours of in-class course work in human anatomy, physiology, and structural kinesiology.   2) Complete 100 hours of in-class course work on theory and demonstration of massage.   3) Complete 420 hours of practical massage training under supervision of teacher or sponsoring massage therapist. 

EXAMINATIONS:
	State Massage Licensing Exam.

FEES:
$50 for application, $64 for 2-year license, and $100 for biennial compliance resolution fund. Renewal every 2 years is $64.
	
OTHER:
There were 6,094 licenses currently active as of February 24, 2022.

