     'Naturopath', 'DESCRIPTION OF OCCUPATION:
	A Naturopath diagnoses, treats, and cares for patients using a system of practice that bases treatment of physiological functions and abnormal conditions on natural laws governing the human body.

REQUIREMENTS FOR LICENSING:
	Education requirements:  Be a graduate of a school, university, or college of naturopathy which has been accredited by or received candidacy status with a regional or national accrediting agency recognized by the U.S. DOE at the time of graduation.

EXAMINATIONS:
	Part I and II of the Naturopathic Physicians Licensing Examination (NPLEX) and if you took the NPLEX prior to August 2007, the exam on homeopathy.

