    ('15', '01', '0000000082', '003',
     'Beauty Instructor', 'DESCRIPTION OF OCCUPATION:
A Beauty Instructor teaches Beauty Operators.
					
REQUIREMENTS FOR LICENSING:
	Personal requirements:  Be a U.S. citizen, U.S. national, or alien authorized to work in the U.S.  Be at least 16 years of age.

EXPERIENCE AND EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:  
Possess a current and valid Hawaii Beauty Operator (BEO) license. Have experience as a licensed Beauty Operator for at least 1 year in Hawaii or in another jurisdiction with standards substantially similar to Hawaii.
Completed 600 hours of Beauty instructor training at a beauty school OR possess an instructor license in another jurisdiction

EXAMINATIONS:
Exam given by Prometric are scheduled three times a year, usually in January, May, and October.

APPLICATION AND FEES:
$20 for application. Temporary permit is $40.
In 2022, pay $145 (license $22 + CRF $100 + 1/2 renewal $23)
In 2023, pay $72 (license $22 + CRF $50)
*All licenses, regardless of date issued, expire on December 31 of every ODD-NUMBERED year.
	
