    ('16', '01', '1011', '002',
     'Acupuncturists', 'Acupuncturists must be licensed by the Idaho Board of Acupuncture.  A person may obtain either a license or a certification for acupuncture. Qualifications for licensure include: 1) Submitting an application with required documents and fees; 2) Graduation from approved acupuncture program; 3) Successful completion of acupuncture internship; 4) Passing the NCCAOM Acupuncture Certification Examination; 5) Completing the Blood Borne Pathogen course and comprehensive exam that incorporates clean needle techniques and OSHA procedures and requirements.  Certification can be obtained if a person holds a license in a profession with similar requirements. Qualifications for certification include: 1.) Passing a board approved exam; 2.) Full membership of the American Academy of Medical Acupuncture OR Earn a doctoral degree from approved school in a related field and successful completion of a minimum of 100 hours of didactic course work in acupuncture taught by an NCCAOM certified acupuncturist; 3.) Completing the Blood Borne Pathogen course and comprehensive exam that incorporates clean needle techniques and OSHA procedures and requirements. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=ACU&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1021', '003',
     'Architect', 'Architects must be licensed to practice in Idaho. Applicants for examination need to meet the following requirements: 1) Submit an application with required documents, and fees; 2) Graduate from a board-approved accredited architectural school; 3) Register as an Architectural Intern with the Board or completed the Intern Development Program; 4) Pass the Architect Licensure Examination.  Applicants may be licensed by endorsement if they hold a current and valid license issued by another jurisdiction recognized by the board and a national council of architectural registration board certificate. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
