     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=ATC&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1035', '004',
     'Athletic Seconds', 'Idaho law and administrative code require all Combatants, Promoters, Matchmakers, Managers, Seconds including trainers, and Ring Officials to be licensed by The Idaho Athletic Commission at the Idaho Bureau of Occupational Licenses. Athletic Trainers must also be licensed by the Idaho Board of Medicine to practice. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bom.idaho.gov/BOMPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=ATH&BureauLinkID=150#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1036', '004',
     'Athletic Ring Official', 'Ring officials for amateur and professional boxing, wrestling, and martial arts matches must be licensed by The Idaho Athletic Commission. The commission regulates all contests and exhibitions involving unarmed combat between individuals. Applicants must: 1) Be at least twenty-one (21) years of age; 2) Have no record of conviction of a felony or other crime involving moral turpitude; 3) Have had at least one year experience in either amateur or professional contest as a ring official; 4) Submit verification of proficiency from three people. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.  Admin code 03.01.01 "Ring Official. Ring officials include referees, judges, timekeepers and glovers"',
