     'http://bom.idaho.gov/BOMPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=ATH&BureauLinkID=150#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1041', '005',
     'Barber', 'Barbers must be licensed by the Idaho State Bureau of Occupational Licenses. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Document completion of the tenth grade; 2) Be at least sixteen and one-half years of age; 3) Document completion of 900 hours of training for barbering, or 1,800 hours for barber-styling from a board-approved school; 4) Pass an exam. The holder of a current license in another state may also be eligible for licensure. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=BAR&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1042', '005',
     'Barber - Instructor', 'Barber instructors must be licensed by the Idaho Board of Barber Examiners at the Idaho Bureau of Occupational Licenses. All applicants for a Barber Instructor''s license must:  1) Hold a current barber license issued by the board;  2) Have satisfactorily completed a minimum six (6) month course of barber instructing as a student in a properly licensed barber college;  3) Have a minimum of one (1) year of experience as an apprentice in a licensed barber college, or as a barber in a licensed establishment, within the last three (3) years;  5) Successfully pass an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=BAR&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1043', '005',
     'Barber - Stylists', 'Stylists must be licensed by the State Bureau of Occupational Licenses. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Be at least sixteen and one-half years of age; 2) Complete of two years of high school or equivalent; 3) Complete an approved course or an apprenticeship in cosmetology or manicuring; 4) Pass a written and practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=BAR&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1051', '006',
     'Chiropractors', 'Chiropractors are licensed by the Idaho State Board of Chiropractic Physicians. Licensing requirements for new applicants include: 1.) Graduation from an approved chiropractic college or university; 2.) Completion of the application and licensing fee; 3.) Passing the National Board Examinations. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=CHI&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1071', '008',
     'Cosmetologists', 'Anyone that practices cosmetology, nail technology, haircutting, esthetics, or electrology must be licensed in the State of Idaho. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Be at least sixteen and one-half years of age; 2) Complete two years of high school or the equivalent; 3) Complete an approved course or an apprenticeship in cosmetology or manicuring; 4) Pass a written and practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=COS&BureauLinkID=105', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1072', '008',
     'Cosmetologist - Instructor', 'cosmetology instructors must be licensed in the State of Idaho. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Complete twelve (12) semester college credit hours or equivalent of required instruction; 2) Pass an exam; 3) Hold a current license as a cosmetologist issued by the board;  4) Have a minimum of two (2) years'' experience as a licensed cosmetologist in a registered cosmetological establishment and complete a three (3) month teacher''s course of instruction at an approved school of cosmetology OR Have a minimum of five (5) years'' experience. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '3', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=COS&BureauLinkID=105##', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1073', '008',
     'Electrologist', 'Electrologists must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Cosmetology. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Be at least sixteen and one-half years of age; 2) Complete two years of high school or the equivalent; 3) Complete 800 hours of training for electrology; 3) Graduate from a board approved school; 4) Pass a written and practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1074', '008',
     'Electrologist - Instructor', 'Electrology instructors must be licensed in the State of Idaho. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Complete twelve (12) semester college credit hours or equivalent of required instruction; 2) Pass an exam; 3) Hold a current license as a electrologist issued by the board;  4) Have a minimum of two (2) years'' experience as a licensed electrologist in a registered establishment and complete a three (3) month teacher''s course of instruction at an approved school OR Have a minimum of five (5) years'' experience. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '3', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1075', '008',
     'Esthetician', 'Estheticians must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Cosmetology. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Be at least sixteen and one-half years of age; 2) Complete two years of high school or the equivalent; 3) Complete 600 hours of training for esthetics; 3) Graduate from a board approved school; 4) Pass a written and practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1076', '008',
     'Esthetician - Instructor', 'Esthetics instructors must be licensed in the State of Idaho. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Complete twelve (12) semester college credit hours or equivalent of required instruction; 2) Pass an exam; 3) Hold a current license as a estheticia issued by the board;  4) Have a minimum of two (2) years'' experience as a licensed esthetician in a registered establishment and complete a three (3) month teacher''s course of instruction at an approved school OR Have a minimum of five (5) years'' experience. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '3', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1077', '008',
     'Nail Technician', 'Estheticians must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Cosmetology. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Be at least sixteen and one-half years of age; 2) Complete two years of high school or the equivalent; 3) Complete 400 hours of training for nail technology; 3) Graduate from a board approved school; 4) Pass a written and practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1078', '008',
     'Nail Technician - Instructor', 'Nail Technology instructors must be licensed in the State of Idaho. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Complete twelve (12) semester college credit hours or equivalent of required instruction; 2) Pass an exam; 3) Hold a current license as a nail technician issued by the board;  4) Have a minimum of two (2) years'' experience as a nail technician in a registered establishment and complete a three (3) month teacher''s course of instruction at an approved school OR Have a minimum of five (5) years'' experience. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '3', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1079', '008',
     'Haircutter', 'Haircutters must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Cosmetology. In order to obtain a license, an applicant must: 1) Be at least sixteen and one-half years of age; 2) Complete two years of high school or the equivalent; 3) Complete 900 hours of training in Hair cutting; 3) Graduate from a board approved school; 4) Pass a written and practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1081', '009',
     'Counselors (LPC)', 'Licensed Professional Counselor (LPCs) in private practice must be licensed by The Idaho State Licensing Board of Professional Counselors and Marriage & Family Therapists. Requirements for licensure include:  1) Graduating with a degree in counseling; 2) 1,000 hours of supervised counseling experience; 3) Passing a written examination. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=COU&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1082', '009',
     'Clinical Practice Counselors (LCPC)', 'Licensed Clinical Professional Counselors (LCPCs) in private practice must be licensed by The Idaho State Licensing Board of Professional Counselors and Marriage & Family Therapists. Requirements for licensure include:  1)1)',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=COU&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1083', '009',
     'Marriage & Family Therapists (LMFT)', 'Marriage & Family Therapists (LMFT) in the State of Idaho must be licensed by The Idaho State Licensing Board of Professional Counselors and Marriage & Family Therapists. Requirements for licensure include: 1) Graduating with a degree in marriage and family therapy; 2) 1 year practicum to include 300 client hours; 3) 3,000 hours supervised experience; 4) Passing a written examination. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=COU&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1084', '009',
     'Associate Marriage and Family Therapists (LAMFT)', 'Associate Marriage and Family Therapists (LAMFT) in the State of Idaho must be licensed by The Idaho State Licensing Board of Professional Counselors and Marriage & Family Therapists. Requirements for licensure include:  1) Graduating with a degree in marriage and family therapy; 2) 1 year practicum to include 300 client hours; 3) Passing a written examination. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=COU&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1091', '010',
     'Denturists', 'Denturists in the State of Idaho must be licensed by Board of Denturitry at the Idaho Bureau of Occupational Licenses. Licensure is available through both endorsement and examination. Applicants must: 1.) Complete at least two years of formal training at an accredited and approved educational institution; 2.) Complete at least two years of internship under the supervision of a licensed denturist or have equivalent experience. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=DEN&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1101', '011',
     'Driving Instructor', 'Driving Instructors in Idaho must be licensed by the Idaho Driving Businesses Licensure Board at the Idaho Bureau of Occupational Licenses. Licensed driving instructors must:  1) Be at least 21 years of age and have a valid driver''s license;  2) Submit a copy of a satisfactory driving record from the Idaho Transportation Department;  3) Submit a criminal history background check;  4) Submit a medical certificate;  5) Submit copies of required completed coursework; 6) Complete a board approved apprenticeship training program or equivalent. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '4', '2', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=DRB&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1111', '012',
     'Geologists', 'Geologists in Idaho must be licensed with the Idaho Board of Registration for Professional Geologists at the Idaho Bureau of Occupational Licenses. Registration requires meeting education and experience requirements as well as passing a fundamentals and practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=GEO&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1121', '013',
     'Landscape Architects', 'Landscape Architects must be licensed to practice in Idaho. Applicants for licensure must: 1) Graduate from an accredited architectural curriculum in a school or college approved by the board; 2) Complete or have started three (3) years of experience through the Intern Development Programor or have eight years of board-approved experience; 3) Pass an exam. The most common way to prepare for licensing exam is to complete a landscape architecture program at an accredited school. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=LAR&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1131', '014',
     'Liquefied Petroleum Gas Dealers', 'Liquefied petroleum gas dealers in Idaho must submit evidence of meeting Board approved education, experience, and examination qualifications to be licensed by the Idaho Liquefied Petroleum Gas Safety Board. Applicants for licensure must: 1) Be at least eighteen (18) years of age and of good moral character;  2) Never have a license revoked or otherwise sanctioned as part of disciplinary action from this or any other state;  3) Never have been convicted, found guilty, or received a withheld judgment for any felony (rehabilitation of the applicant and other mitigating circumstances will be taken into consideration);  4) Never have been found by the board to have engaged in conduct prohibited by the licensure act;  5) Successfully complete a certified educational training program approved by the board;  6) Successfully complete 1 year of supervised experience; 7) Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=LPG&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1141', '015',
     'Massage Therapists', 'Massage Therapists are required to be licensed in Idaho.  Requirements for licensure include: 1) High school diploma or equivalent; 2) Eighteen (18) years of age or older; 3) Good moral character; 4) Successful completion of a board-approved massage program; 5) Passing a nationally recognized competency examination in massage therapy that is approved by the board. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=MAS&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1161', '017',
     'Funeral Directors', 'Funeral Directors in Idaho must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Morticians at the Idaho Bureau of Occupational Licenses. Applicants for licensure must: 1) Be at least 21 years of age; 2) Complete at least 60 semester hours or 90 quarter hours at an accredited college or university with a ''C'' average; 3) Complete at least 15 semester credit hours from a mortuary college accredited by the American Board of Funeral Service Education; 4) Practice as a licensed resident trainee under supervision of licensed resident mortician for at least 12 months; 5) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=MOR&BureauLinkID=105', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1162', '017',
     'Morticians', 'Mortician in Idaho must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Morticians at the Idaho Bureau of Occupational Licenses. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Be at least 21 years of age; 2.)',
     '0', '0', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=MOR&BureauLinkID=105', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1171', '018',
     'Nursing Home Administrators', 'Nursing home and shelter home managers in Idaho must be licensed by the Board of Examiners of Nursing Home Administrators at the Bureau of Occupational Licenses. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Be at least 21 years of age; 2.) Demonstrate good moral character; 3.) Complete a bachelor''s degree program or two (2) years of satisfactory practical experience; 4.) Complete an administrator-in-training program; 5.) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=NHA&BureauLinkID=100', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1181', '019',
     'Occupational Therapists', 'Occupational Therapists must be licensed to practice in the State of Idaho. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Graduate from an approved occupational therapy program; 2.) Complete six months of supervised fieldwork; 3.) Pass a qualifying examination; 4.) Be certified by the American Occupational Therapy Certification Board. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1182', '019',
     'Occupational Therapist Assistant', 'Occupational Therapist Assistants must be licensed to practice in the State of Idaho. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Graduate from an approved occupational therapy program; 2.) Complete four months of supervised fieldwork; 3.) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=OCT&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1191', '020',
     'Optometrists', 'Optometrists must be licensed by the State Board of Optometry to practice. Applicants must: 1.) Be 21 years of age or older; 2.) Graduate from an approved school of optometry; 3.) Pass a licensing exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=OPT&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1201', '021',
     'Physical Therapists', 'Physical Therapists must be licensed by the state. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Graduate from an accredited physical therapist program; 2.) Provide two references from individuals with personal knowledge of the applicantâ€™s character and ability to provide physical therapy; 3.) Pass a qualifying examination. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=PHT&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1202', '021',
     'Physical Therapist Assistant', 'Physical Therapist Assistant must be licensed by the state. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Graduate from an accredited physical therapist assistant program; 2.) Pass a qualifying examination. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=PHT&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1211', '022',
     'Podiatrists', 'Podiatrists must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Podiatry. Applicants must: 1.) Be at least 21 years of age; 2.) Graduate from an accredited podiatric college; 3.) Complete at least two years of podiatric residency; 4.) Pass the national board exam sponsored by the National Board of Podiatric Medical Examiners; 5.) Be of good moral character; Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=POD&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1221', '023',
     'Psychologists', 'Psychologists must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Psychological Examiners. Licensing requirements include: 1) A Doctoral degree or the equivalent from an approved college or university; 2) Two years of supervised experience; 3) Passing a written and oral exam; A license is not required for school psychologists who practice in a university or college setting, social psychologists, or psychologists working for government agencies.  Public School Psychologists in Idaho must hold a Personnel Services Certificate and a School Psychologist Endorsement from the Idaho Department of Education. To be eligible for the certificate and endorsement, an applicant must: 1.) Earn a master''s degree in education or psychology from an approved college or university; 2.) Complete 1,200 hours of internship within a school district under the supervision of a certificated school psychologist. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=PSY&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1231', '024',
     'Residential Care Administrator', 'Residential care facility administrators must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Be at least 21 years old; 2.) Complete a specialized course or a program of study in the area of residential care facility administration; 3.) Have either a high school diploma or equivalent and eight hundred (800) hours of on-site experience under the supervision of a licensed administrator, an associate degree and four hundred (400) hours of on-site experience, or a bachelor''s degree and two hundred (200) hours of on-site experience; 4.) Submit evidence of good moral character; 5.) Pass an open book exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1241', '025',
     'Real Estate Appraiser - Registered Trainee', 'Real Estate Appraisers must be licensed in Idaho. There are four licensure levels for appraisers: Registered Trainee, Licensed Residential, Certified Residential, and Certified General.  Applicants for registered trainee must: 1.)',
     '4', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=REA&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1242', '025',
     'Real Estate Appraiser - Licensed Residential Appraiser', 'Real Estate Appraisers must be licensed in Idaho. There are four licensure levels for appraisers: Registered Trainee, Licensed Residential, Certified Residential, and Certified General. Licensed Residential Appraiser requirements include: 1.) 75 classroom hours of courses in subject related to real estate appraisal; 2.)',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=REA&BureauLinkID=100#http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=REA&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1243', '025',
     'Real Estate Appraiser - Certified Residential Appraiser', 'Real Estate Appraisers must be licensed in Idaho. There are four licensure levels for appraisers: Registered Trainee, Licensed Residential, Certified Residential, and Certified General. Certified Residential Appraiser license requirements include: 1.) 50 hours of courses; 2.) Holding an associate degree or higher; 3.) 2,500 hours of experience credits; 4.) Passing of exam after education and experience is approved by board. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=REA&BureauLinkID=100#http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=REA&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1244', '025',
     'Real Estate Appraiser - Certified General Appraiser', 'Real Estate Appraisers must be licensed in Idaho. There are four licensure levels for appraisers: Registered Trainee, Licensed Residential, Certified Residential, and Certified General. Certified General Appraiser license requirements include: 1.)',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=REA&BureauLinkID=100#http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=REA&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1251', '026',
     'Speech-Language Pathologist', 'Speech-Language Pathologists must possess a master''s or doctoral degree from a nationally accredited school of speech-language pathology and supervised postgraduate professional experience. Applicants must also pass the national Praxis speech-language pathologist examination or other appropriate examination approved by the Idaho Speech and Hearing Services Licensure Board.  Public school speech-language pathologists must hold a Personnel Services Certificate and a Speech-Language Pathologist Endorsement from the Idaho Department of Education. To be eligible for the certificate and endorsement, an applicant must earn a master''s degree in a speech/language pathology program and an institutional recommendation from an approved college or university. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SHS&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1252', '026',
     'Speech-Language Pathologist Assitant', 'Speech-Language Pathologist Assistants must possess an associateâ€™s degree from a nationally accredited school of speech-language pathology, pass a board approved exam, and work under the supervision of a licensed speech-language pathologist. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SHS&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1253', '026',
     'Speech-Language Pathologist Aid', 'Speech-Language Pathologist Aids must possess a bachelor''s degree from a nationally accredited school of speech-language pathology, pass a board approved exam, and work under the supervision of a licensed speech-language pathologist. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SHS&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1254', '026',
     'Audiologist', 'Audiologists must possess a master''s or doctoral degree from a nationally accredited school of audiology and supervised postgraduate professional experience. Applicants must also pass the national Praxis audiology examination or other appropriate examination approved by the Idaho Speech and Hearing Services Licensure Board. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1255', '026',
     'Hearing Aid Dealer and Fitters', 'Hearing Aid Dealer and Fitters  must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants are required to take and pass the International Licensing Examination (ILE) for Hearing Healthcare Professionals and a practical exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SHS&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1261', '027',
     'Shorthand Reporters', 'Shorthand Reporters must be certified by the Idaho State Certified Shorthand Reporters Board. Applicants for certification must: 1.) Be of good moral character; 2.) Have a high school diploma or GED; 3.) Have passed the Idaho certified shorthand reporter exam, the Registered Professional Reporter (RPR) exam, the Registered Merit Reporter (RMR) exam, the Registered Diplomate Reporter (RDR) exam, or the Certified Realtime Reporter (CRR) exam within two years prior to the application date. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SHS&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1271', '027',
     'Social Workers', 'Social Workers must be licensed in Idaho. There are three licensure levels available to social workers: Social Workers, Masters Social Worker & Clinical Social Worker. Licensing requirements for Baccalaureate Social Work or "Social Worker" include: 1.) Good moral character; 2.) Bachelor''s degree in social work from an approved college or university; 3.) Passing an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SWO&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1272', '027',
     'Masters Social Worker', 'Social Workers must be licensed in Idaho. There are three licensure levels available to social workers: Social Workers, Masters Social Worker & Clinical Social Worker. Licensing requirements for Masters Social Worker include: 1.) Good moral character; 2.) Master''s or doctorate degree in social work from an approved college or university; 3.) Passing an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SWO&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1273', '027',
     'Clinical Social Worker', 'Social Workers must be licensed in Idaho. There are three licensure levels available to social workers: Social Workers, Masters Social Worker & Clinical Social Worker. Licensing requirements for Clinical Social Worker include: 1.) Good moral character; 2.) Master''s or doctorate degree in social work from an approved college or university; 3.) Two years of postgraduate supervised clinical experience; 4.) Passing an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=SWO&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1280', '029',
     'Wastewater Laboratory Operator', 'Wastewater Laboratory Operators must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Documenting one (1) year of acceptable lab experience at a class I or higher system; 3.) Passing a laboratory analyst exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1281', '029',
     'Wastewater Treatment Operator', 'Wastewater Operator must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Completing education and experience requirements; 3.) Passing a written exam. Upon obtaining one thousand six hundred (1,600) hours of supervised on-site operating experience, the operator shall be eligible to apply for an unrestricted Class I license. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1282', '029',
     'Wastewater Collection Operator', 'Wastewater Collection Operator must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Completing education and experience requirements; 3.) Passing a written exam. Upon obtaining one thousand six hundred (1,600) hours of supervised on-site operating experience, the operator shall be eligible to apply for an unrestricted Class I license. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1283', '029',
     'Drinking Water Distribution Operators', 'Drinking Water Distribution Operators must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Completing education and experience requirements; 3.) Passing a written exam. Upon obtaining one thousand six hundred (1,600) hours of supervised on-site operating experience, the operator shall be eligible to apply for an unrestricted Class I license. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1284', '029',
     'Drinking Water Treatment Operators', 'Drinking Water Treatment Operators must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Completing education and experience requirements; 3.) Passing a written exam. Upon obtaining one thousand six hundred (1,600) hours of supervised on-site operating experience, the operator shall be eligible to apply for an unrestricted Class I license. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1285', '029',
     'Backflow Assembly Testers', 'Backflow Assembly Testers must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Documenting successful completion of a Board-approved backflow assembly tester training program; 3.) Passing the American Backflow Prevention Association (ABPA) backflow assembly tester exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1286', '029',
     'Drinking Water Very Small System Operator', 'Drinking Water Very Small System Operators must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Documenting eighty-eight (88) hours of acceptable on-site operating experience at a water system; 3.) Completing a six-hour water distribution course; 4.) Passing a written exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1287', '029',
     'Wastewater Very Small System Operators', 'Wastewater Very Small System Operators must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Documenting fifty (50) hours of acceptable on-site operating experience at a wastewater collection system; 3.) Completing education requirements; 4.) Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1288', '029',
     'Wastewater Treatment Lagoon Operators', 'Lagoon Operators must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Documenting twelve (12) consecutive months of acceptable on-site operating experience at a Lagoon system; 3.) Passing a written exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1289', '029',
     'Wastewater Treatment Land Operators', 'Wastewater Treatment Land Operators must be licensed in Idaho. Requirements include: 1.) Possessing a high school diploma or GED; 2.) Documenting six (6) months of on-site operating experience at a wastewater land application system 3.) Passing a written exam; 4.) Possess a wastewater Class 1 or higher operator license. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardAdditional.aspx?Bureau=WWP&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '1291', '030',
     'Genetic Counselors', 'Genetic counselors are required to be licensed in Idaho. Requirements for licensure include:  1.) Submitting an application with required documents, and fees; 2.) Possessing a master''s or doctoral degree in genetics or a related field from a board approved college or university; 3.) Passing a nationally recognized competency examination approved by the board. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibol.idaho.gov/IBOL/BoardPage.aspx?Bureau=GEN#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2000', '111',
     'Electrical Apprentice', 'Electricians must be licensed in Idaho. There are four certificates of competency available to electricians: Electrical Apprentice registration, Journeyman Electrician license, Master Electrician license, and Electrical Contractor license. Electrical Apprentice Applicants must: 1.) Be at least 16 years of age; 2.) Be employed by a licensed Electrical Contractor; 3.)',
     '4', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/ele_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2005', '111',
     'Specialty Journeyman Electrician', 'Specialty electricians must be licensed in Idaho and are only allowed to work in their area of specialization. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of: Elevator; Sign; Manufacturing/Assembling; Limited Energy; Irrigation Sprinkler; Well Driller/Pump Installer; Refrigeration, Heating & Air Conditioning; Outside Wireman (Lineman); and Photovoltaic (Solar) Installer. Specialty Journeyman Electrician must: 1.) Document a minimum of 4,000 hours of work experience as an Idaho Electrical Specialty Trainee; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are valid for three (3) years for specialty apprentices.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2007', '112',
     'HVAC Apprentice', 'Heating, Ventilation & Air Conditioning (HVAC) workers must be licensed in the State of Idaho. There are three certificates of competency available to HVAC workers: apprentice registration, journeyman license, and contractorâ€™s license. HVAC Apprentice applicants must: 1.) Be at least 18 years of age, or provide proof of registration with the U.S. Department of Laborâ€™s Office of Apprenticeship Training certified HVAC program; 2.) Be employed by a licensed HVAC Contractor; 3.) Work under the supervision of an HVAC Journeyman; 4.) Be enrolled in or have completed a related training program. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of:  Hearth, Fuel Gas Piping, Waste Oil Heating, and LP Limited Heating. Term: Registration is valid for 5 years or for 3 years for specialty apprentices.',
     '4', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/hvac_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2008', '112',
     'HVAC Journeyman', 'Heating, Ventilation & Air Conditioning (HVAC) workers must be licensed in the State of Idaho. There are three certificates of competency available to HVAC workers: apprentice registration, journeyman license, and contractorâ€™s license.  HVAC Journeyman applicants must: 1.) Document a minimum of four (4) years of work experience as a registered HVAC apprentice; 2.) Complete four (4) years of approved HVAC apprenticeship school; 3.) Pass an exam. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of:  Hearth, Fuel Gas Piping, Waste Oil Heating, and LP Limited Heating. HVAC specialty journeyman must: 1.) Document required work experience as a registered HVAC Specialty Apprentice; 2.) Complete specific education required for that specialty type; 3.) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are valid for three years before renewal.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/hvac_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2009', '112',
     'HVAC Contractor', 'Heating, Ventilation & Air Conditioning (HVAC) workers must be licensed in the State of Idaho. There are three certificates of competency available to HVAC workers: apprentice registration, journeyman license, and contractorâ€™s license. HVAC Contractor applicants must: 1.) Submit proof of a minimum of two (2) years of experience as an HVAC Journeyman; 2.) Pass an exam. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of:  Hearth, Fuel Gas Piping, Waste Oil Heating, and LP Limited Heating.  Term: Licenses are valid for three years before renewal.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/hvac_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2010', '112',
     'HVAC Specialty Apprentice', 'Specialty Heating, Ventilation & Air Conditioning (HVAC) workers must be licensed in Idaho and are only allowed to work in their area of specialization. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of: Hearth, Fuel Gas Piping, Waste Oil. Heating, and LP Limited Heating. HVAC Specialty Apprentices must:  1.) Be at least 18 years of age, or provide proof of registration with the U.S. Department of Laborâ€™s Office of Apprenticeship Training certified HVAC program; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Be employed by a licensed HVAC Specialty Contractor; 4.) Work under the supervision of an HVAC Specialty Journeyman. Term: Licenses are valid for two (2) years for specialty apprentices.',
     '4', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2014', '113',
     'Specialty Apprentice Plumber', 'Specialty plumbers must be licensed by the state of Idaho and are only allowed to work in their area of specialization. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of: Appliance, Water Pump, and Mobile Home plumbing. Specialty Apprentice Plumbers must: 1.) Be at least 16 years of age; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Be employed by a licensed specialty plumbing contractor; 4.) Work under the constant supervision of a specialty plumbing journeyman. Term: Licenses are valid for three (3) years for specialty apprentices.',
     '4', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2015', '113',
     'Apprentice Plumber', 'Plumbers must be licensed by the state of Idaho. There are three certificates of competency available to plumbers in Idaho: apprentice registration, journeyman license, and contractorâ€™s license. Apprentice plumber applicants must: 1.) Be at least 16 years of age; 2.) Be employed by a licensed plumbing contractor; 3.) Work under the constant supervision of a plumbing journeyman; 4.) Be enrolled in or have completed a related training program. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of: Appliance, Water Pump, and Mobile Home plumbing. Term: Registration is valid for 5 years or for 3 years for specialty apprentices.',
     '4', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/plb_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2016', '113',
     'Journeyman Plumber', 'Plumbers must be licensed by the state of Idaho. There are three certificates of competency available to plumbers in Idaho: apprentice registration, journeyman license, and contractorâ€™s license. Journeyman plumber applicants must: 1.) Document a minimum of 8,000 hours of work experience as an Idaho plumbing apprentice; 2.) Complete four (4) years of approved plumbing apprenticeship school; 3.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 4.) Pass a written and practical work exam. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of: Appliance, Water Pump, and Mobile Home plumbing. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of: Appliance, Water Pump, and Mobile Home plumbing. Plumbing specialty journeyman must: 1.) Document a minimum of 4,000 hours of work experience as an Idaho specialty plumbing apprentice; 2.) Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses are valid for three years before renewal',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/plb_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2017', '113',
     'Plumbing Contractor', 'Plumbers must be licensed by the state of Idaho. There are three certificates of competency available to plumbers in Idaho: apprentice registration, journeyman license, and contractorâ€™s license. Plumbing Contractor applicants must: 1.) Hold an active Idaho State plumbing journeyman certificate; 2.) Document two and a half (2.5) years of experience as a licensed journeyman in Idaho; 3.) Pass an exam. Specialty licenses are available in the areas of: Appliance, Water Pump, and Mobile Home plumbing. Term: Licenses are valid for three years before renewal',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/plb_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2020', '114',
     'Manufactured Home Manufacturer', 'Manufactured home manufacturers must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must: 1.) Post a bond of $20,000 with the Idaho Division of Building Safety; 2.) Provide proof of place of business and compliance with Federal Manufactured Housing and Safety Standards Act (HUD Code) standards; Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2021', '114',
     'Manufactured Home Responsible Managing Employee & Salespersons', 'Manufactured Home responsible managing employee and salespersons must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Document employment including residential address of applicant and the name and address of the employer  3.) Provide a statement as to whether any previous application of the applicant has been denied or license revoked. Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2022', '114',
     'Manufactured Home Retailer', 'Manufactured Home Retailer must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must: 1.) Post a bond of $40,000 with the Idaho Division of Building Safety; 2.) Provide proof of place of business and compliance with Federal Manufactured Housing and Safety Standards Act (HUD Code) standards; 3.) Pass a fingerprint background check; 4.) Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2023', '114',
     'Manufactured Home Resale Broker', 'Manufactured Home Resale Broker must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must:  1.) Post a bond of $30,000 with the Idaho Division of Building Safety; 2.) Provide proof of place of business and compliance with Federal Manufactured Housing and Safety Standards Act (HUD Code) standards; 3.) Pass a fingerprint background check; 4.) Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '9', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2024', '114',
     'Manufactured Home Installer', 'Manufactured Home Installer must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must: 1.) Post a bond of $5,000 with the Idaho Division of Building Safety; 2.) Provide proof of place of business and compliance with Federal Manufactured Housing and Safety Standards Act (HUD Code) standards; 3.)  Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2025', '114',
     'Manufactured Home Responsible Managing Employee', 'Manufactured Home Responsible Managing Employee must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must.  Installerâ€™s, Retailers have RMEâ€™s: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Document employment including residential address of applicant and the name and address of the employer 3.) Provide a statement as to whether any previous application of the applicant has been denied or license revoked. Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2028', '115',
     'Public Works Construction Managers', 'Public Works construction managers must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Have Bachelor''s Degree in architecture, engineering or construction management from an accredited and board approved college or university and a minimum of four years of experience managing construction projects; OR 3.) Have a minimum of five years of experience managing construction projects; 4.) Provide official transcripts and three letters of references; 5.) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/mfg_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2029', '115',
     'Public Works Contractors', 'Public Works contractors must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Provide a current financial statement and three (3) contractor references; 3.) Provide appropriate past work history; 4.) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dbs.idaho.gov/forms/pwc_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2031', '120',
     'Private Pesticide Applicator', 'Idaho workers that use or supervise the use of agricultural chemicals or supply technical advice or recommendations regarding the use of agricultural pesticides need a Pesticide Applicators license. There are three types of licenses: Private Applicator, Professional Applicator and Dealer. To become licensed as a Private Applicator you must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Pass an exam. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agri.state.id.us/Categories/Pesticides/licensing/indexPestLicenseMain.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2032', '120',
     'Professional Pesticide Applicator', 'Idaho workers that use or supervise the use of agricultural chemicals or supply technical advice or recommendations regarding the use of agricultural pesticides need a Pesticide Applicators license. There are three types of licenses: Private Applicator, Professional Applicator and Dealer.  A Professional Pesticide Applicator license is required for anyone who uses or provides technical advice, supervision, or recommendations to users of toxic pesticides. To become licensed as a Professional Applicator you must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Provide proof of insurance; 3.) Pass an exam.  Professional applicators may be certified in the following categories: Law and Safety; Agricultural Herbicide; Agricultural Insecticide/Fungicide; Aquatic Pest Control; Chemigation; Commodity Pest Control; Forest Environment; General Pest Control Operator; General Vertebrate Control; Livestock Pest Control; Ornamental Herbicide; Ornamental Insecticide/Fungicide; Potato Cellar Pest Control; Public Health Pest Control; Rodent Control; Right-of-Way Herbicide; Soil Fumigation; Structural Destroying Pests; Seed Treatment; Wood Preservative; Statewide Consultant; Demonstration and Research.  Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agri.state.id.us/Categories/Pesticides/licensing/indexPestLicenseMain.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2033', '120',
     'Pesticide Dealer', 'Idaho workers that use or supervise the use of agricultural chemicals or supply technical advice or recommendations regarding the use of agricultural pesticides need a Pesticide Applicators license. There are three types of licenses: Private Applicator, Professional Applicator and Dealer. Dealers are individuals who sell restricted use pesticides. A dealer license shall be required for each location, outlet, or warehouse from where such pesticides are distributed. To become licensed as a dealer you must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Have a current Professional Pesticide Applicator license with certification in the appropriate categories for the products being sold. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agri.state.id.us/Categories/Pesticides/licensing/indexPestLicenseMain.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2034', '120',
     'Commodity Dealer', 'Agricultural commodity dealers must be licensed in Idaho by the Idaho State Department of Agriculture. Commodity dealers have two classes of licenses. Class 1 commodity dealers licenses are required for dealers that purchase agricultural commodities by credit-sale contract or if the value during the past 12 months exceeds $250,000. Class 2 licenses are required for dealers that purchases agricultural commodities in a 12 month period exceeding $10,000 and less than $250,000. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Post a surety bond with the Department of Agriculture; 3.) Provide an audited or reviewed financial statement. Term: Licenses are renewed annually. Fees: licensing fees for a commodity dealer are based on the class type. Class 1 is $360, class 2 is $180. Renewal fees for a commodity dealer are also based on the class type. Class 1 is $65, class 2 is $35. A license which has expired may be reinstated for a fee of $500 plus the renewal fee if filed within 30 days of expiration.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agri.idaho.gov/Categories/Warehouse/Commodity/commodityLicenses.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2035', '120',
     'Seed Dealer', 'Seed Dealers with gross annual seed sales exceeding five hundred dollars must be licensed in Idaho. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Have an established plant, warehouse or place of business; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idahoag.us/Categories/Laboratories/Seed/SeedForms.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2036', '120',
     'Florist', 'Anyone who regularly grows, sells, deals, or imports any nursery or florist stock, or works for a nursery, florist, or landscape contractor with sales totaling $500 or more each year, must be licensed. Applicants must submit required documents and fees to the Idaho Department of Agriculture. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agri.idaho.gov/Categories/PlantsInsects/Nursery/indexNurseryHome.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2037', '120',
     'Bulk Milk Hauler', 'Bulk Milk Haulers must be licensed in order to grade, sample, measure and pump milk from a dairy farm bulk tank, and deliver milk to a dairy processing plant, receiving station, or transfer station. Every licensed hauler is required to attend a training session and pass a test to be eligible. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agri.idaho.gov/Categories/Animals/Dairy/dairyPermitsLicensesBulkMilk.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2038', '121',
     'Weighmaster', 'Public weighmaster must be licensed by the Idaho State Department of Agriculture, Bureau of Weights and Measures. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Be 18 years of age or older; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Submit two references signatures of good moral character. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agri.state.id.us/Categories/WeightsMeasures/weighmasters.php#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2041', '123',
     'Farm Labor Contractor', 'Anyone performing farm labor contractor activities on behalf of migrant and seasonal farmworkers in Idaho must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Labor. Applicants must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Post a surety bond to cover unpaid wages; 3.) Submit insurance documents for all vehicles used; 4.) Submit proof of workersâ€™ compensation coverage for all employees; 5.) Provide all employees at the time of hiring with full disclosure of the conditions of employment.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://labor.idaho.gov/dnn/idl/Businesses/AgriculturalServices.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2051', '125',
     'Certified Public Accountant', 'Certified Public Accountants must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Accountancy. To be licensed applicants must: 1.) Be 18 years of age or older; 2.) Be of good moral character; 3.) Earn a  Bachelor''s degree that meets Board of Accountancy class and credit requirements at an approved college or university;  4.) Successfully completed a course in ethics; 5.) Passed the Uniform CPA exam; 6.) Complete one year of accounting and tax experience that includes no fewer than 2,000 hours. Term: Licenses are renewed annually as of July 1.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.isba.idaho.gov/#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2061', '116',
     'Peace Officers', 'All police officers, including conservation officers, must be certified by the Peace Officers Standards and Training program (POST ) within one year after they are hired. To be accepted into the POST program or hired as a peace officer, applicants must: 1.)',
     '0', '9', '1', '9', '9',
