     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2067', '116',
     'Juvenile Detention Officers', 'Juvenile detention officers must be certified by the Peace Officers Standards and Training program (POST ) within one year after they are hired. To be accepted into the POST program or hired as a peace officer, applicants must: 1.) Be a U.S. citizen; 2.)',
     '0', '9', '1', '9', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2068', '116',
     'Juvenile Correction Officers', 'Juvenile correction officers must be certified by the Peace Officers Standards and Training program (POST ) within one year after they are hired. To be accepted into the POST program or hired as a peace officer, applicants must: 1.) Be a U.S. citizen; 2.)',
     '0', '9', '1', '9', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2071', '130',
     'Collection Agency Agents', 'Collection agencies must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Finance. The agents who work for the collection agencies are registered on a quarterly basis. Credit counselors cannot operate in Idaho without obtaining a collection agency license. To be registered, agents must: 1.) Be an Idaho resident; 2.) Have no felony convictions; 3.) Have no outstanding bad debts; 4.) Pay a quarterly registration fee. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/CollectionAgency/CollectionAgency.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2072', '130',
     'Regulated Lender', 'Creditors that making consumer loans, or collect payments from debtors arising from consumer loans, must obtain a regulated lenders license. Regulated lenders are licensed by the Idaho Department of Finance. To be licensed, applicants must: 1.) Register with the Idaho Secretary of State''s Office 2.) Submit current bank statements that reflect a minimum of $30,000 in liquid assets; 3.) Provide a History of Lending; 4.) Submit samples of all forms to be used in the lending process; 5.) Submit an application with required documents and fees. Payday Lenders require a separate license and fees. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/ConsumerFinance/ConsumerCredit.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2073', '130',
     'Payday Lender', 'Payday Lender in Idaho must be licensed with the Idaho Department of Finance. To be licensed, applicants must: 1.) Register with the Idaho Secretary of State''s Office; 2.) Submit current bank statements that reflect a minimum of $30,000 in liquid assets and $5,000 for each additional Idaho physical location; 3.) Provide a History of Lending; 4.) Submit samples of all forms to be used in the lending process; 5.) Submit an application with required documents and fees. Payday Lenders licenses only authorize payday lending. Creditors engaging in the business of making regulated consumer loans or taking assignment of and undertaking direct collection of payments from debtors arising from regulated consumer loans must obtain a regulated lenders license. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/ConsumerFinance/ConsumerCredit.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2074', '130',
     'Money Transmitter', 'Anyone that sells or issues payment transmissions through wire, facsimile, electronic transfer, or other transfer method in Idaho must be licensed as a Money Transmitter by the Idaho Department of Finance. To be licensed, applicants must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Provide audited financial statements demonstrating a minimum net worth of $50,000 with a sliding scale to a maximum of $250,000; 3.) Deliver a surety bond to the Idaho Department of Finance in the amount of $10,000 on a sliding scale to a maximum of $500,000; 4.) Identify all Idaho locations where their business may be conducted. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/MoneyTransmitter/MoneyTransmitter.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2075', '130',
     'Loan Originator Licensees', 'Mortgage loan originators, mortgage loan processors, and mortgage underwriters who operate as independent contractors must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Finance. To be licensed, applicants must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Complete 20 Hours of pre-license education; 3.) Have no felony convictions;  4.) Not have outstanding bad debts; 5.) Provide Fingerprints and pass a background check; 6.) Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/Mortgage/LoanOriginator.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2076', '130',
     'Mortgage Licensees', 'Mortgage Lenders and mortgage brokers must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Finance. To be licensed applicants must: 1.) Register with the Idaho Secretary of State''s Office; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Cocument that the individual in charge of each office has minimum of three (3) years of experience in residential mortgage brokering/lending. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/Mortgage/Mortgage.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2077', '130',
     'Securities Sales Agents and Investment Advisor Representatives', 'Securities Salespeople and Investment Advisor Sales Representatives must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Finance. Applicants for licensure must:  1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Pass exams. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/Securities/Securities.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2078', '130',
     'Securites Investment Advisors & Broker Dealers', 'Securities Investment Advisor and Securities Broker-Dealers must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Finance. Applicants for licensure must:  1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Meet varying capital requirments; 2.) Investment Advisors must deliver an indemnity bond of $10,000 to the Idaho Department of Financ; 3.) Principals must pass an exam. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.finance.idaho.gov/Securities/Securities.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2091', '135',
     'Commercial Drivers', 'Heavy truck, school bus and other commercial drivers in Idaho must hold a commercial driver''s license. To get a commercial driver''s license, applicants can apply at any county sheriff''s office. Bring your current driver''s license, Social Security card, and money to pay any required fees. Applicants must: 1.) Be at least 18 years old; 2.) Present a certified birth certificate, citizenship documents, or legal presence documents; 3.) Pass written and skills tests; 4.) Have and maintain a good driving record; 5.) Have a valid Idaho driverâ€™s license and at least one year of driving experience; 6.) Submit a self-certification report (some commercial drivers will need a U.S. Department of Transportation medical card depending on their self-certification status). Term: Licenses are valid for either four years or eight years.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://itd.idaho.gov/dmv/driverservices/CDL.htm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2111', '041',
     'Child Care', 'Child care providers that care for seven or more children and receive compensation must be licensed in Idaho unless they are otherwise exempt. Licensing requirements include: 1.) Submitting an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Documenting the number of children to receive care and information about every owner, operator, employee, and volunteer at the care facility; 3.) Every owner, operator, employee, and volunteer passing a background check; 4.) Passing facility health and fire inspections; 5.) Having at least one staff member with CPR training on duty at all times.  A state license may not be required in cities with separate licensing procedures. The following Idaho cite have supplemental or alternative licensing requirements: Boise, Chubbuck, Pocatello, Ammon, Idaho Falls, Coeur dâ€™Alene, Moscow, Lewiston, and Hailey.',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '2',
     '9', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.211.idaho.gov/daycare/daycarelicensing.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2113', '040',
     'Emergency Medical Responder (EMR)', 'Emergency Medical Technicians must be licensed in Idaho through the Idaho Department of Health and Welfare, Emergency Medical Services Bureau. There are four levels of levels of practice: First Responder, EMT-Basic, Advanced EMT, and Paramedic. Applicants must: 1.) Successfully complete a training course and be at least 16 years of age; 2.) Pass the National Registry of EMTâ€™s (NREMT) written and practical exams at the EMR level or higher; 3.) Secure affiliation with an Idaho licensed EMS agency; 4.) Submit to and pass a Criminal History Check by the Department of Health and Welfare; 5.) Submit an application with required documents and fees. Term: Licenses are valid for three years before renewal',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://healthandwelfare.idaho.gov/Medical/EmergencyMedicalServices2/ProviderLicensure2/tabid/1601/Default.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2116', '040',
     'Paramedic', 'Emergency Medical Technicians must be licensed in Idaho through the Idaho Department of Health and Welfare, Emergency Medical Services Bureau. There are four levels of levels of practice: First Responder, EMT-Basic, Advanced EMT, and Paramedic. Applicants must: 1.) Successfully complete a training course and be at least 18 years of age; 2.) Pass the National Registry of EMTâ€™s (NREMT) written and practical exams at the paramedic level; 3.) Secure affiliation with an Idaho licensed EMS agency; 4.) Submit to and pass a Criminal History Check by the Department of Health and Welfare; 5.) Submit an application with required documents and fees. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal',
     '0', '3', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://healthandwelfare.idaho.gov/Medical/EmergencyMedicalServices2/ProviderLicensure2/tabid/1601/Default.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2131', '140',
     'Certified Water Right Examiner', 'To become a certified water right examiner with the Idaho Department of Water Resources, applicants must: 1.)',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idwr.idaho.gov/WaterManagement/WaterRights/Examiners/examiners.htm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2132', '140',
     'Well Driller', 'Well Drillers must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Water Resources. To be licensed, applicants must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Document at least 24 months of drilling experience, 12 of which must have occurred within the last 5 years; 2.) Submit three references; 3.) Pass an exam.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idwr.idaho.gov/WaterManagement/WellInformation/DrillerLicensing/dl_default.htm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2151', '145',
     'Outfitter', 'Outfitters and the recreation guides they employ are licensed according to activity. These activities include, but are not limited to, hunting, fishing, rafting and boating, skiing, technical mountaineering/rock climbing, and snowmobiling. In order to operate, all outfitters must be qualified to guide or have in their employment a licensed guide. Outfitter applicants must: 1.) Be at least 18 years of age; 2.) Hold a first aid card and be aware of general emergency procedures; 3.) Have extensive first-hand knowledge of the area and/or waters and/or activities involved; 4.) Guide only those activities for which licensed; 5.) Guide only in the operating area and for those activities the outfitter is licensed. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://oglb.idaho.gov/licensing/#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2152', '145',
     'Recreation Guides', 'Outfitters and the recreation guides they employ are licensed according to activity. These activities include, but are not limited to, hunting, fishing, rafting and boating, skiing, technical mountaineering/rock climbing, and snowmobiling. An applicant for a guide license must: 1.) Be at least 18 years of age; 2.) Hold a first aid card and be aware of general emergency procedures; 3.) Have extensive first-hand knowledge of the area and/or waters and/or activities involved; 4.) Guide only those activities for which licensed; 5.) Guide only in the operating area and for those activities the outfitter is licensed. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://oglb.idaho.gov/licensing/#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2153', '145',
     'Recreation Designated Agents', 'In order to operate, all outfitters must be qualified to guide or have in their employment a licensed guide or a designated agent who is licensed to guide. An applicant for designated agent must meet the following criteria: 1.) Be at least 18 years of age; 2.) Hold a first aid card and be aware of general emergency procedures; 3.) Have extensive first-hand knowledge of the area and/or waters and/or activities involved; 4.) Guide only those activities for which licensed; 5.) Guide only in the operating area and for those activities the outfitter is licensed. Term: Licenses are renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://oglb.idaho.gov/licensing/#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2171', '150',
     'Insurance Producer', 'Insurance Agents, also called Insurance Producers in Idaho, must be licensed by the Idaho Department of Insurance. Applicants must: 1.)',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '9', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.doi.idaho.gov/producer/licensing.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2172', '150',
     'Bail Bond Agent', 'Bail Bond Agents in Idaho must be licensed. Applicants must: 1.) Be at least 18 years of age; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 4.) Have no felony convictions;  5.) Provide a $15,000 Surety bond; 6.) Pass a written exam. Term: Licenses are renewed bi-annually.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.doi.idaho.gov/producer/licensing.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2173', '150',
     'Independent Insurance Adjuster', 'Independent adjusters investigate and negotiate settlements for claims arising under insurance contracts. Adjusters who are salaried employees of an insuring company do not require licensure. To be licensed as an independent adjuster, applicants must: 1.) Be 21 years of age; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 4.) Have no felony convictions;  5.) Pass a written exam; Term: Licenses are renewed bi-annually.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.doi.idaho.gov/producer/licensing.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2174', '150',
     'Public Insurance Adjuster', 'Public Insurance Adjusters advocate for the policyholder in appraising and negotiating a claimant''s insurance claim. To be licensed as an Public Adjuster, applicants must: 1.) Be 18 years of age; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 4.) Have no felony convictions;  5.) Provide a $20,000 Surety bond; 6.) Pass a written exam; Term: Licenses are renewed bi-annually.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.doi.idaho.gov/producer/licensing.aspx#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2191', '155',
     'Real Estate Salesperson', 'Real Estate Salespersons must be licensed in Idaho by the Idaho Real Estate Commission. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Be 18 years of age; 2.) Earn a high school diploma or equivalent; 3.) Complete at least 90 hours of pre-license education; 4.) Pass a national and state exam; 5.) Hold Errors & Omissions insurance; 6.) Undergo fingerprint background check. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://irec.idaho.gov/licensing.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2192', '155',
     'Real Estate Broker', 'Real Estate Brokers must be licensed in Idaho by the Idaho Real Estate Commission. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Be 18 years of age; 2.) Earn a high school diploma or equivalent; 4.) Document 2 years of active real estate sales experience within the past 5 years; 3.) Complete at least 90 hours of pre-license education; 5.) Pass a national and state exam; 6.) Hold Errors & Omissions insurance; 7.) Undergo fingerprint background check. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://irec.idaho.gov/licensing.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2201', '160',
     'Teacher', 'Public school teachers in Idaho must be certified by the Idaho Department of Education. Applicants for certification must: 1.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 2.) Be at least 18 years of age; 3.) Have completed specific minimum requirements in college training required for each certification and endorsement sought; 4.) Pass a test required for each specific certification and endorsement sought; 5.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check.',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '9',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2202', '160',
     'Education Administrators', 'Public school administrators are required to hold an Administrator Certificate. The certificate may be used for service as a school principal, a superintendent, or a director of special education. The minimum certification requirements include: 1.) Pass a proficiency exam; 2.) Have a master''s degree or higher (for principals) or doctorate degree or education; specialist degree or higher (for superintendents) from an accredited college or university; 3.) Have four years of experience working with students in a school setting; 4.) Complete an administrative internship; 5.) Complete a state-approved program of at least (30) semester credit hours or forty-five (45) quarter credit hours, of graduate study in school administration for the preparation of school principals at an accredited college or university.',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2203', '160',
     'School Personnel Services Provider', 'Anyone who serves as school counselors, school psychologists, speech-language pathologists, school social workers, school nurses and school audiologists is required to hold the Pupil Personnel Services Certificate with the respective endorsement(s) for which they qualify.  Public School Counselors must hold a Personnel Services Certificate and a Counselor Endorsement (K-12) from the Idaho Department of Education. To be eligible for the certificate and endorsement, an applicant must: 1.) Earn a master''s degree in counseling from an approved college or university; 2.) Complete 700 hours of supervised field experience, 75% of which must be in a K-12 school setting; 3.) Submit an institutional recommendation.  Public School Psychologists must hold a Personnel Services Certificate and a School Psychologist Endorsement from the Idaho Department of Education. To be eligible for the certificate and endorsement, an applicant must: 1.) Earn a master''s degree in education or psychology from an approved college or university; 2.) Complete 1,200 hours of internship within a school district under the supervision of a certificated school psychologist.  Public school speech-language pathologists must hold a Personnel Services Certificate and a Speech-Language Pathologist Endorsement from the Idaho Department of Education. To be eligible for the certificate and endorsement, an applicant must earn a master''s degree in a speech/language pathology program and an institutional recommendation from an approved college or university.',
     '0', '9', '2', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2301', '165',
     'Attorney', 'Lawyers must be licensed by the Idaho State Bar to practice law. To gain licensure, applicants must pass the Idaho Bar Exam after graduating from an American Bar Association approved law school. The exam is given in February and July.',
     '0', '2', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://isb.idaho.gov/licensing/licensing_mcle.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2311', '170',
     'Engineer', 'Engineers in Idaho are licensed by the Idaho Board of Professional Engineers and Professional Land Surveyors. There are two levels of licensure Engineer Intern and Professional Engineer. To be licensed as a Professional Engineer the applicant must: 1.) Graduate with a bachelor''s degree in engineering or in a related field with coursework required by the board; 2.) Pass the Fundamentals of Engineering (F.E.) exam; 3.) Have four years of approved engineering work experience; 4.) Pass the Principles of Practice exam. Examinations vary by discipline and include: Electrical & Computer, Mechanical, Chemical, Civil, Agricultural, and more. However, Idaho does not license engineers by discipline. All licenses are for "Engineer" regardless of the exam taken for licensing purposes. Engineers working for licensed engineers or whose work is only for the internal use of a corporation or company do not need to be licensed. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ipels.idaho.gov/applist.cfm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2313', '170',
     'Land Surveyor', 'Land Surveyors in Idaho are licensed by the Idaho Board of Professional Engineers and Professional Land Surveyors. There are two levels of licensure surveyor Intern and Professional surveyor. To be licensed as a surveyor an applicant must: 1.) Graduate with a bachelor''s degree in surveying or in a related field with additional coursework required by the board; 2.) Pass the fundamentals of surveying exam; 3.) Have four years of approved land surveying work experience; 4.) Pass the Principles of Practice exam. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ipels.idaho.gov/applist.cfm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2314', '170',
     'Land Surveyor Intern', 'Land Surveyors in Idaho are licensed by the Idaho Board of Professional Engineers and Professional Land Surveyors. There are two levels of licensure surveyor Intern and Professional surveyor. To be licensed as a surveyor Intern, an applicant must: 1.) Graduate with a bachelor''s degree in surveying or in a related field with additional coursework required by the board;  2.) Pass the fundamentals of surveying exam. Term: Licenses are valid for two years before renewal.',
     '4', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.ipels.idaho.gov/applist.cfm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2401', '205',
     'Registered Nurse (RN)', 'Registered Nurses (RN) must be licensed by the State of Idaho. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Graduate from an approved nursing program; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 4.) Pass a licensing exam. Term: Licenses are renewed bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibn.idaho.gov/IBNPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=IBON&BureauLinkID=930#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2402', '205',
     'Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN)', 'Licensed Practical Nurses (LPN) must be licensed by the State Board of Nursing. Applicants for licensure must: 1.)',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibn.idaho.gov/IBNPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=IBON&BureauLinkID=930#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2403', '205',
     'Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN)', 'Nurse Practitioners, Clinical Nurses, Nurse Midwives, and Nurse Anesthetists must be licensed by the State of Idaho as an Advanced Practice Professional Nurse (APPN). To become licensed applicants must complete an approved registered nursing program, pass an exam, and and be licensed as a registered nurse. To become licensed as a Nurse Practitioner, applicants must also: 1.) Complete an accredited advanced practice, nurse practitioner program;  2.) Pass an exam; 3.) Obtain national certification. To become licensed as a Clinical Nurse, applicants must also: 1.) Complete a graduate Nursing program; 2.) Pass an exam; 3.) Obtain national certification. To become licensed as a Nurse Midwife, applicants must also: 1.) Complete an accredited advanced practice nurse midwifery Program; 2.) Pass an exam; 3.) Obtain national certification. To become licensed as a Nurse Anesthetist, applicants must also: 1.) Complete an accredited advanced practice nurse anesthesia program; 2.) Pass an exam; 3.) Obtain national certification. Term: Licenses are renewed bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ibn.idaho.gov/IBNPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=IBON&BureauLinkID=930#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2404', '041',
     'Nursing Assistants', 'Idaho maintains a registry of all certified nursing assistants. In Idaho, CNA certification requires completion of a CNA course including 80 hours of classroom and 40 hours of clinical training or one semester of an accredited nursing school program and passage of the CNA exam. Term: Licenses are renewed bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.healthandwelfare.idaho.gov/?tabid=282#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2411', '210',
     'Dentist', 'Dentists must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Dentistry. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Pass a background check; 2.) Graduate from a dental school accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) of the American Dental Association (ADA); 3.)',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://isbd.idaho.gov/process.htm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2412', '210',
     'Dental Hygienists', 'Dental Hygienists must be licensed by the State Board of Dentistry. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Graduate from a dental hygiene program accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) of the American Dental Association (ADA); 2.) Pass written and clinical exams approved by the Board of Dentistry. Additional license endorsements can be attained as an Extended Access Dental Hygienist and /or an Extended Access Restorative Dental Hygienist. Term: Licenses are renewed bi-annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '3', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://isbd.idaho.gov/process.htm#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2421', '215',
     'Pharmacist', 'Pharmacists must be licensed by the State Board of Pharmacy. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Complete a degree in pharmacy from an accredited school; 2.) Complete a 1740 hour internship under the supervision of a licensed pharmacist, usually completed under the supervision of a college of pharmacy; 3.) Pass the North American Pharmacist Licensure Examination (NAPLEX) and Multistate Pharmacy Jurisprudence Examination (MPJE); 4.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 5.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 6.) Submit references of good moral character and temperate habits. Term: Licenses are renewed annually as of July 1.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bop.idaho.gov/licensing/pharmacists.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2422', '215',
     'Pharmacy Technicians', 'Pharmacy Technicians must be registered with the Idaho Board of Pharmacy. Applicants for registration must: 1.) Have a high school diploma or its equivalent and be 18 years of age; 2.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 3.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 4.) Submit references of good moral character and temperate habits. Pharmacy technicians who register with the Board will need to be nationally certified within 3 years by the Pharmacy Technician Certification Board (PTCB) or the National Healthcareer Association (NHA). Term: Licenses are renewed annually as of July 1.',
     '0', '2', '0', '1', '2',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bop.idaho.gov/licensing/pharm_technicians.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2431', '250',
     'Veterinarian', 'Veterinarians must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Veterinary Medicine. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Complete a veterinary medicine program at an approved school; 3.) Pass national and state licensing exams; 3.) Submit an application with required documents and fees; 4.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check. Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.bovm.idaho.gov/vets/#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2432', '250',
     'Veterinary Technician', 'Veterinary Technicians must be certified by Idaho State Board of Veterinary Medicine. Applicants for certification must: 1.) Be over 18 years of age; 2.) Complete an approved veterinary technology program; 4.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 3.) Pass national and state exams. Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.bovm.idaho.gov/technicians/application_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2433', '250',
     'Veterinary Euthanasia Technician', 'The Board of Veterinary Medicine requires euthanasia technician to be certified. However, controlled substance registrations are issued and renewed by the Drug Enforcement Agency and the Idaho Board of Pharmacy. Applicants for certification must: 1.) Be over 18 years of age; 2.) Complete an approved training course; 3.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 4.) Pass a written and practical exam; 5.) Be employed by a certified euthanasia agency Term: Licenses must be renewed annually.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.bovm.idaho.gov/technicians/application_forms.html#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2501', '200',
     'Physicians & Surgeons', 'Applicants seeking to be licensed to practice medicine in Idaho must be licensed with the Idaho Board of Medicine. Applicants for licensure must: 1.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 2.) Graduate from a board approved medical school; 3.) Complete at least one year of postgraduate training program acceptable to the board; 4.) Pass a board approved exam; 5.) Pass an interview with the Board of Medicine to review the applicantâ€™s qualifications and professional credentials. Term: Licenses can be renewed annually or bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bom.idaho.gov/BOMPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=BOM&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2512', '200',
     'Physician Assistants', 'Physician Assistants must be licensed with the Idaho State Board of Medicine. To become licensed, applicants must: 1.) Submit fingerprints and pass a criminal background check; 2.) Have a Bachelor''s degree; 3.) Complete a nationally accredited physician assistant program; 4.) Pass a national certification exam; 5.) Be supervised by a person licensed to practice medicine. Term: Licenses can be renewed annually or bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '2',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bom.idaho.gov/BOMPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=PAC&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2523', '200',
     'Athletic Trainers', 'Athletic Trainers must be licensed by the Idaho Board of Medicine to practice. To qualify for licensure athletic trainers must: 1.) Graduate with a bachelor''s or advanced degree from an accredited college or university; 2.) Pass a National certification exam; 3.) Submit two certificates of professional recommendation; 4.) Work under the supervision of a licensed directing Physician. Term: Licenses can be renewed annually or bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bom.idaho.gov/BOMPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=ATH&BureauLinkID=150#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2534', '200',
     'Dietitians', 'Dietitians must be licensed by the Idaho State Board of Medicine. To become licensed, applicants must: 1.) Complete an approved dietetics educational program; 2.) Complete approved internship or pre-professional practice program; 3.) Submit two certificates of professional recommendation; 4.) Pass the national registry exam. Term: Licenses can be renewed annually or bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bom.idaho.gov/BOMPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=DIE&BureauLinkID=150#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', '2545', '200',
     'Respiratory Therapists and Polysomnographers', 'Respiratory Therapists are licensed by the Idaho State Board of Medicine. To become licensed, applicants must: 1.) Be at least 18 years of age; 2.) Complete a board approved Respiratory Care program; 3.) Submit two certificates of professional recommendation; 4.) Be registered with the National Board of Respiratory Care (NBRC); 5.) Pass a written and clinical exam; 6.) Pass the Board of Registered Polysomnographic Technologists Exam. Term: Licenses can be renewed annually or bi-annually.',
     '0', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bom.idaho.gov/BOMPortal/BoardAdditional.aspx?Board=RES&BureauLinkID=100#', '20180308'),
    ('16', '01', 'cdl', 'dmv',
     'Commercial Drivers License (CDL)', 'Commercial Drivers Licenses are issued by state departments but are similar from state to state, since the minimum requirements of the licenses and endorsements are set centrally. For more information contact the state DMV or https://cms.fmcsa.dot.gov/registration/commercial-drivers-license/how-do-i-get-commercial-drivers-license.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '1', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20190719'),
    ('16', '01', 'r64', '009',
     'Respiratory Therapists', NULL,
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20100101'),
    ('17', '01', '10', '296',
     'ARCHITECT', 'An individual who furnishes professional services in connection with the design and construction of any private or public building, building structure, building project, or addition to or alteration or restoration thereof. Applicants who have never taken any divisions of the A.R.E. should contact NCARB for eligibility to take the A.R.E.',
     '0', '2', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '103', '87',
     'DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM OPERATOR', 'An individual who operates and maintains the distribution water lines of a drinking water supply system.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www2.illinois.gov/epa/Pages/default.aspx', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '104', '174',
     'DRIVER', 'Any person in the horse racing industry, who is able to drive a standard bred (harness) horse which pulls a sulky at either a trot or pace.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www2.illinois.gov/sites/irb/Pages/Licensing.aspx', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '105', '105',
     'DRIVER TRAINING INSTRUCTOR', 'An individual who teaches driver training for a fee, to adults, teenagers, or applicants required to obtain a Commercial Drivers License (CDL).',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.cyberdriveillinois.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '107', '174',
     'OWNER/TRAINER/DRIVER', 'A person who is both a driver and a trainer as well as an owner in the horse racing industry. Drives a standard bred (harness) horse; trains and enters horses to race at a race meeting; hires grooms, hotwalkers, exercise riders, pony persons, other trainers, veterinarians and blacksmiths.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www2.illinois.gov/sites/irb/Pages/Licensing.aspx', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '11', '11',
     'ART AUCTION HOUSE OWNER', 'Any person, partnership, corporation, association or group engaged for profit primarily in the business of conducting auctions at which they act as agent for any seller of works of art, antiques, furnishings, jewelry, gemstones, coins, stamps, and rare books and manuscripts.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.cyberdriveillinois.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '111', '134',
     'EGG PRODUCER-DEALER/PRODUCER-PACKER/GRADER/DISTRIBUTOR/JOBBER-BROKER', 'A person who feeds and houses poultry and obtains their eggs. Grades, sizes, candles, or packs eggs for sale to consumers, manufactures or retailers. Distributes eggs or egg products.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agr.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '112', '211',
     'ELECTRICAL HOISTING ENGINEER', 'An individual responsible for the safe operation of the electrical and mechanical components of a hoist when workers are being raised or lowered into or out of a coal mine. Responsible for the daily safety check of the hoist.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.dnr.illinois.gov/mines/Pages/default.aspx', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '114', '140',
     'ECRN - EMERGENCY COMMUNICATION REGISTERED NURSE', 'A registered professional nurse who is approved by an Emergency Medical Services (EMS) medical director to monitor telecommunications from and give voice orders to EMS system personnel in accordance with system protocols.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '115', '140',
     'EMD - EMERGENCY MEDICAL DISPATCHER', 'A person who accepts calls from the public for emergency medical services and dispatches designated medical services personnel and vehicles.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '117', '140',
     'EMT- I - EMERGENCY MEDICAL TECHNICIAN - INTERMEDIATE', 'An individual licensed to function in an ambulance and provide intermediate life support services under the direction of an EMS medical director at an approved resource hospital.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '118', '140',
     'EMT - EMERGENCY MEDICAL TECHNICIAN', 'An individual licensed to function in an ambulance and provide basic life support, intermediate life support or advanced life support services under the direction of an EMS medical director at an approved resource hospital.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '12', '137',
     'LIMITED ELEVATOR CONTRACTOR', 'A person or company who is licensed by the state to carry on a business of erecting, constructing, installing, altering, servicing, repairing, or maintaining a specific type of conveyance (elevators) within any building or structure, excluding private residences.',
     '1', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.state.il.us/osfm', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '120', '140',
     'LI - EMS LEAD INSTRUCTOR', 'A person currently approved by the department to coordinate or teach education, training and continuing education courses.',
     '0', '9', '9', '1', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '122', '296',
     'ENGINEER, INTERN', 'An individual who is enrolled as an engineer intern as a result of qualifying by education and examination.',
     '4', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '123', '296',
     'STRUCTURAL ENGINEERING INTERN', 'An individual who is enrolled as a structural engineer intern as a result of qualifying by education and examination.',
     '4', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '125', '296',
     'ENGINEER, STRUCTURAL', 'An individual engaged in the designing or supervising of the construction, enlargement or alteration of structures.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '126', '296',
     'ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH PRACTITIONER', 'A person who, by virtue of education and experience in the physical, chemical, biological, and environmental health sciences, is especially trained to organize, implement, and manage environmental health programs; is trained to carry out education and enforcement activities for the promotion and protection of public health and the environment; and is licensed as an environmental health practitioner.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '127', '296',
     'ESTHETICIAN', 'An individual who engages in beautifying, massaging, cleansing, exfoliating the stratum corneum of the epidermis, or stimulating the skin of the human body, except the scalp, by the use of cosmetic preparations, body treatments, body wraps, hydrotherapy, antiseptics, tonics, lotions or creams, or any device, electrical or otherwise for the care of the skin. Applies makeup or eyelashes to any person. Tints eyelashes and eyebrows and lightens hair on the body, except the scalp. Removes superfluous hair from the body by the use of depilatories, waxing or tweezers.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', 'G', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '128', '296',
     'ESTHETICIAN TEACHER', 'An individual who provides instruction in the theory and practice of esthetics to students in a cosmetology or barber school approved to teach esthetics or an approved esthetics school, and who is authorized to practice as an esthetician.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '13', '17',
     'ASBESTOS AIR SAMPLING PROFESSIONAL', 'An individual who conducts or supervises all air sampling pursuant to the Commercial and Public Building Asbestos Abatement Act and the Illinois Asbestos Abatement Act for schools (Kindergarten through 12th grade) in Illinois.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '131', '174',
     'EXERCISE PERSON', 'An individual who gallops or exercises the horse on the track each morning.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www2.illinois.gov/sites/irb/Pages/Licensing.aspx', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '132', '35',
     'EXPLOSIVES LICENSE HOLDER', 'Any person who acquires, uses, possesses, transfers or disposes of explosive materials in Illinois is required to obtain an explosives license.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.dnr.illinois.gov/mines/Pages/default.aspx', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '134', '134',
     'FEEDER SWINE DEALER', 'An individual who buys and re-sells feeder swine.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.agr.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '135', '137',
     'FIRE EQUIPMENT DISTRIBUTOR (CLASS A, B, C)', 'Any person, company or corporation which services, hydro-tests, installs, maintains, recharges, and inspects all types of fire extinguishers.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.state.il.us/osfm', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '136', '137',
     'FIRE EQUIPMENT EMPLOYEE (CLASS 1, 2, 3)', 'A person who is currently employed by a distributor licensed under this act whose full or part-time duties include servicing, recharging, hydro-testing, installing, maintaining or inspecting all types of fire extinguishers.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.state.il.us/osfm', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '14', '17',
     'ASBESTOS CONTRACTOR', 'Any entity that provides removal, enclosure, encapsulation, or disposal of asbestos-containing materials pursuant to the Illinois Asbestos Abatement Act, the Illinois Commercial and Public Building Act and Code.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '140', '140',
     'PEMR - PROVISIONAL EMERGENCY MEDICAL RESPONDER', 'A person who provides first response services prior to arrival of an ambulance or specialized emergency medical services vehicle.',
     '4', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '146', '174',
     'STABLE - FOREMAN', 'Any person who works directly under the supervision of the head trainer. Responsible for the operation of the stable, feed time, stall upkeep, equipment upkeep, and blacksmith appointments. Oversees the hotwalker, caretakers, etc.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www2.illinois.gov/sites/irb/Pages/Licensing.aspx', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '147', '296',
     'FUNERAL DIRECTOR AND EMBALMER', 'An individual who makes funeral arrangements; prepares, directs or supervises the burial or disposal of deceased human bodies; or performs any act or service in connection with the preparation of the deceased human body. The operation of a place for the preparation for the disposition of deceased human bodies or for caring for deceased human bodies prior to their disposition is also the practice of funeral directing and embalming as is the assumption of custody and the transportation and disposition of deceased human remains.',
     '0', '0', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '148', '296',
     'FUNERAL DIRECTOR AND EMBALMER INTERN', 'A person who is qualified to render assistance to a licensed funeral director and embalmer in carrying out the practice of funeral directing and embalming. All assistance must be performed under the direct supervision of a licensed funeral director and embalmer.',
     '4', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.idfpr.com/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '15', '17',
     'ASBESTOS INSPECTOR', 'An individual licensed by the department to perform asbestos inspections for asbestos containing building materials in accordance with the Illinois Asbestos Abatement Act, the Illinois Commercial and Public Building Asbestos Abatement Act and Code.',
     '1', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.idph.state.il.us', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '154', '7',
     'GINSENG DEALERS, RESIDENT AND NON-RESIDENT', 'Any person engaged in the business of buying wild or cultivated ginseng from homesteads, growers or other dealers for resale.',
     '4', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.dnr.illinois.gov/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '155', '7',
     'GINSENG GROWER', 'Any person engaged in the propagation and harvesting of cultivated ginseng.',
     '1', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.dnr.illinois.gov/', '20240905'),
    ('17', '01', '156', '134',
     'GRAIN DEALER', 'An individual who is engaged in buying grain from producers for resale, milling, or processing.',
