    ('21', '01', '160000001', '16',
     'Apprentice Cosmetologist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Provides cutting, permanent waving, dressing, styling, finger waving, marvelling, coloring, pressing, tinting. bleaching, and shampooing of hair for customers. Gives facials and massages scalp applies cosmetics, lotions, powders, oils and other preparations.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have completed tenth (10) grade plus 1800 hours in an approved school of cosmetology.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examinations in September through June, with dates set by the regulatory agency. Type examination; written and practical. Must score a minimum of 70% in each area. Regulatory agency provides applications. School must submit 1800 hour certification. Examination fee of $25.00. Should you fail, contact the regulatory agency.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least sixteen (16) years of age. Must be of good moral character and temperate habit. First fee of $12.00. All licenses renewed annually, with expiration date being July 31, at fee of $10.00. Reciprocity with other states vary. Contact the regulatory agency for specifics.',
     '4', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://kbhc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '250000002', '25',
     'Professional Engineer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Must have knowledge of mathematics, physical sciences, and the principles of engineering. Works in the evaluation, planning and design of systems involved in the construction of facilities, such as building, utilities, etc., to safeguard the life, health and property of the public.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have a baccalaureate degree from an accredited school of engineering, with a curriculum of four (4) or more years.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for applications. Examinations are scheduled in April and October. Must pass the national uniform examination of the National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying, which is a sixteen (16) hour written examination. Applicant must have four (4) years of satisfactory engineering experience. Application fee is $30.00, examination fee is $130.00 and registration fee is $10.00. Engineers-In-Training are exempt from eight (8) hours of the examination. Should you fail the examination, contact the regulatory agency for retake procedures.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age or residency requirements. You must have no convictions for a felony or moral turpitude. License are renewed biennially, at a fee of $90.00. Kentucky has reciprocity with all states.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '9',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kyboels.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '150000005', '15',
     'Psychologist, Masters', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    The practice of psychology means rendering to individuals, groups, organizations, or the public any psychological service involving the application of principles, methods, and procedures of understanding, predicting, and influencing behavior, such as the principles pertaining to learning, perception, motivation, thinking, emotions, and interpersonal relationships; the methods and procedures of interviewing, counseling, and psychotherapy; of constructing, administering, and interpreting tests of mental abilities, aptitudes, interests, attitudes, personality characteristics, emotion, and motivation. The application of said principles and methods includes, but is not restricted to: diagnosis, prevention and amelioration of adjustment problems and emotional, mental and nervous disorders of individuals and groups; educational and vocational counseling; the evaluation and planning for effective work and learning situations; and the resolution of interpersonal and social conflicts.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a graduate from a regionally accredited educational institution with a master''s degree in psychology. At least six hundred (600) hours of supervised experience which was part of the master''s degree training. These educational experiences typically have titles such as practicum internship or field training and must be reflected on your graduate transcript.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examination for Professional Practice in Psychology (EPPP) is given twice yearly, April and October. The application fee is $300.00.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Contact the regulatory agency for application procedures. You must be at least twenty-one (21) years of age. There are no residency requirements. There are no health requirements. You must demonstrate that you have had at least six hundred (600) hours of supervised experience which was a part of your master''s degree training. These educational experiences typic',
