    ('21', '01', '120000001', '12',
     'Dental Hygienist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Scales and polishes teeth. Takes oral x-rays. Does chair-side assisting. Administers oral hygiene program. Explains preventive dentistry.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Successful completion of training program in a school of dental hygiene that is accredited by the Council on Dental Education of the American Dental Association.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Schedule of examinations are determined by Southern Regional Testing, Inc., Central Regional Board, Northeast Regional Board, or the Western Regional Board who administers the testing. Written National Boards are required.   GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. Must be of good moral character. License are renewed biennially, by December 31. Initial licensure fee is $35.00 with annual renewal license fee being $35.00.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Fifteen (15) annually, ten (10) of which must be scientific based. Must have HIV course annually and CPR biennially. Must have verification of attendance. Proof is required in the event of audit.    SPECIAL COMMENTS OR CONDITIONS    Credentials licensure available if candidate has practiced for three (3) to five (5) years prior to making application.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '2',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://dentistry.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '120000002', '12',
     'Dental Assistant', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Construct dental laboratory appliances based upon instructions and directions received from a licensed dentist.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have at least two (2) years technician education, or two (2) years experience in a registered dental laboratory. Each registered commercial dental laboratory must have at least one (1) certified dental technician.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    There is no written or practical examination. Applicant may secure application for certification as a dental laboratory technician from the regulatory agency.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age requirements. Certification is $10.00 annually, which expires on December 31.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://dentistry.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '120000003', '12',
     'Dentist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Examines, restores, treats, and preserves the structures and tissues of diseased teeth and the mouth. May be classified according to specialty, such as Endodontist, Oral Pathologist, Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeon, Orthodontist, Pediatric Dentist, Periodontist, Prosthodontist, etc.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Graduate with a DDS or DMD Degree from dental programs accredited by the American Dental Association. Specialists are required to secure additional educational training.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Schedule of examinations are determined by Southern Regional Testing, Inc., Central Regional Board, Northeast Regional Board, or the Western Regional Board who administers the testing. Written National Boards are required.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency requirements. Must be of good moral character. License must be renewed biennially by December 31. Initial licensure fee is $60.00 with the annual licensure renewal fee being $90.00.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Fifteen (15) points annually, ten (10) of which must be scientific based. Must have HIV course annually and CPR biennially. Proof required in the event of audit.',
