    ('21', '01', '130000001', '13',
     'Funeral Director and Embalmer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Makes arrangements and directs funerals. Remove bodies from homes, hospitals and institutions after they decease, transports bodies to funeral home and assists in the final disposition of the remains. Embalmers restore, preserve, and disinfect bodies after they decease.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess a G.E.D equivalency. Embalmers must obtain an associate degree in Embalming from an accredited School of Mortuary Science.    EXAMINATIONS REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for applications. Examinations scheduled in June and December annually. The examination is written and requires a passing score of 75%. Examination fee is $75.00 per exam. Retakes require a new fee but not a new application. Renewal fees for licenses are $30.00 per license per year.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be eighteen (18) years of age. Each apprenticeship requires three (3) years but both can be served at the same time. One (1) year of college may be substituted for one (1) year of apprenticeship for funeral directors. Licenses are renewed annually for a fee of $30.00 per license. Out-of-state applicants can apply to take the examination and receive a license if they meet all other requirements.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Attend a minimum of four (4) hours in a continuing education program.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.kbefd.ky.go', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '140000001', '14',
     'Professional Landscape Architect', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Renders planning of outdoor space involving people, flora and fauna, and facilities, with emphasis on the function, preservation, restoration, and enhancement of the physical environment. Involves the preservation of the natural landscape ecology, by arranging land, water and the elements of safety, welfare and health of the public.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Graduate of an accredited landscape architecture curriculum approved by the board.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for applications. The Landscape Architect Registration Examination (LARE) of the Council of Landscape Architectural Registration Boards is given in June and December. Examination fees are established each year.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be at least twenty-one (21) years of age. Must have two (2) years of professional landscape experience satisfactory to the Board. License must be renewed annually at a fee of $150.00. Kentucky has reciprocity agreements with other states.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Fifteen (15) hours of continuing education is required annually.',
