    ('21', '01', '160000002', '16',
     'Cosmetologist - Hairdresser', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Provides cutting, permanent waving, dressing, styling, finger waving, marvelling, pressing, tinting, bleaching and shampooing hair for customers. Gives facials, massages scalp, and applies cosmetics, lotions, powders, oil, and other preparations.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have completed the tenth (10) grade or equivalency PLUS 1800 hours in an approved school of cosmetology.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examinations in September through June, as determined by the regulatory agency. Type examination; practical with a minimum score of 70% required. Contact the regulatory agency for applications. Examination fees of $35.00. Should you fail, contact the regulatory agency.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least sixteen (16) year of age. Must be of good moral character and temperate habit. Must have six (6) months work-experience as an apprentice in a licensed beauty salon. First license fee is $15.00, with license renewed annually, by July 31, at a fee of $12.00. Reciprocity with other states vary. Contact the regulatory agency for specifics.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Effective July 1, 1997, cosmetologists shall provide proof of six (6) hours of continuing education for renewal of license. Contact the regulatory agency for specifics.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://kbhc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '160000003', '16',
     'Cosmetologist Instructor', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Teaches students in all phases of cosmetology.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or equivalent. Must have 1000 additional hours, in an approved school of cosmetology, as an apprentice instructor.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examinations are scheduled in September through June, as determined by the regulatory agency. Type examination; written, with a minimum passing score of 80%, and a practical, with a minimum score of 85%. Examination fee is $50.00. Contact the regulatory agency for applications. Should you fail, contact, the regulatory agency.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least sixteen (16) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. Must be of good moral character and temperate habit. Must have one (1) year work-experience in a licensed beauty salon. License fee is $35.00 for the first license. All license expire July 31, annually, with a renewal fee of $25.00. There are no reciprocity agreements with other states.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Effective July 1, 1997, cosmetology instructors shall provide proof of eight (8) hours of continuing education for renewal of license. Contact the regulatory agency for specifics.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Application for apprentice instructor must be approved by the regulatory agency prior to issuance of the license. Must have a cosmetologist license.',
     '4', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://kbhc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '160000004', '16',
     'Nail Technician', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Provides cutting, trimming, polishing, coloring, cleansing, applying artificial nails, or massaging, cleaning, treating, or beautifying the hands and feet.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have completed tenth (10th) grade plus six hundred (600) classroom hours in an approved school of cosmetology.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examinations in September through June with dates set by the regulatory agency. Examination is both written and practical. Must score a minimum of seventy percent (70%) in each area. School must submit certification hours. Examination fee is $25.00.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least sixteen (16) years of age. Must be of good moral character and temperate habit. All licenses renewed annually by July 31. Initial license fee is $12.00 and renewal fee is $10.00.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Nail technicians shall provide proof of six (6) hours of continuing education for renewal of license. Contact the regulatory agency for specifics.',
