     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kbn.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '270000002', '27',
     'Nurse Anesthetist (APRN)', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Performs registered nurse functions and practices advanced skills related to anesthesia care based on knowledge acquired in a post-basic program of study and clinical experience. A person must hold a current Kentucky advanced registered nurse practitioner (ARNP) registration to practice in Kentucky as a nurse anesthetist.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    In addition to successful completion of a Board approved registered nursing program, a person must have successfully completed an organized post-basic program of study and clinical experience recognized by the regulatory agency, in concert with the national nursing organization.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    The schedule for examinations is determined by the American Association of Nurse Anesthetists. For type of examination, examination fee and retake procedures, contact the regulatory agency (address listed below).    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age, residency or work experience (after completion of the prelicensure program) requirements for licensure requirements. Must have a current active RN license in Kentucky and be certified as a registered nurse anesthetist. Must seek registration as an advanced registered nurse practitioner (ARNP). Initial registration fee is $80.00. Biennial registration must be renewed by October 31 of even years, at a fee of $55.00. Registration and reciprocity with other states varies.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Thirty (30) contact hours are required for biennial renewal of registered nurse license. Continuing education contact hours must be earned via a Board approved provider. An ARNP must complete five (5) contact hours of continuing education in pharmacology (included with the 30 hour requirement) for biennial renewal. The American Association of Nurse Anesthetists requires additional contact hours every two (2) years for recertification.    SPECIFIC COMMENTS or CONDITI',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kbn.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '270000003', '27',
     'Nurse Practitioner (APRN)', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Functions as a registered nurse and practices as an advanced registered nurse practitioner (ARNP) in the management and care of essentially healthy children and/or adults in all aspects and developmental stages of life. Advanced practice is based on knowledge and skills acquired in a post-basic program of study and clinical experience. A person must hold a current Kentucky ARNP registration to be employed as a nurse practitioner in Kentucky.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    In addition to successful completion of a Board approved program of registered nursing, a person must have successfully completed an organized post-basic program of study and clinical experience recognized by the regulatory agency, in concert with the appropriate national nursing organization.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    The schedule of certification examinations is determined by the national certification organizations. For type of examination, examination fees, and retake procedures, contact the regulatory agency (address listed below).    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age or residency requirements. Must have a current, active Registered Nurse (RN) license in Kentucky and be certified as a nurse practitioner by the appropriate national nursing organization. Initial license fee is $80.00. Biennial registration must be renewed by October 31 in even years, at a fee of $55.00. Registration and reciprocity with other states varies. Contact the regulatory agency in the appropriate state for information regarding requirements.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Thirty (30) contact hours required for biennial renewal of the registered nurse license. Continuing education contact hours must be earned via a Board approved provider. An ARNP must complete five (5) contact hours of continuing education in pharmacology (included with the 30 hour requirement) for biennial renewal. For certification requirem',
     '3', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kbn.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '270000004', '27',
     'Nurse, Clinical Specialist (APRN)', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    A registered nurse who, through study and supervised practice at the graduate level (master''s or doctorate degree), functions and practices as an advanced registered nurse practitioner in a selected clinical area of nursing.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    In addition to successful completion of a Board approved registered nursing program, a person must have successfully completed an organized post-basic program of study and clinical experience at the graduate level (master''s or doctorate''s degree) recognized by the regulatory agency, in concert with the national nursing organization.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    The schedule of certification examinations is determined by the American Nurses'' Credentialing Center. For type of examination, fee, and retake procedures, contact the regulatory agency (address listed below).    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age, residency or work experience (after completion of the prelicensure program) requirements for licensure. Must have current, active RN license in Kentucky and be certified as a clinical nurse specialist. Must seek registration as an advanced registered nurse practitioner (ARNP). Initial registration fee is $80.00. Biennial registration must be renewed by October 31 of even years, at a fee of $55.00. Registration and reciprocity with other states varies.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Thirty (30) contact hours are required for biennial renewal of registered nurse license. Continuing education contact hours must be earned via a Board approved provider. An ARNP must complete five (5) contact hours of continuing education in pharmacology (included with the 30 hour requirement) for biennial renewal. Contact the American Nurses'' Credentialing Center for information on recertification.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Individual must hold a current, active Kentucky registered nurse license in order to maintain r',
