    ('21', '01', '280000001', '28',
     'Apprentice Ophthalmic Dispenser', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '4', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bod.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '280000002', '28',
     'Ophthalmic Dispenser', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Fits, adjusts or adapts spectacles or contact lenses for customers.    EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS    Graduate of an Approved School of Ophthalmic Dispensing or two (2) years training and experience as an apprentice.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    For an application, contact the regulatory agency. The Kentucky Practical examination is given in March, July and November each year. The examination fee for the Kentucky Practical is $25.00. You must score an average of 60%, with a minimum of 50% in any of the three (3) sections, and must successfully pass the two (2) national examinations; the National Contact Lens Examiners examination (fee is $125.00) and the American Board of Opticianry examination (fee is $95.00), given in May and November annually.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. Applicant must have completed at least two (2) years of satisfactory training and work experience as a licensed apprentice, approved by the Board, under a licensed Ophthalmic Dispenser, Physician, Osteopath or Optometrist. License are renewed annually, on December 31, at a fee of $25.00. Kentucky does not have reciprocity agreements with any state.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Each ophthalmic dispenser licensee shall be required to complete a minimum of six (6) continuing education hours in order to renew his/her license each year. Each apprentice ophthalmic dispenser licensee shall be required to complete a minimum of four (4) continuing education hours in order to renew his/her license each year. Continuing education hours in excess of the number required at the time of renewal may not be applied to future requirements.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bod.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '280000003', '28',
     'Temporary Registered Telehealth Health Care Provider - BOD', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '4', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bod.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '290000001', '29',
     'Optometrist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Performs examination of the human eye by acceptable means including the prescribing of lenses, prisms or vision training to correct visual defects. Therapeutic Certified Optometrists may write prescriptions for oral and topical drugs.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Minimum of three (3) years of college, with four (4) years of optometry school with a minimum of twelve (12) semester hours (transcript credit) in general and ocular pharmacology.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Parts I, II & III of the National Board of Examiners in Optometry as well as TMOD. Kentucky will give only a State Law Exam and an Oral Orientation. For application and dates, contact the regulatory agency.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Initial and annual renewal licensure fees are $200.00 for Kentucky residents and $400.00 for non-residents. Applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. License must be renewed annually before March 1. For renewal, evidence must be presented reflecting compliance with the Continuing Education Requirements. For specific information regarding reciprocity with other states, contact the regulatory agency.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must complete eight (8) hours annually for those NOT drug certified. Fifteen (15) hours per year for those TPA certified.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://optometry.ky.gov/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '300000001', '30',
     'Pharmacist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Counsels and provides medication related information to patients, physicians, and other practitioners on drug usage. Provides drugs and medical supplies, compounds prescriptions, prepares pharmaceutical preparations, maintains legend drug distribution as required by state and federal regulations. Site of practice includes hospital, nursing home, community, nuclear, medical service representatives, teaching, manufacturing and repacking, research and government.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a graduate of an approved (all Pharmacy schools and colleges approved by the American Council on Pharmaceutical Education are hereby approved by the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy) college of pharmacy B.S. Degree in Pharmacy or an entry level Doctor of Pharmacy Degree and must file proof satisfactory to Board, substantiated by affidavits of completion of approved internship under the supervision of a currently licensed pharmacist, who is a certified preceptor. Must complete no less than one hour HIV/AIDS continuing education approved by the Kentucky AIDS Education Program, Cabinet for Health Services, prior to examination.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy for application procedures. Examinations scheduled two (2) times yearly. Location of examinations conducted within the state as designated by the Board. Type examination; knowledge, education, competency of applicants. Must score at least 75% on operative / practical examinations; and at least 80% on jurisprudence. Examination fee is not to exceed the amount of $150.00 (does not include any direct costs for test materials and supplies). Should you fail the examination, the Board Examination shall be considered as composed of two (2) segments: (1) The NABPLEX Examination, and (2) The Kentucky Examination. Upon satisfactory completion of either segment, a retake of that segment is unnecessary. The Kentucky segment consists of jurisprudence and operative pharmacy c',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://pharmacy.ky.gov/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '300000002', '30',
     'Pharmacist Intern', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '4', '2', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://pharmacy.ky.gov/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '30000001', '3',
     'Coroner', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Investigates all deaths in the Commonwealth of Kentucky occurring under any unusual circumstances as defined in the Kentucky Revised Statutes.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Every Coroner must take and successfully complete a forty (40) hour basic training course within one (1) year of taking office for certification by the Kentucky Justice Cabinet.     EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Applicant must submit Application for Training form to the Kentucky Justice Cabinet, Department of Criminal Justice Training, for admittance to a Coroner''s Training Course. At the conclusion of each course, a written examination must be taken and passed for certification. A score of at least 70% is required for certification. There is no examination fee. Reexamination is given, within thirty (30) days, to anyone who fails to make 70% on the first examination.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be 24 years of age, a resident of Kentucky for at least two (2) years, and at least one (1) year residency in the County in which he/she is a candidate.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Every Coroner must take and successfully complete an eighteen (18) hour in-service course annually after completion of the Coroner''s basic course for certification by the Kentucky Justice Cabinet.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certification standards and review for certification are done by the Medical Examiner Advisory Commission and the Board of Directors of the Kentucky State Coroner''s Association.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://docjt.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '30000002', '3',
     'Deputy Coroner', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Investigates all deaths in the Commonwealth of Kentucky, under the direction of a Coroner, occurring under any unusual circumstances as defined in the Kentucky Revised Statutes.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Every Deputy Coroner must take and successfully complete a forty (40) hour basic training course within one (1) year of taking office for certification by the Kentucky Justice Cabinet.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Applicant must submit Application for Training form to the Kentucky Justice Cabinet, Department of Criminal Justice Training, for admittance to a Coroner''s Training Course. At the conclusion of each course, a written examination must be taken and passed for certification. A score of at least 70% is required for certification. There is no examination fee. Reexamination is given, within thirty (30) days, to anyone who fails to make 70% on the first examination.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Every Deputy Coroner must take and successfully complete an eighteen (18) hour in-service course annually after completion of the Coroner''s basic course for certification by the Kentucky Justice Cabinet.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certification standards and review for certification are done by the Medical Examiner Advisory Commission and the Board of Directors of the Kentucky State Coroner''s Association.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://docjt.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '30000003', '3',
     'Law Enforcement Telecommunicator', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    To receive "calls for service" from the public, collect detailed information and dispatch appropriate public safety services in a timely manner. To serve as a centralized point for coordinating agency activities as well as criminal records entry and inquiry functions.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    A high school diploma or G.E.D. equivalency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    In addition to whatever exams are used by the employing agency for screening prior to employment, all certification training and inservice training requires testing with a minimum of 70% for passing.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must attend and successfully complete a forty (40) hour basic course to be certified as a law enforcement telecommunicator. If employing agency has access to the Law Information Network of Kentucky (LINK) and the National Crime Information Center (NCIC), must attend a forty (40) hour basic course to become certified as an operator.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must attend at least eight (8) hours recertification training annually to retain certification as law enforcement telecommunicator. Must attend at least eight (8) hours recertification training annually to retain certification as a LINK / NCIC operator.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Must be a citizen of U.S. and have reached the age of majority. Have not been convicted of a felony or other crimes involving moral turpitude as determined by submission of fingerprints to the State Police and Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI). Must be free of any physical, emotional or mental conditions which might adversely affect employment performance.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '9', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://docjt.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '30000004', '3',
     'Law Enforcement Training Instructor, General', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Provides classroom instruction in general law enforcement topics, specialized law enforcement fields, management and supervision of law enforcement personnel; and performs other duties as required.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Graduate of a college or university, with a bachelor''s degree in law enforcement or a law enforcement related field, supplemented by three years of experience in law enforcement.     EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for applications. Examination scheduled as vacancies occur. General knowledge test, with oral interview and classroom presentation, using comparative ratings. No examination fee. Retake of exami-nation not applicable.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no minimum age requirements. Must be in excellent physical and mental condition, and within acceptable weight limits. Must be of high moral character and have no criminal arrest / conviction record. Traffic violations will be evaluated. Must have a minimum of three (3) years experience as a police officer, judiciary or related criminal justice experience or expertise. Teaching experience in the area of judiciary, law enforcement, or related fields will be evaluated, as well as specialized training received in areas to be certified. Graduate study in any of the above areas will substitute for the required experience on a year-for-year basis, not to exceed two (2) years.     SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certification standards and review for certification are done by the Kentucky Law Enforcement Council.',
     '3', '1', '2', '9', '9',
     '2', '3', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://docjt.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '30000005', '3',
     'Law Enforcement Training Instructor, Legal', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Provides classroom instruction in legal topics, the Kentucky Revised Statutes, laws of arrest, search and seizure and the law enforcement related legal opinions and court decisions; and performs other duties as required.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be licensed to practice law in the Commonwealth of Kentucky supplemented by one year experience in the practice of law.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for applications. Examination scheduled as vacancies occur. General knowledge test, with oral interview and classroom presentation, using comparative ratings. No examination fee. Retake of examination not applicable.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no minimum age requirements. Must be in excellent physical and mental condition, and within acceptable weight limits. Must be of high moral character and have no criminal arrest / conviction record.     SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certification standards and review for certification are done by the Kentucky Law Enforcement Council.',
     '3', '1', '0', '9', '9',
     '2', '3', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://docjt.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '30000006', '3',
     'Law Enforcement Training Instructor, Telecommunications', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Provides classroom instruction in general law enforcement telecommunications, Law Information Network on Kentucky informational systems, National Crime Information Center System, telecommunications data base files and the supervision of law enforcement telecommunication operations and centers; and performs other duties as required.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Graduate of a college or university with a bachelor''s degree in law enforcement or a law enforcement related field, supplemented by three years of experience in law enforcement telecommunications. Additional experience in law enforcement telecommunications will substitute for the required college on a year-for-year basis.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for applications. Examination scheduled as vacancies occur. General knowledge test, with oral interview and classroom presentation, using comparative ratings. No examination fee. Retake of examination not applicable.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no minimum age requirements. Must be in excellent physical and mental condition, and within acceptable weight limits. Must be of high moral character and have no criminal arrest / conviction record. Traffic violations will be evaluated. Must have a minimum of three (3) years experience as a police officer, judiciary or related criminal justice experience or expertise. Teaching experience in the area of judiciary, law enforcement, or related fields will be evaluated, as well as specialized training received in areas to be certified. Graduate study in any of the above areas will substitute for the required experience on a year-for-year basis, not to exceed two (2) years. Additional experience in the above areas will substitute for the required college on a year-for-year basis.     SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certification standards and review for certification are done by the Kentucky Law Enforcement Council.',
     '0', '2', '2', '9', '9',
     '2', '3', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://docjt.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '30000007', '3',
     'Police Officer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Enforces federal and state laws as well as city and county ordinances. Provides routine police patrols, conducts criminal investigations, investigates traffic accidents, and provides police services to the general public.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess a G.E.D. Must successfully complete four hundred (400) hours of basic training approved by the Kentucky Law Enforcement Council within the first year of employment.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be twenty-one (21) years of age. Must meet the physical and mental requirements of the employing agency. Some agencies may require polygraph and/or drug testing.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must successfully complete forty (40) hours inservice training approved by the Kentucky Law Enforcement Council annually.',
     '0', '0', '1', '1', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://docjt.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '310000001', '31',
     'Physical Therapist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Provides physical therapy services or be a consultant to patients with or without referral. Uses selected knowledge and skills to plan, organize, and direct programs for individuals whose ability and function is impaired or threatened. Performs screening and evaluation, tests in aid of diagnosis as well as physical treatment with emphasis on the skeletal system, neuromuscular and cardiopulmonary function. Therapists may specialize and receive advanced practice certification.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have satisfactorily completed all didactic and clinical portions of a Program in Physical Therapy accredited by the Commission on Accreditation in Physical Therapy (CAPTE) and approved by the Kentucky Board of Physical Therapy. Minimal entry level is baccalaureate.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for application procedures. Following approval by the board, a candidate schedules a date and time to sit for the National Physical Therapy Examination (NPTE) via computer based exam at a Sylvan Learning Center, in Louisville or Lexington. May not practice until examination has been successfully completed, if candidate has failed the examination. Must pay fees for examination and reexamination.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age or residency requirements. Must not be addicted to narcotics or indulge in excessive use of alcohol. Must not have been convicted of a felony or any crime which affects ability to practice competently and safely. License to practice in another state must not have been revoked, suspended, or under current disciplinary review or probation. Must have completed four (4) classroom hours in Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) / AIDS education to be licensed.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must complete two (2) hours of HIV / AIDS education for renewal of license every two (2) years.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '0', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://pt.ky.gov/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '310000002', '31',
     'Physical Therapist Assistant', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Assists the physical therapist by performing physical therapy and related duties delegated by the physical therapist. Reports to and is supervised only by a physical therapist.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have satisfactorily completed all didactic and clinical portions of an accredited associate degree level program in physical therapy which has been approved by the Commission on Accreditation in Physical Therapy Education (CAPTE).    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for application procedures. Once approved by the Board as a candidate, the individual is scheduled to sit for the National Physical Therapy Exam (NPTE) which is computer based and available in Kentucky at a Sylvan Learning Center in Louisville or Lexington. May not practice physical therapy until the examination has been successfully completed, if the candidate has failed the examination.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age or residency requirements. Must not be addicted to narcotics or indulge in excessive use of alcohol. Certificate to practice in another state must not have been revoked, suspended, under current disciplinary review or probation. Must not have been convicted of a felony or any crime which affects ability to practice competently and safely. Must have completed four (4) classroom hours in Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) / AIDS education to be licensed.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must complete two (2) hours of HIV / AIDS education for renewal of license every two (2) years.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '9', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://pt.ky.gov/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '320000001', '32',
     'Podiatrist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Examines, diagnoses, treats and prevents diseases, conditions and malfunctions affecting the human foot and its related or governing structure, by employment of medicine, surgery or other means.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Graduate of a school or college of podiatry that is approved by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Submit application, which is provided by the regulatory agency, at least forty (40) days prior to examination. Examinations are scheduled twice a year. Times and locations designated by the regulatory agency. A written examination is given with a passing score of 75%. The examination fee is $250.00. Should you fail, make application to the regulatory agency forty (40) days prior to examination. Reexamination fee is $250.00.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. You must be a resident of the Commonwealth of Kentucky. You must be in good health and be of good moral character and temperate habits. You must possess good clinical competence. This is determined by the examination. All licenses are renewed by June 30 with a renewal fee of $150.00. Reciprocity is left to the discretion of the regulatory agency.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Fifteen (15) hours a year of study in courses relating to the practice of podiatry of which two (2) hours must be related to Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) / AIDS that have been approved by the Cabinet for Health Services and the Kentucky State Board of Podiatry.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://podiatry.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '320000002', '32',
     'Temporary Registered Telehealth Health Care Provider - BOP', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '4', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://podiatry.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '330000001', '33',
     'Professional Geologist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    The performance of service to the public in connection with the geological description, location, or evaluation of earth materials, liquids, and gases and the natural processes acting upon them.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Bachelor''s degree in Geology, Geophysics, Geochemistry, or Geological / Geotechnical Engineering and five (5) years of professional Geological experience.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Must pass an examination composed of the Fundamentals in Geology, and the Principles and Practices of Geology developed and owned by the Association of States Boards of Geology. Examinations are given twice a year, usually in April and September. The deadline for receiving completed applications for the examination are March 1 and September 1. Application fee is $25.00. Examination fee is $350.00. License verification form is $25.00.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Renewal of license due on October 1 annually. Renewal fee is $25.00 and the late renewal fee is $50.00. Duplicate fee is $10.00. Reinstatement fee is $75.00.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bpg.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '330000002', '33',
     'Geologist In Training', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bpg.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '340000001', '34',
     'Certified Social Worker', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Professional activity of helping for remuneration of individuals, groups, or communities enhance or restore their capacity for social functioning and create societal conditions favorable to this goal.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Possess a master''s or doctorate''s degree in social work from an educational institution approved by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    For application procedures, type examination, passing score, examination fee, and retake procedures, contact the regulatory agency. Examination scheduled three (3) times a year, Spring, Summer and Fall.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) year of age. There are no residency or health requirements. For work experience requirements, contact the regulatory agency. Licenses must be renewed three (3) years from date of issuance or from last date of renewal. The renewal fee is $60.00. You must be of good moral character.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bsw.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '340000002', '34',
     'Certified Social Worker (Master''s Degree)', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bsw.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '340000003', '34',
     'Licensed Clinical Social Worker', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bsw.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '340000004', '34',
     'Licensed Social Worker (Baccalaureate Degree)', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Professional activity of helping for remuneration individuals, groups or communities enhance or restore their capacity for social functioning and create societal conditions favorable to this goal.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    You must have received a baccalaureate degree in social work or social welfare program approved by the regulatory agency; or a baccalaureate degree in another field. Two (2) years experience in a social work capacity and completion of courses equivalent to a social work / social welfare program approved by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    For application procedures, type examination, passing score, examination fee, and retake procedures, contact the regulatory agency. Examination is given three (3) times a year, Spring, Summer and Fall.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. You must be of good moral character. For work experience requirements, contact the regulatory agency. Licenses must be renewed three (3) years from date of issuance or from last date of renewal. The renewal fee is $45.00.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bsw.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '340000005', '34',
     'Social Worker, Independent Practice', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Practice which focuses on the evaluation and treatment of emotional disorders and mental illness as related to the total health of the individual.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    You must have a minimum of two (2) years full-time post-masters experience, consisting of at least thirty (30) hours per week OR three (3) years of part-time consisting of at least twenty (20) hours per week, of post-master''s degree employed in independent practice. Experience having been acquired under appropriate supervision.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    For application procedures, type examination, passing score, examination fee, and retake procedures, contact the regulatory agency. Examination is given three (3) times a year, spring, summer and fall.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. You must be of good moral character. Contact the regulatory agency regarding work experience requirements. License must be renewed three (3) years from date of issuance or from last date of renewal. The renewal fee is $75.00.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://bsw.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '350000001', '35',
     'Audiologist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Audiologist must be knowledgeable in the application of principles and procedures of measurement, testing, appraisal, prediction, consultation, and counseling related to hearing and disorders of hearing.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Possess at least a master''s degree in the area of audiology. Submit official transcript from an educational institution approved by the Board, evidencing the successful completion of at least sixty (60) hours of courses related to speech, hearing and language and courses that provide training information.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    The Board will determine examination requirements on an individual basis. The Board waives the examination and grants license to those who hold the certification of clinical competence of the American Speech and Hearing Association. $25.00 application fee and $50.00 licensure fee, the latter being refundable if not approved.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Every applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. You must be a citizen of the United States. You must be of good moral character. You must present evidence, from a licensed or certified audiologist supervisor for a period of nine (9) months in full-time professional employment. For additional information on work-experience requirements, contact the regulatory agency. Licenses are renewed annually, with a $25.00 fee.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Fifteen (15) hours annually. Twenty-five (25) annually for those with dual licensure.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '1',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://slp.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '350000002', '35',
     'Speech-Language Pathologist', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    The application of principles, methods and procedures for the measurement, testing, prediction, counseling, or instruction related to the development and disorders of speech, voice, or language for the purpose of preventive treating such disorders and conditions in individuals and/or groups of individuals.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    You must possess at least a master''s degree in the area of speech pathology. Submit official transcripts from an educational institution approved by the regulatory agency evidencing the successful completion of at least sixty (60) hours of courses related to speech, hearing, and language and courses that provide training information.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. You must be of good moral character. Contact the regulatory agency regarding work experience requirements, and licensure renewal and fees.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Fifteen (15) hours annually. Twenty-five (25) hours for those who hold dual licenses.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    The regulatory agency waives the examination and grants license to those who hold the Certificate of Clinical Competence of the American Speech and Hearing Association. There is a $25.00 application fee and a $50.00 licensure fee, the latter being refundable if not approved.',
