    ('21', '01', '370000002', '37',
     'Emergency Medical Responder', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Must carefully evaluate the patient''s physical condition following an accident or illness, and provide prompt, appropriate and efficient care of the patient prior to transportation to a medical facility. Must complete reports and maintain records on each patient. Must maintain equipment and possibly vehicles. Must be trained in crowd control and utilize two-way communications equipment.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be able to read, speak, write and understand the English language. Must complete a prescribed training course approved by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency regarding application procedures. Written and practical examinations administered at the end of each approved course. Contact the regulatory agency for additional information. Written and Practical Skills examinations given at the end of the course for those who successfully completed same. Practical Skills Certification exam must be passed before applicant is eligible to submit for the Written Certification exam. Must score a minimum of seventy-five percent (75%) on the written examination. $13.00 examination fee. Should applicant fail, must retake entire course again before reexamination.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. May be subject to disciplinary action for violations pertaining to 902 KAR 13:090. Contact the regulatory agency for more information. There are no work experience requirements. Certificates are renewed every three (3) years from date of first issue. Certificate renewal fees are the same as the original fees.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Continuing education or inservice training is a requirement for recertification. Contact the regulatory agency for more information.',
     '0', '3', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kbems.kctcs.edu/', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '370000003', '37',
     'Paramedic', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    The person primarily involved in the delivery of emergency medical services at the scene of an injury or illness, outside of a permanent medical facility.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    High school graduate or equivalency and has successfully completed an approved paramedic training course, approved by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    To secure an application, contact the regulatory agency. Examinations are scheduled in April and October of each year. Utilization of the National Registry of Emergency Medical Technicians written and practical examinations are used in addition to a Kentucky-administered oral examination. The written examination consists of six (6) sections, of which each section has a minimum passing score in addition to a required overall passing score of 75%. The practical examination is on a pass/fail basis as is the oral examination. There is a $10.00 application fee, a $45.00 state fee, and a $35.00 fee to the National Registry of EMT''s. The fees for retest are $45.00 for a practical or oral and $35.00 for the written.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. Must have had a physical examination within twelve (12) months verifying that the applicant is in good health and has no disabilities that may interfere with a paramedics work. Must be currently certified as an EMT, EMT-Ambulance, EMT-Instructor or EMT-Instructor / Trainer. Must attain the Continuing Education Requirements and successfully pass a renewal examination, prescribed by the regulatory agency, prior to expiration of his / her certificate. Reciprocity is considered on an individual basis.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must obtain a minimum of sixty (60) hours of approved in-service training and successfully pass a renewal examination, with minimum score of 80%, prior to expiration of his / her certificate.',
     '0', '3', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '2', '2', '9', '0',
     'https://kbems.kctcs.edu/', '20240718'),
