    ('21', '01', '420000001', '42',
     'Boiler Inspector', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Inspect boilers, pressure vessels and related piping for compliance with the safety rules and regulations of the American Society of Mechanical Engineers Codes and Standard, and the Kentucky Standards established in the statutes.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess a G.E.D equivalency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Write a letter of request to the regulatory agency for application. Schedule of examinations, first Wednesday and Thursday in the months of March, June, September and December. A written examination, with a passing score of 70% required. $20.00 examination fee. Should you fail, you may retake at the next scheduled examination date.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age or residency requirements. Must be physically able to complete any and all tasks assigned. Must have at least five (5) years of experience in boiler and/or pressure vessel construction, repair, operation or maintenance inspection. National Board license fee for new applicants is $35.00; renewal is $25.00. Kentucky has reciprocity with any state that has adopted the American Society of Mechanical Engineers Boiler and Pressure Code and has issued a Certificate of Competency to the applicant.     SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    A National Board Commission is required, along with the Commonwealth of Kentucky Commission, to inspect boilers, pressure vessels and / or piping.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000002', '42',
     'Boiler Contractor', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION     Install, erect or repair boilers, pressure vessels and related piping.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for application procedures. Examinations are scheduled on second (2nd) Friday every month beginning at 8:30 a.m. Written examination required of every applicant. Minimum passing score is 70%. Examination fee of $125.00. Should you fail, you may retake at any future scheduled date.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age, residency or health requirements. Applicant must have at least three (3) years work experience. License are renewable each December 31, with a $100.00 renewal fee. There are no reciprocity agreements with any state.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000003', '42',
     'Building Inspector, Level I', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Reviews and approves plans and makes on-site inspections only on those buildings which are the responsibility of local governments under Kentucky laws.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    An applicant must show proof that he/she possesses at least one (1) of the following credentials: (a) high school graduate or GED; plus three (3) years experience in a responsible directly related construction position, such as a foreman, requiring the ability to effectively read and interpret building plans and specifications, or three (3) years experience in an architect''s or engineer''s office performing building design or drafting duties; or (b) college or university graduate with an associate degree in construction related subject; or (c) college or university graduate with a bachelor degree in architecture, fire science, engineering, or building technology; or (d) successful passage of at least one (1) examination module listed - 1A, 4A, 1B, 3B, 4B, 1C, 3C, 4C, or (e) compliance with applicable local personnel rules of the jurisdiction for which a person is employed which are equal to or more stringent than the above.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for an application. Examinations are computer generated and given approximately every two months during a one week testing window. Must score 75% to pass. Registration fee of $60.00 PLUS test fee of $45.00 each test.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    To be certified, applicants must pass test modules 1A, 4A, 1B AND 3B and attend a three day orientation session. Any person employed by a local government MUST be registered in the Certification Program. Only certified inspectors may legally function fully as a Building Inspector. These are requirements for State certification only. Officials may continue testing for national certification through Building Officials and Code Administrators Internationals (BOCA). Annual renewal fee is $25.00.    CONTINUING EDUCAT',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000004', '42',
     'Building Inspector, Level II', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Reviews and approves plans and makes on-site inspections only on those buildings which are the responsibility of local governments under the Kentucky Revised Statutes and makes on-site inspections of all buildings regardless of size with agreement from the Kentucky Department of Housing, Buildings and Construction.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    An applicant must show proof that he possesses at least one (1) of the following credentials: (a) high school graduate or GED; plus three (3) years experience in a responsible directly related construction position, such as a foreman, requiring the ability to effectively read and interpret building plans and specifications, or three (3) years experience in an architect''s or engineer''s office performing building design or drafting duties; or (b) college or university graduate with an associate degree in construction related subject; or (c) college or university graduate with a bachelor degree in architecture, fire science, engineering, or building technology; or (d) successful passage of at least one (1) examination module listed - 1A, 4A, 1B, 3B, 4B, 1C, 3C, 4C; or (e) compliance with applicable local personnel rules of the jurisdiction for which a person is employed which are equal to or more stringent than the above.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examinations are computer generated and given approximately every two (2) months during a one (1) week testing window. Must score 75% to pass. Registration fee of $60.00 PLUS test fee of $45.00 each test.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    To be certified, applicants must pass test modules 1B, 4A, 1B, 3B and 4B and attend a three (3) day orientation session. Any person employed by a local government must be registered in the Certification Program. Only certified inspectors may legally function fully as a local Building Inspector. These are requirements for state certification only. Officials may continue testing for national certi',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000005', '42',
     'Electrical Contractor', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Any individual that engages in the business of or employs others for construction, alteration, or repair of any electrical wiring used for the purpose of furnishing heat, light, or power.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Ability to read, comprehend, and write.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    For application procedures, contact Block and Associates. Examinations are administered on a regular basis, with a fee of $50.00 charged by Block and Associates. The examination is Open Book, with the passing score being a minimum of 70%. There is no waiting period for retesting.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Initial application fee is $100.00; annual renewal fee is $25.00. Failure to renew on or before July 1 of each year require a delinquent renewal fee of $100.00. After January 1 the following year a reinstatement fee of $100.00, any unpaid renewal fees plus petition to the Commissioner with reason for lapse renewal. Possession of a Certificate of Electrical Contractor Certification is not a license to do business as an electrical contractor.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000006', '42',
     'Certified Electrical Inspector', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Inspects electrical installations to ascertain that they have been installed in compliance with the National Electrical Code.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Applicant shall possess the ability to speak, read and write in the English language and possess a general education level satisfactory to perform his duties.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for applications and testing information. Certification is based on the National Certification Program for Construction Code Inspectors Tests. Temporary nine (9) month certification is available on request from local officials. Temporary certification test is open book based on NEC standards. Application fee is $25.00.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age, residency or moral requirements. Applicant must have no less than five (5) years work- experience, in the installation and/or design of all types of residential and commercial wiring systems installed in accordance with NEC standards. Kentucky has no reciprocity agreement with any state.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Certificates will be reissued upon request after reexamination or after a presentation of proof by the electrical inspector that he has successfully completed 12 hours of continuing education courses conducted or approved by the Department prior to expiration. The fee for renewal shall be $25.00, payable to State Treasurer, Commonwealth of Kentucky.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Temporary examination can be taken three (3) times for certification.',
     '0', '2', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000007', '42',
     'Elevator Inspector', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Inspects elevators, escalators and moving walks in Kentucky once per year to ascertain that unit meets safety standards. Runs / witness tests and inspects for compliance of code requirements on each new or altered elevator, escalator, moving walk, dumbwaiter, platform / stair / wheelchair lift, and other various equipment in order to issue certificate of compliance, attesting that the installation meets all safety code requirements.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate and hold a Certificate of Competency from the Department.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for application and procedures. Examinations scheduled any normal work day. For specific details contact the agency. Type examination; certification test from the following standards: Safety Code For Elevators and Escalators - ASME A7.1, Inspectors'' manual-ASME A17.2, Safety Code for Existing Elevators and Escalators - ASME A17.3, The National Electric Code - ANSI/NEPA 70. Must score 70% or more to be certified. $10.00 examination should you fail, retake within six (6) months.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. Must be in general good health and able to climb on top of and underneath elevators, and maneuver vertical ladders and stairs to various heights; to check safety equipment. Must be courteous, honest, trustworthy, sober and have good communication skills to deal with the public. There is no license fee, as this is a state employment position. Kentucky has no reciprocity with any state, however other states use the same code requirements.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Seminars are conducted periodically for inservice training.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Hazardous conditions exist for elevator inspectors, which requires that they use extreme caution in their work.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000008', '42',
     'Fire Alarm System Inspector', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Performs inspection of fire alarm systems.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Within the five (5) years preceding application, individual should have a minimum of one and one-half (1 1/2) years experience in the installation, repair or testing of fire alarm systems. Educational courses and special training courses may be substituted for experience.     EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    For applications, procedures, and schedule of examinations, contact the regulatory agency. Examinations are scheduled on a quarterly basis. Type examination; written (open book) based on National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) publications, the Kentucky Building Code (KBC) and "The Kentucky Fire Prevention Code - Standards of Safety". Practical examination given on system(s) simulator(s). Passing score on written examination is 70% and satisfactory on practical examination. Examination fee is $25.00 per examination. Applicants who do not achieve a score of 70% or higher but do score more than 50% will be allowed to retake the examination the next test cycle upon application to do so. Those individuals who attain a score of less than 50% must wait a minimum of six (6) months (two test cycles) to reapply for the examination.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Each successful applicant is issued an identification card (ID) card with their assigned inspector''s number. This number must be entered on all inspection reports. A copy of the completed report must be forwarded to the State Fire Marshal''s Office, (Fire Protection Systems) within fourteen (14) days of the inspection. The reports will be reviewed for completeness. Reports found to be deficient will be investigated.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Inspectors must make every effort to keep abreast of changes in technology, codes and regulations concerning fire alarm systems.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    The certification of fire alarmsystem',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
