    ('21', '01', '420000010', '42',
     'Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning Contractor, Master', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Authorized to contract for and engage in the business of installation, maintenance, altering, remodeling and repair of heating, ventilation and air conditioning systems.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age and been regularly and principally employed or engaged in the heating, ventilation and air conditioning trades as a Journeyman mechanic for not less than two (2) years under the direction and supervision of a Master Contractor before sitting for the Kentucky-specific examination.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    A Master Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC) Contractor license application fee is one hundred dollars ($100.00). Applicant must meet the insurance requirements of $500,000 general liability and $300,000 property damage ($800,000 aggregate).    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Each licensee shall complete ten (10) hours of continuing education approved by the Board prior to the annual renewal of license.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    A licensed Master HVAC Contractor who plans to do mechanic "hands on" work must also obtain a Journeyman HVAC Mechanic license.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000011', '42',
     'Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning Duct Mechanic, Limited', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Authorized to fabricate, install, repair or extend ductwork under the supervision of a Master Contractor.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age and been regularly and principally employed or engaged in the heating, ventilation and air conditioning trades under the direction and supervision of a HVAC Master Contractor for two (2) years and three thousand (3,000) hours as a registered Apprentice. Must pass the ""Limited Kentucky Journeyman Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC) Duct Mechanic"" examination.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Each licensee shall complete ten (10) hours of continuing education approved by the Board prior to the annual renewal of license.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certain classroom or other education may be substituted for up to one (1) year and fifteen hundred (1,500) hours of experience subject to Board approval.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000012', '42',
     'Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning Installer Mechanic', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Authorized to install system of air conditioning, warm air Heating and Ventilation, including startup of equipment and duct system necessary to make a complete system.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age and been regularly and principally employed or engaged in the heating, ventilation and air conditioning trades under the direction and supervision of a HVAC Master Contractor for two (2) years and three thousand (3,000) hours as a registered Apprentice. Must pass the ""Limited Kentucky Journeyman Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC) Installer Mechanic"" examination.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Each licensee shall complete ten (10) hours of continuing education approved by the Board prior to the annual renewal of license.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certain classroom or other education may be substituted for up to one (1) year and fifteen hundred (1,500) hours of experience subject to Board approval.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000013', '42',
     'Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning Mechanic, Journeyman', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Authorized to install, maintain, alter, remodel or repair of heating systems, ventilation systems, hydropic systems, burner service or cooling systems under the supervision of a Master HVAC Contractor.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age and been regularly and principally employed or engaged in the heating, ventilation and air conditioning trades under the direction and supervision of a Master HVAC Master Contractor for two (2) years and three thousand (3,000) hours as a registered Apprentice. Must pass the ""Kentucky Journeyman Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC) Mechanic"" examination.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Each licensee shall complete ten (10) hours of continuing education approved by the Board prior to the annual renewal of license.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Certain classroom or other education may be substituted for up to one (1) year and fifteen hundred (1,500) hours of experience subject to Board approval.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000014', '42',
     'Manufactured Housing Installer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    ""INSTALLATION"" means the on-site work performed and operations involved in the delivery and placement of a manufactured home onto a foundation system. This definition shall include site preparation, foundation construction, underskirting and anchoring devices, together with any accessories and appurtenances specified in the sales contract and the connection of utilities.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    The applicant must attend an approved certified installer school for a minimum of fifteen (15) classroom hours.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    A fifty (50) question exam is administered by the approved school and the Office of the State Fire Marshal, Manufactured Housing Section. The applicant must record a passing grade of 70%. After testing the applicants completes an application for Certification and pays a $50.00 fee.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    The Certified Installer shall attend five (5) class hours of approved education annually and remit a $25.00 annual fee.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000015', '42',
     'Underground Petroleum Storage Tank Installer/Remover Contractor', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Person or organization who installs, repairs, closes or removes an underground petroleum storage tank for an owner or operator. The non-refundable application fee is $150.00.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    An applicant requesting installer/remover contractor certification shall demonstrate experience in installation of three (3) underground petroleum storage tanks and three (3) removals of same.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Each applicant for certified contractor shall take and pass a written examination administered by the State Fire Marshal''s office. Examination fee is $25.00.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Applicant requesting certification as an underground storage tank contractor must show financial capability through proof of insurance. Minimum $500,000 general liability insurance and a minimum $25,000 pollution liability required. Yearly renewal necessary. No re-examination required unless failed to renew for over one (1) year. Also available "tank liner only" certification and a "cathodic protection only" certification. Details available upon request from Hazardous Materials Section, Kentucky State Fire Marshal''s Office, address listed below.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
