    ('21', '01', '420000018', '42',
     'Plans & Specifications Inspector, Level III', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Reviews and approves plans and makes on-site inspections only on those buildings which are the responsibility of local governments under the Kentucky Revised Statutes and with agreement of the Department approve plans and make on-site inspections of all buildings, regardless of size and within the inspector''s jurisdiction to determine if those buildings are constructed in accordance with the plans and the Kentucky Building Code.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    An applicant must show proof that he/she possesses at least one (1) of the following credentials: (a) high school graduate or GED; plus three (3) years experience in a responsible directly related construction position, such as a foreman, requiring the ability to effectively read and interpret building plans and specifications; or three (3) years experience in an architect''s or engineer''s office performing building design or drafting duties; or (b) college or university graduate with an associate degree in construction related subject; or (c) college or university graduate with a bachelor degree in architecture, engineering, fire science or building technology; or (d) successful passage of at least one (1) examination module listed - 1A, 4A, 1B, 3B, 4B, 1C, 3C 4C; or (e) compliance with applicable local personnel rules of the jurisdiction for which a person is employed which are equal to or more stringent than the above.     EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examinations are computer generated and given approximately every two (2) months during a one (1) week testing window. Must score 75% to pass. Registration fee of $60.00 PLUS test fee of $45.00 each test.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    To be certified applicants must pass test modules 1B, 4A, 1B, 3B, 4B, 1C, 3C and attend a three (3) day orientation session. Any person employed by a local government must be registered in the Certification Program. Only certified inspectors may legally function as a local Build',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000019', '42',
     'Plumber, Journeyman', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Engages in the construction, maintenance, installation, alteration, repair, remodeling or removal, and placement of plumbing under the supervision and responsibility of a master plumber.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be able to read, comprehend and write.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    You may secure an application by contacting the regulatory agency. Normally the test is given on the third Saturday of February and May and on the first Saturday in August and November, or as determined by the regulatory agency. Type examination, written, drawing and practical. Passing score of 70% is allowed on one (1) phase of the examination with an overall score of 75%. Examination is in the English language. The examination fee is $50.00. Should you fail, contact the regulatory agency.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be a citizen of the United States or have first papers. Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. You must be of good moral character. Must have two (2) consecutive years experience as an apprentice under the supervision of a master or journeyman plumber. All license are renewed annually by June 30 through the regulatory agency with a renewal fee of $40.00.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dhbc.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '420000020', '42',
     'Plumber, Master', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Assumes responsible charge, supervision, and/or direction of journeyman plumbers and apprentices as well as offers to engage in or contract the construction, installation or alteration of plumbing systems.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be able to read, comprehend and write.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for application procedures. Normally the test is given once each quarter or as determined by the regulatory agency. Written and drawing examination is given, with a passing score of 75% allowed on one (1) phase of the examination with an overall score of 80%. Examination is in the English language. The examination fee is $150.00. Should you fail, contact the regulatory agency.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be a citizen of the United States or have first papers. Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There   are no residency or health requirements. You must be of good moral character. Must possess a journeyman plumber license for two (2) years and actively employed in plumbing in two (2) of the last five (5) years. All license are renewed annually by June 30 through the regulatory agency with a renewal fee of $150.00.',
