    ('21', '01', '480000003', '48',
     'Commercial and Structural Pest Control Applicator (LPCO)/Manager', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Negotiates sale of ""wood destroying organisms"" and ""structural fumigations,"" subcategories of the ""Industrial, Institutional, Structural and Health-Related Pest Control"" category. Must be able to hold training courses for employees.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have two (2) years experience with a pest control company. Must be familiar with the laws and regulations set forth by the Kentucky Department of Agriculture. Must be knowledgeable of minimum standards of all categories. Must be able to identify specimen.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency for application. Examinations are scheduled for the Second Tuesday during May and November, unless the Second Tuesday is a holiday or falls on election day. Should this occur, the examination will be given on the Third Tuesday. The examination is a multiple-choice type, with a score required of at least 70%. The identification portion of the examination also requires a passing score of 70% or more. There is a $50.00 examination fee. Should you not pass the examination, contact the regulatory agency for retake information.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. Applicant must be honest, truthful, trustworthy and of a good reputation. Must have had at least two (2) years work experience, employed with a licensed Structural Pest Control applicator, or have a degree in Entomology. Contact the regulatory agency regarding reciprocity with other states.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must attend at least two (2) training courses within five (5) year period to maintain certification.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.kyagr.com/', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '480000004', '48',
     'Licensed Pest Control Operator', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Applies chemicals to the land of others for a fee, to combat pest problems. Work under the supervision of a Pesticide Applicator. Must have a thorough knowledge of chemicals, spray nozzles, drift problems and the comprehension of labels and their significance.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    No formal educational requirements are necessary; however, applicants must study and have knowledge of materials supplied by the regulatory agency in preparation for the examination.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    To secure an application, contact the regulatory agency. Examinations are scheduled in groups or by appointment as determined by the regulatory agency. The exam is a combination of multiple choice and true / false. Applicants must score at least 70%. There is no examination fee. License fee is $10.00; certification fee is $25.00. Should you fail the examination, contact the regulatory agency for retake procedures.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residence, health or work-experience requirements. License are renewed annually, by December 31st. License renewed after March 1st requires a 25% penalty. You must be retested if you do not renew by June 1st. To secure information concerning reciprocity, contact the regulatory agency.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Attendance at two (2) approved meetings, within five (5) years, for recertification without re-testing if applicant applies Restricted-Use Pesticides.',
