    ('21', '01', '50000001', '5',
     'Apprentice Auctioneer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Apprentice auctioneer works under the supervision of a principal auctioneer. He accepts bids on goods sold at auction. He handles no money and his actions are the responsibility of his sponsoring principal auctioneer. Any monies owed to him for his services must be paid first to his principal and the principal in turn will give the apprentice his share.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Study material for the exam is provided to the applicant by the Board office. Applicants must be at least 18 years of age. Must have a high school diploma or G.E.D. certificate.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application & forms must be received from the Board office and must be completed and returned at least 21 days prior to exam date. Fee is $75.00. Exam offered every February, May, August, and November. Applicants must attain a score of sixty to pass exam. If applicant fails exam, a new application must be completed and again pay the testing fee. Exam is offered in Louisville, KY only.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicants must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. Applicants for apprentice auctioneer license must serve a two-year (2) apprenticeship and also must participate as bid caller in at least ten (10) auction sales during the immediate preceding twelve (12) months before applying to sit for the principal auctioneer examination. Initial license fee is $50.00 for the license and $30.00 for the Auctioneer''s Education Research and Recovery Fund for a total of $80.00. Licenses renewed every June 30th. License renewal fee is $60.00 ($50.00 license fee and $10.00 for contribution to the recovery fund renewal fee).    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Applicants are required to have three (3) hours per year for apprentice auctioneer license.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Examination consists of a three and one-half hour written. Applicant is graded on writing, mathematics, genera',
     '4', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://auctioneers.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '50000002', '5',
     'Auction House Operator', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Auction house operator owns and operates a fixed site auction house where more than one auction is held per year. He/she gives receipts and renders accounting and funds to sellers of items. He/she does not do the auctioneering. He/she must acquire the services of a licensed auctioneer unless he/she is licensed as an auctioneer.     EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    All study material is given to applicant by regulatory agency. Applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. Must have a high school diploma or G.E.D. certificate.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application forms must be completed and returned to the regulatory agency at least twenty-one (21) days prior to the exam date. Examination is three (3) hour written format. Applicant is graded on writing, mathematics, general knowledge of the law, ethics, auction contracts, and final settlements. Examinations are administered in February, May, August, and November. Must score at least sixty (60) to pass. If applicant fails the examination, he/she must reapply and pay the $100.00 examination fee before being permitted to retake same. Examination is administered in Louisville, Kentucky only.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicant must be the owner / operator of an auction house at a fixed site. License renewed every June 30th. Initial license fee is $80.00. Renewal fee is $60.00 ($50.00 for renewal license fee and $10.00 for renewal recovery fund fee).',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://auctioneers.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '50000003', '5',
     'Limited Livestock Auctioneer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    The person who holds a limited livestock license may auction only livestock at fixed based livestock yards operating under the control and guidance of the United States of America pursuant to the Federal Packers and Stockyards Act. These people are exempt from continuing education requirements.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    The applicant must be at least 18 years of age. Must have high school diploma or G.E.D. certificate.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application & forms must be received from the Board office and must be completed and returned at least 21 days prior to exam date. Fee is $100.00. Exam offered every February, May, August, and November. Applicant must attain a score of sixty to pass exam. If applicant fails exam a new application must be completed and again pay the testing fee. Exam is offered in Louisville, KY only.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicants must be at least eighteen (18) years old. Initial license fee is $50.00 for the license and $30.00 for the Auctioneer''s Education Research and Recovery Fund for a total of $80.00. Licenses renewed every June 30th. License renewal fee is $60.00 ($50.00 for the renewal license fee and $10.00 for the recovery fund fee). No apprenticeship experience is required.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Examination consists of a three and one-half hour written test. Applicant is graded on General knowledge and Mathematics. Applicant is also graded on an oral presentation before the Board. Passing grade is sixty (60).',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://auctioneers.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '50000004', '5',
     'Limited Tobacco Auctioneer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    The person can auction only tobacco at a fixed base tobacco warehouse operating under the control and guidance of the United States of America through the Department of Agriculture.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    The applicant must be at least 18 years of age. Must have high school diploma or G.E.D. certificate.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application & forms must be received from the Board office and must be completed and returned at least 21 days prior to exam date. Fee is $100.00. Exam offered every February, May, August, and November. Applicant must attain a score of sixty to pass exam. If applicant fails exam must complete a new application and again pay the testing fee. Exam is offered in Louisville, KY only.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicants must be at least eighteen (18) years old. Initial license fee is $50.00 for the license and $30.00 for the Auctioneer''s Education Research and Recovery Fund for a total of $80.00. Licenses renewed every June 30th. License renewal fee is $60.00 ($50.00 for the renewal license fee and $10.00 for the recovery fund fee.) No apprenticeship experience is required.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Examination consists of a three and one-half hour written test. Applicant is graded on general knowledge and Mathematics. Applicant is also graded on an oral presentation before the Board. Passing grade is sixty (60).',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://auctioneers.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '50000005', '5',
     'Principal Auctioneer', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    An auctioneer accepts bids on property belonging to someone else for the highest possible amount for the seller. He enters into a contract, gives receipts, gives accounting and funds to seller within thirty (30) days along with proceeds.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Study material is provided to applicants by the Board office for preparation for the exam. Applicants for the principal exam must possess a high school diploma or equivalent.     EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application and forms must be received from Board office, must be completed and returned with fee twenty-one (21) days prior to exam date. Fee is $100.00. Exam offered every February, May, August, and November. Score of seventy-five (75) is needed to pass the exam. If applicant fails he must complete new application and pay fee again before retake of test. Exam is offered in Louisville, Kentucky only.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Applicants must be at least eighteen (18) years of age and must have served at least two years (2) apprenticeship. He/she must have been the bid caller in at least ten (10) sales during the immediate preceding twelve (12) months before sitting for the Principal examination. He / she must possess a high school diploma or equivalent. Non-residents who reside in a state where no licensing requirements exist must fill out the proper application and forms and sit for the exam. Applicants who reside in a state with which we have reciprocity must fill out the required forms and pay the fee with no test required. Fee for all tests is $100.00 with the exception of the apprentice which is $75.00. License fees are: initial license $80.00 and renewal fees are $60.00. Renewal are every June 30th.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Applicants are required to have six (6) hours per year for principle auctioneer.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Examination consists of a three and one-half',
