     'http://auctioneers.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '510000001', '51',
     'Drinking Water Treatment and Distribution System Operator', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    See that all equipment at water treatment plants are operating properly and that the plant is producing an acceptable product. Prepares monthly operating reports and maintains operating records. Maintains distribution system and storage for water utilities.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    High school diploma or GED required as a minimum for any type system operation, however, the largest plants and distribution systems (Class IV) require a college Bachelors degree.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency to determine eligibility for certification and examination. Examinations are given quarterly in Frankfort, during the annual operators conference, and on the last day of certification training sessions. Type of examination; multiple choice and true/false. Must score at least 70%. Examination fees of $30.00 per examination. Should you fail, you may register for a retake at the next scheduled session by paying a $30.00 retake fee.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age requirements. You may be required to take a physical examination by the hiring authority. Work experience is required in all classifications. Certificates are good for two years and must be renewed by June 30 of even-numbered years, at a renewal fee of $20.00. Kentucky has reciprocity with several states.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Twelve (12) hours per renewal for Classes I & II. Twenty-four (24) hours per renewal for Classes III & IV. The fee for renewal is $20.00 prior to June 30 and $55.00 after June 30. All state-sponsored continuing education classes re-quire preregistration and payment of a fee which varies per class - $10.00 average.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://eec.ky.gov/Pages/index.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '510000002', '51',
     'Wastewater System Operator', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Sees that all equipment at wastewater plants are operating properly, supervises workers and arranges for the disposal of sludge. Makes sure that the plants are meeting the conditions as required by regulation and within the operating permit. Prepares discharge monitoring reports and maintains operating records.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    High school diploma required as a minimum for any type plant operation, however, the larger plants (class IV) require a baccalaureate degree.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Contact the regulatory agency to determine eligibility for certification. Examinations are scheduled quarterly in Frankfort office, during the annual operators conference, and on the last day of the certification training sessions. Type of examination; multiple choice and true/false. Must score 70% or more. Examination fee is $30.00. Should you fail, you may register for a retake at the next regularly scheduled examination by paying a $30.00 retake fee.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    There are no age requirements. Work experience is required in all classifications. Certifications are valid for two (2) years, and must be renewed by June 30 of odd-numbered years at a renewal fee of $20.00. Kentucky has reciprocity with certain states. Contact the regulatory agency for specific details.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Twenty-four (24) hours per renewal for Class III and IV. Twelve (12) hours per renewal for Class I and II. The fee for renewal is $20.00 prior to June 30 and $55.00 after June 30. All state-sponsored continuing education classes require preregistration and payment of a fee (fee varies per class - $30.00 average).',
