    ('21', '01', '520000001', '52',
     'General Real Estate Appraiser', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    A specialist who provides an analysis, opinion, or conclusion relating to the nature, value or utility of specified interests in, or aspects of, identified real estate, for or in expectation of compensation.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or equivalent. Must successfully complete one hundred eighty (180) classroom hours of courses related to real estate appraisal which shall include fifteen (15) hours of the Uniform Standards of Professional Appraisal Practice (USPAP). Experience may not be substituted for education.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Applicant must successfully pass the written State Certification / Licensing Examination, with a minimum score of (70%) percent. Contact the regulatory agency for specific information. Education requirements must be met prior to being seated for the examination.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be eighteen (18) years of age. Must be deemed as competent by the board. No health requirements. Kentucky residents must maintain a definite place of business in Kentucky. No residency requirements for state certification. There will be annual renewal of certificates, the date to be determined by the board. Annual certificate renewal fee is not to exceed $200.00.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    The equivalent of fourteen (14) classroom hours of instruction in courses or seminars for each year during the period preceding renewal is required.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Applicant must have acquired three thousand (3,000) hours and a minimum of thirty (30) months of appraisal experience. Hours may be treated as cumulative in order to obtain the hours. At least fifty percent (50%) or fifteen hundred (1,500) hours must be in non-residential appraisal work. Residential is defined as one-to-four residential units.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kreab.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '520000002', '52',
     'Residential Real Estate Appraiser', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    A specialist who provide an analysis, opinion, or conclusion relating to the nature, quality, value or utility of specified interests in, or aspects of, identified real estate, for or in expectation of compensation.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or equivalent and successfully complete one hundred twenty (120) classroom hours of courses in subjects related to real estate appraisal which shall include fifteen (15) classroom hours of the Uniform Standards of Professional Appraisal Practice (USPAP). Experience may not be substituted for education.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    The Education Requirements must be met prior to being seated for the examination. You must successfully pass the written State Certification / Licensing Examination, with a minimum score of seventy (70%) percent. Examination fees cannot exceed $200.00. Should you fail the examination, retake procedures are: must pay examination fee and can be retaken at the next scheduled examination date.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be eighteen (18) years of age. Must be deemed as competent by the board. No health requirements. Kentucky residents must maintain a definite place of business in Kentucky. No residency requirements for state certification. There will be annual renewal of certificates, the date to be determined by the board. Annual certificate renewal fee is not to exceed $200.00.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    The equivalent of fourteen (14) classroom hours of instruction in courses and seminars for each year during the period preceding the renewal.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Applicant must have acquired two thousand five hundred (2,500) hours and a minimum of two (2) calendar years of appraisal experience. Hours may be treated as cumulative.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kreab.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '520000003', '52',
     'Licensed Real Property Appraiser', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    A specialist who provide an analysis, opinion, or conclusion relating to the nature, quality, value or utility of specified interests in, or aspects of, identified real estate, for or in expectation of compensation.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or equivalent and successfully complete ninety (90) classroom hours of courses in subjects related to real estate appraisal which shall include fifteen (15) classroom hours of the Uniform Standards of Professional Appraisal Practice (USPAP). Experience may not be substituted for education.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Applicant must successfully pass the written State Certification / Licensing Examination, with a minimum score of seventy (70%) percent. Examination fees cannot exceed $200.00. Should you fail the examination, retake procedures are: must pay examination fee and can be retaken at the next scheduled examination date. Education requirements must be met prior to being seated for the examination.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be eighteen (18) years of age. Must be deemed as competent by the board. No health requirements. Kentucky residents must maintain a definite place of business in Kentucky. No residency requirements for state certification. There will be annual renewal of certificates, the date to be determined by the board. Annual certificate renewal fee is not to exceed $200.00.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    The equivalent of fourteen (14) classroom hours of instruction in courses or seminars for each year during the period preceding the renewal is required.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Equivalent of two (2) years appraisal experience, and a minimum of two thousand (2,000) hours of actual appraisal experience. Hours may be treated as cumulative.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kreab.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '520000004', '52',
     'Associate Appraiser', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kreab.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '530000001', '53',
     'Broker', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Negotiates, or attempts to negotiate, the sale, exchange, rental or leasing of real property, belonging to other people, for a fee, compensation or commission and can supervise sales associates.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    You must be a high school graduate or equivalent and twenty-one (21) credit hours with a minimum of twelve (12) credit hours in real estate from an accredited college or university or three hundred and thirty-six (336) clock hours from a private school approved by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Examinations are scheduled several times a week in Kentucky. Type examination; multiple choice on computer. Must score 75% or higher. Examination fee is $75.00. Secure information from the regulatory agency or an approved real estate school.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be eighteen (18) years of age to make application. There are no health requirements. You must be honest, trustworthy and of a good reputation. You must have worked as a real estate sales associate for at least twenty-four (24) months. All licenses are renewed annually by March 31, fee not to exceed $30.00 plus Education, Research and Recovery Fund not to exceed $30.00. Contact the regulatory agency regarding reciprocity. Errors and Omissions Insurance is required of all licensees whether secured from an insurance company or through the regulatory agency''s group.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    All active real estate licensees must complete six (6) hours of continuing education each calendar year. Two (2) of the six (6) hours must be in real estate law topic. Individuals who were originally licensed prior to June 19, 1976 and who have maintained a continuously active license since that date, as well as licensees in escrow are exempt from this requirement.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://krec.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '530000002', '53',
     'Sales Associate', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Negotiates, or attempts to negotiate, the sale, exchange, rental or leasing of property, belonging to other people, for a fee, compensation or commission. Work under the supervision of a Real Estate Broker.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess G.E.D. equivalency PLUS successfully complete six (6) credit hours or ninety-six (96) classroom hours of instruction in real estate courses from an accredited college, university or a commission approved proprietary school.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Information may be secured from the regulatory agency. Examinations are given several times a week in Kentucky. Multiple choice examination. You must score 75%. The examination fee is $75.00.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be eighteen (18) years of age to make application. You must be a resident of Kentucky. There are no health requirements. You must be honest, trustworthy and of a good reputation. There are no work requirements. All licenses are renewed by March 31, fee not to exceed $30.00 plus Educational, Research and Recovery Fund not to exceed $30.00. Contact the regulatory agency regarding reciprocity. Errors and Omissions Insurance is required of all licensees whether secured from an insurance company or through the regulatory agency''s group.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    All active real estate licensees must complete six (6) hours of continuing education each calendar year. Two (2) of the six (6) hours must be in real estate law topic. Individuals who were originally licensed prior to June 19, 1976 and who have maintained a continuously active license since that date, as well as licensees in escrow are exempt from this requirement.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://krec.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '530000003', '53',
     'Registered Firm Branch', 'Contact the regulatory agency for specific information.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://krec.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '540000001', '54',
     'Property Valuation Administrator', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    It is the primary duty of the Property Valuation Administrator (PVA) to equitably assess all real and personal property in his / her county, based on the fair cash value of the property.     EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    A candidate running for the office of Property Valuation Administrator (PVA) must first pass a written examination. Examinations are administered by the Kentucky Revenue Cabinet in each of the seven (7) Supreme Court Districts of the Commonwealth during the month of November of the preceding year in which PVA''s are to be elected. Successful applicants are issued a certificate by the Kentucky Revenue Cabinet indicating eligibility to run for office.   This certification expires in one (1) year. The next statewide PVA examination will be in November, 2001.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Candidates must be at least twenty-four (24) years of age at the time of election. He / she must be a citizen of the Commonwealth of Kentucky for two (2) years and one (1) year in the county and district in which he/she is a candidate preceding the election. PVA''s, although elected in a specific county, are considered state officials and all deputies and assistants of their offices shall be unclassified state employees.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Every PVA shall annually, within each calendar year, participate in a minimum of thirty (30) classroom hours of professional instruction conducted or approved by the regulatory agency. The annual requirement shall be reduced to fifteen (15) hours for a PVA who earns the Senior Kentucky Assessor (SKA) professional designation, administered by the Revenue Cabinet.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://revenue.ky.gov/Property/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '550000001', '55',
     'Driver Training Instructor', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Any person who gives driver training or offers a course of driver training for which a fee is charged.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or the equivalent (GED).    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    For application, contact the regulatory agency. Examination given according to the Driver Testing schedule in the county where the applicant resides. Examination type; vision, written, and actual road test. Must score a minimum of 80%. If road test is failed, you must wait a minimum of one (1) week.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must be at least twenty-one (21) years of age and of good moral character. Must hold a current, valid Kentucky operator''s license, and must not have been convicted of two (2) moving hazardous violations within the two-year period immediately preceding the application. If instructing commercial drivers, must hold a Commercial Drivers License (CDL). Must have a physical examination. Must be employed by a driver training school licensed by the Kentucky State Police. No work experience is required. License fee is $20.00, and must be renewed annually by June 30, at a fee of $20.00. Kentucky has no reciprocity with any other state.     SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    An instructor cannot be absent one functional eye, hand, or foot. The visual acuity of an instructor cannot be worse than 20/20 in one eye and 20/40 in the other, or 20/30 in each eye separately with or without glasses.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '9',
     '3', '1', '2', '9', '0',
     'https://www.kentuckystatepolice.org/dt', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '560000001', '56',
     'Polygraph Examiner', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Conducts polygraph examinations in order to verify the truthfulness of information or statements given by the examinee.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess a G.E.D. and be a graduate of an examiner training school recognized by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application must be secured from and submitted to the regulatory agency. The examinations are scheduled at the convenience of the applicant once he / she has passed a background investigation. Type examination given, multiple choice and true/false and must score 70% or more. Application fee of $50.00 includes the examination cost. Should you fail, retake the examination within forty-five (45) days.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. You must be of good moral character. For further requirements, contact the regulatory agency. You must have more than one (1) year experience as a polygraph examiner. All licenses are renewed annually by December 31. You must complete a renewal application and pay $40.00 renewal fee. Reciprocity varies. Contact the regulatory agency.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must attend at least twelve (12) hours of instruction in subject matter related directly to the polygraph profession during the licensing year and furnish certification of attendance with license renewal request at the end of the year.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://kentuckystatepolice.org/forensic-laboratory-system/', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '560000002', '56',
     'Polygraph Intern/Trainee', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Conducts polygraph examinations in order to verify the truthfulness of information or statements given by the examinee.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess a G.E.D. and be a graduate of an examiner training school recognized by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATIONS REQUIREMENTS    Applications must be secured from and submitted to the regulatory agency. The examinations are scheduled at the convenience of the applicant once he / she has passed background investigation. Type examination given; multiple choice and true / false and must score 70% or more. Application fee of $50.00 includes the examination cost. Should you fail, you must retake the examination within forty-five (45) days.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. You must be a resident of Kentucky. There are no health requirements. You must be of good moral character. For further requirements, contact the regulatory agency. You may have less than one (1) year work experience as an examiner. All licenses are renewed annually by December 31. You must complete a renewal application and pay a $40.00 renewal fee. Reciprocity varies. Contact the regulatory agency.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    You must complete secondary requirements of an approved training school and be certified by the intern supervisor.',
     '4', '1', '9', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://kentuckystatepolice.org/forensic-laboratory-system/', '20240718'),
