    ('21', '01', '70000002', '7',
     'Barber', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Cuts, styles and arranges hair on the human neck and head, performs shampoos, massages and shaves. Also includes the use of caustic and cosmetic chemicals.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have four (4) years of high school or a G.E.D. equivalency, plus fifteen hundred (1500) hours in an accredited or licensed school of barbering.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application may be obtained by contacting the regulatory agency. Specific examination dates are established by the board. Usually given once each month. Practical demonstration and written exam, with a passing grade of 75% required. Examination fee is $100.00. Should you fail, contact the regulatory agency, address listed below.     GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Every applicant must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. Must be free of any venereal diseases and tuberculosis. Must be of good moral character and temperate habit. Must have nine (9) months of on-the-job training. All licenses must be renewed by July 1, with a 31 day grace period permitted. $30.00 annual renewal fee, with a $30.00 penalty charge, if renewed after the grace period. May restore a license up to five (5) years by paying back fees, plus penalty fee.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Reciprocity with other states varies. Contact the regulatory agency for additional information.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://barbering.ky.gov', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '70000003', '7',
     'Barber Instructor', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Must be able to teach all services and work to be performed by barbers.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must have a high school diploma or G.E.D. equivalency, two (2) years barbering experience PLUS fifteen hundred (1500) hours in an accredited or licensed school of barbering.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Application may be obtained by contacting the regulatory agency. Scheduled examination dates, established by the Board, normally provide for quarterly opportunities. Examination is written multiple choice type and a practical examination. Must average 80%. Examination fee is $100.00. Should you fail, contact the regulatory agency, address listed below.     SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    The initial license fee is $50.00. All licenses must be renewed by July 1, annually with a thirty-one (31) day grace period, at a fee of $30.00. A $30.00 penalty charge if renewed after the grace period. May restore a license up to five (5) years by paying back fees, plus penalty fee.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://barbering.ky.gov', '20240718'),
