    ('21', '01', '600000001', '60',
     'General Certified Radiation Operator (Diagnostic X-Ray)', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Performs all diagnostic radiographic procedures.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess a G.E.D. equivalency, PLUS satisfactorily complete twenty-four (24) months of study in medical, osteopathic, or chiropractic radiography approved by the regulatory agency.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Applications must be made at least sixty (60) days prior to examination with the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists, which is scheduled the third (3rd) Thursday in the months of March, July and October. Type examination; multiple choice. Must have a scaled score of 75%. Should you fail, contact the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists at (612) 687-0048.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no health or residency requirements. You must be honest, trustworthy and of good reputation. There are no work experience requirements. Initial certificate and registration fee is $60.00. Certificates must be renewed every two (2) years from date of issuance with a renewal fee of $35.00. For further details contact the regulatory agency. Contact the regulatory agency regarding reciprocity.    CONTINUING EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    You must obtain eighteen (18) clock hours of continuing education during each twenty-four (24) month period that the certificate is valid.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://chfs.ky.gov/agencies/dph/dphps/rhb/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '600000002', '60',
     'Limited Certified Radiation Operator (Diagnostic X-Ray)', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Performs radiographic procedures, other than those involving contrast media. *    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Must be a high school graduate or possess a G.E.D. equivalency PLUS satisfactorily complete a limited course of study in medical, osteopathic or chiropractic radiography approved by the regulatory agency through an Institutional or Independent Study Course.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Applications must be made to the regulatory agency. Examinations are scheduled three (3) times a year on the third (3rd) Thursday in March, July and October. Type examination: multiple choice. Must have a scaled score of seventy-five percent (75%). Examination fee is $30.00. Should you fail, contact the regulatory agency for retake procedures.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    You must be at least eighteen (18) years of age. There are no residency or health requirements. You must be honest, trustworthy and of a good reputation. There are no work experience requirements. Initial certificate and registration fee is $50.00. Certificate must be renewed every two (2) years from date of issuance with a renewal fee of $35.00. For further details contact the regulatory agency. Contact the regulatory agency regarding reciprocity.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    You must obtain twelve (12) clock hours of continuing education during each twenty-four (24) month period that the certificate is valid.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    * You cannot be employed with a facility which utilizes contrast media.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://chfs.ky.gov/agencies/dph/dphps/rhb/Pages/default.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '60000001', '6',
     'Attorney', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    Conducts criminal and civil lawsuits, draws up legal documents, advises clients as to legal rights, and practices other phases of law. May represent clients in court, or before quasi-judicial or administrative agencies of government. May specialize in a single area of law, such as patent law, corporate law, etc.    EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS    Graduation from an accredited School of Law.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Passing score of 75% on essay portion. Must receive scaled score of 132 to pass the Multistate Bar Examination. Multistate Professional Responsibility Examination must be taken and passed with a scaled score of 75% before sitting for the examination or being admitted without examination. May not represent a client in any manner prior to passing the examination.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    For information on licensure, renewal procedures, fees and reciprocity, contact Kentucky Board of Bar Examiners.     CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Contact the Kentucky Bar Association, West Main and Kentucky River, Frankfort, Kentucky 40601, (502) 564-3795.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://kyoba.org', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '610000001', '61',
     'Certified Water Well Driller', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    By the use of drill rigs or other drilling devices to construct water wells or monitoring wells.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Each driller is required to take and pass with a minimum score of 70%, three (3) different tests. One test is for general knowledge of drilling practices, geology and hydrology. The second tests the driller on knowledge of the type of drill rig that will be used. The final test is for monitoring well construction or water well construction.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must have worked for two (2) years under the supervision of a certified well driller or other suitable experience or education as determined by the regulatory agency. To retain certification must comply with the minimum standards for location, construction and modification of water wells.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must complete and submit documentation certifying completion of three (3) hours of training for certificate renewal. Must be renewed by July 1 of each successive year.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Non-renewal of the certificate for two (2) successive years may not again be renewed without retesting.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://eec.ky.gov/Environmental-Protection/Water/GW/Pages/GWDrillers.aspx', '20240718'),
    ('21', '01', '610000002', '61',
     'Certified Monitoring Well Driller', 'GENERAL JOB DESCRIPTION    By the use of drill rigs or other drilling devices to construct water wells or monitoring wells.    EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS    Each driller is required to take and pass with a minimum score of 70%, three (3) different tests. One test is for general knowledge of drilling practices, geology and hydrology. The second tests the driller on knowledge of the type of drill rig that will be used. The final test is for monitoring well construction or water well construction.    GENERAL INFORMATION for LICENSURE or CERTIFICATION    Must have worked for two (2) years under the supervision of a certified well driller or other suitable experience or education as determined by the regulatory agency. Monitoring well drillers also must comply with the construction standards of other federal and state regulatory programs. To retain certification must comply with the minimum standards for location, construction and modification of water wells.    CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS (after licensure or certification)    Must complete and submit documentation certifying completion of three (3) hours of training for certificate renewal. Must be renewed by July 1 of each successive year.    SPECIAL COMMENTS or CONDITIONS    Non-renewal of the certificate for two (2) successive years may not again be renewed without retesting.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://eec.ky.gov/Environmental-Protection/Water/GW/Pages/GWDrillers.aspx', '20240718'),
