    ('25', '01', '2597941000', '044',
     'HOISTING ENGINEER', 'The Department of Public Safety (Department) licenses and regulates the operation of hoisting equipment. The Department derives its authority to regulate hoisting operators from Massachusetts General Laws chapter 146, section 53. Additionally, the Department has promulgated regulations which are codified in section 6.00 of title 520 of the Code of Massachusetts Regulations.

Anyone who wishes to operate hoisting equipment (including derricks, cableways, machinery used for discharging cargoes, and temporary elevator cars used on excavation work or used for hoisting building material) must obtain a license from the Department. Hoisting operators must be 18 years of age, complete an application, and successfully pass an examination covering all working parts of the hoisting machinery, safe operating practices, hand signals, and inspection procedures in order to obtain a license',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.mass.gov/hoisting', '20180509'),
    ('25', '01', '2599990009', '057',
     'GAMING EMPLOYEE', 'Every employee at a Massachusetts gaming establishment must be licensed or registered by the Massachusetts Gaming Commission prior to commencing employment or performing services at a gaming establishment.  Licenses and registrations are required to ensure that those involved with the gaming industry in Massachusetts meet the statutory requirements of good character, honesty, and integrity.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://massgaming.com/licensing/', '20180509'),
    ('26', '01', '1203132021', '110',
     'Real Estate Appraiser, Certified Residential', 'A real estate appraiser must complete 200 hours of approved prelicensure appraiser education and 1,500 hours of experience. The fee for this license is $175.00.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72602_72731_72859---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '1300171011', '110',
     'Architects', 'To receive a Michigan Architects License, an applicant must have completed an approved internship program, attained a degree in architecture, and complete the Architect Registration Examination. Additionally, an online license application should be submitted along with the $65.00 application fee.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72860---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '1470008364', '250',
     'Certified Stenomask Reporter (C.S.M.R.)', 'To receive certification as a Certified Stenomask Reporter, an individual must have successfully completed an approved, accredited, or recognized course of study in court reporting, which can be found on the National Verbatim Reporters Association website. Additionally, the applicant must pass the certified verbatim reporter skills examination as well as the CSMR examination. Upon meeting these requirements, an applicant must submit an application for certification.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://courts.michigan.gov/Administration/SCAO/OfficesPrograms/CRR/Pages/default.aspx', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2380050391', '130',
     'Stationary Engineer', 'To receive a Stationary Engineer license, an applicant must submit a completed Stationary Engineer Examination application, required documents, and license fee ($80.00). Additionally, the Stationary Engineer Examination must be completed and passed.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_10575_77372-42822--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2912292021', '110',
     'Dental Hygienist, Registered (R.D.H.)', 'To receive a Registered Dental Hygienist License, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental assisting program, pass the National Board Dental Hygiene Examination and pass the ADEX Regional Dental Hygiene Examination. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a Dental Hygienist License Application along with the appropriate fee ($47.70).',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'A', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4203211011', '320',
     'Clinical Supervisor, Certified (Addictions) (C.C.S.)', 'To receive the Certified Clinical Supervisor certification, an applicant must currently hold the CADC, CAADC, CCJP, CCDP, or CCDP-D to be able to apply. 10,000 hours of clinical counseling experience (which includes 4,000 hours of supervisor experience) is required, as is 30 contact hours in clinical supervision with a minimum of four hours of education in Counselor Development, Professional & Ethical Standards, Program Development & Quality Assurance, and Performance Evaluation and Administration.  Additionally, 200 hours of direct supervision specific to the IC&RC/CCS domains is required, and an applicant must take and pass the IC&RC/CCS, Clinical Supervisor examination. Once these qualifications have been met, an applicant must submit an application to the Michigan Certification Board for Addiction Professionals along with a $150.00 application fee.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/ccs', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4210211023', '320',
     'Criminal Justice Professional, Certified (Addictions) (C.C.J.P.)', 'Substance use disorder counselors are required to be certified through the Michigan Certification Board for Addiction Professionals (MCBAP) in addition to any license that may be held.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://search.mcbap.com/certifications/ccjp-certified-criminal-justice-professional/', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4301291060', '110',
     'Medical Doctor, Clinical Academic (M.D.)', 'A clinical academic medical doctor must be a graduate of an approved medical school and be appointed to a teaching or research position in Michigan. A renewal fee of $31.80 must be paid annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
