    ('25', '01', '2581005000', '043',
     'CONSTRUCTION SUPERVISOR', 'For one and two-family houses of any size:  A person with a MA construction supervisor license (CSL) is required to provide construction oversight, with few exceptions.  For most work on existing one-to-four family owner-occupied dwellings, a contractor must also register with the Office of Consumer Affairs home improvement program.

For buildings less than 35,000 cu ft: A person with a MA construction supervisor license (CSL) is required to provide construction oversight including for manufactured buildings.

For other buildings greater than 35,000 cu ft: Construction of such larger buildings and structures, commercial and residential, must be done under the control of a registered engineer or architect or  their designee and no contractor license is necessary per the building code. See Section 107.6 entitled Construction Control in the MA building code. A few municipalities may have other contractor licensing requirements.   

Out of state contractors: Licensing is only required as described above.  Out of state contractor licenses are not recognized in MA.  A few larger municipalities have additional licensing requirements - contact the local building official.  The building code applies uniformly to all municipalities in MA and is enforced by the local officials with few exceptions.',
