     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-61343_35414_60647_35453---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '1600291121', '110',
     'Audiologist', 'To obtain an Audiology License, an applicant must hold the equivalent of a U.S. master''s or doctoral degree in audiology. Those without a doctor of audiology degree must complete at least 9 months (1,260 hours) of supervised clinical experience in audiology.  Additionally, an applicant must submit a license application with fee ($286.40), undergo a fingerprint/criminal background check, and pass the PRAXIS exam. Licenses must be renewed every 2 years.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_31491---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '1700395011', '110',
     'Barber', 'To receive a Barber''s License, an applicant must beat at least 17 years old, have completed the equivalent of a 10th grade education, complete at least 1,800 hours at a licensed barber college, and pass the theory and practical examination administered by PSI Services, LLC. The license application fee is $20.00, with an annual renewal fee of $30.00.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72861---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '1702251194', '110',
     'Barber Instructor', 'To receive a Barber Instructor License, an applicant must first have attained the equivalent of a high school diploma. Beyond high school, an applicant must have attended a licensed barber college with 1 year of instruction completed, OR have completed 60 semester hours in an approved course with 6 months of instruction in barbering. Finally, a theory exam administered by PSI Services, LLC must be passed, and a license application with $20.00 fee submitted to the Department of Licensing and Regulatory affairs. The annual renewal fee is $40.00.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72861---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '1703395011', '110',
     'Barber Student', 'To receive a Barber Student License, an applicant must have an education equivalent to completing the 10th grade. They must also submit a license application along with the appropriate licensing fee ($80.00).',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72861---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '1872355127', '110',
     'Chiropractic - Educational Limited', 'To apply for a Michigan Chiropractic Educational Limited License, an individual must complete at least two years, four semesters, or six quarter terms in a chiropractic school that has been accredited by the Council on Chiropractic Education. An applicant must also have arranged for supervision from a Michigan-licensed Chiropractor for the 6-months duration of a the chiropractic education. Once this has been completed, a license application along with the appropriate application fee ($53.00) must be submitted, and a fingerprint report and background check completed.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27531---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2100119021', '130',
     'Residential Builder', 'A residential builder must have 60 hours of approved prelicensure education prior to taking the licensure exam. The fee for this license is $195.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372_88024---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2102119021', '130',
     'Residential Maintenance and Alteration Contractor', 'A maintenance and alteration contractor must have 60 hours of approved prelicensure education prior to taking the licensure exam. The fee for this license is $195.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372_88024---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2104131051', '130',
     'Residential Builder Salesperson', 'A residential builder salesperson must have 60 hours of approved prelicensure education prior to taking the licensure exam. The fee for this license is $195.00',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372_88024---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2205627927', '110',
     'Barber Student Instructor', 'To receive a Barber Student Instructor license, an applicant must have received a high school diploma or equivalent, and must be a licensed barber with at least 2 years of experience.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72602_72731_72861_73050-141871--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2300291011', '110',
     'Chiropractic', 'To apply for a Michigan Chiropractic License, an individual must first graduate from a chiropractic educational program that has been accredited by the Council on Chiropractic Education. Once this has been completed, Parts 1, 2, 3, and 4 of the National Board of Chiropractic Examiners examination must be passed. Finally, a licensure application along with the appropriate fee ($53 to $127.25) should be submitted to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs, and a fingerprint report and background check completed.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27531---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2370780615', '320',
     'Certified Prevention Specialist?(C.P.S.)', 'A certified prevention specialist must have 2,000 hours of experience, 120 hours of education, 120  hours of supervision and pass the IC&RC/PS, Prevention Specialist examination. The fee for this license is $65.00.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/cps-certified-prevention-specialist', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2401431011', '110',
     'Collection Agency Manager', 'An applicant for a Collection Agency Manager License must be at least 18 years old, have a high school diploma or equivalent level of education, and complete at least 6 months of full-time experience in account collection. Upon completing these requirements , the required exam administered by PSI Services, LLC must be passed (exam fee is $56.00). Finally, an application along with appropriate fee should be submitted to the Michigan Bureau of Licensing and Regulatory affairs. The application fee is $85.00 for non-owner managers OR no fee for owner managers.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72863---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2560983034', '110',
     'Dental Hygienist, Educational Limited (R.D.H.)', 'To receive a RDH Educational Limited License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental hygiene program,  must be enrolled in a postgraduate educational program, and take and pass a fingerprint report and criminal background check. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a license application along with the appropriate fee ($31.80).',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'A', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2560983035', '110',
     'Dental Hygienist, Clinical/Nonclinical (R.D.H.)', 'To receive a RDH Clinical/Nonclinical Limited License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental hygiene program,  must be enrolled in a postgraduate educational program, and take and pass a fingerprint report and criminal background check. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a license application along with the appropriate fee ($31.80).',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'A', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2597885846', '110',
     'Dental Educational Limited', 'To receive a Dental Educational Limited License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental school, be enrolled in a postgraduate educational program, and take and pass a fingerprint report and criminal background check. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a license application along with the appropriate fee ($53.00).',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2633674001', '320',
     'Certified Prevention Consultant?(C.P.C.)', 'A certified prevention consultant must have 8,000 hours of experience, 240 hours of education, 240 hours of supervision and pass the IC&RC/PS, Prevention Specialist examination. The fee for this license is $65.00.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/cpc-r-certified-prevention-consultant', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2700395012', '110',
     'Cosmetologist', 'To receive a Cosmetology License in Michigan, an applicant must be at least 17 years old, have attained the educational equivalent of 9th grade, and have completed at least 1,500 of cosmetology training OR performed a 2-year cosmetology apprenticeship. Upon meeting these requirements, they must pass the required exam administered by PSI Services and submit a license application along with the accompanying application fee.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2701251194', '110',
     'Cosmetology Instructor', 'To receive a Cosmetology Instructor License in Michigan, an applicant must  have attained a high school diploma or its equivalent, have a current Michigan cosmetology license, and have at least 3 years of practical experience in natural hair cultivation, hair service, skin care services, and manicuring services (which includes 1 year in a cosmetology establishment). Finally, the applicant must have at least 500 hours of instructor training, and must pass the theory and practical examination administered by PSI Services. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant can then submit an Instructor License application along with the appropriate fee.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2702251194', '110',
     'Cosmetology, Limited Instructor', 'To receive a Cosmetology Limited Instructor''s License in Michigan, an applicant must  have attained a high school diploma or its equivalent, have a current Michigan cosmetology  license, and have completed at least 500 hours of instructor training. Finally the theory and practical examination administered by PSI Services must be passed. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant can then submit an Instructor License application along with the appropriate fee ($63.00).',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2707395012', '110',
     'Electrologist', 'To receive an Electrologist License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must be at least 18 years old, have attained the educational equivalent of 9th grade, and have completed at least 400 hours of cosmetology training OR performed a 6-month cosmetology apprenticeship. Upon meeting these requirements, they must pass the required theory and practical exam administered by PSI Services and submit a license application along with the accompanying application fee.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2710395094', '110',
     'Esthetician', 'To receive an Esthetician license in Michigan, an applicant must be at least 17 years old, have attained the educational equivalent of 9th grade, and have completed at least 400 hours of training in a licensed cosmetology school OR performed a 6-month cosmetology apprenticeship. Upon meeting these requirements, they must pass the required theory and practical exam administered by PSI Services and submit a license application along with the appropriate application fee.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2712395092', '110',
     'Manicurist', 'A manicurist must complete not less than 400 hours of training in a licensed school of cosmetology or perform a 6-month apprenticeship program within a licensed cosmetology establishment. A manicurist must pass the required theory and practical examination administered by PSI Services, LLC (PSI).  Licenses expire biennially, the renewal fee is $48.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2714395012', '110',
     'Natural Hair Culturist', 'A manicurist must complete not less than 400 hours of training in a licensed school of cosmetology or perform a 6-month apprenticeship program within a licensed cosmetology establishment. A manicurist must pass the required theory and practical examination administered by PSI Services, LLC (PSI). Licenses expire biennially, the renewal fee is $48.00.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2716395012', '110',
     'Cosmetologist, Apprentice', 'To receive a Cosmetology Apprentice License, an applicant must submit a registration application the Michigan Bureau of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs and remit the $25.00 application fee.',
     '4', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2717395012', '110',
     'Electrologist, Apprentice', 'To receive an Electrologist Apprentice License, an applicant must submit a registration application the Michigan Bureau of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs and remit the $25.00 application fee.',
     '4', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2718395094', '110',
     'Esthetician, Apprentice', 'To receive an Esthetician Apprentice License, an applicant must submit a registration application the Michigan Bureau of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs and remit the $25.00 application fee.',
     '4', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2719395092', '110',
     'Manicurist, Apprentice', 'An apprentice must be under the supervision of a license holder and pay the registration of $25.00.',
     '4', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2720395012', '110',
     'Natural Hair Culturist, Apprentice', 'An apprentice must be under the supervision of a license holder and pay the registration of $25.00.',
     '4', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2721251194', '110',
     'Manicurist Instructor', 'A manicurist instructor must hold a current Michigan license, have at least 3 years of practical experience, and completed 300 hours of instructor training. Licenses expire biennially, the renewal fee is $48.00.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2722251194', '110',
     'Esthetician Instructor', 'To receive an Esthetician Instructor License in Michigan, an applicant must have attained a high school diploma or its equivalent, have a current Michigan cosmetology license, and have at least 3 years of practical experience in natural hair cultivation, hair service, skin care services, and manicuring services (which includes 1 year in a cosmetology establishment). Finally, the applicant must have at least 500 hours of instructor training, and must pass the theory and practical examination administered by PSI Services. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant can then submit an Instructor License application along with the appropriate fee ($63.50).',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2723251194', '110',
     'Natural Hair Culturist Instructor', 'A natural hair culturist instructor must hold a current Michigan license, have at least 3 years of practical experience, and completed 300 hours of instructor training. Licenses expire biennially, the renewal fee is $48.00.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2725251194', '110',
     'Electrologist Instructor', 'To receive an Electrology Instructor License in Michigan, an applicant must  have attained a high school diploma or its equivalent, have a current Michigan electrologist license, and have at least 3 years of practical experience in electrology (which includes 1 year in a cosmetology establishment holding a limited license for the practice of electrologist). Finally, the applicant must have at least 300 hours of instructor training, and must pass the theory and practical examination administered by PSI Services. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant can then submit an Instructor License application along with the appropriate fee ($63.00).',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2899345628', '150',
     'Prepaid Funeral Contract Providers', 'A prepaid funeral contract provider must submit a copy of the escrow agreement, an application, and the $120.00 fee to the Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_61343_35414_60647_35468---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2900291021', '110',
     'Dentist (D.D.S.)', 'To receive a Dentist License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental school, pass Parts 1 and 2 of the National Board Dental Examinations,  and pass the ADEX Dental Examination  (including the periodontal section). After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a Dentist License Application along with the appropriate fee ($127.25).',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2918319091', '110',
     'Dental Assistant, Registered (R.D.A.)', 'To receive a Registered Dental Assistant License, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental assisting program, have competency in applying and removing a dental dam, and pass the Michigan Clinical and Written RDA Examination. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a Registered Dental Assistant Application along with the appropriate fee ($106.05).',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'A', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2920291024', '110',
     'Prosthodontist', 'An applicant must graduate from a dental school that is in compliance with the standards of the Board, pass all parts of the national board examination and pass the combined regional examination in dentistry. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2921291029', '110',
     'Endodontist', 'To receive an Endodontics License from the State of Michigan, an applicant must hold a current Michigan Dentist license, graduate from a CODA/ADA accredited dental specialty program, and pass the appropriate American Board written examination OR hold Diplomate status. Once these requirements have been met, an applicant must submit the Dental Specialty license application along with the appropriate fee ($47.70).',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2922291022', '110',
     'Oral Maxillofacial Surgeon', 'An applicant must graduate from a dental school that is in compliance with the standards of the Board, pass all parts of the national board examination and pass the combined regional examination in dentistry. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2923291023', '110',
     'Orthodontist', 'An applicant must graduate from a dental school that is in compliance with the standards of the Board, pass all parts of the national board examination and pass the combined regional examination in dentistry. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2924291029', '110',
     'Pediatric Dentist', 'An applicant must graduate from a dental school that is in compliance with the standards of the Board, pass all parts of the national board examination and pass the combined regional examination in dentistry. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2925291029', '110',
     'Periodontist', 'An applicant must graduate from a dental school that is in compliance with the standards of the Board, pass all parts of the national board examination and pass the combined regional examination in dentistry. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2926291029', '110',
     'Pathologist, Oral', 'An applicant must graduate from a dental school that is in compliance with the standards of the Board, pass all parts of the national board examination and pass the combined regional examination in dentistry. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2955556234', '810',
     'Motor Fuels Service Person', 'To be registered as a Motor Fuels serviceperson, an applicant must submit an Application for Serviceperson registration along with a $100 fee. Additionally, they must have completed and passed the Michigan Jurisdictional Exam, NIST Handbook 44 Exam, and Vehicle and Axle-Load Scales exam.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdard/0,4610,7-125-1569_19192_20787---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '2986708890', '110',
     'Pharmacy Technician', 'To receive a Pharmacy Technician license in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have obtained a high school diploma or equivalent and pass the certified pharmacy technician exam. Additionally, an applicant must submit the Pharmacy Technician License application along with the $55.55 licensing fee to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs. Finally, a fingerprint report and criminal background check must be completed.',
     '0', '2', '0', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27548---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3000299091', '110',
     'Athletic Trainer', 'To receive a Michigan Athletic Trainer License, an applicant must undergo a fingerprint and criminal background check and complete training to identify victims of human trafficking. Additionally, an applicant must complete a minimum of 1 hour of first aid training with the 3 years prior to the application date, attain certification in emergency cardiac care, complete the Board of Certification, Inc. examination, and submit a license application with the appropriate fee remitted.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_45355---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3068647880', '110',
     'Esthetician Limited Instructor', 'To receive an Esthetician Limited Instructor License in Michigan, an applicant must first have attained a high school diploma or its equivalent, have completed at least 300 hours of instructor training and have passed the theory and practical exam administered by PSI Services. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant can then submit an Instructor License application along with the appropriate fee ($63.00).',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3100319011', '110',
     'Massage Therapist', 'Massage therapy licensees must graduate from an approved massage therapy supervised curriculum and pass a national certification exam. The license fee is $100.75.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_53660---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3201533011', '310',
     'Medical First Responder', 'Medical first responders must take an initial education course, register nationally, and pass the cognitive exam. There is no fee for this license.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdhhs/0,5885,7-339-73970_5093_28508-47472--,00.html#Personnel_Licensing', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3211292041', '310',
     'Emergency Medical Technician (E.M.T.)', 'To receive an EMT license in the State of Michigan, an individual must be at least 18 years old, complete a Michigan EMT course within the last 2 years, and be nationally registered. Once these requirements have been met, an applicant must submit a license application online and remit the appropriate fees. Additionally, upon receiving a license, a recipient must accrue Michigan approved continuing education credits OR complete a Michigan approved refresher course.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdhhs/0,5885,7-339-73970_5093_28508-47472--,00.html#Personnel_Licensing', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3213253099', '310',
     'Emergency Medical Technician, Instructor/Coordinator (E.M.T.)', 'To receive an EMT Instructor/Coordinator license in the State of Michigan, an individual must have completed a Michigan Instructor-Coordinator course within the prior two years, have three years of field experience providing direct patient care with a licensed Life Support Agency, and must be currently licensed as an EMT in Michigan at or above the level being applied for. Finally, an applicant must take the Instructor Coordinator exam via the Michigan Department of Health and Human Services. Once these requirements have been met, an applicant must submit a license application online and remit the appropriate fees.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdhhs/0,5885,7-339-73970_5093_28508-47472--,00.html#IC_Education', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3214292041', '310',
     'Emergency Medical Technician, Specialist (E.M.T.)', 'To receive a Specialist license in the State of Michigan, an individual must be at least 18 years old, complete a Michigan  course within the last 2 years, and be nationally registered. Once these requirements have been met, an applicant must submit a license application online and remit the appropriate fees. Additionally, upon receiving a license, a recipient must accrue Michigan approved continuing education credits OR complete a Michigan approved refresher course.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdhhs/0,5885,7-339-73970_5093_28508-47472--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3221292041', '310',
     'Emergency Medical Technician, Paramedic (E.M.T)', 'To receive a Paramedic license in the State of Michigan, an individual must be at least 18 years old, complete a Michigan  course within the last 2 years, and be nationally registered. Once these requirements have been met, an applicant must submit a license application online and remit the appropriate fees. Additionally, upon receiving a license, a recipient must accrue Michigan approved continuing education credits OR complete a Michigan approved refresher course.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdhhs/0,5885,7-339-73970_5093_28508-47472--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3500419099', '110',
     'Hearing Aid Trainee', 'To receive a Hearing Aid Trainee License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must submit a license application along with the $50.00 application fee.',
     '4', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72868---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3501414011', '110',
     'Hearing Aid Dealer', 'To receive a Michigan Hearing Aid Dealer License, an applicant must be at least 18 years old, have completed at least two years of experience as a hearing aid salesperson under the direct supervision of a licensed hearing aid dealer, and must pass the Hearing Aid Dealer examination administered by PSI Services. The cost of the exam is $76.00. Upon meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit the Hearing Aid Dealer application along $180.00 application fee.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72868---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3502289934', '320',
     'Certified Clinical Supervisor?(C.C.S.)', 'A certified clinical supervisor must have 10,000 hours of clinical counseling, 30 contact hours in clinical supervision, 200 hours of direct supervision specific to the IC&RC/CCS Performance Domains, and pass the IC&RC/CCS, Clinical Supervisor examination. The fee for this license is $150.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/ccs', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3502419099', '110',
     'Hearing Aid Salesperson', 'For an applicant to receive the Hearing Aid Salesperson License in the State of Michigan, they must be at least 18 years old, have completed at least six months as a trainee, and must pass the Hearing Aid Salesperson Examination  ($72.00). Upon completion of these requirements, the applicant must then submit a license application along with the $120.00 application fee.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72868---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3600492098', '150',
     'Security Alarm Contractor', 'A security alarm system contractor must post a $25,000 surety bond with the Department or furnish an insurance policy in the amount of $25,000 for property damages, $100,000 for injury or death of one person, and $200,000 for injuries to or deaths of more than one person. In addition, a candidate must have the correct combination of work experience or take the exam. The fee for this license is $500.00.',
     '2', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-61343_35414_60647_35476---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3899784351', '110',
     'Manicurist Limited Instructor', 'To receive a Manicurist Limited Instructor License in Michigan, an applicant must first have attained a high school diploma or its equivalent, have completed at least 300 hours of instructor training and have passed the theory and practical exam administered by PSI Services. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant can then submit an Instructor License application along with the appropriate fee ($63.00).',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '3901171012', '110',
     'Landscape Architect, Licensed', 'For an applicant to receive a Landscape Architect License from the State of Michigan, they must have completed an accredited bachelor''s or master''s program and completed three years of professional experience in the practice of landscape architecture (two years if a master''s degree is possessed). Additionally, an applicant must establish a Council of Landscape Architects Registration Boards Council Record ($150.00 cost) and complete the Landscape Architecture Registration Examination ($1,780 cost for four-part exam). Upon completing these requirements, an applicant must then submit a license application along with the $260 license fee.',
     '0', '2', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72869---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4000171022', '110',
     'Professional Surveyor', 'Surveyors must obtain the required education credits and pass the national exam. In addition, surveyors must complete four years of experience if bachelor?s degree is possessed or three years of experience if a graduate degree in surveying is held. The fee for this license is $85.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72872---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4100211013', '110',
     'Marriage & Family Therapist', 'A marriage and family therapist needs to be a graduate from an accredited educational program. A licensee then needs to complete at least 1,000 hours direct client contact that supervised by a licensed MFT. After passing the National Marital and Family Therapy Examination, a licensee must pay the $85.85 fee.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27538---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4103483321', '110',
     'Dental Clinical/Nonclinical Limited', 'To receive a Dental Clinical/Nonclinical Limited License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental school,  must be appointed to a clinical or nonclinical academic faculty position, and take and pass a fingerprint report and criminal background check. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a license application along with the appropriate fee ($53.00).',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4202211011', '320',
     'Prevention Specialist, Certified (C.P.S.)', 'A prevention specialist must obtain  2,000 hours, full- or part-time providing Substance Use Disorder Prevention services at a program licensed by the State of Michigan as a substance use disorder services provider. In addition, 120 hours of education and supervision must be obtained. Finally, a prevention specialist must pass an examination. The fee for this license is S150.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/cps-certified-prevention-specialist', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4303291060', '110',
     'Medical Doctor, Educational Limited (M.D.)', 'A medical doctor intern must be a graduate from an approved medical school and appointed to a postgraduate training program in Michigan. The renewal fee for this license $31.80 annually.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27541---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4700292061', '110',
     'Nurse, Licensed Practical (L.P.N.)', 'Nurses need to graduate from an approved education program and pass the NCLEX examination. To specialize, a nurse must hold an additional certification. The fee for renewing a nursing license is $123.60.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27542---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4710291111', '110',
     'Nurse, Registered (R.N.)', 'Nurses need to graduate from an approved education program and pass the NCLEX examination. To specialize, a nurse must hold an additional certification. The fee for renewing a nursing license is $123.60.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27542---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4720291111', '110',
     'Nurse Anesthetist', 'Nurses need to graduate from an approved education program and pass the NCLEX examination. To specialize, a nurse must hold an additional certification. The fee for renewing a nursing license is $123.60.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27542---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4721291111', '110',
     'Nurse Midwife', 'Nurses need to graduate from an approved education program and pass the NCLEX examination. To specialize, a nurse must hold an additional certification. The fee for renewing a nursing license is $123.60.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27542---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5365420611', '110',
     'Natural Hair Culturist Limited Instructor', 'To receive a Natural Hair Culturist Limited Instructor License in Michigan, an applicant must first have attained a high school diploma or its equivalent, have completed at least 300 hours of instructor training and have passed the theory and practical exam administered by PSI Services. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant can then submit an Instructor License application along with the appropriate fee ($63.00).',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4305291060', '110',
     'Medical Doctor (M.D.)', 'A medical doctor must be a graduate from an approved medical school, complete two years of accredited postgraduate training and pass the U.S. Medical Licensure Examination. The fee for this license is $302.25 and a license must be renewed on a three year cycle.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27541---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4400291126', '110',
     'Respiratory Therapist', 'Respiratory Therapists must obtain a degree from an accredited program and pass the national examination. The fee for this license is $100.75.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_29413---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4500119061', '150',
     'Funeral Director (Mortuary Science) Resident Trainee', 'A mortuary science trainee must be of good moral character, possess a high school diploma or its equivalent.  The fee due at the time of the application is $45.00.',
     '4', '0', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-61343_35414_60647_79102---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4501119061', '150',
     'Funeral Director (Mortuary Science)', 'To receive a Mortuary Science (Funeral Director) License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have graduated from a three-year course in mortuary science at an accredited school. This includes completing at least 60 semester/90 quarter hours of non-remedial college courses (with at least a 2.00 grade point average), as well as completing at least one year of instruction at an accredited mortuary science program (with at least a 2.00 grade point average). Additionally, an applicant must serve as a resident trainee for at least one year under the supervision of a mortuary science license holder. Finally, an applicant must pass the National Arts and National Science examination (exam fee is $250 per section), pass the Michigan Mortuary Science examination ($56), and submit a license application along with the $100 application fee.',
     '0', '0', '2', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-61343_35414_60647_79102---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4600311012', '160',
     'Nurse Aide, Certified (C.N.A.)', 'To become a CNA, new candidates must first complete a Michigan approved training course. Following successful completion of a training course, a candidate must apply to Prometric for testing and eligibility. The fee for this license is $115.00, renewed biennially.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-63294_75200---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4662179393', '110',
     'Dental Assistant, Clinical/Nonclinical Limited (R.D.A.)', 'To receive an RDA Clinical/Nonclinical Limited License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental assisting program,  must be enrolled in a postgraduate educational program, and take and pass a fingerprint report and criminal background check. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a license application along with the appropriate fee ($21.20).',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'A', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4662179399', '110',
     'Dental Assistant, Educational Limited (R.D.A.)', 'To receive an RDA Educational Limited License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must graduate from a CODA/ADA-accredited dental assisting program,  must be enrolled in a postgraduate educational program, and take and pass a fingerprint report and criminal background check. After meeting these requirements, the applicant must submit a license application along with the appropriate fee ($21.20).',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'A', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27533---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4722291111', '110',
     'Nurse Practitioner', 'Nurses need to graduate from an approved education program and pass the NCLEX examination. To specialize, a nurse must hold an additional certification. The fee for renewing a nursing license is $123.60.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27542---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4800119111', '160',
     'Nursing Home Administrator', 'Nursing home administrators must take an approved course of instructional training in Nursing Home Administration and pass the NHA and NSBL examinations. The fee for this license is $80.50, biennially.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27543---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4900291041', '110',
     'Optometrist', 'An optometrist needs to be a graduate of an accredited program. In addition, optometrists need to pass the jurisprudence exam and parts I, II, and III of the National Board of Examiners in Optometry (NBEO) examination as well as the Treatment and Management of Ocular Disease (TMOD) examination embedded in part II. The fee for this license is $127.25, biennially.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27546-42769--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4949264588', '230',
     'Vehicle Dealer Broker', 'To receive a Vehicle Dealer-Broker license, an applicant must submit and complete a License Application, have Michigan no-fault insurance, have written verification of zoning and municipal approval, an established place of business, a surety bond, Michigan no-fault fleet insurance, and pay the appropriate license fee ($75-$160).',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/sos/0,4670,7-127-49534_50300_50308-29797--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '4998918581', '250',
     'Certified Electronic Recorder (C.E.R.)', 'To receive certification as a Certified Electronic Recorder, an individual must have successfully completed an approved course of study (either the Michigan Electronic Court Reporters Association CER Workshop, OR Lansing Community College''s CER course). Additionally, they must pass the CER certification examination. Upon meeting these qualifications, an applicant must submit an application for certification.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://courts.michigan.gov/Administration/SCAO/OfficesPrograms/CRR/Pages/default.aspx', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5012654160', '410',
     'Hospital Heliport/Helistop Manager', 'To receive a Helistop Manager License, an applicant must the Hospital Heliport/Helistop and Manager License Application and submit to the Michigan Department of Transportation.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/aero/MDOT_form_4088_280879_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5100291060', '110',
     'Osteopathic Physician (D.O.)', 'An osteopathic physician must be a graduate of an approved program, pass the national examination, and complete 1 year of post graduate training. The fee for this license is $159.05.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27547---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5103291060', '110',
     'Osteopathic Physician, Educational Limited (D.O.)', 'An osteopathic physician intern must be a graduate of an approved program and complete a certification of appointment. The fee for this license is $180.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72603_27529_27547---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5200291122', '110',
     'Occupational Therapist', 'Occupational therapists must be graduates from an accredited program and pass both the certification examination and the jurisprudence examination. The fee for this license is $100.75.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27545---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5210312011', '110',
     'Occupational Therapy Assistant', 'Occupational therapists assistants must be graduates from an accredited program and pass both the certification examination and the jurisprudence examination. The fee for this license is $100.75.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27545---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5250866531', '160',
     'EBL Investigator', 'A EBL Investigator must first become a lead inspector and risk assessor. There is no fee for this license.',
     '0', '1', '9', '0', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lead/0,5417,7-310-84218---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5302291051', '110',
     'Pharmacist', 'Pharmacists must graduate from an accredited program,  complete at least 1,600 hours internship experience, and pass the NAPLEX and jurisprudence examinations. The fee for this license is $60.60.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27548---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5304291051', '110',
     'Pharmacist, Educational Limited', 'Pharmacist interns must provide proof of enrollment in an accredited pharmacy program. The fee for this license is $40.40.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27548---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5371528702', '320',
     'Certified Alcohol and Drug Counselor?(C.A.A.D.C.)', 'To receive a Certified Alcohol and Drug Counselor certification, an applicant must first acquire up to 2,000 hours of full or part-time clinical counseling experience (post-Masters degree) working with substance use disorder or co-occurring disorder clients. A Master''s Degree or higher (or equivalent license) in psychology, social work, counseling, psychiatric nursing, addiction science, or marriage and family therapy with a clinical application is required. This includes completion of 186 education contact hours, with 180 hours specific to substance use disorders, and 6 hours face-to-face. Furthermore, up to 100 hours of direct supervision (post-Masters degree) specific to the IC&RC/AADC Performance Domains (minimum of 10 hours per Domain) is required. Once these qualifications have been met, the IC&RC/AADC  exam must be taken and passed and a licensing application submitted to the Michigan Certification Board for Addiction Professionals. The accompanying application fee is $150.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/caadc', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5400291127', '110',
     'Speech - Language Pathologist', 'Speech-Language Pathologists must be a graduate of an accredited university and pass an exam. The fee for this license is $95.00.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_53664---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5500291123', '110',
     'Physical Therapist', 'Physical therapists need to be a graduate of an accredited program and pass the national exam. The fee for this license is $116.65.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27549---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5508312021', '110',
     'Physical Therapist Assistant', 'Physical therapists assistants need to be a graduate of an accredited program and pass the national exam. The fee for this license is $116.65.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27549---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5584596207', '130',
     'Fire Protection System Plan Reviewer', 'A Fire Protection System Plan Reviewer must execute the statement of attestation of understanding of the building code and provide copies of NFPA or ICC Fire Inspector I and Plan Examiner certifications. The fee for registration is $25.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/lara/dleg_bcc_inspector_registration_app_530888_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5600291071', '110',
     'Physician''s Assistant', 'A physician''s assistant is licensed by the Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs to examine, diagnose, and treat patients under  a licensed physician.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27550---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5700291199', '110',
     'Acupuncturist', 'To receive an Acupuncture License, an applicant must be certified by the National Certification Commission for Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine. Additionally, an examination application along with a $275.75 fee should be submitted, and a fingerprint report and criminal background check completed.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_45354---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5800291066', '110',
     'Psychiatrist', 'A psychiatrist must be licensed as a M.D. or D.O. in Michigan. The fee for this license is in accordance with the type of license, $302.25 or $159.05.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27541---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5900291081', '110',
     'Podiatrist', 'A Podiatrist must be a graduate of an approved program. In addition, they must pass  parts I, II, and III of the examination developed and scored by the National Board of Podiatric Medical Examiners and the jurisprudence exam. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27551---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '5903291081', '110',
     'Podiatrist, Educational Limited', 'An intern in postgraduate podiatric study with a hospital, clinic, or preceptorship program must obtain a limited license. The fee for this license is $143.15.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27551---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6000194092', '150',
     'Forensic Polygraph Examiner Intern', 'To become an intern, an applicant is required to have satisfied the educational requirement for a polygraph examiner''s license, submit proof of enrollment in an approved polygraph school and submit an application with the required fee ($25.00).',
     '4', '0', '1', '9', '0',
     '1', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_61343_35414_60647_35467---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6001194092', '150',
     'Forensic Polygraph Examiner, Public', 'A polygraph examiner must be a graduate of an accredited bachelor''s program with not less than 15 semester hours of academic credit in the social or behavioral sciences. Additionally, applicant for a polygraph examiners license is required to have completed an internship training program consisting of an academic component and a practical training component. The applicant will need to submit an application with the required fee ($25.00).',
     '0', '0', '1', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_61343_35414_60647_35467---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6001294092', '150',
     'Forensic Polygraph Examiner, Private', 'A polygraph examiner must be a graduate of an accredited bachelor''s program with not less than 15 semester hours of academic credit in the social or behavioral sciences. Additionally, applicant for a polygraph examiners license is required to have completed an internship training program consisting of an academic component and a practical training component. The applicant will need to submit an application with the required fee ($100.00).',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_61343_35414_60647_35467---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6102131071', '110',
     'Personnel Agent', 'To receive a Employment Agent License, an applicant must pass the Personnel Agent examination administered through PSI Services. The exam fee is $56.00. Additionally, an applicant must submit the Consulting Agent License application and remit the $70.00 application fee.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72870-365206--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6200172199', '110',
     'Engineer, Licensed Professional', 'To receive a Professional Engineers License from the State of Michigan, an applicant must attain a bachelor''s or master''s degree from a an accredited school and program and possess four years or more of acceptable engineering work experience AFTER having received a bachelor''s degree. Additionally, an applicant must pass the Fundamentals of Engineering NCEES examination ($225 cost) as well as the Principles of Engineering NCEES examination ($350). Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant must submit an online license application along with the $75.00  application fee.',
     '0', '2', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72865---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6300193031', '110',
     'Psychologist', 'A psychologist must graduate from an approved doctoral program and complete an internship at least 2,000 hours as part of the doctoral degree program. In addition, a candidate must complete at least 2,000 hours of supervised post-degree psychology experience and pass the examination. The fee for this license is $159.05.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27552---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6310193031', '110',
     'Psychologist, Masters Degree Limited', 'To obtain a master''s limited license in psychology, a candidate must complete at least 2,000 hours of supervised post-degree psychology experience and a 500 hour practicum. In addition, the candidate must pass an examination. The fee for this license is $127.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27552---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6319287916', '320',
     'Certified Peer Recovery Mentor (C.P.R.M.)', 'To receive a Certified Peer Recovery Mentor certification, an applicant must first acquire up to 500 hours of full or part-time alcohol or drug addiction peer recovery support services. Additionally, they must have a high school diploma or equivalency and up to 46 education hours of education in Peer Recovery support within the areas defined by the IC&RC Peer Recovery Performance domains. Furthermore, an applicant must have 25 hours or more of direct supervision performing peer recovery mentor functions, with at least 5 hours in each domain. Finally, once these qualifications have been met, the IC&RC/PR exam must be taken and passed and a licensing application submitted to the Michigan Certification Board for Addiction Professionals. The accompanying application fee is $65.00.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/cprm-m-certified-peer-recovery-mentor-michigan', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6400211019', '110',
     'Counselor, Licensed Professional', 'To receive a Professional Counselor License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have received a master''s or doctoral degree in counseling and have completed at least 48 semester hours or 72 quarter hours in counseling topics. Additionally, those with a master''s degree are required to accrue at least 3,000 hours of post-degree counseling experience within a 2-year period, with 100 hours gained in the direct presence of a supervisor. Less is required for those studying counseling beyond a master''s degree. Finally, after passing the National Counselor Examination, an individual may submit a license application along with the appropriate application fee ($84.80 to $121.90).',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27536---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6403211019', '110',
     'Counselor, Limited Licensed Professional', 'To receive a  Limited Professional Counselor License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have received a master''s or doctoral degree in counseling and have completed at least 48 semester hours or 72 quarter hours in counseling topics. Finally, an individual may submit a license application along with the appropriate application fee ($84.80 to $121.90).',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27536---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6420327267', '110',
     'Electrologist Limited Instructor', 'To receive an Electrologist Limited Instructor license, an applicant must have at least a high school diploma or equivalent level of education, have a current Michigan electrologist license, must have completed at least 300 hours of instructor training, and must have passed the theory and practical examination administered by PSI. Upon meeting these requirements, a licensure application along with the appropriate fee ($63.00) should be submitted to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory affairs.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'H', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_72600_72602_72731_72864---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6502419021', '110',
     'Real Estate Broker, Associate', 'An associate real estate broker must complete 90 hours of approved prelicensure education, complete 3 years of experience, and pass an examination. The fee for this license is $143.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72871---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6503419021', '110',
     'Real Estate Broker, Individual', 'An individual real estate broker must complete 90 hours of approved prelicensure education, complete 3 years of experience, and pass an examination. The fee for this license is $143.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72871---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6504419022', '110',
     'Real Estate Salesperson', 'A real estate salesperson must complete 40 hours of approved prelicensure education and pass an examination. The fee for this license is $88.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72602_72731_72871---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6561679217', '130',
     'Fire Protection System Inspector', 'A Fire Protection System Plan Inspector must execute the statement of attestation of understanding of the building code and provide copies of NFPA or ICC Fire Inspector I and II certifications. The fee for registration is $25.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/lara/dleg_bcc_inspector_registration_app_530888_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6700299011', '110',
     'Sanitarian, Registered', 'A Sanitarian must hold the National Environmental Health Association (NEHA) Registered Environmental Health Specialist/Registered Sanitarian (REHS/RS) credential, or complete a bachelor''s degree in an environmental health field and two years of work experience in an environmental health field, or complete a master''s or doctoral degree in an environmental health related field and one year of work experience in an environmental health field. All candidates must pass the NEHA REHS/RS Examination and pay the fee of $80.80.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27553---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6781691430', '250',
     'Certified Electronic Operator (C.E.O.)', 'To receive certification as a Certified Electronic Operator, an individual must have successfully completed the 4-week online CEO examination preparation course through Lansing Community College. Additionally, they must pass the CEO certification examination. Upon meeting these qualifications, an applicant must submit an application for certification.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://courts.michigan.gov/Administration/SCAO/OfficesPrograms/CRR/Pages/default.aspx', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6820211093', '110',
     'Social Service Technician (S.S.T)', 'Social Service Technician must have completed an Associate''s degree in Social Work from a CSWE-accredited program, or be currently employed in social or human services and have either completed at least 2,000 hours of supervised social work experience over at least a one year period, or have completed at least two years of college in a regionally-accredited institution with at least four courses relevant to human service needs. The fee for this license is $42.40.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27554---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6900291131', '110',
     'Veterinarian', 'Veterinarians must graduate from an accredited educational program and pass the North American Veterinary Licensing Examination. The fee for this license is $82.20.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27555---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '6910292056', '110',
     'Veterinary Technician', 'Veterinary Technicians must graduate from an accredited educational program and pass the Veterinary Technician Licensing Examination. The fee for this license is $41.00.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-72600_72603_27529_27555---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7001474011', '130',
     'Inspector, Building', 'To receive a Building Inspector License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have four years of experience actively engaged in the construction business, must possess a license as an architect or engineer with the State of Michigan, and must have either an Associates or Bachelor''s degree in a construction-related field. Upon meeting these requirements, an applicant must submit a license application along with the appropriate application fee ($25.00 per classification).',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/lara/dleg_bcc_inspector_registration_app_530888_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7003474011', '130',
     'Inspector, Electrical', 'To receive an Electrical Inspector registration, an applicant must have at least 2 years of experience as a licensed electrical journey worker OR should be licensed as a master electrician. Additionally, an applicant must complete the required number of hours of education in approved educational or training programs. Upon meeting these requirements, an application must be submitted to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs along with the $25.00 application fee.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/lara/dleg_bcc_inspector_registration_app_530888_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7004474011', '130',
     'Inspector, Mechanical', 'To receive a Mechanical Inspector License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have a minimum of three years of experience in hydronic heating and cooling and process piping, HVAC equipment, ductwork, refrigeration, limited heating service, unlimited heating service, limited refrigeration and air conditioning service, unlimited refrigeration and air condition service, and fire suppression. They must also obtain a specialty license if applicable. Upon meeting these requirements, an applicant must also take and pass an examination for each work classification desired. To do so, they must submit of a license application to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs, along with the $300.00 license and application fee.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_17412---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7005474011', '130',
     'Inspector, Plumbing', 'To receive a Plumbing Inspector registration, an applicant must first have possessed a journey license for at least 2 years OR should be licensed as a master plumber. Additionally, an applicant must complete the required number of hours of education in approved educational or training programs. Upon meeting these requirements, an application must be submitted to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs along with the $25.00 application fee.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/lara/dleg_bcc_inspector_registration_app_530888_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7006474011', '130',
     'Elevator Inspector', 'To receive a General Elevator Inspector License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have three years of experience in elevator construction (with at least one reference certifying the applicant''s experience). Additionally, an applicant must also pass the written and oral examination.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-45138--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7101472011', '130',
     'Boiler Installer', 'To receive a Boiler Installer License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must apply for the exam and remit the $80.00 application fee to the Michigan Bureau of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs. An applicant must then take and pass the exam.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_10575_77372-42822--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7102472011', '130',
     'Boiler Repairer', 'To receive a Boiler Repairer''s License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must apply for the exam and remit the $80.00 application fee to the Michigan Bureau of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs. An applicant must then take and pass the exam.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_10575_77372-42822--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7103499021', '130',
     'Mechanical Contractor', 'Mechanical contractors must have three years of experience and pass an exam before becoming licensed. The fee for this license is $300.00.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-45140--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7201472111', '130',
     'Electrician, Master', 'To receive a Master Electrician License, an applicant must be at least 22 years old, have held an Electrical Journeyman''s license for at least 2 years, and have had at least 12,000 hours of practical experience over a period of at least 6 years that is related to electrical construction, maintenance of buildings, electrical wiring, or equipment. This experience must be under the direct supervision of a Master Electrician. Additionally,  the applicant must take and pass the Master Electrician examination and submit the $50.00 license fee.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7202472111', '130',
     'Electrical Contractor', 'An applicant for an Electrical Contractor license must hold a Master Electrician License or have at least 1 master electrician residing in the State of Michigan who is in his or her full-time employ. Additionally, the applicant must take and pass the Electrical/Fire Alarm/Sign Contractor examination along with the $300.00 fee payable to PSI.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7203472111', '130',
     'Electrician, Journeyperson', 'An applicant for an Electrical Journeyman license must be at least 20 years old and must have at least 8,000 hours of practical experience over a period of at least 4 years that is related to electrical construction, maintenance of buildings, electrical wiring, or equipment. This experience must be under the direct supervision of a licensed person. Additionally,  the applicant must take and pass the Journeyman examination and submit the $40.00 license fee.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7204472111', '130',
     'Electrical Apprentice', 'To receive an Electrical Apprentice license in the State of Michigan, an applicant must submit an application online or mail the completed application and required documents to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs. Additionally, they must remit the $15.00 application fee.',
     '4', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7301474021', '130',
     'Elevator Journeyperson', 'To receive a General Journeyperson License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have three years of continuous employment as a supervisor of elevator construction or service, OR as an elevator constructor, serviceman, maintenance man, or repairman. Additionally, an applicant must also pass the Journeyperson  examination.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-45138--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7302474021', '130',
     'Elevator Contractor', 'To receive an Elevator Contractor''s License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have at least five years of experience as an elevator constructor, journeyperson, or equivalent, and must take and pass the examination.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-45138--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7401472152', '130',
     'Plumber, Master', 'A master plumber must have 4,000 hours experience in work as a journey plumber over a period of not less than 2 years immediately preceding the date of the application. They must also pass an exam. The fee for this application is $300.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-42835--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7402472152', '130',
     'Plumber, Journeyperson', 'A journey plumber must have more than 6000 hours experience attained over a period of not less than 3 years as a registered plumbing?apprentice in the practical installation of plumbing under the supervision of a licensed authorized master plumber. In addition, they must also pass an exam. The fee for this license is $40.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-42835--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7501492098', '130',
     'Fire Alarm Contractor', 'To receive a Fire Alarm Contractor License, an applicant must hold a Fire Alarm Specialty Technician''s License OR must have at least 1 fire alarm specialty technician residing in Michigan who is employed by the applicant full-time. Additionally, an applicant must take and pass the Electrical/Farm Alarm/Sign Contractor exam and submit the $300.00 license fee.',
     '2', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7502492098', '130',
     'Fire Alarm Specialty Technician', 'An applicant for a Fire Alarm Specialty Technician License in the State of Michigan must be at least 20 years old, have received a certification by the National Institute for Certification in Engineering Technology as an engineering technician, level 2, or equivalent level, and must take and pass the Fire Alarm Specialty Technician examination. The license application fee is $50.00.',
     '2', '1', '0', '0', '1',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7503492098', '130',
     'Fire Alarm Specialty Apprentice Technician', 'To receive a Fire Alarm Specialty Apprentice Technician license in the State of Michigan, an applicant must submit an application online or mail the completed application and required documents to the Michigan Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs. Additionally, they must remit the $15.00 application fee.',
     '4', '1', '0', '0', '1',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7524334390', '320',
     'Certified Criminal Justice Professional?(C.C.J.P.)', 'A certified criminal justice professional must complete 100 hours of education, 2,000 hours of criminal justice work experience, 100 hours of supervision, and pass the IC&RC CCJP (Supplemental) Examination. The fee for this license is $65.00.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.mcbap.com/certifications/ccjp-certified-criminal-justice-professional', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7601119021', '130',
     'Sign Specialty Contractor', 'A sign contractor must hold a sign specialist license and provide proof of public liability insurance. The fee for this license is $200.00',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7602474099', '130',
     'Sign Specialist', 'A sign specialist must have at least 4,000 hours of experience, complete the approved training course and pass the examination. The fee for this license is $40.00.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_10575_17394_77372-42954--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7650364904', '150',
     'Security Guard', 'A security guard must sumbit an application and the $200.00 fee to the Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '2', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_61343_36737-339603--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7701474041', '140',
     'Asbestos Abatement Contractor/Supervisor', 'To receive an Asbestos Abatement Contractor License, an applicant must have workers'' compensations insurance, acquire Michigan/EPA-approved training, acquire accreditation from MIOSHA Asbestos program, complete the Asbestos Abatement Contractor License application, and remit the $200-$400 application fee. The fee schedule for accreditation is $50.00.',
     '0', '9', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_11407_15369---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7702474011', '140',
     'Asbestos Abatement Inspector', 'To receive an Asbestos Abatement Inspector License, an applicant must have worked at least one year in asbestos-related work or general building inspections that are related to environmental and health concerns, OR have at least five years of supervisory experience in general building operations and maintenance. Additionally, an applicant must receive Michigan or EPA-approved training and receive accreditation from MIOSHA Asbestos Program. The fee schedule for accreditation is $150.00.',
     '0', '9', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_11407_15369---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7703192041', '140',
     'Asbestos Abatement Project Designer', 'To receive an Asbestos Abatement Project Designer License, an applicant must have had at least two years of experience in Asbestos-related work, OR have had at least five years of experience in school building operations and maintenance. Additionally, an applicant must receive Michigan or EPA-approved training and receive accreditation from MIOSHA Asbestos Program. The fee schedule for accreditation is $150.00.',
     '0', '9', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_11407_15369---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7705474041', '140',
     'Asbestos Abatement Worker', 'To receive an Asbestos Abatement Worker License, an applicant must receive Michigan or EPA-approved training and receive accreditation from MIOSHA Asbestos Program. The fee schedule for accreditation is $50.00.',
     '0', '9', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_11407_15369---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7706192041', '140',
     'Asbestos Management Planner', 'To receive an Asbestos Management Planner License, an applicant must have had at least two years of experience in Asbestos-related work, OR have had at least five years of experience in school building operations and maintenance. Additionally, an applicant must receive Michigan or EPA-approved training and receive accreditation from MIOSHA Asbestos Program. The fee schedule for accreditation is $150.00.',
     '0', '9', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-89334_11407_15369---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7774077879', '820',
     'Sport Trolling (Charter Captains)', 'An individual interest in sport trolling must submit an application with a $16.00 fee to the Department of Natural Resources.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/PR9411E_APPLICATION_FOR_MISCELLANEOUS_LICENSES_70191_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7801474011', '311',
     'Lead Abatement Inspector', 'To receive a Lead Abatement Inspector certification, an applicant must first have a high school diploma or equivalent level of education and taken and passed a lead training course from one of the approved providers. After meeting these requirements, a Certified Lead Professional application should be submitted to the Michigan Department of Health and Human Services along with the initial fee ($175 to $250). Finally, the state exam must be taken within 6 months of successfully passing the training course.',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lead/0,5417,7-310-84218---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7802192041', '311',
     'Lead Abatement Project Designer', 'To receive a Lead Abatement Project Designer certification, an applicant must first have either a Bachelor''s degree in engineering, architecture, or related field, OR have at least 2 years of experience in a related field. An applicant must also have passed the Abatement Supervisor class. After meeting these requirements, a Certified Lead Professional application should be submitted to the Michigan Department of Health and Human Services along with the initial fee ($105 to $180). Finally, the state exam must be taken within 6 months of successfully passing the training course.',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lead/0,5417,7-310-84218---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7804471011', '311',
     'Lead Abatement Supervisor', 'To receive a Lead Abatement Supervisor certification, an applicant must first have at least 1 year of experience as a certified Abatement Worker or at least 2 years of experience in a related field. Additionally, an applicant must take and pass an approved lead training course. After meeting these requirements, a Certified Lead Professional application should be submitted to the Michigan Department of Health and Human Services along with the initial fee ($125 to $150). Finally, the state exam must be taken within 6 months of successfully passing the training course.',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lead/0,5417,7-310-84218---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7805474041', '311',
     'Lead Abatement Worker', 'To receive a Lead Abatement Worker certification, an applicant must  take and pass an approved lead training course. After meeting this requirement, a Certified Lead Professional application should be submitted to the Michigan Department of Health and Human Services along with the initial fee ($115 to $125). Finally, the state exam must be taken within 6 months of successfully passing the training course.',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lead/0,5417,7-310-84218---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '7900499095', '130',
     'Manufactured Home Installer and Repairer', 'When installing and repairing manufactured homes, an individual should be licensed with the Department of Licensing and Regulatory Affairs. The fee for this license is $150.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-10575_17394_81070-474017--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8001453011', '820',
     'Wholesale Fish Dealer', 'Any person engaged in wholesale of fish must apply for license with the Department of Natural Resources. The Licensees must submit monthly reports to the Department of Natural Resources. The fee for this license is $5.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0,4570,7-350-79136_79236_80538-424529--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8003131021', '810',
     'Livestock Dealer', 'For a livestock dealer or broker to receive the Livestock Dealer license, they must submit a completed application and proof of bonding to the Michigan Department of Agriculture and Rural Development. Along with the application, the appropriate license fee amount ($50.00) should also be submitted.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdard/0,4610,7-125-1569_16979_21264---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8004452011', '810',
     'Certified Field Person', 'To receive a Certified Field person License, an individual must  work with a dairy inspector on 25 farms and agree within 80% of those farm inspections. Additionally, an application along with a $150 application fee must be submitted to the Michigan Department of Agriculture.',
     '0', '0', '0', '0', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdard/0,4610,7-125-1569_16958_16960_16973---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8006533032', '810',
     'Bulk Milk Sampler/Hauler', 'To receive a Hauler/Sampler/In-Line Sampler License, an individual must complete a written and practical exam, as well as an inspection. After passing the exam, an applicant must apply for the license and submit a $50.00 license fee. The license expires every two years on June 30th, and must be renewed with a $50.00 fee.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdard/0,4610,7-125-1569_16958_16960_16963---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8111271012', '820',
     'Taxidermist', 'A taxidermy license is required by the Department of Natural Resources. The fee for this license is $100.00 every third year.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0,4570,7-350-79136_79608_84089_84096---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8113131021', '820',
     'Fur Dealer', 'A fur dealer must apply for a permit with the Department of Natural Resources.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0,4570,7-350-79136_79236_80538_80539-424529--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8143453011', '820',
     'Minnow, Wiggler & Crayfish Dealer', 'A license must be obtained from Michigan Department of Natural Resources for Minnow, Wiggler, & Crayfish Dealers. The fee is $25.00.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0,4570,7-350-79136_79236_80538_80539-424529--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8201373012', '810',
     'Pesticide Applicator, Private', 'A certified pesticide applicator must take the technician exam and pay the $50.00 fee every third year.',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdard/0,4610,7-125-1569_16988_35289---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8202373012', '810',
     'Pesticide Applicator, Commercial', 'A certified pesticide applicator must take the technician exam and pay the $50.00 fee every third year.',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdard/0,4610,7-125-1569_16988_35289---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8293807356', '160',
     'Family/Group Child Care Home', 'To receive a Family Child Care Home license, an applicant must read the Licensing Rules for Family and Group Child Care Homes, as well as the Child Care Organizations Act. After meeting these requirements, the online application must be submitted along with the $50.00 application fee.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-63294_5529_49572-82366--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8301533032', '830',
     'Water Hauler', 'A Water Hauler must have an evaluation of the water hauling transportation tanks and equipment, approval of the water source facilities, knowledge of the use of chlorine for disinfection of water.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/documents/deq/deq-odwma-ehs-ncws-waterhaulerapp_402391_7.pdf', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8302475021', '830',
     'Water Well Contractor', 'A Well Drilling Contractor must have at least two years of experience, provide records of 20 water wells and pumps installed, provide references, and pass the examination offered by the Department of Environmental Quality. The fee for this license is $40.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/deq/0,4561,7-135-3313_3675_3694-137857--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8303518031', '830',
     'Drinking Water Operator (Distribution System)', 'To receive a Drinking Water Operator certification, an applicant must meet the education and experience requirements, submit a license application ($95) and take the Drinking Water Exam ($45.00-$75.00 per exam).',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/deq/0,4561,7-135-3308_3333_4171-10155--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8402474041', '830',
     'Hazardous Waste and Liquid By-Products Transporter', 'To receive this certification, an applicant must complete the Michigan Department of Environmental Quality Webinar Series.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/deq/0,4561,7-135-3308_3333-264752--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8411518031', '830',
     'Storm Water Operator', 'Storm Water Operators must pass an exam offered by the Department of Environmental Quality. The fee for this license is $95.00.',
     '0', '1', '0', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/deq/0,4561,7-135-3308_3333_4171-10121--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8412474071', '830',
     'Septage Hauler', 'Septage Haulers need a license provided by the Department of Environmental Quality to remove and transport septage waste for disposal. The fee for this license is $200.00.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/deq/0,4561,7-135-3313_71618_3682_3717---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8413518031', '830',
     'Wastewater Treatment Plant Operator', 'To receive an Industrial/Commercial Wastewater Treatment Plant Operator License in the State of Michigan, an applicant must have completed 6 months of operational experience in each unit process, the ability to read and write, comprehension of the principles and problems of management of the treatment process and facilities, the ability to perform arithmetic calculations to operate the waste treatment or control, and the ability to prepare the required report to the Department. Additionally, Level 3 requires the equivalent of 2 years of college education in engineering, chemistry, biological sciences, or an allied field, as well as 4 courses of post-high school level chemistry of biological sciences. Once these requirements have been met, an applicant must take and pass the exam for each unit process applied for.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/deq/0,4561,7-135-3308_3333_79877-10101--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8414518031', '830',
     'Municipal Wastewater Treatment Plant Operator', 'Municipal wastewater treatment plant operators need approved college credits and a certification examination to be licensed. The renewal fee is $95.00, annually.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/deq/0,4561,7-135-3308_3333_79877-10073--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8499198540', '810',
     'Livestock Trucker', 'For a livestock trucker to receive the Livestock Trucker license, they must submit a completed application and proof of bonding to the Michigan Department of Agriculture and Rural Development. Along with the application, the appropriate license fee amount ($25.00) should also be submitted.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mdard/0,4610,7-125-1569_16979_21264---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8501119070', '610',
     'Casino Employees Level 1', 'An applicant for a Casino Level 1 License must first apply to the casino''s or supplier''s Human Resources Department, who must provide a written statement that the casino/supplier has hired or intends to hire the applicant. An application along with a $500 application fee must be submitted to the Michigan Gaming and Control Board. Finally, a background examination must be completed and a $250 license fee submitted.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mgcb/0,4620,7-351-79127_79360_84204-244779--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8502393010', '610',
     'Casino Employees Level 2', 'An applicant for a Casino Level 2 License must first apply to the casino''s or supplier''s Human Resources Department, who must provide a written statement that the casino/supplier has hired or intends to hire the applicant. An application along with a $100 application fee must be submitted to the Michigan Gaming and Control Board. Finally, a background examination must be completed and a $100 license fee submitted.',
     '0', '0', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/mgcb/0,4620,7-351-79127_79360_84204-244779--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8911232099', '220',
     'Bail Bondsman', 'To receive a Bail Bondsman License, an applicant must take and pass one of the following exams: Surety and Fidelity Exam, Limited Lines Property and Casualty Exam, or the Full Property and Casualty Exam. Additionally, an applicant must hold the Surety, Limited Lines P&C or the full P&C line of authority, and must hold an active fidelity & surety appointment with each insurer. Finally, a bondsman must obtain and maintain prior approval of their financial status and business character by each court and jurisdiction in which they operate.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/difs/0,5269,7-303-22535-69197--,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8921132072', '220',
     'Loan Originator, Mortgage', 'To receive a Loan Originator License, an applicant must have completed at least three hours of federal law and regulations, three hours of ethics (including instruction on fraud, consumer protection, and fair lending issues), two hours of training related to lending standards for nontraditional mortgage product markets, and twelve hours of undefined instruction on mortgage origination. This pre-licensure education must include 2 hours of Michigan content. Upon completion of these requirements, an applicant must then either pass both the National and Michigan State components of the SAFE test, OR pass the National and stand-alone UST components of the SAFE Test, OR pass the National Test Components with Uniform State Content. Finally, the applicant must submit a license application to the NMLS. License fees include a $30.00 initial processing fee, $250.00 license/registration fee, $15 for a credit report, and $36.25 for an FBI criminal background check.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/difs/0,5269,7-303-79189_54462---,00.html', '20200225'),
    ('26', '01', '8931413031', '150',
     'Securities Broker-Dealer', 'Securities Broker-Dealers must provide proof of registration with the Financial Industry Regulatory Authority and pay the $300.00 fee.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.michigan.gov/lara/0,4601,7-154-61343_32915---,00.html', '20200225'),
