    ('27', '01', '6182', '026',
     'Qualified Rehabilitation Consultants, QRC Firms, and Registered Rehabilitation Vendors', 'A qualified rehabilitation consultant (QRC) is a vocational rehabilitation counselor who is registered with the Minnesota Department of Labor and Industry (DLI). 
To become a QRC, an individual must submit an R-20 Application for Approval and Registration as a Qualified Rehabilitation Consultant/Intern form and complete a one- to three-year internship. During the internship, the applicant must become either a:


Certified Rehabilitation Counselor (CRC); or a


Certified Disability Management Specialist (CDMS).


More information about registration can be found in Minn. Rules 5220.1400 - .1500, or by contacting the department at rehabregistrationspecialist.dli@state.mn.us
 None',
