     'Dietitian License', 'An individual specifically trained in the integration and application of scientific principles of food, nutrition, biochemistry, physiology, food management, and behavioral and social sciences to achieve and maintain human health through the provision of nutrition care services. Minnesota Board of Dietetics and Nutrition Practice Review Applicants
INSTRUCTIONS FOR DIETITIAN OR NUTRITIONIST ONLINE LICENSE APPLICATION
All applications for a new Minnesota License must be completed using the online application. The board is no longer accepting paper applications.


All licenses issued before November 1 will expire November 30 of issuing year. If licensed November 1 or after expire November 30 of the following year.
1. Read the laws that govern the practice of dietetics and nutrition in Minnesota.
You will be asked to approve via electronic signature upon completing the online application stating that you have read Minn. Stat. § 148.621-.634&lt;
2. Read the rules established by the Board of Dietetics and Nutrition Practice.
You will be asked to approve via electronic signature upon completing the online application stating that you have read Minn. Rules 3250.0010 - .0050
3. Before beginning the online application process, you will need detailed information to expedite the online process including:


Social Security number
Education History-names and dates of all educational institutions attended from high school through doctoral programs.
Practical and/or Work Experience-List completed Internship information and related work experience. If you are a new graduate this may not apply just enter your Internship information.
Current and former license numbers, dates issued and expired from Minnesota and/or any other jurisdictions, if applicable.
Visa, MasterCard, or Discover credit card to pay all fees. ALL FEES ARE NON-REFUNDABLE



4. Complete the online application.Enter your name the way you want it to appear on your Official License Certificate.  The name you enter must exactly match the name of the supporting documents, or documentation of formal name change must be submitted, i.e., marriage certificate, official court document (Photocopies only do not send original document).
After completing the Online Application, you will receive an email from the board that your application has been received and need to submit the required documentation:

If you are applying for a Licensed Dietitian:

Application Basis - Current Registration with the Commission on Dietetic Registration (Preferred Method):  You must submit a notarized copy of your current registration card from the Commission on Dietetic Registration.
Application Basis - Transcript, Preprofessional Practice Experience (completed internship) and CDR (Commission on Dietetic Registration) Exam Results: 

You must submit an official transcript showing your degree as required in Minn. Rules 3250.0010, Subp. 2, Para. A.; sent directly from your university/college to the board office
Submit a photocopy of the official CDR Exam results received at the test site.
Submit a photocopy of Verification Statement of completed Dietetic Internship Program.




If you are applying for a Licensed Nutritionist:

You must submit an official transcript showing your degree as required in Minn. Rule 3250.0020, Subp. 2, Para A.; sent directly from your university/college AND documented proof of completing a preprofessional practice experience component in nutrition practice; OR submit a notarized copy of certification as a Certified Nutrition Specialist by the Certification Board for Nutrition Specialist.
