Review:
Animal Chiropractic Registration Requirements
Pursuant to Minn. Stat. §  148.032, Doctors of Chiropractic may provide chiropractic services to animals under these conditions:

Completion of an Approved Course in Animal Chiropractic of at least 210 hours, with a minimum of 30% in-person/hands-on.
Register with the MBCE (see ??How to Apply?).
Pay the requisite fees ($125.00 initial application; $75.00 annual renewal).
Complete 6 additional hours of MBCE approved continuing education in the subject of animal chiropractic annually.
Referral from a Doctor of Veterinary Medicine must be maintained in the animal??s record.
A licensed chiropractor who treats both animal and human patients in the same facility must post a sign in the reception area and maintain a separate non-carpeted room for adjusting animals.

