     'Journeyworker High Pressure Pipefitter (HPP)', 'The Minnesota Department of Labor and Industry (DLI) license individuals as master and journeyworker pipefitters. Unlicensed individuals registered with DLI or in an approved apprenticeship program who work under supervision of a licensed pipefitter may assist in the installation of high pressure piping systems. Review Pipefitter Licensing
An individual must have four years of experience in the practical installation or fabrication of high pressure piping systems, apply for and be approved to take the journeyworker pipefitter exam, and receive a minimum score of 70 on the exam. See the License Exam Schedule
Included in the Master / Journeyworker Pipefitter exams:
Both examinations are drawn from the Minnesota''s high pressure piping and code for power piping systems: Minn. Stat. § 326B.90-925 and Minn. Rules 5230. 

Refer to:
High Pressure Piping License Examination Guide
FAQs about High Pressure Piping
