     'Mortgage Loan Originator License', 'Minnesota Department of Commerce Review:
Mortgage
Mortgage Originator
Apply

Minnesota uses the Nationwide Multistate Licensing System (NMLS). Company/business entities applying for the Mortgage Originator (MO) License are required to use NMLS
Read Minn. Stat. Chapter 58 before applying for a Mortgage Originator (MO) license. Unlicensed activity may result in administrative action.

Renewal

Mortgage loan originator licenses licenses expire on December 31 of each year and are renewable on January 1 of each year after that date. The renewal fee is $500.

Renewal is done through NMLS



Reapply
 If a license was not renewed, has lapsed, or was surrendered and you would like the license activated,follow the instructions at NMLS and reapply for the license.

 Out-of-state
 An out-of-state mortgage company does not need to physical presence in Minnesota; however, registration as a foreign corporation with the Office of the Minnesota Secretary of State may be required.

 See the Office of the Minnesota Secretary of State, Business &amp; Liens None',
