     'Racing Class C License (Occupational)', 'The Minnesota Racing Commission (MRC) licenses Owners Bloodstock Agents, Drivers, Exercise Riders, Farriers, Farrier Assistants, Groom Hot-walkers, Jockeys, Jockey Apprentices, Jockey Agents, Pony Riders, Trainers, Trainer Assistants, or Stable Supervisors. <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">As Required by <a href="https://www.revisor.mn.gov/statutes/cite/240.08">Minn. Stat. Â§ 240.08</a>
<br />
<br />
(a) is not in default in the payment or obligation to the state.
<br />
<br />
(b) have not been convicted of a felony or a crime involving fraud or misrepresentation within ten years of application, have been discharged from any supervision related to a disqualifying offense for at least five years, have never been convicted of a gambling-related offense, and do not have a state or federal felony charge pending.</p>
<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">(c) is not and never has been connected with an illegal business.
<br />
<br />
(d) has never been found guilty of fraud in connection with horse racing or breeding.
<br />
<br />
(e) has never been found guilty of a violation of law or rule relating to horse racing, parimutuel betting, or any other form of gambling.
<br />
<br />
(f) has never knowingly violated a rule or order of the commission or a MN law relating to racing.
<br />
<br />
Licensing information is available at <a href="https://www.mrc.state.mn.us/licensing/">Licensing</a>
<br /></p>
<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><strong style="font-size: 9pt;"><br />
GENERAL LICENSING INFORMATION</strong></p>
<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Minnesota Racing Commission must license everyone who is employed at a racetrack in Minnesota. Applicants are fingerprinted and authorize the release of personal information to verify application content. The applicants must also complete a notarized Affidavit of Qualification stating that they are not in debt to the State of Minnesota, have never been convicted of a felony, have never been involved in illegal business or fraud, nor have they been convicted of a crime related to horse racing or gambling. View theÂ <a href="https://www.revisor.mn.gov/rules/7877/">State of Minnesota Licensing Rules and Fees, Minn. Rules 7887</a></p>
<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">-All licenses expire December 31st of the calendar year in which they are issued.Â 
<br />
<br />
-Every individual must be licensedÂ <em>prior</em>Â to racing.Â 
<br />
<br />
-Minnesota law prohibits issuing licenses to convicted felons. Fingerprints are required of all applicants ages 18 through 70. <a href="https://www.revisor.mn.gov/rules/7877.0120/">Minn. Rules 7877.0120</a>, subpart 2D requires that all applicants who have not previously been licensed by the Commission must submit fingerprints with their initial application. Each set of fingerprints submitted must include a fingerprintÂ  processing fee of $21.50. Contact the Licensing Office for a fingerprint card. A fingerprint affidavit will be accepted as described on the reciprocity form.Â 
<br />
<br />
-All partnerships, corporations, and stable names must be licensed. If you are in a partnership, each individual owner must be licensed as well as the partnership.
<br />
<br />
-Trainers please note. Workers'' Compensation Insurance is required.Â <em>A current Certificate of Insurance must be on file in the Racing Commission office in order to be eligible for a trainer''s license and before any employees may be licensed.</em>Â Trainers should also note that work authorization documentation is required of and verified for all employees.Â 
<br />
<br />
-Individuals applying for licensure in certain occupations may be required to obtain approval of the Board of Stewards prior to issuance.Â 
<br />
<br />
-Applications that have been completely filled out and notarized may be submitted along with the appropriate fees made payable to the Minnesota Racing Commission in person or by mail.
<br />
<br />
-Confirmation will be mailed after processing.</p>
<p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Minnesota and/or multi-jurisdictional license applications are available atÂ <a href="https://www.mrc.state.mn.us/">MN Racing Commission</a>Â (seeÂ <a href="https://www.mrc.state.mn.us/licensing/">Licensing</a>) or from the Association of Racing Commissioners International atÂ <a href="https://www.arci.com/">RacingÂ Commissioner''s International (ARCI)</a>
<br />
<br />
All applicants age 18-70 who have not previously been licensed by the commission must submit fingerprints with their initial application.</p> None',
