     'Minnow Hauler -Nonresident', 'The Minnesota Department of Natural Resources (DNR) authorizes the licensee to transport fathead and sucker minnows beyond the boundaries of the state of Minnesota.  <p style="orphans: 2; text-align: left; widows: 2;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">A non-resident minnow hauler license is required for a non-resident to transport minnows (purchased from a licensed minnow dealer) out of the state. Leeches are considered and defined as minnows. Non-resident minnow haulers are required to have one licensed <a href="https://mn.gov/elicense/agencies/#/detail/appId/0/id/230697">Minnow Hauler Vehicle -Nonresident</a>Â </p>
