     'Plumbing Contractor', 'Minnesota Department of Labor and Industry (DLI) 
Plumbing contractor:

a person who may contract to perform or offer to perform plumbing work in all areas of the state provided the contractor has at all times a licensed master plumber as a responsible individual and maintains compliance with the required bond, general liability insurance and workers'' compensation insurance requirements (Minn. Stat § 326B.46). Person is defined as an individual proprietor, partnership, corporation, limited liability company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or any other legal entity.
Review:
Plumbing and Mechanical Contractors

Plumbing Contractor / Restricted Plumbing Contractor Business License Application Packet


Plumbing Employer Registration Application Packet


Plumbing Contractor Surety Bond


Continuing Education Requirements for Plumbers


Plumbing Contractor License Renewal


Fee reductions, continuous bond and streamlined online renewal among changes


    - Plumbing contractor license renewal fee - $128

    - New continuous bond means contractors do not have to submit a bond with their renewal.

    - New online business renewal process eliminates most paperwork.

All current plumbing contractor licenses expired December 31, 2017. Instructions for renewing plumbing contractor and restricted plumbing contractor licenses are below.

Apply for or Renew a License

    - During the renewal, you can review the information we have on file for your company, make changes and pay the renewal fee.

    - Renewal fees cannot be paid over the telephone.

    - If DLI does not have current liability insurance information for your company, you will need to submit an updated Certificate of Insurance. Insurance certificates can be emailed to DLI.license@state.mn.us

You will also need to submit a Certificate of Compliance - Minnesota Workers'' Compensation to DLI.license@state.mn.us

License bond is continuous


    - Bonds required for plumbing contractors and restricted plumbing contractors are continuous, so you do not have to submit bond forms with your renewal.

    - The amount of the bond is also cumulative, which means there will be $25,000 in coverage for each two-year license term.

Secretary of State filing


    - To renew your license, your corporate, LLC or assumed name filing with the Minnesota Secretary of State must be up-to-date.

    - On all renewal forms, especially your insurance certificates, your business name must appear EXACTLY as it is filed with the Minnesota Secretary of State.

    - Check the status of your Minnesota Secretary of State filing and update it if necessary. Your license cannot be renewed if your Secretary of State filing is inactive.

If you have changed your business structure (going from a sole proprietorship to an LLC or corporation, or from a corporation to an LLC), you will need to apply for a new license for your new business entity.

Paper renewal

    - Download and complete the Plumbing Contractor or Restricted Plumbing Contractor License Renewal Application. Be sure to provide an email address in case DLI has questions.

    - Include proof that your business filing is active. A printout of the page from the Minnesota Secretary of State Office showing the business filing is sufficient.

    - Completed renewals can be submitted by mail or in person

Questions?
Contact DLI at 651-284-5034 or DLI.license@state.mn.us

DLI does not accept cash as payment for licenses, inspections, copy requests and other DLI services. Accepted methods of payment include checks, money orders and electronic payments that can be made through the DLI website.

