    ('28', '01', '205CNM', '205',
     'Certified Nurse Midwives (CNM)', 'Certified Nurse-Midwife (referred to in document as nurse-midwife). 1. Shall currently be licensed as a registered nurse and certified nursemidwife by the Mississippi Board of Nursing. 2. Shall have a least one year of experience in labor and delivery and/or Newborn Intensive Care and be trained and annually certified in adult and infant CPR and infant resuscitation. 3. Shall have good mental and physical health.  
Initial State Certification. Prior to Board certification allowing the RN to practice as an APRN, the RN must:

