    ('28', '01', '206291011', '206',
     'Chiropractor', 'Qualifications to be licensed in Mississippi:
1. Adult of good moral character,
2. Graduate of Council on Chiropractic Education (CCE) approved chiropractic college,
3. Sixty (60) hours of undergraduate college work or pre-chiropractic college work,
4. Passage of Parts 1, 2, 3, 4, and Physical Therapy of the National Board of Chiropractic Examiners examination,
Process for licensure for the chiropractor:
1. Request an application online. There is a $100.00 application fee which must be paid online before an application can be emailed.
2. Other materials needed are:
a. Official transcript of pre-chiropractic hours from the college,
b. Official transcript of chiropractic college hours from the college,
c. Certified copy of chiropractic college diploma,
d. Completed application,
e. Payment of $200.00 examination fee (money order or cashier’s check), and
f. Official copy of National Board scores from National Board of Chiropractic Examiners.
3. Pass a jurisprudence examination in the state on the state chiropractic law and rules and regulations of the Mississippi Board of Chiropractic Examiners',
