    ('32', '01', '18704', '187',
     'Point of Care Analyst', '1) To qualify for a certificate as a POINT OF CARE ANALYST, a person must be employed in a medical facility with a licensed lab; provide verification from his/her laboratory director that he/she has successfully completed the education and training for preanalytical, postanalytical, and analytical phases of the testing process, and;

2) Must be one of the following medical professionals:
   a. Registered nurse as described in NRS 632.019;
   b. Advanced practitioner of nursing as described in NRS 632.012;
   c. Licensed practical nurse as described in NRS 632.016;
   d. Practitioner of respiratory care as described in NRS 630;
   e. Physician assistant as described in NRS 630;
   f. Registered pharmacists participating as described in NRS 639.0124(8);
   g. Certified laboratory assistant with a high school diploma or equivalent education and subsequent training under a point-of-care testing program.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial certification--$75; biennial renewal--$60.',
