    ('32', '01', '18705', '187',
     'Music Therapist', 'Music Therapists must be licensed in Nevada.  Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 18 years old.
2)  Have completed an academic program approved by the American Music Therapy Association with a bachelor''s or higher degree in music therapy.
3)  Provide proof of current board certification from the Certification Board for Music Therapists (if applicable).
4)  Provide 2 sets of fingerprints for a criminal history check. (Note:  NRS 640D.170- Grounds for license denial, suspension or revocation.)


Note:  100 units of continuing education are required for renewal (every 3 years.)

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  license --$200 (valid 3 years); fingerprints--$37.50',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://dpbh.nv.gov/Reg/RegulatoryPgms/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '18706', '187',
     'Dietitian', 'Dietitians must be licensed in Nevada.  Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 years old and of good moral character.
2)  Have a bachelor''s degree or higher from an accredited university in human nutrition, nutrition education, dietetics, food & nutrition, food systems management or a program approved by the Board.
3)  Have completed at least 1,200 hours of training and experience within the US in the practice of dietetics under the direct supervision of a licensed or registered dietitian, or an individual holding a doctorate degree in a program approved by the Board.
4)  Has passed the registration exam given by the Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR) (credential verification from CDR must be included with the application).
5)  Submit 2 sets of fingerprints to the Central Repository for NV Records of Criminal History for a background check.  (Note:  NRS 449.174- Grounds for license denial, suspension or revocation.)

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  license --$200 (valid 2 years); fingerprints--$37.50.',
     '0', '2', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://health.nv.gov/HCQC_Dietitian.htm', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '21501', '215',
     'Manufactured & Mobile Home General Serviceperson', 'In Nevada, the owner or responsible managing employee (RME) of a business that installs or repairs manufactured homes, mobile homes or commercial coaches must be licensed.  Licensing categories are:  General Serviceman and Specialty Serviceman.  
General serviceman applicants must pass the required exam with a score of at least 75%, and submit fingerprints for a background check. 

Specialty serviceman must have a Nevada contractors license. They are limited to performing repairs in their licensed specialty only.

Fees are subject to change.  Fees are:  exam --$50; license fee --$450; background check --$38.25 (money order payable to DPS); exam study guide --$15; renewal (2 years)- $350.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://mhd.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '21502', '215',
     'Manufactured & Mobile Home Salesperson', 'In Nevada, anyone who sells, rents or leases a manufactured structure must be licensed.  Licensing categories are:  Salesman and Responsible Managing Employee (RME).  Applicants must pass the required exam with a score of at least 75% and submit fingerprints for a background check.

Fees are subject to change.  License fees:  Salesman --$200 (renewal --$175 every 2 years); RME --$350 (renewal --$250 every 2 years); exam --$50; background check --$38.25 (money order payable to DPS); exam study guide --$15.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
