    ('32', '01', '11399', '113',
     'All Other Licensed Contractor Primary Classifications', 'The State Board of Contractors issues licenses in the following contractor primary classifications which are not listed separately. 
Primary Classification AB--General Engineering and General Building
Primary Classification C6--Erecting Signs
Primary Classification C7--Elevation and Conveyance
Primary Classification C9--Movement of Buildings
Primary Classification C11--Spraying Mixtures Containing Cement
Primary Classification C13--Using Sheet Metal
Primary Classification C24--Erecting Scaffolds and Bleachers
Primary Classification C25--Fencing and Equipping Playgrounds
Primary Classification C26--Institutional Contracting
Primary Classification C27--Individual Sewerage
Primary Classification C28--Fabricating Tanks
Primary Classification C30--Installing Equipment to Treat Water
Primary Classification C31--Wrecking
Primary Classification C36--Installing Urethane
Primary Classification C37--Solar Contracting
Primary Classification C38--Installing Equipment Used With Liquefied Petroleum and Natural Gas
Primary Classification C39--Installing Heaters
Primary Classification C40--Specialties Not Authorized by Other Classifications
Primary Classification C41--Fire Protection
Primary Classification C42--Constructing, Altering, or Improving Community Antenna Television Systems
Primary Classification E1--Owner/Builder Not to Exceed Three Stories (B-2 examination)
Primary Classification E2--Owner/Builder Exceeding Three Stories (B examination)

Applicants must:
1)  Have four years of experience as a journeyman, foreman, supervising employee or contractor in the specific classification in which he/she is applying.  The experience must have been obtained within the preceding 10 years.  Training received at an accredited college or university may be used to satisfy a portion of the required experience.
2)  Prove financial responsibility (the board determines the amount of the bond that will be required.)
3)  Possess good character and provide 4 reference certificates from individuals with firsthand knowledge of the applicant''s experience.
4)  Pass the Contractors Management Survey (CMS) exam.
5)  Pass the applicable trade exam, if required for the specific license.
Exams are given daily in Las Vegas, on various days in Reno, and on a limited basis in Elko.

Visit the website for more detailed information on the requirements and application process.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial application--$300; initial license and biennial renewal--$600; Residential Recovery Fund Assessment (for residential contractors only) based upon monetary license limit--$200 - $1,000; CMS and Trade exam: exam provider sets the fee.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvcontractorsboard.com/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '11704', '117',
     'Aesthetician', 'Applicants must have completed 900 hours in a program approved by the State Board; completed school through at least the 10th grade or the equivalent; be at least 18 years old; and pass the written and practical exams.

If you are transferring from another state, you must have a current license in good standing, and you must prove that you have passed the national exam or you must take the written exam in Nevada.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$15; examination, written and practical--$110; examination, national written --$110; 2-year license--$70; 4-year license renewal--$140.',
     '0', '3', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://cosmetology.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '11705', '117',
     'Electrologist', 'Applicants must have completed 500 hours in a program approved by the State Board; completed school through at least the 10th grade or the equivalent; be at least 18 years old; and pass the written and practical exams.

If you are transferring from another state, you must have a current license in good standing, and you must prove that you have passed the national exam or you must take the written exam in Nevada.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$15; examination, written and practical--$110; examination, national written --$110; 2-year license--$70; 4-year license renewal--$140.

Related Note:  Threading Practitioners must register with the Board annually.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://cosmetology.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '11706', '117',
     'Cosmetic Demonstrator', 'Applicants must be at least 18 years old; have completed a sanitation course provided by the board and scored at least 75% on the exam given by the board.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$15; examination--$75; 2-year license--$70; 4-year license renewal--$140.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://cosmetology.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12101', '121',
     'Dentist', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be over 21 and of good moral character. 
2)  Be a U.S. citizen, or legally entitled to live and work in the U.S..
3)  Have graduated from a dental school accredited by the ADA.
4)  Pass the National Board of Dental Examiners examination with an average score of at least 75%.
5)  Pass one of the following clinical examinations:
  5a)  Western Regional Examining Board (WREB) exam, or
  5b)  ADEX-Dental Exam (must have been taken after October 1, 2007).
6)  Submit the results of a National Practitioner Data Bank self-query (on-line @ www.npdb-hipdb.com.)
7)  Pass the online Nevada jurisprudence examination.

*Notes:  ADEX = American Board of Dental Examiners; ADLEX = American Dental Licensing Examination;  PBIS = Professional Background Information Service; CCBS = Complete Credentialing & Background Services.
  
Reciprocity:  Nevada offers licensure by examination.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application packet - $25; license application by WREB or ADEX - $1200; biennial license renewal--$600; self-query - $16.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvdentalboard.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12102', '121',
     'Dental Hygienist', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 18 years old and of good moral character.
2)  Be a U.S. citizen, or legally entitled to live and work in the U.S..
3)  Have graduated from a dental hygiene school accredited by the ADA.
4)  Pass the National Board of Dental Examiners dental hygiene examination with a score of at least 75%.
5)  Pass a clinical examination (WREB or ADEX Dental Hygiene).
6)  Pass the online Nevada jurisprudence examination.

Reciprocity:  Nevada offers licensure by examination (WREB or ADEX Dental Hygiene).

*Notes:  WREB = Western Regional Examining Board; ADEX = American Board of Dental Examiners; PBIS = Professional Background Information Service; CCBS = Complete Credentialing & Background Service.
 
Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application packet - $25; initial license application by WREB or ADEX - $600; biennial license renewal--$300.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '3', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://www.nvdentalboard.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12301', '123',
     'Optician', 'Applicants must pass the Nevada state optical exam.  To qualify for the exam, applicants must: 
1)  Be at least 18 years old, and of good moral character, and have graduated from an accredited high school or its equivalent.
2)  Hold current American Board of Opticianry (ABO) & National Contact Lens Exam (NCLE) certifications.
3a) Have completed an approved opthalmic education course and have 3 years of opthalmic dispensing experience as a licensed NV apprentice dispensing optician under the supervision of a licensed optician, ophthalmologist or optometrist; or
3b) Have graduated from an approved school with an associate of applied science degree in ophthalmic technology and had 1 year of ophthalmic dispensing experience as a licensed NV apprentice under the supervision of a licensed dispensing optician, ophthalmologist or optometrist.
4)  Have completed at least 100 hours of training and experience in fitting and filling contact lens prescriptions (under direct supervision as listed above).
5)  Have 3 letters of reference, including one from a dispensing optician or a person who has worked in the optical industry with the applicant; letters must be mailed directly to the Board by the authors.

Fees are subject to change. Fees are:  apprentice application--$100; optician application/examination--$350; optician examination retake--$250; annual optician license renewal --$300; annual apprentice license renewal--$50.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvbdo.nv.gov#http://www.nvbdo.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12501', '125',
     'Speech Pathologist', 'Speech pathologists practicing in the state must be licensed through the Board.  Those persons working in the school districts must be licensed through the Department of Education and are not required to maintain the state licensure, however, if they also work outside of the schools, both would be required.  

Applicants must: 
1)  Be of good moral character.
2)  Have a master''s degree or higher in Speech Pathology from an accredited college (official transcripts required) or possess equivalent training and experience as determined by the Board.
3)  Hold current  American Speech-Language & Hearing Association (ASHA) certification. 

For more information on the requirements or on special licenses (temporary, provisional and limited) visit the Board website.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial application/license--$250; annual license renewal--$100.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvspeechhearing.org#http://www.nvspeechhearing.org#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12502', '125',
     'Audiologist', 'Audiologists practicing in the state must be licensed through the Board.  Those persons working in the school districts must be licensed through the Department of Education and are not required to maintain the state licensure, however, if they also work outside of the schools, both would be required.  Audiologists who also dispense hearing aids must pass the dispensing written and practical State Board examinations.

Applicants must: 
1)  Be of good moral character.
2)  Have a doctorate degree in Audiology from an accredited college (official transcripts required), and 
3a)  Hold current American Board of Audiology (ABA) or American Speech Language Hearing Association (ASLA) certification.
4)  Provide three professional references.

For more information on the requirements or on special licenses (temporary, provisional and limited) visit the Board website.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial application/license--$250; annual license renewal--$100.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvspeechhearing.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12503', '125',
     'Hearing Aid Specialist', 'Applicants must meet the following requirements:  
1)  Be of good moral character.
2)  Have a high school diploma or equivalency, or higher education degree in any field.
3)  Complete a 2-year apprenticeship with a licensed Dispensing Audiologist or Hearing Aid Specialist.
4)  Be certified by the National Board for Certification in Hearing Instrument Sciences (NBC-HIS). 
5)  Pass a written and practical State Board examination. 

For more information on the requirements, apprenticeship or special licenses (temporary and provisional) visit the Board website.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial application/license--$250; annual license renewal--$100.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvspeechhearing.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12701', '127',
     'Nursing Facility Administrator', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 years old, of good moral character, physically and mentally able to care for disabled or elderly patients, and free of communicable diseases.
2)  Be able to speak, read, understand and write in English. 
3)  Have at least a bachelor''s degree.
4)  Have at least 1,000 hours of the NAB-approved Administrator-in-Training Program that is also approved by the board.
5)  Complete 8 hours of regulation training.
6)  Pass the National Board of Examiners of Long Term Care Administrators'' exam (NAB).  
7)  Submit 2 fingerprint cards (or a receipt of electronic submission) for a background check.

Visit the board website for more information on the education and training requirements. 

Fees are subject to change. Fees are:  application request-- $25; initial application/license-- $645; biennial license renewal-- $350; background clearance-- $60 (cards) or $15 (electronic).',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://beltca.nv.gov#http://beltca.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12702', '127',
     'Residential Group Care/Assisted Living Administrator', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 years old, of good moral character, physically and mentally able to care for disabled or elderly patients, and free of communicable diseases.
2)  Have at least a high school diploma or the equivalent. 
3)  Be able to speak, read, understand and write in English. 
4)  Have completed the board-approved 100-hour Certificate Program Introductory Course.
5)  Complete the board-approved Administrator-in-Training program.
6)  Complete 8 hours of regulation training.
7)  Pass the National Board of Examiners of Long Term Care Administrators'' (NAB) RC/AL exam.
8)  Submit 2 fingerprint cards (or a receipt of electronic submission) for a background check.

Visit the board website for more information on the education and training requirements. 

Fees are subject to change. Fees are:  application request-- $25; licensure program introductory course - $2,450; biennial license renewal-- $350; background clearance-- $60 (cards) or $15 (electronic).',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://beltca.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12901', '129',
     'Marriage and Family Therapist', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 years old, a U.S. citizen (or legally entitled to work in the United States), and be of good moral character.
2)  Have an undergraduate degree from an accredited college or university approved by the Board.  
3)  Have completed residency training in psychiatry, or have a graduate degree in marriage and family therapy, psychology, or social work from an accredited institution approved by the State Board, or an equivalent combination of education and training approved by the Board. (Contact the Board for information on the required graduate coursework.) 
4)  Have at least 2 years of postgraduate experience in marriage and family therapy (and at least 3,000 hours of supervised experience, 1,500 of which must consist of direct client contact).
5)  Pass an examination.
6)  Provide three references (must be submitted directly from the references to the board.)

Licensed Intern
To obtain the required supervised experience indicated above, applicants must first obtain licensure as a marriage and family therapist intern.  In general, applicants must meet the requirements listed above in items 1 - 3 and have a supervision agreement with an approved supervisor.  Contact the Board for more information on the intern requirements.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$75; examination--$220; license processing--$50; annual license--$150.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://marriage.nv.gov#http://marriage.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '12902', '129',
     'Clinical Professional Counselor', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 years old, a U.S. citizen (or legally entitled to work in the United States), and be of good moral character. 
2a)  Have completed residency training in psychiatry from an accredited institution approved by the Board or,
2b)  have a graduate degree from an approved* program in mental health counseling or community counseling or,
2c)  have a degree acceptable to the Board that includes the completion of a practicum and internship in mental health counseling (taken concurrently with the degree program and supervised by a licensed mental health professional).
3)  Have at least 2 years of postgraduate experience in professional counseling.
4)  Have at least 3,000 hours of supervised experience in professional counseling including: at least 1,500 hours of direct client contact and at least 100 hours of counseling under the direct supervision of an approved supervisor (at least 1 hour per week must have been completed for each work setting at which the applicant provided counseling).
5)  Have passed the National Clinical Mental Health Counseling Exam administered by the National Board for Certified Counselors.

*  Program approved by the Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs.

Licensed Intern
To obtain the required supervised experience indicated above, applicants must first obtain licensure as a clinical professional counselor intern.  In general, applicants must meet the requirements listed above in items 1 - 3, and have a supervision agreement with an approved supervisor.  Contact the Board for more information on the intern requirements.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$75; examination--$220; license processing--$50; annual license--$150.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://marriage.nv.gov#http://marriage.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13101', '131',
     'Social Worker - LSW', 'Applicants must:
1)  Hold a bachelor''s or master''s degree in social work from a program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) (official transcripts required).
2)  Pass the national (ASWB) examination at the bachelor''s or master''s level. 
3)  Be at least 21 years of age.
4)  Submit fingerprints for a background check.

Note:  If an applicant holds a master''s degree in social work, the applicant will be given an option to take either the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB) master''s or the ASWB bachelor''s examination to satisfy the examination requirement for the SOCIAL WORKER level. (Traditionally, the master''s examination in other states has been used for applicants who hold a master''s degree with little or no experience.)  The applicant will need to show proof of the ASWB master''s examination if planning on applying for an internship in Nevada to complete hours for the CLINICAL or INDEPENDENT license.

A three-year provisional Social Worker license may be obtained by individuals who already hold a bachelor''s or master''s degree in a related field that contains social work curriculum and are enrolled in a program leading to a bachelor''s degree or master''s degree in social work that is accredited by CSWE.

A three-month provisional license is available for individuals meeting the eligibility requirements for the next scheduled ASWB examination.  Provisional licenses may not be renewed.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$40; initial license--$100; annual license renewal--$100; examination--$230 (payable to ASWB); license by endorsement (no exam required)--$100; 3-year provisional license--$75; annual 3-year provisional license renewal--$100; 3-month provisional license (no renewal)--$75; fingerprints - $38.25.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://socwork.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13102', '131',
     'Independent Social Worker - LISW', 'Applicants must:
1)  Hold a master''s or doctorate of social work degree from a program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (official transcripts required).
2)  Submit verification of completion of 3,000 hours of supervised, postgraduate social work meeting Board specifications.
3)  Pass the national (ASWB) advanced generalist examination. 
4)  Be at least 21 years old.
5)  Submit fingerprints for a background check.

A three-month provisional license is available for individuals meeting the eligibility requirements for the next scheduled State Board examination.  Provisional licenses may not be renewed.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$40; initial license--$100; annual license renewal--$150; examination--$260 (payable to ASWB); license by endorsement (no exam required)--$100; 3-month provisional license--$75; fingerprints - $38.25.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '1', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://socwork.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13103', '131',
     'Clinical Social Worker - LCSW', 'Applicants must:
1)  Hold a master''s or doctorate degree in social work from a program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (official transcripts required).
2)  Submit verification of completion of 3,000 hours of supervised, postgraduate clinical social work meeting State Board specifications, including 2,000 psychotherapeutic hours.
3)  Pass the national (ASWB) examination at the "clinical" level. 
4)  Be at least 21 years old.
5)  Submit fingerprints for a background check.

A three-month provisional license is available for individuals meeting the eligibility requirements for the next scheduled State Board examination.  Provisional licenses may not be renewed.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$40; initial license--$100; annual license renewal--$150; examination--$260 (payable to ASWB) ; license by endorsement (no exam required)--$100; 3-month provisional license--$75; fingerprints - $38.25.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '1', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://socwork.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13301', '133',
     'Funeral Director', 'Applicants for licensure as funeral directors must:
1)  Be at least 18 years old and provide evidence of good moral character.
2)  Pass 2 State Board examinations (one for funeral director and one on the applicable Nevada laws). 
3)  Complete one year as a Funeral Arranger.

Note:  If an applicant for licensure has already passed the National Board examination given by the Conference of Funeral Services Examining Boards of the United States,  it is only necessary to take the Nevada laws test.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial license/application--$375; examination--$375 per exam; license renewal--$200 every two years.',
     '0', '3', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://funeral.nv.gov#http://funeral.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13302', '133',
     'Embalmer and Apprentice Embalmer', 'Applicants must:  
1)  Be at least 18 years old and be of good moral character.
2)  Have graduated from high school and completed 2 academic years of instruction (60 semester hours or 90 quarter hours) at an accredited college or university (Note - credits earned at an embalming college or school of mortuary science do not fulfill the 60 university/college credit requirement).
3)  Complete a 12-month program at an accredited embalming college or school of mortuary science.
4)  Complete 1 year of practical experience under the supervision of a licensed embalmer with proof of having embalmed at least 50 bodies (see Apprentice information below).
5)  Pass 2 examinations (one for embalming and one on the applicable Nevada laws).

Requirements for Apprentice Embalmer certificate of registration:
1)  Be at least 18 years old and of good moral character.
2)  Have graduated from high school and completed 2 academic years of instruction (60 semester hours or 90 quarter hours) at an accredited college or university (note - credits earned at an embalming college or school of mortuary science do not fulfill the 60 university/college credit requirement).
3)  Provide verification of the apprenticeship.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial license/application--$375; examination--$375 per exam; apprentice embalmer--$375; license renewal--$200 every two years.',
     '4', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://funeral.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13701', '137',
     'Doctor of Homeopathic Medicine', 'Applicants must:
1)  Have either a Doctor of Medicine (M.D.) degree or a Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (D.O.) degree from an accredited school approved by the State Board.
2)  Have completed at least 3 years of approved postgraduate training in allopathic or osteopathic medicine.
3)  Have completed at least 600 hours of postgraduate training in homeopathy; 300 of which must be in Nevada under the supervision of a homeopathic physician (or a program deemed equivalent by the Board).
4)  Pass State Board written and/or oral examinations and meet any other additional requirements established by the State Board.

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  initial license/application--$500; license renewal--$600; reexamination--$400; temporary, special or limited license (initial)--$300; temporary, special, or limited license (renewal)--$300; fingerprint cards - $50.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://NVBHME.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13702', '137',
     'Advanced Practitioner of Homeopathy', 'Applicants must:
1) Have completed an educational program of at least 400 hours of training in homeopathy; 200 of which must be in Nevada under the supervision of a homeopathic physician (or a program deemed equivalent by the Board).

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are: advanced practitioner license-$300; fingerprint cards-$50.',
     '0', '0', '1', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://NVBHME.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13703', '137',
     'Homeopathic Assistant', 'Applicants must:
1) Have completed an educational program of at least 200 hours of training in homeopathy; 100 of which must be in Nevada under the supervision of a homeopathic physician (or a program deemed equivalent by the Board).

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  assistant license--$150; fingerprint cards-$50.',
     '0', '0', '1', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://NVBHME.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '13901', '139',
     'Landscape Architect', 'Applicants must have a combination of 6 or more years of education and experience in landscape architecture that is acceptable to the Board and pass the state and national exams.  
For example:
1)  Have a bachelor''s or master''s in landscape architecture (or a degree in a related subject acceptable to the Board) from an approved school.
2)  Have completed 2 years of post graduate work experience under the direct supervision of a registered landscape architect (or a combination of education and experience acceptable to the Board).  
3)  Pass a State Board examination and the national Landscape Architect Registration Exam (LARE). The national examination is administered by CLARB*. 

Applicants for the Landscape Architect in Training (LAIT) certificate must:
1)  Be 21 years old, of good moral character and a U.S. citizen (or lawfully entitled to be in the U.S.).
2a)  Have a 4 year landscape architecture degree, or
2b)  Have 4 years of work experience under the supervision of a licensed landscape architect.
3)  Have passed Section A and B of the LARE exam.

*CLARB = Council of Landscape Architect Registration Boards.

Reciprocity: For those registered in good standing in another state (or province of Canada), with no disciplinary action ever taken.  Visit the Board website for specific requirements.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  registration by exam--$175 ($100 for LAIT); national examination administration--$100 ($50 for LAIT); national exam fee -  cost varies depending on the number of sections the applicant is taking; examination fee for the Nevada-specific exam--$75; annual license renewal - determined annually by Board--$150-$200 ($100 for LAIT).',
     '0', '3', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://nsbla.nv.gov#http://nsbla.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14101', '141',
     'Physician', 'The following general requirements apply; contact the Board for more information.
Applicants must:
1)  Have completed a doctor of medicine program at an AMA Liaison Committee for Medical Education (LCME) approved medical school. 
2)  Have completed 2 years of accredited postgraduate training (unless applying by endorsement of license).
3a)  Pass the United States Medical Licensing examination; or
3b)  Be board-certified by one of the specialty boards of the American Board of Medical Specialists and pass a state written licensing examination.
4)  Pass other State Board required written and/or oral exams relating to the practice of medicine in Nevada.
5)  Applicants applying by endorsement may be required to appear before the Board and may still be required to take an exam or meet other requirements.

An applicant may also be required to take the Special Purpose Examination (SPEX) if he or she has not taken a major written exam within the ten years prior to the date of application.

Foreign medical school graduates must submit proof of the degree of Doctor of Medicine or its equivalent. Foreign graduates must also hold the standard certificate given by the Educational Commission for Foreign Medical Graduates (ECFMG) or have written proof of having passed the examination given by the Commission.

The State Board may grant a license in one of the following categories to an applicant who has received a license in another state or who is otherwise eligible for a permanent license. The categories of licensure include locum tenens, special, temporary and endorsement.

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  application--$600; background check - $75; biennial registration--$800; resident physician application/licensing per year--$300/$50, respectively, plus $75 for the background check.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://medboard.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14102', '141',
     'Physicians'' Assistant', 'The following general requirements apply; contact the Board for more information.
Applicants must:
1)  Be of good moral character.  
2)  Be able to adequately speak and write in English.
3)  Have graduated from a physician assistant program approved by the American Medical Association (AMA) Committee on Allied Health Education and Accreditation.
4)  Be certified by the National Commission on Certification for Physician Assistants.
5)  Pass a written exam concerning the statutes and regulations relating to the practice as a physician assistant in Nevada. 
Applicants may be required to appear before the State Board.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$300; biennial registration--$400; background check - $75.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '2',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://medboard.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14103', '141',
     'Respiratory Therapist', 'The following general requirements apply; contact the Board for more information.
Applicants must:  
1)  Be of good moral character.  
2)  Be able to adequately speak and write in English.
3)  Have a high school diploma or general equivalency diploma (GED) and an Associate (AA) degree.
4)  Complete an educational program for respiratory care approved by the National Board for Respiratory Care.
5)  Pass the examination as an entry-level or advanced practitioner of respiratory care administered by the National Board for Respiratory Care.
6)  Be certified by the National Board for Respiratory Care.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application (non refundable) --$100; active license registration (biennial) --$200; background check - $75.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '2',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://medboard.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14104', '141',
     'Perfusionist', 'The following general requirements apply; contact the Board for more information:
Applicants must:  
1)  Be of good moral character.
2)  Have successfully completed a perfusion education program approved by the Board.
3)  Pass the certification exam given by the American Board of Cardiovascular Perfusion (ABCP).*

* The exam may be waived if the applicant is licensed as a perfusionist in another state if the requirements for licensure are substantially similar to those required by the Board; or if the applicant holds a current certificate as a certified clinical perfusionist issued by the ABCP before 10/1/2009.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application --$300; license registration (biennial) --$400; background check - $75.',
     '0', '2', '1', '0', '2',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://medboard.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14301', '143',
     'Registered Nurse (RN)', 'Applicants for licensure by examination must:
1)  Have graduated from an approved school of nursing with a diploma or nursing degree.
2)  Have passed the National Council Licensure Examination (NCLEX).
3)  Submit fingerprint cards (fingerprint reports must be cleared by the Board to obtain licensure).

Applicants for licensure by endorsement must:
1)  Have graduated from an approved school of nursing with a diploma or nursing degree.
2)  Have passed the NCLEX or State Board Test Pool Examination (SBTPE).
3)  Have been licensed or registered as a RN under the laws of another jurisdiction.
4)  Submit fingerprint cards (fingerprint reports must be cleared by the Board to obtain licensure).

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application by examination--$100; application by endorsement--$105; fingerprinting - $50 (may vary);  biennial renewal - $100.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nevadanursingboard.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14302', '143',
     'Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN)', 'Applicants for licensure by examination must:
1)  Have graduated from an approved school of nursing with a nursing certificate (LPN).
2)  Have passed the National Council Licensure Examination (NCLEX).
3)  Submit fingerprint cards (fingerprint reports must be cleared by the Board to obtain licensure).

Applicants for licensure by endorsement must:
1)  Have graduated from an approved school of nursing with a nursing certificate (LPN).
2)  Have passed the NCLEX or State Board Test Pool Examination (SBTPE).
3)  Have been licensed or registered as a LPN under the laws of another jurisdiction.
4)  Submit fingerprint cards (fingerprint reports must be cleared by the Board to obtain licensure).

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application by examination--$90; application by endorsement--$95; fingerprinting - $50 (may vary);  biennial renewal - $100.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nevadanursingboard.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14303', '143',
     'Advanced Practitioner of Nursing (APN)', '(Areas of practice are nurse practitioner, clinical nurse specialist and certified nurse midwife.)
Applicants for Nevada''s certificate of recognition as an APN must:
1)  Meet all requirements for Registered Nurse licensure (have an active RN license). 
2)  Have a master''s degree from an accredited school in nursing or a related health field approved by the board. 

Applicants for APN certification by endorsement (if the program was completed after June 1, 2005) must have a master''s degree in nursing or a related health field.  Additionally, if the applicant has not worked 800 hours in APN practice during the past 5 years, and has not completed a nurse practitioner education program in the preceding 2 years, he or she must work 1,000 hours under the supervision of a qualified physician or Nevada certified APN upon receipt of APN certification.

For those applicants applying for certification by endorsement who completed an APN program prior to June 1, 2005, modified requirements apply.  Visit the Board''s website for more information.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application/initial certificate--$200; biennial certificate renewal (RN+APN)--$300.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nevadanursingboard.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14304', '143',
     'Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA)', 'Applicants for CRNA certification by examination must: 
1)  Meet all requirements for Registered Nurse licensure (have an active RN license).
2)  Have a master''s degree in nursing or anesthetic care from an approved school.

Applicants for CRNA certification by endorsement must:
1)  Meet all requirements for Registered Nurse licensure (have an active RN license).
2)  Have an official transcript sent directly to the Board by the educational institution that granted their master''s degree in nursing or anesthetic care (if the nurse anesthetist program was completed on or after June 1, 2005)*.

*Note:  For those who graduated from an nurse anesthetist program between June 1, 1988 and May 31, 2005, the official transcript must be sent directly to the State Board from the educational institution that granted their bachelor''s degree in nursing.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application/initial certificate--$200; biennial certificate renewal--$200.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nevadanursingboard.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14305', '143',
     'Certified Nursing Assistant (CNA)', 'Applicants for certification by examination must:
1a)  Have completed a state-approved training program that meets current OBRA (federal) requirements, or
1b)  Submit a transcript showing completion of a Nursing Fundamentals course from an approved nursing school (training program is valid 2 years from date of completion.)
2)  Have passed the Clinical and Knowledge exams.
3)  Submit fingerprint cards (fingerprint reports must be cleared by the Board to obtain licensure).

Applicants for certification by endorsement must:
1)  Submit a copy of their active certification/license from another state.
2)  Meet the requirements listed above under 1a or 1b.
3)  Have worked 8 hours as a CNA in a licensed medical facility within the past 2 years. 

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  initial application--$50; biennial renewal--$50; fingerprinting--$50.',
     '0', '1', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nevadanursingboard.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14501', '145',
     'Occupational Therapist', 'Applicants must: 
1)  Have graduated with a bachelors or masters degree in Occupational Therapy (official transcripts required).
2)  Passed the national exam given by the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT).
3)  Provide verification of certification from NBCOT (must be sent directly to the Board by NBCOT).
 
If licensed in another state, verification must be sent directly to the Board from the licensing agency in that state.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$150; license--$250; license renewal--$175.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', 'J', '0',
     'http://www.nvot.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14502', '145',
     'Occupational Therapy Assistant', 'Applicants must: 
1)  Have graduated with an Associate degree (official transcripts required).
2)  Passed the national exam given by the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT).
3)  Provide verification of certification from NBCOT (must be sent directly to the Board by NBCOT).
4)  Provide verification of supervision by an Occupational Therapist licensed in Nevada.

If licensed in another state, verification must be sent directly to the Board from the licensing agency in that state.

Fees are subject to change. Fees are:  application--$150; license--$175; license renewal--$125.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'J', '0',
     'http://www.nvot.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14701', '147',
     'Optometrist', 'Applicants must:
1)  Have graduated from an approved school of optometry.
2)  Pass the national board examination.
3)  Pass a state examination (75% minimum score) on the laws and regulations governing the practice of optometry in Nevada. 

If an optometrist is certified to administer and prescribe therapeutic pharmaceutical agents (TPA), she/he is required to obtain 30 hours of continuing education for annual renewal, 15 hours of which must be therapeutic-related. If an optometrist is NOT certified in therapeutics (designated as diagnostic pharmaceutical agents (DPA)), eighteen hours of continuing education are required for annual renewal.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  examination--$250; initial license--$25; annual license renewal--$350.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '9',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.optometry.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14901', '149',
     'Pharmacist', 'Applicants must:
1)  Have a degree in pharmacy from a school accredited by the Am. Council on Pharmaceutical Education and approved by the board.
2)  Have 1,740 internship hours under the direct supervision of a registered pharmacist (to fulfill this requirement you must register as an intern pharmacist and meet the state board requirements).
3)  Pass a state board and a national examination (NAPLEX and MPJE)*.

Reciprocity:  Applicants may reciprocate from another state but must take the State Board examination. (Those reciprocating from California must have taken the NAPLEX exam.)  Graduates from foreign schools must pass the FPGEC, TOFEL and TSE exams before taking the national and state exams.

*Notes:  NAPLEX = No. American Pharmacist Licensure Exam; MPJE = Multistate Pharmacy Jurisprudence Exam.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application (includes registration) --$330; examination--$680 (paid to NABP); reciprocity--$330; license renewal--$180; intern application-- $40.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.bop.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '14902', '149',
     'Pharmaceutical Technician', 'Pharmaceutical technicians and pharmaceutical technicians-in-training must register with the State Board. They may practice in all pharmacy settings under the direction of a pharmacist registered with the Nevada Board of Pharmacy.  Pharmacy Technician applicants must:
1)  Be at least 18 years old. 
2)  Have a high school degree or the equivalent.
3)  Have not been convicted of a misdemeanor or felony that involves moral turpitude, dishonesty or the unlawful possession, sale or use of drugs.
4)  Have no history of drug abuse.

In addition applicants must meet one of the following requirements:
1)  Be licensed or registered as a pharmaceutical technician in another state that licenses pharmaceutical technicians or,
2)  Have completed at least 1,500 hours in Nevada as a registered pharmaceutical technician-in-training or,
3)  Have graduated from a school accredited by the Am. Society of Healthsystem Pharmacists (ASHP) and have completed 350 hours in Nevada as a registered pharmaceutical technician-in-training or,
4)  Graduated from a school in another state that is not accredited by the ASHP and have passed the Pharmacy Technician Certification Board''s (PTCB) national exam or,
5)  Have passed the PTCB exam and completed 500 hours in Nevada as a registered technician-in-training.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  registration--$40; renewal--$40.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.bop.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15101', '151',
     'Physical Therapist', 'Applicants must:
1)  Have completed a curriculum of physical therapy approved by the Board (official transcripts required).
2)  Pass the national examination. 
3)  Submit fingerprints, photo, original transcripts and references with application.
Notes:  Application signature must be notarized.
A minimum of 1.5 continuing education units are required for physical therapist license renewal.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application and initial license--$300; national examination--$370; testing center fee--$85; examination processing fee--$25; fingerprinting--$37.50; annual license renewal--$150.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ptboard.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15102', '151',
     'Physical Therapist Assistant', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 18 years old.
2)  Completed a curriculum for physical therapist assistant approved by the State Board.
3)  Pass a national examination.
4)  Submit fingerprints, photo, original transcripts (including high school) and references with application.
Notes:  Application signature must be notarized.
The physical therapist assistant curriculum must be at least a 2-year program requiring a minimum of 60 semester hours at an accredited school.  A minimum of 1.5 continuing education units are required for physical therapist assistant license renewal.

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  application and initial license--$200; national examination--$370; testing center fee--$70; examination processing fee--$25; fingerprinting--$37.50; annual license renewal--$100.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://ptboard.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15301', '153',
     'Podiatrist', 'Applicants must:
1)  Have completed the necessary undergraduate program and graduated from an accredited doctor of podiatric medicine (DPM) program.
2)  Have completed an *APMA accredited, one-year residency.
3)  Pass the National Board of Podiatric Medical Examiners examination.
4)  Pass the American Podiatric Medical examination Part III administered by the National Board of Podiatric Medical Examiners (contact the board for more information on the required examinations).
5)  Submit fingerprints for a background check.
6)  Submit letters of verification from the hospitals and surgical centers where you had privileges in the last year.

*American Podiatric Medical Association (APMA).

If an applicant is currently licensed in another state, a certificate from that state''s licensing board is required.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application --$600 ($100 of this fee is not refundable); annual license renewal--$400; fingerprints --$38.25 (may vary).',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://podiatry.nv.gov#http://podiatry.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15302', '153',
     'Podiatry Hygienist', 'Podiatry hygienists must be licensed by the State Board.  Applicants must take the exam issued by the Board or work under the supervision of a Podiatrist for six months.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  license --$100; annual renewal -$100; fingerprints --$38.25 (may vary).',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://podiatry.nv.gov#http://podiatry.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15501', '155',
     'Professional Engineer', 'To work at the level of Professional Engineer, licensure must be obtained in one of the following disciplines of engineering:  agricultural, chemical, civil, control systems, electrical, environmental, fire protection, geological, industrial, manufacturing, mechanical, metallurgical and materials, mining/mineral, nuclear, petroleum, naval architecture/marine, structural or any other discipline deemed appropriate by the Board.  

Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 years old, of good character and good reputation.
2)  Have a bachelor''s degree in engineering from an accredited engineering program. 
3)  Pass the Fundamentals of Engineering (EI) exam*.
4)  Have 4 years of approved active engineering work experience; 2 years of the required work experience must be under the direct supervision of an engineer licensed in the discipline of engineering in which the applicant is applying.
5)  Pass the Principles and Practice of Engineering (PE) exam*.

*National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying (NCEES) exams; both are 8-hour, written examinations.

Engineer Intern:
To be eligible for certification as an engineer intern, applicants must:
1)  Be a graduate of or in the final year of an engineering curriculum of 4 years or more that has been approved by the Board and have passed the EI exam, OR
2)  Have had 4 years or more experience in engineering work that is satisfactory to the Board and have passed the EI exam.

PE exam note: Nevada offers an "early exam" option for those who have completed a BS in Engineering, have passed the Fundamentals of Engineering exam and wish to take the PE exam prior to completing the 4 years of experience that are required for licensure.  Visit the Board''s website for specific requirements.  

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  PE exam/license application--$200; reciprocity application--$200; early exam application -$100; biennial license renewal (professional engineer)--$100 for the first classification plus one-half of the renewal fee ($50) for each additional classification up to a maximum of $200; application for fundamentals of engineering (EI) exam--$30.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvboe.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15502', '155',
     'Land Surveyor', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 years old, of good character and good reputation.
2)  Pass a 2-hour Nevada State Board land surveying examination.
3)  Pass the Fundamentals of Land Surveying (LSI) exam.* 
4)  Pass the Principles and Practice of Land Surveying (PLS) examination.*
Note:  An applicant for the PLS exam must have completed a 4 year approved college program in surveying and have 4 years of experience in land surveying.

*National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying (NCEES) exams (8-hour and 6-hour written tests.)

To be eligible for certification as a land surveyor intern applicants must:
1)  Be a graduate of, or in the final year of, a land-surveying or engineering curriculum of 4 years approved by the board.
2)  Have passed the Fundamentals of Land Surveying (LSI) exam.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application and exam (professional land surveyor)--$200; biennial license renewal (professional land surveyor)--$100; application for Fundamentals/Intern (LSI) exam--$30; PLS Nevada specific exam--$100.',
     '0', '1', '2', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.nvboe.org', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15701', '157',
     'Psychologist', 'Psychologists working in private practices, as well as those working for the Nevada State Department of Human Resources, must be licensed through the Board of Psychological Examiners. (Psychologists who intend to work in public schools must meet the requirements necessary to obtain an endorsement through the Department of Education. Requirements for school psychologists are listed separately.)

Applicants must:
1)  Be at least 21 and of good moral character.
2)  Have a doctoral degree from an accredited institution in an APA-accredited program or a regionally accredited program shown to be equivalent.
3)  Have completed pre and post doctoral supervised experience under a licensed psychologist (1,750 hours in each).
4)  Pass a national written examination.
5)  Pass a State Board examination. 
6)  Submit fingerprints for a background check.

Note on Psychological Interns and Assistants:  individuals must register with the Board as a psychological intern if they wish to obtain predoctoral internship supervised experience and as a psychological assistant if they wish to obtain the postdoctoral supervised experience required for licensure.  Visit the Board''s website for registration requirements.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$100; state examination--$270; license certificate--$25; biennial license renewal--$500; late license renewal penalty--$100; psychological assistant application--$100; psychological assistant registration--$250;  psychological intern application - $100; psychological intern registration- $75.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://psyexam.nv.gov#http://psyexam.nv.gov#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15702', '157',
     'Behavior Analyst and Assistant Behavior Analyst', 'Applicants for Behavior Analyst licensure must:
1)  Be at least 21 and of good moral character.
2)  Have a master''s degree from an accredited institution in a field of social science or special education.
3)  Hold current certification as a Board Certified Behavior Analyst (from the BACB).
4)  Pass a State Board examination. 
5)  Submit fingerprints for a background check.

Applicants for Assistant Behavior Analyst licensure must: 
1)  Be at least 21 and of good moral character.
2)  Have a bachelor''s degree from an accredited institution in a field of social science or special education.
3)  Hold current certification as a Board Certified Assistant Behavior Analyst (from the BACB).
4)  Pass a State Board examination. 
5)  Submit fingerprints for a background check.

Note:  The Board also certifies Autism Behavior Interventionists.  Visit the Board Website for more information.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$100; state examination--$75; biennial license renewal--$400 (Behavior Analyst) - $275 (Assistant Behavior Analyst).',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '9',
     '0', '4', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://psyexam.nv.gov#http://psyexam.nv.gov/#', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15901', '159',
     'Veterinarian', 'Applicants must:
1)  Have completed a four-year veterinary medicine program at a school approved by the American Veterinary Medical Association with course work emphasizing the area of specialization.
2a)  Pass the national board (NBE) and clinical competency (CCT) examinations; or
2b)  Pass the North American Veterinary Licensing Examination (NAVLE) within 5 years of application.
3)  Pass a State Board jurisprudence examination.

The Board accepts candidates for the Nevada examination who are within a year of graduating. The applicant must submit a letter of good standing from the dean of the school from which he/she will graduate.

Applicants who have been licensed in another state must submit a letter of good standing from the state in which he/she is currently licensed as well as a letter of good standing from each state in which he/she was previously licensed.

Applicants who have completed a veterinary medicine program outside the U.S. must also present the Education Committee of Foreign Veterinary Graduates (ECFVG) certificate to the Board before being accepted to take the examination.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application/examination/initial licensing--$200; annual license renewal (active status)--$250; annual license renewal (inactive status)--$130.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://nvvetboard.us', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15902', '159',
     'Veterinary Technician', 'Veterinary technicians working in veterinary hospitals must be licensed.  Applicants must:
1a)  Have graduated from an animal health technology program approved by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA), by the state Education Department (or its equivalent in the state where the college is located) or by the Board, or
1b)  Have a bachelor''s in an animal science related field and meet the experience requirement listed in item 1d, or
1c)  Complete an accelerated veterinary technician program approved by the board and meet the experience requirement listed in item 1d.
1d)  Options 1b and 1c must provide proof of at least 4,000 hours of supervised clinical experience in a veterinary hospital that is verified by an active, practicing veterinarian.
2)  Pass the Nevada Veterinary Technician Jurisprudence Examination (covering applicable state laws).
3)  Pass the Veterinary Technician National Examination (VTNE) which is offered three times per year.
4)  Provide a letter of recommendation from a person associated with the practice of veterinary medicine.

Veterinary Technician-in-Training:  Candidates must be 18 years of age, have a high school diploma or equivalent, be of good moral character, be enrolled in a school or program of training that is approved by the AVMA or the Board, and participate in training while on the job.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  Nevada jurisprudence examination/initial licensing--$100 (VTNE=$300; administered at Prometric Testing Centers); annual license renewal--$75; tech-in-training application - $50.',
     '0', '3', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://nvvetboard.us', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '15903', '159',
     'Euthanasia Technician', 'People who work for organizations that euthanize animals using controlled substances must be trained and licensed by the Board of Veterinary Medical Examiners. The one-day training is scheduled once or twice per year. Participants must pass a written and practical exam to receive a certificate. Those receiving a euthanasia technician certificate are also registered with the Board of Pharmacy.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  examinations/initial licensing--$200; annual license renewal--$100.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '2', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://nvvetboard.us', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '16101', '161',
     'Certified Court Reporter', 'Applicants must pass the dictation test at 200 words per minute with 97.5 percent accuracy and must pass a written test with at least 70 percent. The written test covers punctuation, grammar, vocabulary, spelling, medical and legal terminology, as well as Nevada Revised Statutes, Nevada Administrative Code and Supreme Court rules applying to court reporting. Examinations are held in Las Vegas.  Continuing education hours are required for license renewal.

Subject to the approval of the Board, applicants must have one of the following to qualify to take the examination:
1)  Proof of satisfactory completion of a court reporting program; or 
2)  A current license from another state; or 
3)  A valid Registered Professional Reporter (RPR) certificate or higher from the National Court Reporters Association; or 
4)  A certificate as a certified verbatim reporter from the National Verbatim Reporters Association; or
5)  One year of continuous work experience as a shorthand reporter in a non-certifying state in the year immediately preceding the date of application.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  certificate of application/renewal--$200; application for exam--$150; application for inactive--$100; reinstatement (after inactive status)--$75.',
     '0', '1', '9', '1', '9',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://crptr.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '16301', '163',
     'Emergency Medical Technician - Clark County', 'EMTs who want to work in Clark County must be certified through the Southern Nevada Health District. EMTs outside of Clark County must be certified through the State of Nevada. (State of Nevada requirements are listed separately.) 

Applicants for EMT certification must:
1)  Be at least 18 years of age.
2)  Have a current, valid driver''s license.
3)  Have successfully completed a state-approved EMT course that meets the U.S. Department of Transportation''s (DOT) national EMT certification standards.
4)  Have current EMT certification from the National Registry of EMT''s (NREMT).
5)  Have a current, valid healthcare provider level CPR card as approved by SNHD.

Applicants for Advanced EMT (AEMT) must:
1)  Meet the EMT requirements (above).
2)  Have successfully completed a state-approved AEMT course that meets the U.S. Department of Transportation''s (DOT) national AEMT certification standards.
3)  Have current AEMT certification from the National Registry of EMT''s (NREMT).

Applicants for Paramedic must:
1)  Meet the EMT requirements (above).
2)  Have successfully completed a state-approved Paramedic course that meets the U.S. Department of Transportation''s (DOT) national Paramedic certification standards.
3)  Have current Paramedic certification from the National Registry of EMT''s (NREMT).
4)  Have a current, valid course in Advanced Cardiac Life Support procedures.

Notes:  EMT, AEMT and Paramedic applicants must not currently be under investigation or have had any healthcare-related certification, license, medical direction/control, or clinical privileges limited, suspended or revoked.  Applicants for licensure to work for a permitted ambulance agency will be fingerprinted for an FBI background report.

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees:  certificate issuance - $37; renewal - $36; attendant license (EMT & AEMT) - $61; attendant license (Paramedic) - $99; attendant license renewal - $15.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '2',
