     'http://southernnevadahealthdistrict.org/ems', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '16501', '165',
     'Pest Control Applicator -  Principal', 'Major fields of pest control are aerial, agricultural-ground, and urban-structural. Specific categories of pest control are included with each major field of pest control.

Individuals applying for licensure as company principals must:
1a)  Have 2 years of documented pesticide application or pest control experience in the category(ies) applied for; or
1b)  Have a combination of 6 months of documented pesticide application or pest control experience in the category(ies) applied for and 16 college credit hours in biological science (at least 8 hours must be directly related to the field of pest control applied for.)
2)  Pass the appropriate examinations. 

Note:  Primary principals must also submit fingerprints for a background check.

Contact the Department of Agriculture for information on training sessions, the exam or appointments.

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  examination--$25/exam; initial pest control licensing--$50; annual pest control license renewal--$50.',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '0',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://agri.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '16502', '165',
     'Pest Control Applicator - Operator or Agent', 'Individuals applying for pest control applicator licensure in the operator/agent category must pass the appropriate examinations, but do not need to have previous pest control experience. 

Contact the Department of Agriculture for information on training sessions, the exam or appointments.

Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  examination--$25/exam; initial pest control licensing--$50; annual pest control license renewal--$50.',
     '0', '1', '9', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://agri.nv.gov/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '16701', '167',
     'Boxer, Kickboxer and Mixed Martial Artist (Professional Contestant)', 'Applicants must be at least 18 years old and have a current Federal ID card (if professional boxer or mixed martial artist.)  They must submit results from a dilated ophthalmologic exam done by an Ophthalmologist; a yearly sports physical (Physical Examination Report - Professional Boxer/Unarmed combatant) including an original laboratory report with the applicant''s name and the date the HIV,  CBC, Hepatitis B and Hepatitis C tests were taken.  The HIV test must be done within 30 days of submitting all requirements to become licensed, the CBC and Hepatitis tests can be done within the calendar year.  Also required are the results of an MRI and MRA done within the last 5 years. Applicants must submit to drug testing if required by the Commission.   
There are additional requirements for the following individuals:
1)  Amateur boxers making their professional debut.
2)  Boxers over the age of 35 and younger than the age of 18.
3)  Boxers with no activity for 36 months.
4)  Boxers who have competed in over 425 professional rounds.  

Visit the Athletic Commission website for more detailed information on the licensing requirements.  

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  application--$25, plus actual costs for a physical examination by a qualified physician and for laboratory tests.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '2', '9', '0',
     'http://boxing.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '16702', '167',
     'Boxing Promoter', 'Boxing promoters must be licensed by the Athletic Commission. Visit the Commission website for further information about requirements.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are:  promoters--$500; fingerprint cards - $38.25 each (NHP).',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://boxing.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '16703', '167',
     'Timekeeper or Judge (Professional Ring Officials)', 'Professional Ring Officials (referees, timekeepers and judges) must be licensed by the Athletic Commission.  Applicants must be at least 21 years old and not have been convicted of a felony or other crime involving turpitude.  The Commission determines when additional ring officials are needed and when the licensing exam will be conducted.  Visit the Commission website for further information about requirements.

Fees may be subject to change. Fees are: referees--$75; timekeepers and judges--$50; ringside doctor--$100.',
