     'http://www.ndow.org/', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '20501', '205',
     'Nevada Certified Court Interpreter', 'Applicants for Certified Court Interpreter must:
1)  Complete the orientation workshop for interpreters in Nevada courts offered by the Administrative Office of the Courts (AOC).
2)  Pass the Nevada written exam given by the AOC (minimum score of 80%).
3)  Pass the Nevada oral exam given by the AOC (minimum score of 70%), 
4)  Obtain 40 hours of Nevada court observation or work within the 12 months immediately preceding request for certification, 
5)  Submit the Certification Request form which includes a criminal history check, 
6)  Swear to the required oath and the Code of Professional Responsibility for Interpreters in Nevada courts.

Applicants for Registered Interpreter (applies to those for whom no oral exam has been developed in his/her particular language by the Consortium for Language Access in the Courts (CLAC)) must:
1)  Complete the orientation workshop for Interpreters in Nevada courts offered by the Administrative Office of the Courts (AOC), 
2)  Pass the Nevada written exam given by the AOC (minimum score of 80%),
3)  Undergo the oral proficiency interview (OPI) by ALTA Language Services (score of at least 12) or Language Testing International (rating of "Superior" proficiency),
4)  Completed the Nevada court observation requirement of 40 hours,
5)  Submit the Certification Request application which includes a criminal history check,
6)  Swear to the required oath and the Code of Professional Responsibility for Interpreters in Nevada courts.

Fees are subject to change.  Fees are:  application --$50; orientation workshop registration --$200 (NV residents) or $400 (non-residents); written exam -- $75 (NV residents) or $150 (non-residents); oral exam -- $300 (NV residents) or $600 (non-residents).',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '9',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://interpreters.nvcourts.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '20701', '207',
     'Athletic Trainer', 'Applicants must:
1)  Be of good moral character.
2)  Be a U.S. citizen or lawfully entitled to work in the U.S.
3)  Have at least a bachelor''s degree in a program of study approved by the Board.
4)  Submit fingerprints for a criminal background report.
5)  Pass the National Athletic Trainers Association Board of Certification Exam (NATABOC), or submit proof of current NATABOC certification.

Fees are subject to change.  Fees are:  initial license --$300; annual renewal --$150.',
     '0', '2', '2', '1', '1',
     '0', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://nevadaathletictrainers.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '20901', '209',
     'Participants in Horse Racing', 'Horse racing participants, officials and support staff must be licensed in Nevada.  This includes, but is not limited to:  trainers, jockeys, grooms, exercise riders, owners, veterinarians, outriders, vendors, scale personnel, timers, paddock judges, race office personnel, stewards, announcers, mutuel managers and employees.  

Fees range from $17 to $63 for a two-year license.

For more information on the functions requiring licensure and the license requirements, contact the Gaming Control Board''s Elko office.',
     '0', '1', '0', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://gaming.nv.gov', '20160114'),
    ('32', '01', '21101', '211',
     'Massage Therapist', 'Applicants must:  
1)  Be at least 18 years old.
2)  Have at least 500 hours of schooling (transcripts must be submitted directly to the Board).
3)  Have passed the Federation of State Massage Therapy Boards'' written exam (Massage and Bodywork Licensing Exam (MBLEx)).
4)  Provide a passport sized photo and a photocopy of a current state issued I.D., or alien resident card if applicable.
5)  Submit to fingerprinting for a background check.

Note:  Visit the Federation of State Massage Therapy Board''s website for more information on the MBLEx.

Reciprocity:  In addition to items 1-5 listed above, applicants must submit a copy of their current massage therapist/business license and have their current licensing authority submit verification of their status being in good standing with no disciplinary actions pending.  This verification must be sent directly from the out-of-state board to the Nevada Board via the form provided or a letter.

Fees:  Fees may be subject to change.  Fees are:  application - $100; license - $150;  background check - $125; temporary license application - $100; temporary license (90 days) - $50.',
