    ('32', '01', '21301', '213',
     'Certified Public Librarian', 'This certification is for employees of public libraries that serve a population under 50,000 and do not have an employee with a Master''s in Library Science (MLS) performing the administrator, reference and children''s librarian duties; it does not apply to individuals who hold a MLS.

Applicants for certification must:
1a)  Have a bachelor''s degree and at least 2 years of library experience, or
1b)  Have an associate degree and at least 4 years of library experience, or
1c)  Have a high school diploma or GED and at least 7 years of library experience.
2)  Have taken 21 semester credit hours in subjects specified by State Library and Archives.
3)  Submit two fingerprint cards.
4)  Provide a professional letter of recommendation.
The completed application must be notarized and official transcripts are required (no photocopies).',
