     'https://www.nhes.nh.gov/elmi/products/licertocc/documents/gameopse.pdf', '20240906'),
    ('33', '01', 'RAC03', 'RAC',
     'Game Operator (Professional), Employer', '<p>Professional Game Operators operate games of chance on behalf of charitable organizations licensed to host such games. A Game Operator Employer employs, supervises, and controls game operators. A Primary Game Operator may serve as the Game Operator Employer.</p>
<p><strong>Legislation:</strong>&nbsp;NH RSA 287-D; Administrative Rules Chapter Pari 1200 (being renumbered as Lot 7200)</p>
<p><strong>Application Requirements:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Submit a fully completed license application form</li>
<li>Provide supporting documentation, including:</li>
<ul>
<li>A description of the licensed premises where the games will be played;</li>
<li>A copy of the entity''s certificate of good standing from the New Hampshire Department of Revenue Administration; and</li>
<li>A copy of all required bonds, as established by the Commission based on the applicant''s normal outstanding obligations of charity payments and state taxes</li>
</ul>
<li>Submit application fee</li>
<li>Submit a complete and notarized Criminal Records Release Authorization form, along with a complete set of fingerprints taken by a qualified law enforcement agency, and payment of the applicable fee (please refer to the NH State Police for additional information or to confirm current charges)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Examination:</strong>&nbsp;Not required</p>
<p><strong>Continuing Education:</strong>&nbsp;Not required</p>
<p><strong>Fees:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Application: $750</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<ul>Licenses expire on December 31 of the licensed year</ul>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Reciprocity:</strong> Not permitted</p>
<p>revised Jan 2018</p>',
