    ('33', '01', 'WMD02', 'WMD',
     'Solid Waste Operator, Principal', '<p>Solid Waste Operators deal with a wide range of solid wastes. Principal Solid Waste Operators may work at any solid waste facility in any capacity.</p>
<p><strong>Legislation:</strong>&nbsp;NH RSA 149-M:6; Administrative Rules Chapter Env-Sw 1600</p>
<p><strong>Certification Requirements:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>First-time applicants must complete the New Hampshire Department of Environmental Services'' Basic Solid Waste Operator Training Course</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Examination:</strong>&nbsp;Written examination required</p>
<p><strong>Continuing Education:</strong> 2.5 hours of continuing education required annually</p>
<p><strong>Fees</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Application: $50</li>
<li>Annual renewal: $50</li>
<li>Late renewal: $75</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Reciprocity:</strong>&nbsp; Not specified</p>
<p>revised Jan 2018</p>',
