    ('47', '01', '1700000004', '37',
     'ENGINEER INTERNS', 'ENGINEER INTERN

S<br><br>An individual certified as an engineer intern may work on engineering projects under the supervision of a registered professional engineer. 

<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:
<br>Must be of good character and repute, and satisfy education and examination requirements. 

<br><br>EDUCATION AND EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:
<br>Graduation from a curriculum of 4 years or more leading to a baccalaureate degree in engineering approved by the board <BR><br>OR

<br>A prospective graduate and senior in good standing in a curriculum of 4 years or more leading to a baccalaureate degree in engineering approved by the Board may qualify by passing a minimum eight-hour written examination prepared by the National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying in the Fundamentals of Engineering.

<br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:
<br>Tennessee Society of Professional Engineers<br>
Corner Stone Square, Suite 503
<br>530 Church Street
<br>Nashville, Tennessee  37219<br>
(615)242-2486

<br><br>Source of Additional Information:

<br>National Council of Examiners for Engineering & Surveying  (NCEES)<br>
P. O. Box 1686<br>
Clemson, S.C.  29633-1686
<br>(800)250-3196<br><br>YEAR ACTIVE LICENSES:  1999 - 217',
