    ('47', '01', '1700000005', '58',
     'LAND SURVEYOR', 'LAND SURVEYOR<br><br>Land Surveyor means a person who is engaged in the practice of land surveying.<BR><BR>Practice of land surveying means any service of work, the adequate performance of which involves the application of special knowledge of the principles of mathematics, the related physical and applied sciences and the relevant requirements of law for adequate evidence to the act of measuring and locating lines, angles, elevations, natural and man-made features in the air, on the surface of the earth, within underground workings and on the beds of bodies of water for the purpose of determining areas and volumes, for the monumenting of property boundaries and for the platting and layout of lands and subdivisions of land, including the topography, drainage, alignment and grades of streets, and for the preparation and perpetuation of maps, records, plats, field notes, records and property descriptions that represent these surveys.<BR><BR>REQUIREMENTS:  You are required to submit the following with your Professional Land-Surveyor-in-Training (PLSIT) application:<BR>1. A $25 application licensure fee<BR>2. Proof of Education: A copy of your high school diploma or GED certificate; or a copy of an associate''s degree transcript along with a completed course reporting form; or a copy of a bachelor''s degree transcript along with a completed course reporting form.<BR>3. Proof of 4 years of progressive practical experience, 2 years of which shall have been under the direct supervision of a practicing professional land surveyor; or proof of 10 years of progressive practical experience satisfactory to the board, 6 years of which shall have been under the direct supervision of a practicing professional land surveyor.<BR>4. Three character references, one of whom is a professionaive regulatory environment for consumer service industries.<BR><BR>The PLSIT Examination must be passed prior to application for full licensure.',
     '1', '2', '2', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '1700000006', '37',
     'PROFESSIONAL LANDSCAPE ARCHITECT', 'PROFESSIONAL LANDSCAPE ARCHITECT<br><br>Landscape architecture is the art and science of analysis, planning, design, management, preservation, rehabilitation, and integration of the man-made environment with the natural environment. Landscape architects plan and design land areas for parks, recreational facilities, private homes, campuses, and other open spaces.<BR><BR>Applicants for registration must complete:<BR> a degree in landscape architecture accredited by the Landscape Architectural Accreditation Board (LAAB)<BR> obtain three (3) years of landscape architectural experience satisfactory to the Board<BR> pass the Landscape Architect Registration Examination prepared by the Council of Landscape Architectural Registration Boards (CLARB)<BR><BR>REQUIREMENTS:<BR>1. Notarized and completed application<BR>2. Fees<BR>3. Five (5) professional references (three must be from registered architects, engineers, or landscape architects) - references in the CLARB record may be accepted if they meet the requirements of Rule 0120-01-.09 and are less than two years old<BR>4. Official transcript(s) - not required if CLARB record is submitted<BR>5. CLARB Record (comity and reapply only)<BR>6. Continuing education documentation and expired license affidavit (reapply only)<BR><BR>FEES:<BR>Exam Application Fee: $30<BR>Comity Application/Reapplication Fee: $55<BR>Biennial Registration/Renewal Fee: $140<BR>Late Renewal Penalty Fee: $10 (per month or fraction of a month for six months following registration expiration date)<BR>Duplicate Wall Certificate: $25<BR><BR>ADDITIONAL:<BR>Comity applicants (applicants registered in another jurisdiction) must hold an unexpired CLARB certificate and must be currently registered in at least one other jurisdiction. Individuals who are reapplying must have been previously registered in Tennessee, must complete 24 hours of continuing education in the two years preceding reapplication, and must hold an unexpired CLARB certificate.',
     '1', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '2700000015', '77',
     'TATTOO PROFESSIONAL', 'TATTOO PROFESSIONAL<br><br>A person who employs any method of placing designs, letters, figures, symbols, cosmetics or other marks under the skin of a person with ink or color by aid of needles or instruments under the auspices of a licensed tattoo studio. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>Must train for one year under a licensed tattoo artist who has practiced under a Tennessee licensee for three years and satisfy the education and examination requirements. (A temporary license can be issued under appropriate circumstances to a person licensed in another state.)<br><br>EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS: <br>Successfully complete the Alliance of Professional Tattooist course in sterilization, a local or state program in sterilization offered by the Health Department, or a course approved by the local health department. <br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS: <br>Pass an examination administered by a local health department. <br><br>RENEWAL:<br>Annual renewal is required.',
     '1', '2', '1', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '2700000016', '77',
     'BODY PIERCING ARTISTS/TECHNICIAN', 'BODY PIERCING ARTISTS/TECHNICIAN<br><br> Body piercing means the piercing of any part of the body for compensation by someone, other than a physician, who utilizes a needle or other instrument for the purpose of inserting an object into the body for non-medical purposes; body piercing includes ear piercing, except when the ear piercing procedure is performed with an ear piercing gun.  This includes an individual who engages in the practice/service of body piercing, regardless of the type of body ornament utilized or body area to be pierced.  Such individual must be licensed by the Tennessee Bureau of Health Services, Division of General Environmental Health.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS<br>Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Each applicant for a body piercing establishment permit (i.e., the body piercing operator) and/or for a body piercing technician license shall undergo a training program before receiving a permit or license.  The training shall include at least one of the following: (a) the Alliance of Professional Tattooist course in sterilization; (b) a course approved by the Commissioner in methods and techniques for the proper sterilization of instruments and materials used in body; or (c) present acceptable evidence of having satisfactorily completed an approved course of instruction in sterilization techniques for blood borne pathogens and methods through a college medical sterilization course.   Each applicant for a body piercing technician''s license shall be required to take and pass an examination concerning blood borne pathogens, sterilization techniques and the provisions of T.C.A. Title 62, Chapter 38.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Yes, written exam prescribed by the Commissioner or documentation of a similar exam given with a course as required in 1200-23-6-.07(2) and approved by the Commissioner.<br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Not listed<br><br>RENEWAL:<br> Every year in January.<br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:<br>ALLIANCE OF PROFESSIONAL TATTOOISTS<br>22052 W. 66TH STREET, SUITE 225, SHAWNEE, KS 66226<br>INFO@SAFE-TATTOOS.COM <.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '9',
     '2', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.tn.gov/content/dam/tn/health/documents/1200-23-06.pdf', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '3100000001', '59',
     'AESTHETICIAN', 'AESTHETICIAN<br><br>An aesthetician does one or more of the following:  massages, cleans, stimulates, manipulates, exercises, beautifies or performs similar work with hands or mechanical or electrical apparatus or by use of cosmetic preparations, tonics, lotions or creams; places or applies artificial eyelashes, gives facials, applies makeup, gives skin care or removes superfluous hair by tweezing, depilatories or waxing.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>	Be at least sixteen years of age having completed and passed a course of instruction of not less than 750 hours in the practice and theory of aesthetics at a school of cosmetology.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>A written and practical examination is required Total included with Cosemetologists.',
     '1', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '3100000002', '44',
     'DENTAL ASSISTANTS', 'DENTAL ASSISTANTS<br><br>A dental assistant assists in the care of dental patients under the direct supervision of the dentist. A dental assistant may not remove hard or soft deposits by scaling or curettage from surfaces of teeth, and may not perform any dental function that requires professional judgment or skill. A dental assistant can perform coronal polishing, monitoring nitrous oxide sedation, expose radiographs, placing sealants, restorative or prosthetic function only if certified to do so by the Board. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>Be eighteen (18) years of age. Be of good moral character and reputation. Be a U.S. or Canadian citizen or entitled to live in the United States.  Must have graduated high school or have gotten a GED.  <br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS: <br>Successful completion of examinations administered by the course providers approved by the Board is required for each certification. <br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION: <br>Must maintain current training in C.P.R. <br><br>RENEWAL REQUIREMENTS: <br>Every two years. License expires in birth month according to even or odd birth year.',
     '1', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '4', '9', 'D', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '3100000003', '34',
     'MASSAGE THERAPIST', 'MASSAGE THERAPIST<br><br>A massage therapist is a person who is licensed by the board and who practices massage for compensation.  Massage means the manipulation of the soft tissues of the body with the intention of positivelyt affecting the health and well being of the client.

<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:
<br>Be at least 18 years of age; of good moral character, free of conviction of the offense of prostitution or sexual misconduct; satisfy education or experience requirements.

<br><br>EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>
Successfully complete the curriculum of one or more postsecondary academic institutions for massage, bodywork, and/or somatic therapy totaling 500 hours or more, where the institution is approved by the Tennessee Higher Education Commission or its equivalent in another state.<BR><BR>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<BR>Massage and Bodyworks Licensing Examination (MBLEx). A temporary license may be issued if a person works at all times under the supervision of a licensed person and successfully completes an exam.

<br><br>RENEWAL:
<br>Renewal is required every two years and is contingent on satisfying continuing education requirements.<BR><BR>CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<BR>All licensees must complete twenty-five (25) hours of continuing education every two (2) calendar years.',
