    ('47', '01', '1300000012', '29',
     'REGISTERED TRAINEE, APPRAISER', 'REGISTERED TRAINEE, APPRAISER<br><br> A registered trainee in the appraisal field is taking qualifying education courses and working with a supervising appraiser to learn the fundamentals involved in inspecting properties and preparing appraisal reports presenting an opinion on the market value of adequately described properties. <br><br> REQUIREMENTS:  Satisfy the education and other requirements, pledge to comply with the standards set forth by statute, and understand the types of misconduct which can bring about disciplinary action. Be 18 years of age. <br><br> EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Hold a GED or high school diploma. Complete 79 hours of qualifying education  as specified by the Board within five years preceding the date of application.<br><br> OTHER REQUIREMENTS:  Obtain the following certificates:  Fifteen hour US PAP,  Appraiser Principles, Appraiser Procedures, and Sponsor/Trainee.  Complete a sponsor/trainee supervisor course. Submit fingerprint receipts. To obtain experience, must have a supervisor appraiser.',
