     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '1700000003', '37',
     'PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER', 'PROFESSIONAL ENGINEER<br><br>

Engineers use the knowledge of mathematical and natural sciences to develop ways to utilize the materials and forces of nature for the benefit of humankind. Engineers practice in a wide range of disciplines, from traditional disciplines like civil, mechanical, and electrical, to more specialized disciplines like nuclear and industrial.<BR>Applicants for registration must complete:<BR>  a four-year degree in engineering approved by the Board<BR>  pass the Fundamentals of Engineering examination (which is waived if the applicant has 12 or more years of engineering experience acceptable to the Board)<BR>  obtain four (4) years of engineering experience satisfactory to the Board<BR>  pass the Principles and Practice of Engineering examination.<BR><BR>REQUIREMENTS:<BR>1. Notarized and completed application<BR>2. Fees<BR>3. Five (5) professional references (three must be from registered engineers)<BR>4. Official transcript(s)<BR>5. Verification of registration or examination from other state(s) (comity and reapply only)<BR>6. Continuing education documentation and expired license affidavit (reapply only)<BR><BR>Note: If an applicant has a National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying (NCEES) record, the references (provided they meet the requirements of Rule 0120-01-.09 and are less than two years old), transcript(s), and verification(s) in the record will be accepted and do not need to be submitted separately.<BR><BR>',
