     'ATTORNEY', 'ATTORNEY<br><br>A lawyer prepares legal documents, does courtroom work and acts as advocate, counsel, and negotiator for clients.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Be of good moral character and satisfy education and examination requirements.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>A Juris Doctor (JD) degree from an ABA accredited or Tennessee Board of Law Examiners approved law school.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>A written examination with two sections: the multi-state (multiple choice) and an essay examination.  Administered biannually, February and July.<br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Twelve hours of continuing legal education (CLE) plus 3 hours of ethics professionalism CLE must be completed annually.  Of this 12 hours, all attorneys must include 5 in classroom hours.  There is a cap of 8 hours of distance learning or online hours that can be counted towards compliance each year.<br><br>RECIPROCITY WITH OTHER STATES:<br>An attorney who has been actively engaged in the full time practice of law for five of the last seven years, may waive into Tennessee without taking the Bar examination.<br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:<br>A complete list of professional organizations can befound on the Tennessee Bar Association website at:  www.tba.or/info/tennessee-legal-organizations',
     '1', '1', '2', '1', '2',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '2300000002', '102',
     'COURT REPORTERS', 'COURT REPORTER<br><br>Court reporters make  a verbatim record by means of manual shorthand, machine shorthand, closed microphone voice dictation silencer or by electronic recording of any testimony given under oath before or for submission to, any court, referee or court examiner, by any board, commission or other body or in any other proceeding where a verbatim record is required.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Satisfactory proof of graduation from a court reporting program or its equivalent. <br><br> EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Proof of passage of the National Court Reporters Association registered professional reporter examination, the National Verbatim Reporters Association certified verbatim reporter examination, or the American Association of Electronic Reporters and Transcribers certified electronic court reporter examination.<br><br>CONTINUING  EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Twenty (20)  hours  or 2 continuing education credits.<br><br>RENEWAL:<br>Every two years<br>',
