     'TEACHER', 'TEACHERS<BR><BR>Teachers instruct students in subject matter using various teaching methods including lecture and demonstration; use audiovisual aids and other materials to supplement presentations; prepare an outline for course work; assign lessons and correct homework; keep attendance records; and maintain discipline in the classroom.  Teacher''s license can be endorsed for many specialties, including elementary education, middle grades and secondary subject-specific endorsements, as well as many others.<br><br>

REQUIREMENTS:
<br>Be at least 18 years old and satisfy education and examination requirements.  Contact license authority for additional requirements for endorsements. 

<br><br>EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:
<br>Completion of teacher preparation program at an approved educator preparation provider.  Contact the licensing authority for additional requirements for endorsements and for updated requirements for the practitioner occupational teacher''s license.

<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Praxis Exams (Core Academic Skills & Specialty Area Tests) administered by the Educational Testing Services<br><br>

RECIPROCITY WITH OTHER STATES:  <br>Yes

