     'ATHLETIC TRAINER', 'ATHLETIC TRAINER<br><br>Athletic trainers provide medical management, prevention, and treatment of athletic injuries.  They design training programs, treat and rehabilitate injuries under the direction of a physician or therapist and use knowledge of nutrition, conditioning, protective equipment and psychology to help athletic performance. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Satisfy education and experience requirements and examination requirements.<br><br>EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS:<br>The applicant must have received a baccalaureate degree, have obtained at least 1,500 hours of supervised athletic training experience and successfully completed at least one formal course in each of the following areas: health, human anatomy, kinesiology/biomechanics, human physiology, physiology of exercise, basic athletic training, and advanced athletic training.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Administered four (4) times a year.<br><br>RENEWAL REQUIREMENTS:<BR> Every two years.<BR><BR>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:<br>National Athletic Trainers Association<br>1620 Valwood Parkway, Suite 115<br>Carrollton, Texas  75006<br>(214) 637-6282',
