     'CHIROPRACTIC PHYSICIAN', 'CHIROPRACTIC PHYSICIAN<br><br>A chiropractor manipulates the spinal column and adjacent tissues to prevent disease and correct abnormalities of the human body believed to be caused by interference with the nervous system.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Be of good moral character, satisfy education and examination requirements.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Must have 60 hours from an accredited college or university and be a graduate from an accredited (CCE) Chiropractic College. <br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>The national exam parts I, II, III and  physiotherapy are required; a written and practical examination are administered at the discretion of the board.  (Part IV of the national examination is under consideration as an additional requirement.)<br><br>RENEWAL:<br>Renewal is required every two years<br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:<br>Tennessee Chiropractic Association<br>2123 8th Avenue South<br>Nashville, TN  37204<br>Phone:  (615) 383-6231',
