     'DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST', 'DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONISTS<br><br>Dietitians and nutritionists provide medical nutrition therapy and nutritional education; set up and supervise food service systems for institutions such as hospitals, prisons and schools; do research; and develop and administer nutrition care standards and systems.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Be at least 18 years of age, of good moral character and satisfy education, experience, and examination requirements.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>	Minimum of a baccalaureate degree in a program approved by the Board of Dietitian/Nutritionist Examiners.<br><br>EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENT:  <br>As required by the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics (Formerly the American Dietetic Association).  Must be completed prior to taking the examination.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:  <br>National examination administered by the Commission on Dietetic Registration of the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics.<br><br>RENEWAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Every two (2) years.<br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:<br>Academy of Nutrition and Dietetucs<br>120 South Riverside Plaza, Suite 2000<br>Chicago, IL  60606-6995<br>Toll-Free:  (800) 877-1600<br>Phone:  (312) 899-0040',
