     'PHARMACIST', 'PHARMACIST<br><br>A pharmacist prepares, compounds, and dispenses drugs and devices, whether dispensed on the prescription of a medical practitioner or legally dispensed or sold directly to the ultimate consumer; insures the proper and safe storage and distribution of drugs; maintains proper records and relates information as required concerning such drugs and medicines and their therapeutic values and uses in the treatment and prevention of disease.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Be at least 21 years of age and satisfy the experience, education and examination requirements.  <br><br>EXPERIENCE:<br>Fifteen hundred (1,500) hours internship.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Graduate of an accredited College of Pharmacy (BS or Pharm. D degree)<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>National licensing examination (NAPLEX) administered several times each year.<br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Thirty (30) contact hours each two (2) years of which fifteen (15) shall be in line contact programs as determined by the ACPE designation.  A maximum of six (6) contact hours may be approved for programs approved by the board.  <br><br>RECIPROCITY WITH OTHER STATES:<br>All states except California and Florida.',
