     'REFLEXOLOGIST', 'REFLEXOLOGISTS  <br><br>Engage in the practice and application of specific pressures to reflex points in the hands and feet only.  A registered reflexologist may not use invasive procedures during the practice of reflexology, and may not diagnose or treat for specific diseases, practice sponal or other joint manipulations, prescribe, administer, or adjust medication, or prescribe or administer vitamins.<BR><BR>REQUIREMENTS:  <BR>Be at least 18 years of age and of good moral character.<BR><BR>EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:  <BR>Completion of a two hundred (200) hour reflexology only course offered by an institution approved by the Tennessee higher education commission or its equivalent in other states.<br><br>RENEWAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Every two (2) years.<br><BR>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:<BR>American Reflexology Certification Board<BR>2586 Knightsbridge Road SE<BR>Grand Rapids, MI  49546<BR>Phone:  (303) 933-6921>BR?Fax:  (303) 904-0460',
