     'SPEECH LANGUAGE PATHOLOGIST', 'SPEECH LANGUAGE PATHOLOGIST<br><br>Applies non-medical procedures for measurement, testing, assessment, prediction, consultation or instruction in relation to development disorders of speech, voice or language or oral, pharyngeal and laryngeal sensorimotor competencies. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Be at least 18 years of age, of good moral character, and satisfy education and examination requirements.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>A Master''s Degree in Speech Pathology  from an accredited institution.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>ASHA certified or has taken the Praxis examination in Speech Pathology with a minimum score of 600 or 162, depending on the version taken; administered by Education Testing Service, Princeton, New Jersey  08541.<br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION:<br>A minimum of 10 hours per year of approved coursework.<br><br>RENEWAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Every two years contingent on satisfying continuing education requirements.<br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS:<br>Tennessee Association of Audiologists and Speech Pathologists (TAASLP)<br>P.O. Box 331307<br>Nashville, TN  37203<br>(615) 254-3687<br><br>American Speech-Language Hearing Association (ASHA)<br>2200 Research Blvd<br>Rockville, MD  20850<br>(301) 296-5700',
