     'PEST CONTROL OPERATOR', 'PEST CONTROL OPERATOR<br><br>A Pest Control Operator applies, for a fee for any substance or mixture of substances or chemicals intended for defoliating or desiccating plants, or for preventing, destroying, repelling, or mitigating any insects, rodents, fungi, bacteria, weeds or other forms of plant or animal life declared a pest by the Commissioner of Agriculture. Licensing is for one or more categories specified.  Must be 18 years of age prior to becoming licensed to apply general or restricted use pesticides. Supervises technicians. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>Satisfy education and experience and examination requirements. <br><br>EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: <br>A degree or its equivalent with a major or minor in a discipline reasonably related to the category of pest OR at least two years of full time verifiable work experience under a licensee in the category of license applying for in compliance with the rule except the categories of Agricultural-- Ground Equipment and Horticulture-- Lawn and Turf OR a combination of experience, education or 24 continuing education units. <br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS: <br>Category of license, (2 hours) covers specifics of the category of license.  A subsequent exam (3 hours) covers identification relating to the specific category or categories for license. Categories of license are good for 2 years and are required to maintain a current certification to use, buy or sell general or restricted pesticides.  <br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION: <br>Must meet requirements of the licensing every two years and recertification for general or restricted use pesticides every three years. <br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS: <br>Tennessee Pest Control Association, Professional Lawn Care Association of America, Tennessee Vegetation Management Association, West Tennessee Pest Control Association, Tennessee Plant Food Educational Association, and Tennessee Agricultural Production Association (TAPA).',
     '1', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '3700000003', '57',
     'PEST CONTROL SOLICITOR/TECHNICIAN', 'PEST CONTROL SOLICITOR/TECHNICIAN<br><br>A pest control solicitor/technician performs duties of a pest control solicitor, pest control technician, or both. A solicitor is a salesperson or agent employed by a chartered pest control business who is authorized to solicit business or any employee authorized to enter into a pest control contract on behalf of a chartered pest control business. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>A solicitor must possess commercial certification in each category of service offered for sale or provided and be registered by the holder of the charter. Certification, required of a technician, is attained by completing the examination requirements and must be 16 years of age. <br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS: <br>Pass the CORE and category applicable to work. The CORE part covers general knowledge of pest control materials, safety methods and label interpretation and the category part tests knowledge relating to the specific category or categories in which the applicant is seeking a certification. An applicant may be tested in as many categories as desired within the time allowed. The examination must be taken every three years if the required number of continuing education units are not accrued to maintain certification. <br><br>RENEWAL REQUIREMENTS: <br>The renewal fees are staggered. Contact the registration authority for additional information.',
     '1', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '3700000004', '57',
     'RESTRICTED USE PESTICIDE DEALER', 'RESTRICTED USE PESTICIDE DEALER<br><br>A Restricted Use Pesticide Dealer is engaged in wholesale or retail sales of restricted use pesticides. Each dealer location selling restricted use pesticides must have a certified dealer at that location. Each certified dealer shall be responsible for the actions of every person who acts as the dealer''s employee or agent in the sale of restricted use pesticides.  This category does not allow for custom application of pesticides for a fee.  <br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:   <br>Pass the CORE and category for Pesticide Dealer. The CORE part covers general knowledge of pest control materials, safety methods and label interpretation and the category tests knowledge relating to the specific category in which the applicant is seeking a certification. The examination must be taken every three years if the required number of continuing education units are not accrued to maintain the certification. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>Must be certified in certification category 12 (Pesticide Dealer) prior to applying for the Dealer''s License. <br><br>RENEWAL REQUIREMENTS: <br>Must pay the Dealer''s License fee on an annual basis and provide the RUP sales records. Maintain the Pesticide Dealer certification.',
