     'INSURANCE PRODUCER', 'INSURANCE PRODUCE<br><br>An individual is required to be licensed under the laws of this state to sell, solicit or negotiate a policy of insurance on an insurer''s behalf.   Insurance producer licenses are issued for the following lines of authority:   Life, Accident & Health, Property, Casualty, Title and Personal Lines.<br><br>LICENSE REQUIREMENTS: <br> Applicant must be 18 years of age  <br> Has not committed any act that is a ground for denial, suspension or revocation<br> Complete 20 hours of pre-licensing education for each line of authority  <br>NOTE:  Pre-licensing and continuing education providers and courses must be approved by the Department of Commerce and Insurance for the licensing of insurance producers<br> Pass state examination for the applicable line of authority<br> Submit a finger-print based criminal background check <br> Complete and file the NAIC uniform application and fee of $50.00 <br><br>RENEWAL AND CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS: <br> Completion of 24 hours of continuing education (including 3 hours ethics) is required biennially with the renewal of the license <br> Licenses may be renewed for 2 years by submitting a completed NAIC uniform renewal application, fee and required continuing education',
