    ('47', '01', '4100000007', '24',
     'HEARING INSTRUMENT SPECIALISTS', 'HEARING INSTRUMENT SPECIALISTS<br><br>A hearing instrument specialist dispenses or fits hearing instruments (hearing aids). This may include evaluation or measurement of the powers or range of human hearing by means of an audiometer and subsequent selection or adaptation of hearing instruments intended to compensate for hearing loss. Provides the appropriate instructions, consultations, suggestions, recommendations or opinions related to the practice including making an impression of the ear or ear mold, as well as any necessary counseling. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>Be at least 18 years of age, of good moral character, be a high school graduate with at least two years of college level coursework or equivalent, and satisfy examination requirements.<br><br>APPRENTICESHIP REQUIREMENTS:<br>A minimum of 3 months and maximum of one year apprenticeship after passing an examination to serve as apprentice under direct supervision of a licensed specialist during which time the candidate completes at least 60 hours of prescribed coursework. Apprenticeship is not required for licensure.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Written and oral exams covering basic physics of sound, the human hearing mechanism including the science of hearing and the causes and rehabilitation of abnormal hearing and hearing disorders, and the structure and function of hearing instruments.  Exams also test on Pure tone audiometry, including air conduction testing and bone conduction testing;  Live voice or recorded voice speech audiometry, including speech reception threshold testing and speech discrimination testing;  Effective masking; Recording and evaluation of audiograms and speech audiometry to determine hearing instrument candidacy;  Selection and adaption of hearing instruments and testing of heariNAL ORGANIZATIONS:<br> International Hearing Society (IHS)<br> 136880 Middlebelt Rd, Suite 4<br>Livonia, MI  48154<br> (734) 522-7200',
     '1', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '4', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '4100000013', '30',
     'REAL ESTATE AFFILIATE BROKER', 'REAL ESTATE AFFILIATE BROKER<br><br>Engaged under contract by or on behalf of a licensed broker and, for expected profit, and solicits or negotiates listing, sale, purchase, exchange, lease, option to buy, sell, rent or exchange any real estate, collect rent, or auction real estate. May be employed by owners at a salary or for other compensation to sell real estate . May promote sale of real estate through publications or for profit.   May study  property listings to become familiar with properties for sale, accompany clients to sites, draw up contracts and negotiate loans. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>At least 18 years old, a resident of the state for at least 45 days, good reputation for honesty, trustworthiness, and integrity, and competent to transact the business of affiliate broker, and satisfy education and examination requirements.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>60 classroom hours in a pre-licensing covering basic principles of real estate at an institution approved by the commission.  A 30-hour course for new affiliates must be completed within the first year of licensure.  <br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>	Examination covering business ethics, composition, arithmetic, elementary principles of land economics and appraisal, closing statements, general knowledge of the statutes of Tennessee relating to deeds, mortgages, trust deeds, contracts of sale, leases and other related matters, and the Tennessee Real Estate Broker License Act of 1973. (Exemption from the uniform principles portion allowed for agents in other states passing certain recognized examinations.) <br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Completion of 16 classroom hours in real estate courses at an institution approved by the commission every two years.  <br><br>RENEWAL:shville, Tennessee',
