     'FACTORY MANUFACTURED STRUCTURES INSTALLER', 'FACTORY MANUFACTURED STRUCTURES INSTALLER<br><br> Installation of manufactured homes.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Register with the Consumer Affairs Division of the Department of Commerce and Insurance and post a $10,000 surety bond .<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS: <br>Completion of a 15 hour course approved by the commissioner in the installation of manufactured homes.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Pass an examination approved by the commissioner in the installation of manufactured homes.<br><br>RENEWAL: <br>Annual.<br><br>',
     '0', '1', '1', '9', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.tn.gov/commerce/fire/sections-programs/fire-manufactured-housing/installer-resources.html', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '4700000007', '13',
     'LIMITED LICENSED PLUMBERS', 'LIMITED LICENSED PLUMBERS <br><br>The Limited Licensed Plumber (LLP) state license is only required by plumbers performing work in a municipality utilizing the Division of Fire Prevention for permits, inspections and covers work less than $25,000 per project; general maintenance work, less than $500 is exempt from the LLP license.<br>Always check with local government to see if they accept the LLP or if they have local licensing requirements for permits and inspections. The LLP license is issued to individuals passing the LLP trade exam.   More information can be found in T.C.A.  62-6-403.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br> Photo-ID and Social Security Number. Exam (PSI is the exam vendor). Completed Application. Fee of $75.00 for two (2) year license. A Business" tax license may also be required by local government.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS: <br> The Tennessee Limited License Plumber exam. <br> PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS: Plumber Training Institute, 3135 Logan Valley Rd, Traverse, MI 49684   800-727-7104',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     '"https://www.plumberstraininginstitute.com/"', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '4900000002', '19',
     'FIRE EXTINGUISHER SPECIALIST', 'FIRE EXTINGUISHER SPECIALIST<br><br>A person employed by a company which installs or services portable fire extinguishers or fixed fire extinguisher systems who is certified as an extinguisher specialist.  The specialist inspects and approves installation and repair or servicing.<br><br>PROSPECTIVE:<br>A firm which installs or services portable fire extinguishers or fixed fire extinguisher systems must employ at least one certified extinguisher specialist.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Pass a state examination.  (Applicants can be exempted if they work only on a fixed system and provide satisfactory proof of successful completion of a course on the system and test by a major manufacturer).',
     '1', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '4900000003', '19',
     'FIRE EXTINGUISHER TECHNICIAN', 'FIRE EXTINGUISHER TECHNICIAN<br><br>Installs and/or repairs fire extinguishing systems for a company.<BR>Must work only under the direct supervision of a person holding a valid license as a registered specialist.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>An applicant shall show satisfactory proof of successful completion of a manufacturer''s test, and pass a state examination.  (Such test may be less comprehensive and rigorous than that required by an applicant for an extinguisher specialist license.)',
     '1', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '4900000004', '62',
     'WEIGHTS AND MEASUREMENT SERVICEPERSON', 'WEIGHTS AND MEASURES SERVICEPERSON<br><br>Installs, services, repairs or reconditions a commercial weighing or measuring device for hire, award, commission or any other payment of any kind. <br><br>PROSPECTIVE:<br>Certification for a device is required for any service that can affect the accuracy of measurement of the device, accuracy of charges or fees derived by the use of the device, or the metrological integrity of the device.  Only a certified serviceperson has authority to remove an official rejection tag or seal placed on a device by authority of the Commissioner; place in service a device that has been officially rejected until an examination can be made; or place in service a new or used weighing or measuring device. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Provide acceptable evidence of being fully qualified by training or experience to install, service, repair, or recondition a commercial weighing or measuring device; having thorough working knowledge of all appropriate weights and measures laws, orders, rules and regulations; and having possession of or available for use and intention to use calibrated weights and measures standards and testing equipment appropriate in design and adequate in amount.  Certification authority is authorized to administer a written examination of applicant''s knowledge. <br><br>RENEWAL:<br>Required every two years.',
     '1', '2', '1', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '4900000007', '78',
     'REGISTERED EMPLOYEE, ALARM SYSTEMS', 'REGISTERED EMPLOYEE, ALARM SYSTEMS<br><br> An alarm system contractor employee is a specific type of employee with access to records, diagrams, plans or other sensitive information pertaining to monitored, installed or proposed alarm systems.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>Employing company must register employees in accordance with the law within 30 days of employment. <br>A signed, notarized application along with the appropriate non-refundable application fee of $100.00.  Three completed fingerprint cards issued by this office with the required $60.00 fee.  Or an electronically scanned fingerprint receipt.<br>  Two 1 x 1 color passport-style photos with the name of the applicant printed on the back of each.  <br>Be at least 18 years of age. Must be of good moral character.<br><br>EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS:<br>Not listed<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Not Listed<br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS:<br>Not listed <br><br>RENEWAL: <br>Employee renewal in conjunction with company renewals.<br><br>PROFESSIONAL ORGANIZATIONS <.',
     '0', '1', '1', '0', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://www.tn.gov/commerce/regboards/alarm/license-applicant-resources/get-a-license.html', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '5100000001', '67',
     'BIOLOGICAL/NATURAL WASTEWATER SYSTEM OPERATOR', 'BIOLOGICAL/NATURAL WASTEWATER SYSTEM OPERATOR<br><br>Person qualified to control the manipulation of equipment and thereby determine the quality of the effluent from a wastewater treatment plant that is classified as biological/natural. A plant in that classification uses natural biological treatment as the predominant means of treatment, including stabilization ponds, intermittent sand-filters, spray irrigation, constructed wetlands, aerated lagoons, and overland flow systems. <br><br>PROSPECTIVE: <br>Certification is required for persons in direct charge of a wastewater treatment plant classified as a biological/natural system.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>Must have a high school education or equivalent, have twelve months of operating experience in a wastewater system classified as a biological/natural system, and meet the examination requirement. <br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION: <br>Within each 3-year period each certified operator must satisfactorily complete a conference, training course, or school approved by the Board. <br><br>EXAMINATIONS: <br>Examination is written (except for accommodations made for disability). It may contain matching, multiple choice, true-false, discussion, and short answer questions and may contain problems. 70% is required to pass.',
     '1', '2', '1', '1', '2',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'No URL Provided', '20240909'),
    ('47', '01', '5100000002', '81',
     'BOILER INSPECTOR', 'BOILER INSPECTOR<br><br>A boiler inspector is commissioned by the state to inspect power boilers, low pressure heating boilers, and unfired pressure vessels as to construction, installation, condition and function before regular operation and periodically before certificates expire, and to certify the satisfactory inspection and the maximum pressure under which the boiler may be operated.  <br>[The inspector is a state employee, an employee of an insurer of boilers in the state, or an employee of a company with an approved inspection program for boilers it owns or uses.]     <br><br>PROSPECTIVE:<br>A certificate of competency is required for appointment as chief inspector, assistant chief, deputy inspector, or special inspector in Tennessee.   <br><br>REQUIREMENTS:<br>A commission or user-owner commission (as applicable) issued by the National Board of Boiler and Pressure Vessel Inspectors.  Education and experience requirements below must be met to sit for the examination.<br><br>EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS:<br>A degree from an accredited school in mechanical engineering, plus one year of experience in design, construction, operation or inspection of high-pressure boilers and pressure vessels <BR><br>OR<br>An associate degree from an accredited school in mechanical technology, plus two years of experience in design, construction, operation or inspection of high-pressure boilers and pressure vessels <BR><br>OR<br> A high school education (or the equivalent) plus three years experience in high pressure boiler and pressure vessel construction or repair, as an operating engineer in charge of high-pressure boiler operation, or as an inspector of high-pressure boilers and pressure boiler operation.<br><br>EXAMINATION REQUIREMENT:<br>Satisfactory prough the certifying authority.',
