    ('47', '01', '5100000006', '67',
     'WASTEWATER COLLECTION SYSTEM OPERATOR GRADE I', 'WASTEWATER COLLECTION SYSTEM OPERATOR GRADE <br><br>Person who is qualified to control the manipulation of equipment and thereby determine the integrity of a system classified as Grade I for the collection and transmission of wastewater to a treatment plant.<br><br>PROSPECTIVE: <br>Certification is required for persons in direct charge of wastewater collection systems of Grade I. <br><br>REQUIREMENTS: <br>An applicant must have a high school education or equivalent, twelve months operating experience in a wastewater collection system, and meet examination requirements. A maximum of three months of college classwork or related training can be substituted for the same amount of experience. <br><br>CONTINUING EDUCATION:<br>Within each 3-year period each certified operator must satisfactorily complete a conference, training course, or school approved by the Board. <br><br>EXAMINATIONS: <br>Examination is written (except accommodations made for disability). It may contain matching, multiple choice, true-false, discussion, and short answer questions and may contain problems. 70% is required to pass.',
