     'Loan Originator', 'Individuals must pass the national and state mortgage loan originator tests (at a cost of $143 for both), have a high school diploma or equivalent, complete 22 hours of NMLS-approved pre-licensing education, including 4 hours in Washington law, complete a criminal background check and file a credit report authorization.',
