    ('54', '01', '0', '9',
     'Registration for Foresters', 'The West Virginia Board of Registration for Foresters was established by the West Virginia
Legislature in 1963 to register foresters and forestry technicians in the state of West Virginia.  There
are five board members, who are licensed professional foresters in this state and have held
their license for at least 10 years preceding appointment.  Appointments to the Board are made by
the Governor.

EXAMINATION INFORMATION
Next examination date: March 20, 2021
Location: Beckley Room at the Days Inn - Flatwoods, WV
Time: Arrive by 9:00 AM - Test begins at 10:00 AM
Please contact wvborf@gmail.com if you plan to
attend. 
The cost is $ 100.00 to be paid one week in advance.
 Please plan to wear a mask and social distance before, during and after the examination.
 ANNUAL RENEWALS: ONLINE PAYMENTS
Step 1: Pay the annual renewal fee online at the following link.
CLICK HERE to pay ONLINE renewal fee
Step 2: After you pay your registration on-line, please send an email to the wvborf@gmail.com.  with the following information to the
WV BORF.
1.  In the subject line of the email, write: Your name, registration number and the word
"renewal".
2.  In the body of the email, clearly state your  a) name, b) registration number, and c) phone
number   
3.  Attach a scanned or photographed image of your payment confirmation page - this will come
in an email to you after you pay online (above) - and
4.  Attach a scanned or photographed image of your Continuing Forestry Education (CFE)
certificates or SAF list of credits.
INSTRUCTIONS FOR RENEWING YOUR LICENSE BY MAIL
 CLICK HERE to renew your registration by
mail
RECIPROCITY GUIDELINES
CLICK HERE to view RECIPROCITY
GUIDELINES
FILING A COMPLAINT FORM
The following complaint form can be used to file a complaint against anyone using the title "forester" or
advertising they are providing "forestry services.  Once completed, signed and dated, please print the form
and mail toWVBORF, PO Box 1032, Ripley, WV 25271.  The form can also be sent via email to wvborf@gmail.com, 

CLICK HERE for COMPLAINT FORM',
     '1', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.wvlicensingboards.com/foresters/index.cfm', '20100101'),
    ('54', '01', '1', '30',
     'Sanitarians', 'NEHA R.S. Exam Information
All Sanitarians:
              If you are interested in taking the test, you 
should contact me, and I will send you the required letter / application to 
take it to submit to NEHA.  Taking the test and passing it is a requirement 
to obtain your "Registered Sanitarian" status in West Virginia.  
Without taking it, you can advance to "Sanitarian"status after 2 years of tenure.  You start 
as a "Sanitarian I". 

David P. Thornton, R.S., Executive Director
WV State Board of Sanitarians
PO Box 927
Charleston, WV  25523
Phone:  304-344-5243 Extension 2074          
Email:  David.P.Thornton@wv.gov 

ATTENTION:
          NEHA R.S. Study materials are available at each Public Health Sanitation Division District
Office. 
          
          To obtain these study materials contact the District Sanitarian and complete the
          
Reference Study Material Borrowing Agreement

NEHA R.S. Study Courses:
Visit the WV
Public Health Sanitation Division - Training page.',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '9',
     '9', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.wvlicensingboards.com/BoardOfSanitarians/NEHA.cfm', '20100101'),
    ('54', '01', '10', '14',
     'Massage Therapists', 'Licenses


              The Massage Therapy Board is responsible for issuing licenses to
              qualified professionals within the state of West Virginia. In
              order to practice within the state, you must successfully attain
              and maintain licensure with the Board. You will find all
              information needed in this section of our website to apply for
              your license or license renewal.

Two Year
              License
              If you are not currently licensed to operate in the state of West
              Virginia, you must apply for the Two Year License. Licenses can be
              issued at any time, and expire two years after issuance at the end
              of the month.

Two Year
              Renewal
              If you are currently licensed as a Massage Therapist in the state
              of West Virginia, you need to apply for a renewal in order to keep
              your license current. All licenses expire two years after
              issuance, so you will need to apply for a renewal before before
              you current license expires. Your renewal will then be valid for
              two years after it is issued and expires at the end of the month.

Code of Ethics
              All licensed therapists are required to post the complete code of
              ethics at their place of business. This code is included in the
              license application packet or can be downloaded directly from
              here.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', 'D', '0',
     'http://www.wvmassage.org/licenses.asp', '20100101'),
    ('54', '01', '100', '22',
     'Foreign Trained Physical Therapist', 'West Virginia does not consider licensure for anyone from a foreign country who alleges to have the equivalent of a PTA degree. It is not possible for a foreign-educated person who does not prove equivalency towards a PT degree to then qualify as a PTA. Only applicants who believe that they have the equivalent of a PT degree should apply.

 If you have a BS degree from a foreign country and then graduate from a US PT program, the degree you are working towards or have received must be "Entry-Level Masters" and NOT "Advanced". The advanced PT masters degree is not accredited and not
 recognized by any state PT board in the United States.

 Please be advised that effective June 7, 2010 all sections of the TOEFL must have passing scores on one test, and multiple tests cannot be combined. You may be exempt from this requirement if you have been awarded a bachelor’s degree or higher from the United States, United Kingdom, Ireland, Australia, New Zealand, or Canada (except Quebec). If this exemption applies, your
 school must submit an official transcript showing that the degree was awarded and the date of conferral. 

Physical Therapist Assistant:
To be eligible for a license to practice, you must have a Physical Therapist Assistant Associate''s degree from a CAPTE accredited program.  You must be planning to take the National Physical Therapy Assistant Exam, or have already taken the exam and successfully passed.

Verification of graduation from a CAPTE accredited school is required.

If you received a MASTER''S, the transcript must state the degree received as a Master''s in Physical Therapy.
If you received a BACHELOR''S or DOCTORATE, the transcript must state the degree received as a Bachelor''s OR Doctorate in Physical Therapy. 
If you received an ASSOCIATE''S, the transcript must state the degree received as an associate''s degree for Physical Therapist Assistant.',
     '0', '2', '1', '1', '9',
     '0', '9', '9', '9', '0',
     'http://www.wvbopt.com/page.cfm?sectionID=4&pageID=42', '20100101'),
    ('54', '01', '101', '22',
     'Physical Therapist Assistant', 'To be eligible for a license to practice, you must have a Physical Therapist Assistant Associate''s degree from a CAPTE accredited program.  You must be planning to take the National Physical Therapy Assistant Exam, or have already taken the exam and successfully passed.

Verification of graduation from a CAPTE accredited school is required.

If you received a MASTER''S, the transcript must state the degree received as a Master''s in Physical Therapy.
If you received a BACHELOR''S or DOCTORATE, the transcript must state the degree received as a Bachelor''s OR Doctorate in Physical Therapy. 
If you received an ASSOCIATE''S, the transcript must state the degree received as an associate''s degree for Physical Therapist Assistant.',
