Authority:

 West Virginia Code, Chapter 29, Article 3D "Supervision of Fire Protection Workers" 

& 

West Virginia Code of State Rules Title 103, Series 3 "Supervision of Fire Protection Work"


Important Notices:?
No person may perform fire protection work as defined in 29-3D unless licensed by the State Fire Marshal. 


 Effective June 16, 2021, due to the passage of new legislative rules?, Fire Damper Technicians, Fire Damper Technicians In-Training, and Sprinkler Fitter''s In-Training no longer require licensure to perform fire protection work. 

Types of Fire Protection Worker Licenses:

Fire Protection Layout Technician
Journeyman Sprinkler Fitter

Engineered Fire Suppression System Installer

Engineered Fire Suppression System Technician

Pre-Engineered Fire Suppression System Installer

Pre-Engineered Fire Suppression System Technician

Portable Fire Extinguisher Technician 




Licensure Process:


Persons wishing to obtain their Fire Protection License shall provide the following prior to the issuance of the license:




 



1.  Complete the Fire Protection Worker application.



2.  Be at least 18 years of age.



3.  Pay all application review and license fees. Must be paid by check or money order only. 



4.  Submit ALL work experience, certifications and supporting documentation with the application.


 


Individual requirements for all FPW licenses are listed on the application. Please click the link below for a copy. 
Application for Fire Protection Worker
Licensure Renewal:
Renewal Notices are mailed to? the licensee address on file approximately ninety (90) days prior to the license expiration date.
Fire Protection Workers  will have the option of paying for either a one (1) year license renewal or a three (3) year license renewal. 
Please be advised no grace period exists for Fire Protection Worker licenses. All FPW license renewals must be postmarked by the expiration date.
 For more information on FPW license renewals or to request copies of renewal forms, please contact the Regulatory and Licensing Division directly at 304-558-2191 and press option 1. 


