     'Radiologic Technologists', 'The Medical Imaging & Radiation Therapy Technology Board of Examiners was created in 1977 to promote, preserve, and protect the public health, safety and welfare of the citizens of West Virginia by licensing individuals who use ionizing radiation as medical imaging professionals. The Board is funded by license application fees. West Virginia Code §30-23-1 authorizes the Board to regulate the following professions:


