(to be used ONLY after passing the PE Exam if registered as a WV PE Examinee).   The WV PE Licensure application process is a post-exam process that cannot be completed until the applicant has successfully passed the NCEES Principles and Practice (PE) Exam. Eligible candidates will first register directly with NCEES to sit for the PE Exam as a WV applicant.  Once the eligible WV examinee successfully passes the PE Exam, and has obtained the required qualifying experience, they will then be permitted to apply to the WV Board for PE Licensure consideration.


















