If you receive a passing result on the Principles and Practice Exam (PE) within two years of having had a full PE exam application packet pre-approved by the West Virginia State Board of Registration for Professional Engineers, simply forward a copy of your NCEES Exam Result Notice with this form to the WV PE Board office. If it has been more than two years since your last full application packet was approved, you must submit a full new Initial Licensure Candidate application packet, including the $80 filing fee and all required documents outlined in the Professional Engineer Application Materials table above.  A fee waiver is available for military families and qualified low income applicants.

If you are unsure of the “receipt date” of your previous PE Exam application packet, and whether it is within the 2-year window of acceptance, please do not hesitate to contact the WV PE Board office for assistance. 

Submission of this form will ensure that the Board has your most current and preferred address for mailing official Board correspondence as you complete the final phase of the PE licensure process.













