The table below contains the Certificate of Authorization (COA) application form, and relevant application fees, to be used by all firms/companies who want to provide (or even offer to provide) engineering services for projects in West Virginia.  This authorization is completely separate from the business license obtained from the WV Secretary of State.  Before applying for a COA, all firms and sole-proprietors should consult the  License/COA Verification link on this website at https://services.wvpebd.org/verification/ to determine if they have an existing COA.  If unsure of whether you have a COA, or if you are required to obtain a COA, simply contact the Board office for assistance.   It is IMPORTANT to remember that one is not legally permitted to practice engineering (or even offer to provide engineering services) in this state until the COA has been issued (W.Va. Code §30-13-17(a)).

