    ('55', '01', '239', '122',
     'COMMERCIAL PLUMBING INSPECTOR', 'Reason for Credential: A person who holds a credential issued by the department as a certified commercial plumbing inspector may conduct inspections of public buildings and places of employment for the purpose of administering and enforcing the Plumbing Code.  Requirements of Credential: A person who inspects public buildings and places of employment as a certified commercial plumbing inspector shall: - Maintain a record of the inspections made including the date and the findings of the inspections;  - Provide a copy of the inspection report to the owner of the property or his or her agent; and -Make available to the department upon request his or her inspection records.  A person who holds the credential shall carry on his or her person the credential issued by the department while performing or conducting the activity or activities permitted under the credential.',
     '0', '1', '2', '1', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     'https://dsps.wi.gov/Pages/Professions/CommercialPlumbingInspector/Default.aspx', '20201202'),
    ('55', '01', '24', '5',
     'DRIVER INSTRUCTOR', 'License required for any person who gives driving instruction to persons over 18 years of age. This does not include a person who is employed as a full-time instructor by a high school, vocational school, or institution of higher learning. 

A license is also required to instruct students less than 18 years of age, instruct individuals on how to drive a motorcycle, and anyone receiving compensation for giving instruction on driving a truck.  

Prerequisites: Must have a regular, non-probationary drivers'' license for the last 12-month period, an acceptable driving record and no felony convictions against public morals within the last 5 years. The Applicant must be employed by a licensed commercial driving school. 

Wisconsin Statutes: Operators'' Licenses (S. 343.60 to 343.75)',
