     'ELECTRICIAN', 'ELECTRICIANS  SOC Code 47-2111    Entry Salary  $24.47/hr  Average Salary  $31.06/hr    Job Description  Electricians install wiring and maintain electrical equipment covered by the National Electrical  Code. Limited electrical technicians and low voltage technicians maintain and install systems  under 90 volts or specific items per license, as covered by the National Electrical Code.    Requirements  Apprentices:      1. Must be registered with the State Electrical Board,      2. Four years (576 hours) apprenticeship training.  Journeyman:     1.  Four years (8,000 hours) of work experience beyond apprenticeship training.     2  Pass written examination.  Master:     1 Additional four years (8,000 hours) experience beyond journeyman license.     2.Pass written examination.  Limited Technician (three types):     1.  Years and hours of training dependent on license type.  Contact licensing agency for more information.     2.  Pass written examination.  Low Voltage Technician (six types):     1.  Years and hours of training dependent on license type.  Contact licensing agency for more information.     2.  Pass written examination.    Continuing Education  Journeyman and Master electricians are required to complete sixteen hours of continuing education units including eight from a code related source, within three years of licensee last renewal. See Department of Fire Prevention and Electrical Safety website for a list of Wyoming approved continuing education providers and course options.    Restrictions  Fraud  Any flagrant violation of the rules and regulations of the State Electrical Board.    Schools Located in Wyoming  Casper College - Casper  http://www.caspercollege.edu/electrical-apprenticeship  Central Wyoming College - Riverton  For information on the electrical apprenticeship program at CWC, see   https://www.cwc.edu/electrical/  Western Wyoming College - Rock Springs - Electrical & Instrumentation Technology  https://www.westernwyoming.edu/academics/electrical/  Wyoming Electrical Joint Apprenticeship and Training Committee (JATC)  http://wyojatc.org/    See Department of Fire Prevention and Electrical Safety website for more information on approved training programs    License  Electricians must be licensed by the State Electrical Board.  Licenses expire every three years on July 1st.    Examination  Examinations for journeyman electricians, master electricians, limited technicians, and low voltage technicians are administered on demand after approval by the Chief Electrical Inspector.    Fees  Apprentice Electrician:  Initial Registration. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $20.00  Yearly Registration Renewal. . . . . . .$20.00    Apprentice Low Voltage:   Initial Registration. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $20.00  Yearly Registration Renewal. . . . . . .$20.00    Apprentice Limited Technician::  Initial Registration. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $20.00  Yearly Registration Renewal. . . . . . .$20.00    Journeyman:  License . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $100.00  Renewal (Every 3 Years). . . . . . . . . $50.00    Master:  License . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$200.00  Renewal (Every 3 Years). . . . . . . . . .$100.00    Limited Technician:  License . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $100.00  Renewal (Every 3 Years). . . . . . . . . $  50.00    Low Voltage Technician:  License . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $100.00  Renewal (Every 3 Years). . . . . . . . . $  50.00    For Journeyman, Limited Technician and Low Voltage Technician waiting to be tested:   Temporary Work Permit . . . . . . . . . .$  50.00    Licensing Agency  Bridget McGheoghegan  Attn: Electrical Safety Division  Department of Fire Prevention & Electrical Safety  320 West 25th Street, 3rd Floor  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-7907  Fax: (307) 777-7119   http://wsfm.wyo.gov/             Additional Sources of Information  International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers  900 Seventh St., NW   Washington, DC 20001  Phone: (202) 833-7000   http://ibew.org/    National Electrical Contractors Association  1201 Pennsylvania Ave. NW, Suite 1200  Washington, D.C. 20004  Phone:  (202) 991-6300  http://necanet.org/    Wyoming Electrical Joint Apprentice and Training Committee (JATC)  2080 N. Skyview Drive  Casper, WY 82601  Phone: (307) 234-8311 or (888) 286-3151  http://wyojatc.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:   Electricians"   https://www.bls.gov/ooh/construction-and-extraction/electricians.htm    Last Updated April 2023      "',
