     'PROFESSIONAL COUNSELOR', 'MENTAL HEALTH COUNSELORS  SOC Code 21-1014    Entry Salary  N/A  Average Salary  N/A    Job Description  Professional Counselors render services to individuals, couples, families, groups, organizations, corporations, institutions, government agencies or the general public. They integrate a wellness, pathology and multicultural model of human behavior. This model applies a combination of mental health, psychotherapeutic, and human development principles and procedures to help clients achieve effective mental, emotional, physical, social, moral, educational, spiritual or career development and adjustment throughout the life span, and includes the diagnostic description and treatment of mental disorders or disabilities within the range of the professionals preparation.    Requirements     1.  Age of majority.     2.  Has received a Masters or Doctorate degree in professional counseling.     3.  Demonstrated knowledge in the field of professional counseling.     4.  Demonstrated that (s)he has completed 3,000 hours of supervised clinical experience including a minimum of 1,200 hours of direct client contact.and 100 post graduate degree hours of clinical supervision with a DQCS     5.  A passing examination score on the National Board for Certified Counselors (NBCC) National Counselor Examination (NCE) or the National Clinical Mental Health Examination (NCMHE), or a passing score on the Certification Examination administered by the Commission on Rehabilitation Counselor Certification (CRCC) or a passing score on other examinations as may be approved by the Board.    Continuing Education  Licensee must have at least three hours of continuing education activities in professional ethics and three hours of continuing education activities in suicide assessment and prevention every renewal period.    Restrictions  Felony conviction.  Misdemeanor convictions involving moral turpitude.    School Located in Wyoming  Central Wyoming College - Riverton - Behavioral and Social Sciences - Associates  https://www.cwc.edu/programs/socialsciences/  Laramie County Community College - Cheyenne - Human Services program - Associates  https://www.lccc.wy.edu/pathways/humanPublic/    License  Professional Counselors engaged in practice in Wyoming are licensed by the Mental Health Professions Licensing Board.  Licenses are valid for two years and expire on licensee birthday.    Examination  Exams accepted by the Board are The National Board for Certified Counselors (NBCC) National Counselor Examination or the National Clinical Mental Health Examination (NCMHE) which is also administered by NBCC.    Fees  Licensure by reciprocity. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$350.00  Licensure by examination. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $350.00  Licensure by completing provisional. . . . . . . . . . . . $200.00  Provisional license. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$150.00  License renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $125.00 for the initial discipline, $75.00 for every additional discipline    Licensing Agency  Mental Health Professions Licensing Board  2001 Capitol Avenue  Emerson Building, Rm 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://mentalhealth.wyo.gov/      Additional Sources of Information  National Board for Certified Counselors and Affiliates, Inc.  3 Terrace Way  Greensboro, NC 27403  Phone: (336) 547-0607  http://nbcc.org/    American Counseling Association  PO Box 31110   Alexandria, VA 22310  Phone: (800) 347-6647  http://www.counseling.org/    Additional Sources of Information  Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Community and Social Service Occupations"   http://www.bls.gov/ooh/community-and-social-service/home.htm    Last updated April 2023"',
