     'CERTIFIED ADDICTIONS PRACTITIONER', 'SUBSTANCE ABUSE AND BEHAVIORAL DISORDER COUNSELORS  SOC Code 21-1011    Entry Salary  N/A  Average Salary  N/A    Job Description  The practice of Certified Addictions Practitioner consists of addictions treatment, prevention, intervention, diagnosis, referral and follow-up under the supervision of a designated qualified clinical supervisor licensed in the state of Wyoming.    Requirements     1. Age of majority.     2. Hold a current National Certified Addictions Counselor Level II (NCAC II)  certification in good standing. OR     3.  Completion of a baccalaureate degree program with a concentration in addictionology, chemical dependency, or  substance abuse from an educational institution accredited by one of the regional or national  institutional accrediting bodies recognized by the Council for Higher Education Accreditation  (CHEA)     4. A passing score on the Association for Addictions Professionals  (NAADAC) NCAC Level II exam OR International Certification and Reciprocity Consortium (IC&RC) Alcohol and Other Drug Abuse Counselor (AODA) exam; OR Other examination as may be approved by the Board.    Continuing Education  Licensees must complete a minimum of three hours of continuing education activities in professional ethics and three continuing education activities in suicide assessment and prevention during each license renewal period.  Certified addictions practitioners must also complete a minimum of fifteen contact hours of continuing education in addictions specific topics.    Restrictions  Felony conviction.  Misdemeanor conviction involving moral turpitude.    School Located in Wyoming  Casper College - Casper -School of Social and Behavioral Sciences - Addictionology (Associates)  http://caspercollege.edu/addictionology/  Central Wyoming College - Riverton - Behavioral and Social Sciences - Psychology (Associates)  https://www.cwc.edu/programs/socialsciences/psychology/  Sheridan College - Sheridan - Addictions Practitioner (Certificate of Completion)  https://www.sheridan.edu/academics/programs-a-z/addictions-practitioner/  University of Wyoming -  Laramie - Counseling (Master of Science)  https://www.uwyo.edu/uw/degree-programs/counseling-masters.html      License  Certified Addictions Practitioners are certified in Wyoming by the Mental Health Professions Licensing Board.  Licenses expire every two years on licensee birthday.    Examination  The Board accepts The Association for Addiction Professionals (NAADAC), National Certified Addictions Counselor (NCAC) exam at Level II    Fees   Certification by reciprocity. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$300.00  Certification by examination. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $300.00  Certification renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$100.00 per discipline      Licensing Agency  Mental Health Professions Licensing Board  2001 Capitol Avenue  Emerson Bldg, Rm 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://mentalhealth.wyo.gov/            Additional Sources of Information  The Association for Addiction Professionals (NAADAC)  44 Canal Center Plaza, Ste 301  Alexandria, VA 22314  Phone: (703) 741-7686  http://www.naadac.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  https://www.bls.gov/ooh/community-and-social-service/substance-abuse-behavioral-disorder-and-mental-health-counselors.htm    Last updated April 2023',
