     'CERTIFIED ADDICTIONS PRACTITIONER ASSISTANT', 'SOCIAL AND HUMAN SERVICE ASSISTANTS  SOC Code 21-1093    Entry Salary  $15.51/hr  Average Salary  $18.79/hr    Job Description  Certified Addictions Practitioner Assistants (CAPA) assist in the practice of addictions treatment, prevention, intervention, referral and follow-up under the supervision of a designated qualified clinical supervisor licensed in the state of Wyoming. Therapeutic interventions are limited to education and skill development activities. The practice of a CAPA does not include assigning diagnosis, making treatment recommendation, or acting as a primary treatment provider.    Requirements     1.  Age of majority.     2.  Legal inhabitant of the United States.     3.  Complete the education requirements specified in Chapter 4 of the Rules of the Board, which may be met by:         A. Holding a current National Certified Addictions Counselor Level 1 (NCAC1) certificate in good standing from the Association for Addicions Professionals (NAADAC) or a current Alcohol and Other Drub Abuse Counselor (AODA) from the International Certification and Reciprocity Cionsortium (IC&RC), or         B. Completion of an associates degree in addictionology, chemical dependencey, substance abuse counseling, or an equivelantly termed degree program, or         C. Completion or 270 hours of addiiction specific course work and/or training including a maximum or 70 hours of general mental health discipline subjects (with 30 hours in counseling ethics) and a minimum of 200 hours related specifically to addictions therapy (with 6 hours of specialty training in communicable diseases).     4. A passing score on either the Association for Addictions Professionals (NAADAC), NCAC Level I exam or on another examination as may be approved by the Board.    Continuing education  Licensees must complete a minumum of three hours of continuing education activities in professional ethics and three hours of continuing education activities in suicide assessment and prevention.  Certified addictions practitioner assistants must also complete fifteen contact hours of continuing education in addictions specific topics.    Restrictions  Felony conviction.  Misdemeanor conviction involving moral turpitude.    Schools Located in Wyoming  Casper College - Casper - School of Social and Behavioral Sciences - Addiction Studies program  http://caspercollege.edu/addictionology/  Central Wyoming College - Riverton - Behavioral and Social Sciences Program - Psychology  https://www.cwc.edu/programs/socialsciences/psychology/  Sheridan College - Sheridan - Addictions Practitioner program (Certificate of Completion)  https://www.sheridan.edu/academics/programs-a-z/addictions-practitioner/    License  Certified Addictions Practioner Assistants are certified in Wyoming by the Mental Health Professions Licensing Board.  Licenses expire every two years on the licensee birthday.    Examination  The Board accepts The Association for Addiction Professionals (NAADAC), National Certified Addictions Counselor (NCAC) Level I exam.    Fees  Certification by reciprocity. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$300.00  Certification by examination. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $300.00  Certification renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$100.00 per discipline    Licensing Agency  Mental Health Professions Licensing Board  2001 Capitol Avenue  Emerson Bldg, Rm 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://mentalhealth.wyo.gov/          Additional Sources of Information  The Association for Addiction Professionals (NAADAC)  44 Canal Center Plaza, Ste 301  Alexandria, VA 22314  Phone: (703) 741-7698   http://www.naadac.org/    National Association of Addiction Treatment Providers  PO Box 271686  Louisville, CO 80027  Phone: (888) 574-1008  https://www.naatp.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Social and Human Service Assistants"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/community-and-social-service/social-and-human-service-assistants.htm    Last Updated April 2023"',
