     'MIDWIFE', 'HEALTHCARE PRACTITIONERS AND TECHNICAL WORKERS, ALL OTHER  SOC CODE 29-9099    Entry Salary  $24.52/hr  Average Salary  $36.63/hr    Job Description  Midwives provide primary prenatal, intrapartum and postpartum care to women and newborns.    Requirements     1.  Have a high school diploma or equivalent.     2.  Have current certification as a Certified Professional Midwife (CPM) by the North American Registry of Midwives (NARM).     2.  Graduate of a midwifery program accredited by the Midwifery Education Accreditation Council (MEAC).     3.  Provide evidence of successful completion of Board approved courses in the treatment of respiratory distress in newborns, pharmacology, the treatment of shock, intravenous therapy, and suturing specific to midwives.    Continuing Education  No continuing education is currently required for midwives in Wyoming.    Restrictions  Convicted of a crime which renders the person unfit to practice midwifery.  Violations of the Midwives Licensure Act.  Providing false or misleading information to the Board.    School Located in Wyoming  There are no midwifery schools in Wyoming.    License  Midwives must be licensed by the State Board of Midwifery.  Licenses expire every two years.    Examination  An examination is not required but applicants must provide proof of current certification as a certified professional midwife by the North American Registry of Midwives (NARM).    Fees  Application . . . . . . . . . . . . .  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $1,200.00  Provisional License Fee . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$200.00  Provisional Undertaking Practicum  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$400.00  Provisional Education/Instruction/Locum Tenens . . . . .$200.00 per provisional  Renewal. . . . . . . . . . . .. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .. . . . . . .$1,200.00     Licensing Agency  Chris Frint  Board of Midwifery  2001 Capitol Avenue, Room 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://midwifery.wyo.gov/    Additional Sources of Information  Midwifery Education Accreditation Council  850 Mt. Pleasant Ave  Ann Arbor, MI 48103  Phone: (360) 466-2080  http://meacschools.org/    National Association of Certified Professional Midwives  PO BOX #1448  Williston, VT  05495  (802) 556-1522  https://nacpm.org/    North American Registry of Midwives  5257 Rosestone Dr.  Lilburn, GA 30047  Phone: (888) 842-4784  http://narm.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Nurse Anesthetists  Nurse Midwives and Nurse Practitioners"  https://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/nurse-anesthetists-nurse-midwives-and-nurse-practitioners.htm    Last updated May 2023"',
