     'CLASS B STORAGE TANK OPERATOR', 'FIRST-LINE SUPERVISORS OF TRANSPORTATION AND MATERIAL-MOVING MACHINE AND VEHICLE OPERATORS  SOC Code 53-1031    Entry Salary  N/A  Average Salary  N/A    Job Description  Class B Storage Tank Operators have day-to-day responsibility for the onsite operation and maintenance of up to 15 underground storage tank (UST) systems.    Requirements     1.Pass the International Code Council (ICC) test for Class B UST System Operator - BU" and/or the ICC test for "Wyoming AST System Operators - ICC Test W-5".     2.In lieu of both of the above tests the ICC test on "Wyoming State Specific Storage Tank Laws - ICC Test W-6" is acceptable.    Restrictions  False reporting.  False licensing.    School Located in Wyoming  There are no schools in Wyoming for storage tank operators.  However the Department of Environmental Quality occasionally holds informational seminars.  See the DEQ website for information.    License  All Class B Storage Tank Operators must be licensed in Wyoming by the Department of Environmental Quality.  Licenses are valid for five years    Examination  Exams are administered by the International Code Council.    Fees  None    Licensing Agency  Oma Gilbreth  Department of Environmental Quality   SHWD Storage Tank Program  200 West 17th Street  Cheyenne WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-7097  Fax: (307) 777-7682  http://deq.wyoming.gov/shwd/    Additional Sources of Information  International Code Council  Western Regional Office  3060 Saturn Street Suite 100  Brea California 92821  Phone: (888) 422-7233 ext 0  http://www.iccsafe.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  "First-Line Supervisors of Transportation and Material-Moving Machine and Vehicle Operators"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/about/data-for-occupations-not-covered-in-detail.htm#Transportation and Material Moving Occupations    Last updated June 2023"',
