     'CATHODIC PROTECTION TESTER', 'INSPECTORS, TESTERS, SORTERS, SAMPLERS, AND WEIGHERS  SOC Code 51-9061    Entry Salary  $19.72/hr  Average Salary  $25.06/hr    Job Description  Cathodic Protection Testers ensure that storage tanks are protected against corrosion.     Requirements  Must be certified by the Association for Materials Protection and Performance (AAMP, formerly NACE) or the Steel Tank Institute (STI).    Restrictions  Falsifying license application.  Falsifying reports.  Revocation by another agency.    School Located in Wyoming  Contact NACE International or STI for training information.    License  Cathodic Protection Testers are licensed in Wyoming by the Department of Environmental Quality (DEQ).  Licenses issued for Cathodic Protection Testers and Corrosion Experts shall expire on the date when the underlying certification by NACE or STI expires, or on the date an underlying license issued by another state or city expires, or on the date the underlying P.E. license expires    Examination  Examinations are conducted by NACE International and STI.    Fees  None.    Licensing Agency  Oma Gilbreth  Solid & Hazardous Waste Division  Wyoming Dept. of Environmental Quality  200 West 17th Street  Cheyenne, WY 820002  Phone: (307) 777-7097  Fax: (307) 777-7682  http://deq.wyoming.gov/shwd/    Additional Sources of Information  Association for Materials Protection and Performance (AAMP, formerly NACE-International and Society for Protective Coatings, SSPC)  15835 Park Ten Place  Houston, Texas 77084  Phone: (800) 797-6223  https://www.ampp.org/home    Steel Tank Institute  944 Donata Ct.  Lake Zurich, IL 60047  Phone: (847) 438-8265  http://www.steeltank.com/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Quality Control Inspectors"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/production/quality-control-inspectors.htm    Last updated June 2023"',
