     'MORTGAGE LOAN ORIGINATORS', 'LOAN OFFICERS  SOC Code 13-2072    Entry Salary  $24.56/hour  Average Salary  $31.43/hour    Job Description  Mortgage loan originators typically work with a borrower to complete a mortgage transaction.  This may include interviewing mortgage applicants, screening initial loan requests, collecting financial information to be used in the loan underwriting process, and monitoring the loan from application to closing.    Requirements    1. Complete an individual application form through the Nationwide Mortgage Licensing System (NMLS) website (http://mortgage.nationwidelicensingsystem.org/Pages/default.aspx)    2. Provide certification of 20 completed hours of pre-licensure education courses.    3. Obtain a passing grade on both the state and national components of the SAFE test.    4. Provide fingerprints for background check.    5. Authorize a credit report.    6. Be sponsored employed by and sponsored by a company with a unique NMLS number.    Continuing Education  There is no continuing education requirements for mortgage loan originators.    Restrictions  Had a mortgage loan originator license revoked by any governmental jurisdiction.  Has been convicted or pled guilty to a felony crime during the 7 years preceding the loan application or at any time preceding the loan application in the case of fraud, dishonesty, breach of trust, or money laundering.  Has not demonstrated financial responsibility, character, and/or general fitness.    Schools located in Wyoming  American Mortgage Training, AMT Campus- Cheyenne  http://amtcampus.com/   The courses required for this license are offered online by the NMLS at http://mortgage.nationwidelicensingsystem.org/profreq/education/Pages/default.aspx    License  A license to practice as a mortgage loan originator must be obtained through the Wyoming Division of Banking.  Licenses expire annually on December 31st.    Examination  The examination required for this license are offered online by the NMLS at http://mortgage.nationwidelicensingsystem.org/profreq/education/Pages/default.aspx     Fees  National exam with uniform state component . . . . . . ... $110  License. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  . . .. . . . . . . . . . . .$150  Renewal (annually). . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . ..  .$120    Licensing Agency  Christina Straw  Wyoming Division of Banking  122 W 25th Street  3rd Floor West  Cheyenne, WY 82001  Phone: (307) 777-6483  http://wyomingbankingdivision.wyo.gov/home    Additional Sources of Information  The Association of Mortgage Brokers  601 Pennsylvania Ave. NW, South Building  Washington, DC 20004  Phone: (202) 434-8250  Fax: (530) 484-2906  https://www.namb.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook  https://www.bls.gov/ooh/business-and-financial/loan-officers.htm    Last Updated June 2023',
