     'PODIATRIC ASSISTANT', 'MEDICAL ASSISTANTS  31-9092    Entry Salary  $15.93/hr  Average Salary  $19.86/hr    Job Description  Podiatric assistants perform x-rays for podiatrists in podiatry offices.    Requirements     1. Successfully pass the ASPMA examination OR     2. Intern with a Podiatrist for training which shall consist of not less than twenty (20) hours of educational instruction or supervised training in the following areas: Podiatric nomenclature; machine operation exposure factor; operator and patient safety; AND practical or clinical experience in the following: foot and ankle techniques for exposing radiographs; film handling and storage, if applicable; processing procedures; and patient record documentation for radiographs.    Continuing Education  There are currently no continuing education requirements for podiatric assistants    Restrictions  Certified podiatry assistant duties are limited to performing x-ray duties for podiatrists.    Schools located in Wyoming  There are no schools in Wyoming that offer podiatry assistant programs.    License  Certified podiatry assistants must have a certificate from the Wyoming Board of Podiatry to work in Wyoming.  A certificate will remain valid without needing to be renewed as long as the certificate holder remains employed with the same podiatrist.  Upon termination of employment with a podiatrist, the certificate holder may return the certificate to the Board office and a new certificate for the certificate holders current employer will be issued upon payment of transfer fee.    Examination  The ASPMA examination is available from the American Society of Podiatric Assistants https://aspma.org/    Fees  Podiatric Assistant Certificate . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $50.00  Certificate transfer fee . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  $20.00    Licensing Agency  Emily McIlvaine  Wyoming Board of Registration in Podiatry  2001 Capitol Avenue, Room 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://podiatry.wyo.gov/home    Additional Sources of Information  American Society of Podiatric Assistants  109 First Street  Itsaca, IL 60143  Phone: 1-888-88ASPMA (27762)  Fax: (847) 773-9976  https://aspma.org/      Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Medical Assistants"  https://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/medical-assistants.htm    Last updated May 2023"',
