     'NOTARY PUBLIC', 'OFFICE & ADMINISTRATIVE SUPPORT WORKERS, ALL OTHER  43-9199    Entry Salary  $20.57/hr  Average Salary  $23.61/hr    Job Description  Notaries public witness the signing of important documents and verify the identity of the signer(s), their willingness to sign the document(s), and their awareness of the contents of the document(s) or transaction.    Requirements     1.  Must be a resident of Wyoming.     2.  Must be 18 years of age or older.     3.  Must be able to read and write English.     4.  Must pass an examination.     4.  A $500 bond is required to be filed with the county clerk in the county where the notary public will be working.    Continuing Education:  There are no continuing education requirements for Notaries Public    Restrictions  Cannot be a convicted felon    Schools located in Wyoming  The Wyoming Secretary of State office regularly offers a course of study to applicants for new or renewed commission that covers laws, rules, procedures, and ethics related to the duties of a Notary Public.    License  Anyone wishing to become a notary public must obtain a commission from the Wyoming Secretary of States office.   Notary Public commissions are valid for six years.    Examination  An applicant for a new or renewed commission as a notary public in this state must pass an examination administered by the secretary of state or an entity approved by the secretary of state.    Fees  Commission . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $60  Commission Renewal (every 6 years) . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  $60    Licensing Agency  Wyoming Secretary of State  Compliance Division  Herschler Building East  122 West 25th Street Suite 100  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-7370  Fax: (307) 777-7640  https://sos.wyo.gov/Services/Notaries.aspx    Last updated June 2023',
