     'ACUPUNCTURISTS', 'ACUPUNCTURISTS  SOC CODE 29-1291    Entry Salary  N/A  Average Salary  N/A    Job Description  Acupuncturists diagnose, treat, and prevent disorders by stimulating specific acupuncture points within the body using acupuncture needles. May also use cups, nutritional supplements, therapeutic massage, acupressure, and other alternative health therapies.    Requirements  General License Requirements:     1.  A complete and legible application form with a recent, unmounted, full-face photograph     2.  Proof of lawful presence in the United States     3.  Payment of the fees set by the Board     4.  An official transcript giving evidence of graduation from an accredited American College of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine (ACAOM) program and     5.  Official passing score of the NCCAOM examination OR Evidence of continuous practice of acupuncture in Wyoming for the last ten (10) years prior to January 1, 2018 OR Official passing score of the California Acupuncture Licensing Examination.     6.  Verification of license in good standing from all jurisdictions in which the applicant is currently, or has ever been licensed or certified in any health care profession    Auricular Acupuncture License (trained through the National Acupuncture Detoxification Association (NADA) or a Board approved equivalent course to apply up to five fine-gauge, sterilized, one-time use stainless steel needles just under the skin at designated points in each ear) requirements:     1.  A complete and legible application form with a recent, unmounted, full-face photograph     2.  Proof of lawful presence in the United States     3.  Payment of the fees set by the Board     4.  Evidence of completion of NADA certification training or an equivalent training certificate approved by the Board.    Continuing Education  Licensees must complete a minimum of thirty hours of continuing education every two years.    Restrictions  No applicant for license shall have been convicted of an offense involving moral turpitude.  No applicant for license shall have been convicted of an offense involving controlled substances which may impair the applicant ability to provide competent health care or which could pose a threat to the safety of the consumer public    Schools located in Wyoming  There are currently no schools for acupuncture in Wyoming.     License  Licenses are issued by the Wyoming Board of Acupuncture.  Licenses expire annually    Examination  Exams are conducted by:  American College of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine https://www.acaom.edu/  California Board of Acupuncture https://www.acupuncture.ca.gov/students/examination.shtml  National Acupuncture Detoxification Association https://acudetox.com/    Fees  Acupuncturie application fee. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $200.00  Initial Acupuncture license fee. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $900.00  Initial Auricular Acupuncture License Fee. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $80.00  Acupuncture license annual renewal fee. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$450.00  Auricular Acupuncture License Annual Renewal Fee. . . . . . $50.00    Licensing Agency  Wyoming Board of Acupuncture  Emma Garcia, Licensing Specialist  2001 Capitol Ave  Room 127  Cheyenne, WY  82002  Phone: (307) 777- 5403   Fax: (307) 777- 3508  https://acupuncture.wyo.gov/    Additional Sources of Information  American College of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine  9100 Park W Dr  Houston, TX 77063  Phone: (713) 780-9777  https://www.acaom.edu/    National Acupuncture Detoxification Association  PO Box 367  Clinton, Maryland 20735  Phone: (888) 765- 6232  https://acudetox.com/    National Certification Commission for Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine  2001 K Street, NW, 3rd Floor North  Washington, D.C. 20006  Phone: (888) 381-1140 (toll-free number)  (202) 381-1140 (direct phone number)  Fax: (202) 381-1141   https://www.nccaom.org/    California Acupuncture Board  1625 North Market Blvd., Suite N-219  Sacramento, CA 95834  Phone: (916) 515-5200  Fax: (916) 928-2204  www.acupuncture.ca.gov    Wyoming Acupuncture Society  15 Shrine Club Road, Suite C  Lander, WY 82520  Phone: (307) 349-6120  https://www.wyoas.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  AcupuncturistsGÇ¥  https://www.bls.gov/oes/current/oes291291.htm    Last Updated June 2023"',
