     'SPEECH PATHOLOGIST', 'SPEECH-LANGUAGE PATHOLOGISTS  SOC Code 29-1127    Entry Salary  $30.88/hr  Average Salary  $31.74/hr    Job Description  Audiologists and speech pathologists help people with speech, language or hearing problems by examining the patient, diagnosing the disorder and providing treatment.     Requirements     1.  Submit evidence of clinical competency by verifying current ASHA certification;   or Complete the following:     2.  Clinical fellowship OR     3.  Education requirements identified in Section 4(b)(ii) of this chapter (submit transcripts complying with Wyoming Statute 33-33-105(a)(i) directly from the college, university, or institution); and     4.  Successful passage of the Praxis within the previous five (5) years.    Continuing Education  Twelve continuing education units (CEU) are required annually for license renewal.    Restrictions  Fraud.  Conviction of a felony.   Unprofessional conduct.  Violating any provision of the License Act for Speech Pathologists and Audiologists.    School Located in Wyoming  University of Wyoming - Laramie - Division of Communication Disorders  http://www.uwyo.edu/comdis/    License  Speech Pathologists must be licensed in Wyoming by the Board of Speech Pathology and Audiology.   Licenses expire annually on December 31st.    Examination  ASHA examinations are conducted online and in hard copy. For more information go to   http://www.ets.org/praxis/asha    Fees  Provisional Application. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .. . . . $200.00  Initial License by Completing Provisional . . . . . . $100.00  Initial License. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $300.00  Endorsement. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$300.00  Annual Renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  . . .$100.00    Licensing Agency  Emily McIlvaine  Board of Speech Pathology & Audiology  2001 Capitol Avenue, Room 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://speech.wyo.gov/home        Additional Sources of Information  American Speech-Language-Hearing Association  2200 Research Blvd.  Rockville, MD 20850-3289  Phone:   Members: (800) 498-2071  Non-Member: (800) 638-8255  http://www.asha.org/    Speech-LanguagePathologist.org  P.O. Box 880053  Boca Raton, FL 33488-0053  Phone: (561) 998-9501  http://www.speech-languagepathologist.org/index.htm    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Speech-Language Pathologists"   http://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/speech-language-pathologists.htm    Last updated April 2023"',
