     'ESTHETICIAN', 'SKINCARE SPECIALISTS  SOC Code 39-5094    Entry Salary  $19.31/hr  Average Salary  $20.28/hr    Job Description  Performs services for others for the beautification of the skin. Practice is limited to applying make-up, moisturizing, cleansing and facial or neck massage.     Requirements     1.  Must have a minimum 10th grade education.     2.  Be a graduate of a cosmetology school and have met training requirements comparable to those set forth in board rules.     3.  Must complete no less than 600 hours of theory and practical instruction.     4.  Submit proper credentials as required by the board no less than fifteen (15) days before the examination is to be given;     5.  Pass a written and practical examination.     Continuing Education  There are no continuing education requirements for cosmetologists.    School Located in Wyoming  There are numerous beauty schools located throughout Wyoming. Contact the Wyoming Board of Cosmetology for a listing of licensed schools.     License  A license is issued by the Wyoming Board of Cosmetology after meeting the requirements of the state.   A first year license is issued for one year from the month of acquisition.  After that, licenses expire every two years during the licensees month of birth.      Examination  The examination is administered by the Wyoming Board of Cosmetology.    Fees  Examination Fee . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $100.00  License. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .. $48.00  Biennial Renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $96.00     Licensing Agency  Sharon Bennett  Wyoming Board of Cosmetology  2515 Warren Ave., Ste. 302  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3534  Fax: (307) 777-3681  http://cosmetology.wy.gov/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Skincare Specialists"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/personal-care-and-service/skincare-specialists.htm    Last updated June 2023"',
