     'LAWYER', 'LAWYERS  SOC Code 23-1011    Entry Salary  $24.83/hr  Average Salary  $39.20/hr    Job Description  Lawyers advise clients regarding legal rights, procedures and obligations, in addition to representing them in courts of law.  Lawyers also represent clients before government agencies and prepare any appropriate legal documents.     Requirements  By Exam:     1.  Graduate from an approved ABA-accredited law school.      2.  A score of at least 270 on the Uniform Bar Exam (UBE)      3.  A score of at least 85 on the Multistate Professional Responsibility Examination (MPRE)     4.  Must be found to be of good moral character and fitness to practice law as found by the National Conference of Bar Examiners (NCBE) character report and review by the Character and Fitness committee.    By Motion:     1.  Must have engaged in active practice of law for 5-7 years preceding application for motion     2.  Certificates of admission and good standing from the highest court for each jusrisdiction in which the applicant is admitted to practice law     3.  Evidence of compliance with the continuing legal education (CLE) requirements of all  jurisdictions in which the applicant is admitted to practice law (if applicable)     4.  Must be found to be of good moral character and fitness to practice law as found by the National Conference of Bar Examiners (NCBE) character report and review by the Character and Fitness committee.     5.  J.D. from an ABA-approved law school     6.  A scaled score of 85 or higher on the Multistate Professional Responsibility Examination  (MPRE)     By Uniform Bar Exam (UBE) Score Transfer:     1.  Graduate from an approved ABA-accredited law school     2.  Transfer of a score of at least 270 on the Uniform Bar Exam (UBE)     3.  Transfer of a score of at least 85 on the Multistate Professional Responsibility Examination (MPRE)     4.  Must be found to be of good moral character and fitness to practice law as found by the National Conference of Bar Examiners (NCBE) character report and review by the Character and Fitness committee.    Continuing Education Requirements:  Fifteen hours of continuing education are required per year, including two hours of ethics.    For more information, please visit: https://www.courts.state.wy.us/supreme-court/bar-admission/    Restrictions  Admission depends on detailed background investigation.     School Located in Wyoming  University of Wyoming - Laramie - College of Law  http://www.uwyo.edu/law/    License  Lawyers must be licensed by the Wyoming Supreme Court and be admitted to the Wyoming State Bar to practice law.   Licenses expire annually on October 1st    Examination  Multiple-choice and essay examinations are administered on the last Tuesday and Wednesday in February and the last Tuesday and Wednesday in July.    Fees  Examination . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  $600.00 plus $395-$555 for character investigation  Admission by Motion. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$600.00 plus $555 for character investigation  Uniform Bar Exam Score Transfer . . . . . . . . . . . . . $600.00 plus $395 for character investigation  Yearly Dues. . . . . . . . . . .  . . .  . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  . . ..$237.50-$355    Licensing Agency  Cathy Duncil, Admissions Director  Wyoming State Bar  Board of Law Examiners  P.O. Box 109  Cheyenne, WY 82003  Phone: (307) 432-2105  Fax: (307) 632-3737  http://www.wyomingbar.org/    Additional Sources of Information    American Bar Association  321 N. Clark St.  Chicago, IL 60654-7598  Phone: (31) 988-5000  http://www.americanbar.org/aba.html    Federal Bar Association  4075 Wilson Boulevard, 8th Floor  Arlington, VA 22203  Phone: (571) 481-9090  http://www.fedbar.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Lawyers"   http://www.bls.gov/ooh/legal/lawyers.htm    Last Updated May 2023"',
