     'HEARING AID SPECIALIST', 'HEARING AID SPECIALISTS  SOC Code 29-2092    Entry Salary  N/A  Average Salary  N/A    Job Description  Hearing aid specialists provide technical assistance to those who are hearing impaired. Duties include audiometric testing, fitting, dealing and dispensing of hearing aid equipment.     Requirements     1.  References from three (3) individuals familiar with the applicant with whom the applicant has had contact within the past five (5) years. References shall: (A) Be written within the last six (6) months; (B) Not be from relatives of the applicant; and (C) Contain an original signature and be submitted directly to the office of the Board from the respondent and not  orwarded through the applicant.     2.  Submit a certification of calibration of all audiometric equipment in use signed by a qualified person during the pevious twelve (12) months     3.  Successfully pass the written, practical, and jurisprudence examinations.    Continuing Education  Licensees must complete ten hours of continuing education during the twelve months prior to license expiration.    Restrictions  All applications are reviewed by the State Board.     School Located in Wyoming  There are no schools for Hearing Aid Specialists in Wyoming.     License  Hearing aid specialists must be licensed by the Wyoming Board of Hearing Aid Specialists.   Licenses expire annually on January 30th.    Examination  Written examinations are conducted by the International Hearing Society.  See their website for information https://myhome.ihsinfo.org/myhome/Licensing_Exam/ILE_Home.aspx    Fees  Application. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $200.00  Jurisprudence Exam Fee . . .  . . $50.00  Practical Examination  . . . . . . . $300.00  Initial License Fee . . . . . . . .  . . .$200.00  Temporary Permit. . . . . . . . . . . $300.00  Annual Renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . .$300.00    Licensing Agency  Chris Frint  Wyoming Board of Hearing Aid Specialists  2001 Capitol Avenue  Room 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://hearingaid.wyo.gov/home    Additional Sources of Information  Hearing Industries Association  655 New York Avenue NW, Floor 6  Washington DC 20001  Phone: (202) 975-0905  http://hearing.org/    International Hearing Society (IHS)  33900 W. 8 Mile Road., Suite 101   Farmington, MI 48335  Phone: (734) 522-7200  https://www.ihsinfo.org/home    Additional Information  Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Hearing Aid Specialists"  https://www.bls.gov/oes/current/oes292092.htm    Last updated April 2023"',
