     'CERTIFIED PUBLIC ACCOUNTANT', 'ACCOUNTANTS AND AUDITORS  SOC Code 13-2011    Entry Salary  $25.06/hr  Average Salary  $31.85/hr    Job Description  Certified Public Accountants (CPAs) examine, analyze, and interpret accounting records for the purpose of giving advice or preparing statements for establishments and individuals. They install or advise on systems of recording costs or other financial and budgetary data, provide tax advice, and prepare tax returns.     Requirements    1.  Is a resident of Wyoming or has a place of business in Wyoming or, as an employee, is regularly employed in Wyoming;    2. Has attained the age of majority in Wyoming;    3. Has passed a written examination in accounting and auditing and other related subjects the Board determines to be appropriate (Uniform AICPA Examination);    4. Provide a transcript, delivered directly to the board office by an accredited college or university, showing proof of graduation from a baccalaureate or higher degree program which must include a minimum of 24 semester hours of accounting courses and a minimum of 24 semester hours of business courses.    5. Must be currently employed in Wyoming or have a valid, documented, and accepted offer of employment with a Wyoming CPA firm or other Wyoming set to begin within six months of acceptance, or must be a current student at the University of Wyoming or a Wyoming community college.  6. Provides evidence of lawful presence in the United States.    Continuing Education  1. No continuing education requirement for the first renewal period after licensure.  2. 60 credits of continuing education must be completed within the two years before the second renewal period after licensure.  3. 120 credits of continuing education must be completed every three years after the second license renewal period.  4. At least 66% of credits must relate to the technical aspects of the licensee field of business as a Certified Public Accountant. The remaining credits may contribute to the professional competence of a Certified Public Accountant.  5. A credit of continuing education is equal to 50 minutes of a nano learning program.  One semester hour of a college course equals 15 credits.  Credits can be earned by presenting, instructing, publishing research or articles, etc. See state statutes for more information.     Restrictions  Conviction of a felony or any crime which is dishonest or fraudulent.  Grounds for revocation or suspension include:  Failure to furnish evidence of completion on continuing professional education requirements.  Cancellation, revocation, suspension or refusal to renew the authority to practice as a Certified Public Accountant by any other state for any cause except failure to pay fees.  Dishonesty, fraud or gross negligence in the practice of public accounting.  Violation of the Boards Practice Act and/or rules.    School Located in Wyoming  University of Wyoming - Laramie - College of Business - Accounting   http://www.uwyo.edu/acct-fin/    License  All individuals who practice in Wyoming as Certified Public Accountants must be licensed by the Wyoming Board of Certified Public Accountants.     Examination  The examination is administered by the American Institute of CPAs (AICPA).    Fees  For complete information about fees, go to the Wyoming Board of Certified Public Accountants website at https://sites.google.com/a/wyo.gov/wyoming-cpa/licensing-permit-fees-instructions or call (307) 777-7551.    Licensing Agency  Christopher Stout, Business Office and Licensing Coordinator  Wyoming Board of Certified Public Accountants  325 W. 18th St., Ste. 4  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone : (307) 777-7551  https://sites.google.com/a/wyo.gov/wyoming-cpa/    Additional Sources of Information  American Institute of CPAs  Princeton South Corporate Center  100 Princeton South, Ste. 200  Ewing, NJ 08628  Phone: (609) 671-2902  https://www.aicpa-cima.com/home    National Association of State Boards of Accountancy  150 Fourth Avenue, N, Ste. 700  Nashville, TN 37219-2417  Phone: (615) 880-4200  http://nasba.org/    Wyoming Society of CPAs  504 W 17th St, Ste 250  Cheyenne, WY 82001  Phone: (307) 634-7039  https://www.wyocpa.org    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Accountants and Auditors"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/business-and-financial/accountants-and-auditors.htm    Last Updated April 2023  "',
