     'SCHOOL LIBRARIAN', 'LIBRARIANS AND MEDIA COLLECTIONS SPECIALISTS  SOC Code 25-4022    Entry Salary  $18.99/hr  Average Salary  $25.05/hr    Job Description  Librarians organize information in libraries and help people locate materials. They order, catalog, classify, and maintain collections of books, periodicals, films, and recordings. They answer routine and complex requests for information. In addition, librarians often teach library skills.     Requirements  Must complete an approved program for preparation as a school librarian.     Continuing Education  Must complete 5 credits or 70 clock hours of continuing education per renewal period    Restrictions  Conviction of a felony or committing an immoral act.   Gross negligence, incompetence, immorality, or other reprehensive conduct.   Fraud or deceit in obtaining certification.     School Located in Wyoming  Wyoming does not currently have any schools that offer degrees in libary science.    License  School librarians must meet Professional Education and Library Media Standards.   Licenses are valid for five years    Examination  None.     Fees  Fingerprinting . . . . . . .. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $50.00  License (In-State) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $175.00  License (Out-of-State) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$225.00  Renewal . . . . . . . . . . . . . .. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $225.00    Licensing Agency  Brendan OConnor, Assistant Director  Professional Teaching Standards Board  Emerson Bldg  2001 Capitol Ave, Room 128  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone : (307) 777-1926  Fax: (307) 777-8718  http://ptsb.state.wy.us/    Additional Sources of Information  Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Librarians and Media Collections Specialists"   https://www.bls.gov/oes/current/oes254022.htm    Last Updated June 2023"',
