     'TEACHER', 'TEACHERS  SOC Codes 25-2012, 25-2021, 25-2023, 25-2022, 25-2031, 25-2032    Go to http://doe.state.wy.us/lmi/oes.htm for wage information for each of the SOC codes listed above.    Job Description  Elementary and Secondary Teachers provide classroom instruction to students in kindergarten through twelfth grade.     Requirements  Earn a Standard Teaching license which requires completion of a nationally or regionally accredited teacher preparation program in the specific program.     Continuing Education  Must complete 5 credits or 70 clock hours of continuing education per renewal period.    Restrictions  Conviction of a felony or committing an immoral act.  Incompetence, immorality, gross negligence or other reprehensible conduct.  Fraud or deceit in obtaining certification.    School Located in Wyoming  University of Wyoming - Laramie - College of Education  https://www.uwyo.edu/education/index.html  The Elementary Education Degree can be obtained either at Casper College through the University of Wyoming at Casper College (UWCC) program (http://www.uwyo.edu/distance/programs/bachelor.html).    License  All Public School Teachers must be licensed by the Professional Teaching Standards Board.   Licenses are valid for five years    Examination  The Praxis II examination is administered by ETS and is required for teachers with endorsements in elementary education and social studies comprehensive. For more information go to http://www.ets.org/praxis/wy or call ETS at (609) 771-7395.    Fees  Fingerprinting. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $50.00  License (In-State) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $175.00  License (Out-of-State) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$225.00  Renewal (Every 5 Years) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$225.00    Licensing Agency  Brendan OConnor, Assistant Director  Professional Teaching Standards Board  Emerson Building  2001 Capitol Ave, Room 128  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-1926  Fax: (307) 777-8718  http://ptsb.state.wy.us/    Additional Sources of Information  National Education Association  1201 16th Street, NW  Washington, DC 20036-3290  Phone: (202) 833-4000  http://www.nea.org    Council for Accreditation of Educator Preparation  1140 19th St NW, Suite 400  Washington, DC 20036  Phone: (202) 223-0077  http://caepnet.org    American Federation of Teachers, AFL-CIO  555 New Jersey Avenue, NW  Washington, DC 20001  Phone: (202) 879-4400  http://www.aft.org/    Wyoming Education Association  115 E. 22nd Street  Cheyenne, WY 82001  Phone: (307) 634-7991  http://wyoea.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Kindergarten and Elementary School Teachers"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/education-training-and-library/kindergarten-and-elementary-school-teachers.htm    "Middle School Teachers"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/education-training-and-library/middle-school-teachers.htm    "High School Teachers"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/education-training-and-library/high-school-teachers.htm    Last Updated June 2023"',
