     'LICENSED PRACTICAL NURSE', 'LICENSED PRACTICAL AND LICENSED VOCATIONAL NURSES  SOC Code 29-2061    Entry Salary  $23.74/hr  Average Salary  $24.44/hr    Job Description  Licensed Practical Nurses perform technical services requiring basic knowledge of the biological, physical, behavioral, psychological, and sociological sciences, as well as knowledge of nursing procedures.     Requirements     1.  Graduate from a State-approved practical nursing program.     2.  Pass the NCLEX-RN or NCLEX-PN accordingly.     3.  Pass a criminal background check     4.  Meet continued competency requirement.    Continuing Education  Although there are no set continuing education requirements in Wyoming, a licensed practical nurse must meet specific continuing competency requirements for license renewal.  These include completion of at least 400 hours of active nursing during the previous two years or completion of 200 hours of active nursing and 15 hours of continuing education during the previous two years or completion of thirty hours of continuing education during the previous two years or successfully passing the NCLEX exam during the prior two years.    Restrictions  All applications are reviewed by the State Board.     School Located in Wyoming  Laramie County Community College - Cheyenne - Nursing Program  http://www.lccc.wy.edu/programs/nursing  Northern Wyoming Community College District - Gillette and Sheridan - Nursing  https://www.sheridan.edu/academics/programs-a-z/nursing/  Western Wyoming Community College - Rock Springs - Practical Nursing   https://www.westernwyoming.edu/academics/major-programs/health-care/nursing/index.php    License  Practical nurses must be licensed by the State Board of Nursing.   Licenses expire on October 1st of even numbered years.    Examination  Successfully pass the NCLEX specific to LPN education program    Fees  Licensing by Endorsement (Out of State). . . . . . . . . $120.00  Licensing by Examination. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $130.00  Renewal . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$90.00  Background Check. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . ..  $60.00    Licensing Agency  Raymie Bingman, Licensing Lead  Wyoming State Board of Nursing  130 Hobbs Avenue, Ste. B  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone : (307) 777-7601  Fax : (307) 777-3519  http://nursing-online.state.wy.us/    Additional Sources of Information  National Association of Licensed Practical Nurses  3801 Lake Boone Trail, Suite 190  Raleigh, NC 27607  Phone: (919) 779-5642  https://nalpn.org/    National Association for Practical Nurse Education and Service, Inc.  2071 N Bechtle Avenue PMB 307   Springfield, OH 45504-1583  Phone:(703) 933-1003  https://napnes.org/site/    Wyoming Nurses Association  301 Thelma Dr., Ste. 200  Casper, WY 82609  Phone: (800) 795-6381  http://wyonurse.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Licensed Practical and Licensed Vocational Nurses "  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/licensed-practical-and-licensed-vocational-nurses.htm    Last updated May 2023"',
