     'PHYSICAL THERAPIST', 'PHYSICAL THERAPISTS   SOC Code 29-1123    Entry Salary  $39.87/hr   Average Salary  $40.52/hr    Job Description  Physical Therapists help people overcome or adjust to physical disabilities caused by injury, illness or birth defects. Therapists work in the areas of neurology, orthopedics, pediatrics, geriatrics, sports medicine, pain management and cardiology.    Requirements     1.  An official transcript giving evidence of graduation from nationally accredited program approved by the Board;     2.  Passing scores on the National Physical Therapy Examination (NPTE);     3.  A successfully completed state jurisprudence examination with a passing score of at least seventy-five (75) percent;    Continuing Education  Licensees just successfully complete thirty continuing competence units and successfully complete the jurisprudence examination every two years.      Restrictions Conviction of a felony.  Habitual use of alcohol or drugs. Failure to adhere to the Practice Act. Misconduct or negligent practice.  Mental incompetence.    School Located in Wyoming  There are no schools offering Physical Therapist degrees located in Wyoming.    License  Physical Therapists must be licensed and Physical Therapy Assistants must be registered by the Wyoming Board of Physical Therapy.  Licenses expire annually on October 1st.    Examination  The NPTE is given by Computer Based Testing and can be taken throughout the year. The NPTE is given through the Federation of State Boards of Physical Therapy (FSBPT).  The state Jurisprudence Exam is conducted by the Wyoming Board of Physical Therapy.    Fees  Application. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $240.00  Examination. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $400.00  Annual Renewal . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $75.00    Licensing Agency Carla Fleming  Wyoming Board of Physical Therapy   2001 Capitol Avenue  Room 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-5403  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://physicaltherapy.wyo.gov/    Additional Sources of Information American Physical Therapy Association   1111 North Fairfax Street  Alexandria, VA 22314-1488  Phone: (800) 999-2782  http://www.apta.org/    Federation of State Boards of Physical Therapy   124 West Street South, Third Floor  Alexandria, VA 22314  Phone: (703) 299-3100  http://www.fsbpt.org/    Wyoming Physical Therapy Association   1347 S. Wisconsin Avenue  Casper, WY 82609   http://www.wypta.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook: Physical Therapists"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/physical-therapists.htm     Last updated May 2023  "',
