     'DENTAL HYGIENIST', 'DENTAL HYGIENIST  SOC Code 29-1292    Entry Salary  $38.80/hr  Average Salary  $39.33/hr    Job Description  Dental Hygienists work under the supervision of dentists to help people prevent tooth decay, gum disease and maintain oral health. They clean and polish teeth, noting conditions of decay and disease for diagnosis by a dentist. They also take and develop X-rays and may place, carve and finish amalgam restorations, as well as place and finish composites and administer local anesthesia if they obtain an expanded function certificate.     Requirements     1.  Complete a Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) approved U.S. or Canadian dental hygiene program.      2.  Passing score from one of the following: Western Regional Examining Board (WREB), Central Regional Dental Testing Service (CRDTS), Commission on Dental Competency Assessments (CDCA), Council of Interstate Testing Agencies (CITA), or Southern Regional Testing Agency (SRTA).     3.  Pass the American Dental Association National Board Examination (NBDHE).      4.  Proof of successful passage of patient or non-patient (manikin) based clinical licensure examination.     4.  Must have current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification.    Continuing Education  Licensees must acquire sixteen hours of continuing education which must be completed by the end of odd numbered years.  Dental hygienists newly licensed during even years must acquire eight hours of continuing education before license renewal.    Restrictions  Qualifications fraudulently obtained.  Conviction of a felony.  Dishonest or illegal practice of dental hygiene.  Habitual addiction to drugs, including alcohol.    Schools Located in Wyoming  Sheridan College - Sheridan - Dental Hygiene  https://www.sheridan.edu/academics/programs-a-z/dental-hygiene/  University of Wyoming - Laramie - Dental Hygiene  http://www.uwyo.edu/hs/divisions-and-programs/dental-hygiene-program.html  Laramie County Community College - Cheyenne   http://lccc.wy.edu/pathways/healthSciencesWellness/dentalHygieneProgram/index.aspx    License  Dental Hygienists must be licensed by the State Board of Dental Examiners.   Licenses expire on December 31st on odd numbered years.    Examination  Information about the CRDTS examination can be found at https://crdts.org/DentalHygiene  Information about the CDCA-KWREB-CITA examination can be found at https://adextesting.org/adex-dental-hygiene/      Fees  Application/examinations. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $150.00  Application by Endorsement . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$200.00  Expanded Function Application . . . . . . . . . . . . .$30.00  Biennial Renewal. . . . . . .. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  $170.00    Licensing Agency  Felisha Ojeda  Wyoming Board of Dental Examiners  2001 Capitol Ave, Room 127  Cheyenne, WY  82002  Phone: (307) 777-7387  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://dental.wyo.gov/home              Additional Sources of Information  American Dental Hygienists Association  444 North Michigan Ave., Ste. 3400  Chicago, IL 60611  Phone: (312) 440-8900  http://www.adha.org    American Association of Public Health Dentistry  136 Everett Road  Albany, NY 12205  Phone: (518) 694-5525  http://aaphd.org/    Wyoming Dental Association  2700 Carey Ave.  Cheyenne, WY 82001  Phone: (307) 237-1186  http://wyda.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Dental Hygienists"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/dental-hygienists.htm    Last updated April 2023"',
