     'NURSING HOME ADMINISTRATOR', 'MEDICAL AND HEALTH SERVICES MANAGERS  SOC Code 11-9111    Entry Salary  $38.88/hr  Average Salary  $49.67/hr    Job Description  Nursing home administrators develop, manage, and direct health care programs such as preventive medicine and staff training.  Other duties include managing institution employees, overseeing building and/or equipment maintenance, and reviewing budgets and accounting procedures.     Requirements     1.  Possess as a minimum a college Bachelors degree.      2. Complete 500 hours administrator-in-training under the supervision of a licensed nursing home administrator.     3. .Every applicant for licensure shall have successfully completed a national written examination with a passing scaled score that is acceptable to the Board.     4. .All licenses previously held must be verified.      5.  Two (2) letters of recommendation from professional associates, attesting to the applicants ability to perform as a Nursing Home Administrator;    Continuing Education  Licensees must complete twenty five hours of continuing education annually for license renewal.    Restrictions  Conviction of a felony or misdemeanor involving moral turpitude.  Soliciting residents by any form of false, deceptive, or misleading communication including advertisements.  Unprofessional or unethical conduct.  Gross incompetence or malpractice.  Knowingly submitting false information to the Board.  Mental or physical incompetency as to render the licensee unable to perform with reasonable skill and safety.  Incompetent or negligent practice.  Intemperate use of alcohol or controlled substances.  Violation of the Wyoming Controlled Substances Act.  Violation of the statutes, rules and regulations of the Board.  Violation of any state or federal law relating to operation or licensing of nursing homes or other health care facility.  Fraud.  Practice without a current license issued by the Board.  Failing to exercise regard for the safety, health or life of a resident or acting in a manner inconsistent with the health or safety of a resident.  Discrimination of residents, employees or staff on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin or handicap.    School Located in Wyoming  There are no colleges specializing in health care administration located in Wyoming. The following colleges offer business management and/or administration degrees:  Casper College - Casper - Business Administration - Associates  http://www.caspercollege.edu/business-administration  Central Wyoming College - Riverton - Accounting and Business - Associates   http://www.cwc.edu/programs/business--entrepreneurship--/business/  Eastern Wyoming College - Torrington - Business Administration - Associates  https://ewc.wy.edu/academic-services/majors/accounting-and-business/  Laramie County Community College - Cheyenne - Business Administration - Associates  http://lccc.wy.edu/pathways/businessAccounting/appliedManagmentProgram/index.aspx  Northern Wyoming Community College District - Sheridan and Gillette - Business - Associates  https://www.sheridan.edu/academics/programs-a-z/business/  Northwest Community College - Powell - Business - Associates  https://nwc.edu/sites/business/  Western Wyoiming Community College - Rock Springs - Business and Technology - Associates  https://www.westernwyoming.edu/academics/major-programs/business/index.php  University of Wyoming - Laramie - Department of Management and Marketing - Undergraduate and Graduate degrees  http://www.uwyo.edu/mgtmkt/index.html  http://www.uwyo.edu/mba/index.html    License  All nursing home administrators must be licensed in Wyoming by the Board of Nursing Home Administrators.   Licenses expire annually on December 31st.    Examination  Contact the National Association of Long Term Care Administrator Boards at http://www.nabweb.org/ or (202) 712-9040 for testing information.    Fees  Application Fee. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$350.00  ProvisionalLicense . . . . .  . . . . . . .  .$400.00  Annual Renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . .. $300.00     Licensing Agency  Felisha Ojeda  Board of Nursing Home Administrators  2001 Capitol Avenue, Room127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone : (307) 777-3628  Fax:  (307) 777-3314  http://nha.state.wy.us/    Additional Source of Information  National Association of Long Term Care Administrator Boards (NAB)  1120 20th Street, NW, Ste. 750  Washington, DC 20036  Phone: (202) 712-9040  http://www.nabweb.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Medical and Health Services Managers"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/medical-and-health-services-managers.htm    Last updated June 2023"',
