     'BARBER', 'BARBERS  SOC Code 39-5011    Entry Salary   N/A  Average Salary   N/A    Job Description  Barbers cut, style and color hair to each customers preference. Other services include shaves, scalp treatment and facials. Some barbers also sell lotions, tonics and other cosmetic supplies.     Requirements     1.  Graduate from an accredited barber school.      2.  Pass the written and practical examination.     Continuing education  No continuing education is required for license renewal.    Restrictions  Unprofessional conduct, incompetence or gross malpractice.  Making a false statement on an application to the Board.    School Located in Wyoming  Barber School  Rocky Mountain Academy  315 E 5th Street  Casper, WY 82601  (307) 262-4247  http://rockymountainacademy.net/    Cheeks Beauty Academy  Wyoming Barber Program  207 W 18th Street  Cheyenne, WY 82001  (307) 637-8700  https://www.cheeksbeautyacademy.com/    Chopped Beauty Academy  440 Nevada Avenue  Lovell, Wyoming 82431  (307) 548-2122  https://choppedbeautyacademy.com/    Eastern Wyoming College - Torrington - Barbering  https://ewc.wy.edu/academic-services/majors/cosmetology/  Central Wyoming College - Riverton - Barbering  https://www.cwc.edu/cosmo/      License  A license to practice as a barber in Wyoming must be obtained from the Board of Barber Examiners.   Licenses must be renewed annually.    Examination  The examination is given at least once every six months.    Fees  Registered Barber/Barber Stylist Examination . . . . . . . . . . . $125.00  Certificate/license of registration (annual). . . . . . . . . . .  . . . $75.00    Licensing Agency  Sharon Bennett  Board of Barber Examiners  2515 Warren Ave., Ste. 302   Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3534  Fax: (307) 777-3681  https://cosmetology.wyo.gov/barber-information    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Barbers Hairdressers and Cosmetologists"  https://www.bls.gov/ooh/personal-care-and-service/barbers-hairstylists-and-cosmetologists.htm  