     'ADDICTIONS THERAPIST', 'SUBSTANCE ABUSE AND BEHAVIORAL DISORDER COUNSELORS  SOC Code 21-1011    Entry Salary  N/A  Average Salary  N/A    Job Description  Addictions Therapists provide services based on theory and methods of counseling, psychotherapy, and addictionology to persons who are experiencing cognitive, affective or behavioral pychosocial dysfunction as a direct or indirect result of addiction, chemical dependency, abuse of chemical substances or related disorders. The practice of addictions therapy includes, but is not limited to, performing mental health procedures, addiction prevention, crisis intervention, assessment, diagnosis, referral, direct treatment, and follow-up treatment which is rendered to individuals, families, groups, organizations, schools and communities who are adversely affected by addictions or related disorders.    Requirements     1.  Age of majority.      2.  Has received a Masters or Doctorate degree in concentration in addictionology, chemical dependency, or substance abuse, healing arts or related field.     3.  Has completed 3,000 hours of supervised clinical experience including a minimum of 100 hours of face-to-face individual clinical supervision from a qualified clinical supervisor; of the 3,000 hours required, at least 1,200 shall be direct client contact hours.     4.  A passing score on  the Association for Addictions Professionals (NAADAC), NCAC Master Addiction Counselor (MAC) exam or  the National Board for Certified Counselors (NBCC) Master Addiction Counselor (MAC) exam or the  International Certification & Reciprocity Consortium (IC&RC) Advanced Alcohol and Drug Counselor (AADC) exam or another examination as may be approved by the Board.    Continuing Education  All licenseess must complete a minumum of three hours of continuing education activities in professional ethics and three hours of continuing education activites in suicide assessment and prevention.   Addictions therapists much also complete a minumum of fifteen contact hours of continuing education in addictions specific topics.    Restrictions  Felony conviction.  Misdemeanor conviction involving moral turpitude.    School Located in Wyoming  Casper College - Casper - School of Social and Behavioral Sciences - Addictionology - Associates  http://caspercollege.edu/addictionology/  Central Wyoming College - Riverton - Psychology (Associates)  https://www.cwc.edu/programs/socialsciences/psychology/  Sheridan College - Sheridan - Addictions Practitioner (Certificate of Completion)  https://www.sheridan.edu/academics/programs-a-z/addictions-practitioner/  University of Wyoming - Laramie - Counseling  (Masters of Science)  https://www.uwyo.edu/uw/degree-programs/counseling-masters.html    License  Addictions Therapists engaged in practice in Wyoming are licensed by the Mental Health Professions Licensing Board.   Licenses expire every two years on licensee birthday.    Examination  The Board accepts the following examinations: The Association for Addiction Professionals (NAADAC), National Certified Addictions Counselor (NCAC), Master Addiction Counselor (MAC); and the National Board for Certified Counselors (NBCC) Master Addiction Counselor (MAC) Exam.    Fees  Licensure by reciprocity. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$350.00  Licensure by examination. . . . . . . . . . . . . . $350.00  Licensure by completing provisional. . . . . . $200.00  License renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $125.00 plus $75.00 for every additional discipline    Licensing Agency  Mental Health Professions Licensing Board  2001 Capitol Avenue  Room 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307) 777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3508  http://mentalhealth.wyo.gov/        Additional Sources of Information  American Counseling Association  PO Box 31110  Alexandria, VA 22310  Phone: (800) 347-6647  http://counseling.org/    The Association for Addiction Professionals (NAADAC)  44 Canal Center Plaza, Ste 301  Alexandria, VA 22314  Phone: (703) 741-7686   http://www.naadac.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Substance Abuse and Behavioral Disorder Counselors"  https://www.bls.gov/ooh/community-and-social-service/substance-abuse-behavioral-disorder-and-mental-health-counselors.htm    Last updated April 2023"',
