     'OCCUPATIONAL THERAPIST', 'OCCUPATIONAL THERAPISTS  SOC Code 29-1122    Entry Salary  $31.22/hr  Average Salary  $39.51/hr    Job Description  Occupational Therapists plan, organize, and conduct occupational therapy programs to facilitate rehabilitation of mentally, physically, or emotionally handicapped individuals.     Requirements     1.  Completed application and fee;     2.  Passing score on the national certification examination, administered by the National Board for Certificaton in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT).      3.  Verification of all health care profession licenses held, active or inactive.     4.  Verification of lawful presence in the United States.    Continuing Education  Licensees must complete twenty-four hours of continuing education every two years.    Restrictions  Conviction of a felony.  Fraud.  Unprofessional conduct.  Violating any provision of the Occupational Therapy Practice Act.    Schools Located in Wyoming  University of North Dakota, offered at the Casper College campus - Occupational Therapy  http://www.med.und.edu/occupational-therapy/    License  Occupational Therapists must be licensed by the Board of Occupational Therapy to practice in Wyoming.   Licenses expire annually on July 31st.  License renewal applications must be postmarked or hand delivered to the Board no later than June 15th.    Examination  Examinations are given by the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT).     Fees  License Fee. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .   $225.00  Temporary license . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .  $50.00  Limited permit . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .$50.00  License renewal. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . $110.00    Licensing Agency  Chris Frint  Board of Occupational Therapy  2001 Capitol Avenue, Room 127  Cheyenne, WY 82002  Phone: (307)-777-3628  Fax: (307) 777-3314  https://occupationaltherapy.wyo.gov/    Additional Sources of Information  The American Occupational Therapy Association, Inc.  6116 Executive Boulevard, Suite 200  North Bethesda, MD 20852-4929  Phone: (301) 652-6611  http://www.aota.org/    National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy, Inc. (NBCOT)  One Bank Street, Ste 300  Gaithersburg, MD 20877  Phone: (301) 990-7979  http://www.nbcot.org/    Wyoming Occupational Therapy Assocation  1695  N Mill Creek Rd  Casper, WY  82604  Phone: (307) 251-0884  http://www.wyota.org/    Occupational Outlook Handbook:  Occupational Therapists"  http://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/occupational-therapists.htm    Last updated May 2023"',
