    ('66', '01', 'cdl', 'dmv',
     'Commercial Drivers License (CDL)', 'Commercial Drivers Licenses are issued by state departments but are similar from state to state, since the minimum requirements of the licenses and endorsements are set centrally. For more information contact the state DMV or https://cms.fmcsa.dot.gov/registration/commercial-drivers-license/how-do-i-get-commercial-drivers-license.',
     '0', '1', '0', '0', '0',
     '0', '0', '1', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20190719'),
    ('69', '01', '0000000001', '001',
     'Attorney', 'Description of Occupation:  Attorneys advise individuals and businesses on legal matters.  They consult with clients to determine the details of programs, advise them of the law, and suggest action that might be taken.  They also study and interpret laws, draft legal papers, and represent clients in courts of law.

Requirements for Licensing:  No person may practice law in the Commonwealth unless that person has been admitted to practice.  The requirements for admission are set forth in 1 Commonwealth Code, Division 3, Chap. 6.

Examinations: Must take and pass MBE and MPRE bar examination administered by the CNMI Supreme Court.  The exam consists of a multiple choice section, known as the Multi - State, and an essay portion. 

Application and Fees:  Fee to take bar exam $250.00.  For practising attorney  $300.00.  Annual fee $75.00 for active members, $40.00 for inactive members.

Relaterd Classification Codes:     DOT  110.107-010      SOC  211',
     '0', '2', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20100101'),
    ('69', '01', '0000000002', '004',
     'Acupuncturist', 'Description of Occupation:  An Acupuncturist administers specific therapeutic treatment of symptoms and disorders amenable to acupuncture procedures.  Selects  appropriate needles and inserts them at locations of the body known to be effective in treating certain disorders.  Requirements for Licensing:  The Board may issue a license to practice acupuncture to any person who makes application to the Board and meets the following requirements:
	A.  Is at least 21 years of age.
	B.  Furnishes satisfactory evidence of completion of (1)  a course or tutorial program in acupuncture which is acceptable to the Board and furnishes satisfactory evidence of three years of experience performing acupuncture or (2)  is licensed to practice acupuncture by a state or territory of the United States.
	C.  Is sufficiently proficient in the English language to carry on an appropriate conversation with patients. 
	
Examinations:  Endorsement.  Must submit a status report of license from National Practioner Data Bank.  1-800-767-6732.Application and Fees:  $50.00Related Classification Codes:  DOT  079.271-010   SOC  289',
     '0', '9', '1', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20100101'),
    ('69', '01', '0000000003', '002',
     'Architect', 'Description of Occupation:   An Architect Provides professional services in research , development design, construction, alteration, or repair of Property such as private residences, office buildings, theaters, public buildings or factories.  Determines functional and spatial requirements and prepares information regarding design, specifications, materials, equipment, estimated costs, and building time.  Plans layout of project and integrates engineering elements into unified design.Requirements for Licensing:   Masters Degree from an approved school,  1 year full time lawful experience,  passed NCARB Examination,
                                                                             or
Bachelors Degree from approved school,  2 years full time lawful experience,  passed NCARB Examination,
                                                                             or
Graduate of approved school,  5 years full time lawful experience,  passed NCARB Examination,
                                                                             or
 12 years full time lawful experience,  passed NCARB Examination.                                          
 
 Examinations:  NCARB Examination.
 
 Application and Fees:   $500 application fee and $500 registration fee - after approval of application.
 
Related Classification Codes:   DOT  001.061-010    SOC  161',
     '0', '2', '2', '9', '0',
     '2', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20100101'),
    ('69', '01', '0000000004', '004',
     'Chiropractor', 'Description of Occupation:  A Chiropracter examines patients to determine nature and extent of disorder and adjusts spinal column and other parts of the body to prevent disease and correct abnormalities.Requirements for Licensing:  Comply with Board Regulations,  satisfactorily complete a written and oral, practical and demonstrative examination of skill in Chiropractic technique.  Is a graduate of an approved College of Chiropractic.  Is and/or was licensed to practice in another jurisdiction, if he has ever been so licensed to practice.  Is lawfully entitled to remain and work in the CNMI.Examinations:  Endorsement.  Must submit status report of license from National Practitioner Data Bank.  1-800-767-6732.Application and Fees:  $50.00Related Classification Codes:  DOT  079.101.010   SOC  289',
     '0', '9', '2', '9', '0',
     '9', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20100101'),
    ('69', '01', '0000000005', '004',
     'Dental Hygienist', 'Description of Occupation:  A Dental Hygienist, working under the general direction of a dentist, provides direct patient care by removing deposits and stains from patients'' teeth, exposing and developing dental x-ray film, and performing various other preventative and therapeutic services.  They also help people develop and maintain good oral health by instructing individuals and groups in proper oral hygiene.Requirements for Licensing:  A person is eligible to take an examination for a license to practice as a dental hygienist in the CNMI who is:  Of good moral character,  is lawfully entitled to remain and work in the CNMI,  is a graduate of a school or college program in dental nursing/hygiene, approved by the Board, and is physically and mentally capable of performing the duties of a dental hygienist.Examinations:  Endorsement.  Must submit a status report of license from National Practioner Data Bank.  1-800-767-6732.Application and Fees:  $50.00Related Classification Codes:  DOT  078.361-010   SOC  3630',
     '0', '1', '2', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20100101'),
    ('69', '01', '0000000006', '004',
     'Dentist', 'Description of Occupation:   A Dentist examines teeth and tissues of the mouth to diagnose and treat diseases or abnormalities.  They take x-rays, place protective plastic shields on children''s teeth, fill cavities, straighten or repair teeth, treat gum disease, and perform corrective surgery of the gums and supporting bones.  Dentists may be general practitioners or they may specialize in one of the areas recognized by the American Dental Association.Requirements for Licsening:   Any person is eligible to practice dentistry in the CNMI upon submision and approval by the Board of the following proof and documentation:  proof of graduation from an accredited dental school or college,  or proof of licensure and practice of dentistry in another state, territory, or jurisdiction of the US;  proof of good moral character;  three professional references.Examinations:   Endorsement.  Required submition of status report on license from National Practitioner Data Bank.  1-800-767-6732.  Application and Fees:   $100.00Related Classification Codes:   DOT  072.101-010          SOC  2620',
     '0', '2', '2', '9', '0',
     '0', '0', '9', '9', '0',
     NULL, '20100101'),
